26b3f388531bc4680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d32243aefdd4446c270a33926b3f388531bc4680"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4ab3982b7226294a45295203c7cfdce441f7df32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:07:58Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:07:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): lint and test the storage opt-in scaffold (#650) (#655)\n\n* fix(python-common): ignore missing joblib stubs in mypy\n\njoblib ships no stubs and is imported only by the storage opt-in''s\nchassis/db_wschema, so the per-module blocks measured on a no-opt-in scaffold\nnever saw it and poe lint failed on every storage-enabled project (#650).\n\n* fix(joblib): default to zlib, lz4 is declared by no tier\n\nA bare JoblibHandler(dir).create(...) raised ''LZ4 is not installed'' in a\ngenerated project, because no tier''s pyproject declares lz4. zlib is in\nthe standard library, so the default needs no new dependency (#650).\n\n* refactor(storage): split the csv, json and sanity_check handlers\n\nNine functions in chassis/db_wschema exceeded the src complexity ceiling of\n2, invisible because CI never scaffolds with the storage opt-in (#650).\n\ncsv and json shared a copy of the same find/update logic; move it to one\nmodule of pure functions (_row_ops) instead of annotating each copy with\ncomplexity-ok. SanityCheck.validate splits into _check_class and\n_check_attrs. Behaviour is unchanged: a 219-line operation trace over both\nhandlers (duplicate ids, a pinned id, missing ids, an emptied store, a\nwhitespace-only JSON file) and six SanityCheck cases hashes identically\nagainst the previous modules.\n\n* ci: lint and test the storage opt-in scaffold\n\nscaffold-lint-test scaffolds with no opt-ins, so a file that ships only on an\nopt-in was never linted, type-checked or complexity-checked (#650). Add a\njob that answers the storage prompt yes through the named-key spec, and let\nscaffold_lint_test.sh say which opt-ins a run used.\n\napi-service-native-db also offers the opt-in but has no key map in\nbin/lib/spec.sh, so it is not covered yet.\n\n* fix(templates): allow joblib in the chassis layer policy\n\nThe storage opt-in''s joblib_handler imports joblib, which the per-tier\n.layer-policy.yaml did not list, so the layer-import gate failed on every\nstorage-enabled project. The no-opt-in scaffold never imports it (#650).\n\n* refactor(joblib): split _verify and delete under the src ceiling\n\n_verify (7) and delete (3) exceeded the complexity ceiling of 2 on the\nstorage opt-in (#650). _verify becomes four small checks and delete uses\nunlink(missing_ok=True). Behaviour is unchanged: an operation trace over a\nvalid read, a sha mismatch, a _saved_at mismatch, a tampered, missing and\nrestored signature, and delete with and without a sidecar hashes\nidentically against the previous version, with and without a secret key.\n\nAlso ship a witness for the zlib default and unit tests for _row_ops.\n\n* fix(joblib): pass the key to the signature check for mypy\n\nSplitting _verify lost the narrowing of self._key from bytes | None, so\nmypy rejected hmac.new on the storage-enabled scaffold. Pass the key in.\n\n* refactor(storage): keep the row helpers module-private\n\ncheck_all_exports requires every public name in a package module to be in\nthe package __all__. The helpers are an implementation detail shared by two\nhandlers, so prefix them with an underscore instead of widening the API.\n\n* test(chassis): type-prefix row_ops params, add explicit None-id case\n\nstr_expected held a bool and value had no prefix; the None case actually\ntested a missing key. Parametrize whole rows so both a missing key and an\nexplicit None id are covered, with no conditional in the test body.\n\n* test(chassis): block lz4 in the default-codec witness, name vars\n\nThe default-codec test passed even on a regression whenever lz4 was\ninstalled transitively; it now makes lz4 unimportable. Comprehension vars\ntake the type prefix (dict_row, dict_out, str_attr), and the storage CI\nstep name says it runs integration tests too.\n\n* test(chassis): patch joblib''s cached lz4, not sys.modules\n\njoblib imports lz4 once into joblib.compressor.lz4, so blocking sys.modules\nafter collection changed nothing joblib reads. Patching the cached module\nmakes (''lz4'', 3) raise ValueError while zlib still round-trips.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"c105d039e7b916bc7a77ef4a6a816c7b1d68b4a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/c105d039e7b916bc7a77ef4a6a816c7b1d68b4a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/4ab3982b7226294a45295203c7cfdce441f7df32","verification":{"payload":"tree c105d039e7b916bc7a77ef4a6a816c7b1d68b4a6\nparent 8a97b002b5ff3ee3f70b8bfc80705152b9ee0e72\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791436078 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791436078 -0300\n\nfix(ci): lint and test the storage opt-in scaffold (#650) (#655)\n\n* fix(python-common): ignore missing joblib stubs in mypy\n\njoblib ships no stubs and is imported only by the storage opt-in''s\nchassis/db_wschema, so the per-module blocks measured on a no-opt-in scaffold\nnever saw it and poe lint failed on every storage-enabled project (#650).\n\n* fix(joblib): default to zlib, lz4 is declared by no tier\n\nA bare JoblibHandler(dir).create(...) raised ''LZ4 is not installed'' in a\ngenerated project, because no tier''s pyproject declares lz4. zlib is in\nthe standard library, so the default needs no new dependency (#650).\n\n* refactor(storage): split the csv, json and sanity_check handlers\n\nNine functions in chassis/db_wschema exceeded the src complexity ceiling of\n2, invisible because CI never scaffolds with the storage opt-in (#650).\n\ncsv and json shared a copy of the same find/update logic; move it to one\nmodule of pure functions (_row_ops) instead of annotating each copy with\ncomplexity-ok. SanityCheck.validate splits into _check_class and\n_check_attrs. Behaviour is unchanged: a 219-line operation trace over both\nhandlers (duplicate ids, a pinned id, missing ids, an emptied store, a\nwhitespace-only JSON file) and six SanityCheck cases hashes identically\nagainst the previous modules.\n\n* ci: lint and test the storage opt-in scaffold\n\nscaffold-lint-test scaffolds with no opt-ins, so a file that ships only on an\nopt-in was never linted, type-checked or complexity-checked (#650). Add a\njob that answers the storage prompt yes through the named-key spec, and let\nscaffold_lint_test.sh say which opt-ins a run used.\n\napi-service-native-db also offers the opt-in but has no key map in\nbin/lib/spec.sh, so it is not covered yet.\n\n* fix(templates): allow joblib in the chassis layer policy\n\nThe storage opt-in''s joblib_handler imports joblib, which the per-tier\n.layer-policy.yaml did not list, so the layer-import gate failed on every\nstorage-enabled project. The no-opt-in scaffold never imports it (#650).\n\n* refactor(joblib): split _verify and delete under the src ceiling\n\n_verify (7) and delete (3) exceeded the complexity ceiling of 2 on the\nstorage opt-in (#650). _verify becomes four small checks and delete uses\nunlink(missing_ok=True). Behaviour is unchanged: an operation trace over a\nvalid read, a sha mismatch, a _saved_at mismatch, a tampered, missing and\nrestored signature, and delete with and without a sidecar hashes\nidentically against the previous version, with and without a secret key.\n\nAlso ship a witness for the zlib default and unit tests for _row_ops.\n\n* fix(joblib): pass the key to the signature check for mypy\n\nSplitting _verify lost the narrowing of self._key from bytes | None, so\nmypy rejected hmac.new on the storage-enabled scaffold. Pass the key in.\n\n* refactor(storage): keep the row helpers module-private\n\ncheck_all_exports requires every public name in a package module to be in\nthe package __all__. The helpers are an implementation detail shared by two\nhandlers, so prefix them with an underscore instead of widening the API.\n\n* test(chassis): type-prefix row_ops params, add explicit None-id case\n\nstr_expected held a bool and value had no prefix; the None case actually\ntested a missing key. Parametrize whole rows so both a missing key and an\nexplicit None id are covered, with no conditional in the test body.\n\n* test(chassis): block lz4 in the default-codec witness, name vars\n\nThe default-codec test passed even on a regression whenever lz4 was\ninstalled transitively; it now makes lz4 unimportable. Comprehension vars\ntake the type prefix (dict_row, dict_out, str_attr), and the storage CI\nstep name says it runs integration tests too.\n\n* test(chassis): patch joblib''s cached lz4, not sys.modules\n\njoblib imports lz4 once into joblib.compressor.lz4, so blocking sys.modules\nafter collection changed nothing joblib reads. Patching the cached module\nmakes (''lz4'', 3) raise ValueError while zlib still round-trips.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxyUuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4IAQACFXl8JPgjwaP+nIrLJJkLhG\nQtoLgMdqDdcHLIKPcWS9tmWdav5Gc+97MS5kIAMCDqJKoFAuUzBccPyvliaQVk0o\nKiHtIk20iwgrCVFG8ZZ9oTUWM0Du2TwSU5zVhx8ygG8fqdJoDbT5LX+5BBBJNwEC\nylrLAfmD80nrBYrmWDOBLI+sah5qbHTbXerc4T7uqURKgxjXFF1JS2NCA4UAvrIg\neL6gcG7X6lem3ZZuFATDxf760a3XpeeS0AN9nciaaY/YQnJAxHEAzWGJhA77cs2U\nqIydOkS0JdkwC6nQGSMoOG6wyrtNIkfrL/ZzRlt9S62IBwwywnlZlIV+bDA3WXzS\n8QPlqr8l+d8k9JN//ZtxDABnqNzhsNoBRSkp8m2Oq4NKasI1mmhFKp5pSZeBmFR0\nYOXXnV904V9H5uXsWV5q3FAllD9f1aVUI+4F2cKfGXooqLYZXqVOPBM/4THdGBVR\nYvEpVBJiEJxJHHfD3EOxwZz3u7kLlmDx3H+6+c5+5QIJh+g+6e7lg8nRXq70wdut\nY1lPfxiQI8mAaT7pvUXZa/zFyg3i6BQXACdDyXjdz/n+2kXnNUYPhCIyChilwQ/C\nYJCNsaOIya8gnzh5r1tC0kD+QenXznQQPlKH4c5Ri45aAdar0yq0IS1Vvrx9Kbl8\nmkzgRVC/dder0oaAdyX4\n=EjFQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T05:07:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/4ab3982b7226294a45295203c7cfdce441f7df32","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDRhYjM5ODJiNzIyNjI5NGE0NTI5NTIwM2M3Y2ZkY2U0NDFmN2RmMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/8a97b002b5ff3ee3f70b8bfc80705152b9ee0e72","sha":"8a97b002b5ff3ee3f70b8bfc80705152b9ee0e72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/8a97b002b5ff3ee3f70b8bfc80705152b9ee0e72"}],"sha":"4ab3982b7226294a45295203c7cfdce441f7df32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4ab3982b7226294a45295203c7cfdce441f7df32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/8a97b002b5ff3ee3f70b8bfc80705152b9ee0e72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:20:44Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:20:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(spec): trim spec values, exact skeleton match, check the stream (#662)\n\n* fix(spec): trim spec values, exact skeleton match, check the stream\n\nTrim leading and trailing whitespace in spec_get, so a CRLF spec''s\ntrailing \\r no longer garbles any key (otel=yes\\r failed loudly).\nMatch a skeleton by exact equality per name instead of a substring.\nCheck the answer stream''s PIPESTATUS in scaffold_from_spec. Say in the\n--dev --clean notice that the printed path is deleted on exit.\n\nAdd witnesses: CRLF trim, the y/n keys the emitters read versus the\nkey map, exact skeleton match, a failing answer stream, and the --dev\ntemp path lying under the sandbox. Widen the spec-answers hook''s\nfiles: to what the suite exercises. Document the unconditional refusal\nof an unmapped skeleton as a decision.\n\nCloses #636\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(spec): resolve answers before the scaffold runs\n\nThe stream status was read only after the scaffold had consumed an empty\nstdin, and a scaffold exiting early could surface the writer''s SIGPIPE as a\nfailure. Resolve the answers into a file first, then redirect it in. The\ntest now asserts the scaffold never ran, the drift test fails on call sites\nits regex cannot parse, the docs say values (not keys) are trimmed, and the\npre-commit trigger covers every python scaffold.\n\n* test(spec): skip comment lines in the spec_yn drift check\n\nA commented example such as ''# spec_yn \"$file\" key y'' was read both as an\nunparseable call site and as a real caller, failing the test for no\ndefect. Drop comment lines in both the guard and the key extraction.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"e379a93750bc769c877ffc2d9c75ac446499cc10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/e379a93750bc769c877ffc2d9c75ac446499cc10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/8a97b002b5ff3ee3f70b8bfc80705152b9ee0e72","verification":{"payload":"tree e379a93750bc769c877ffc2d9c75ac446499cc10\nparent 85d1f6581e67a3a8ed2f5f1efb1c8f27b3c13899\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791418844 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791418844 -0300\n\nfix(spec): trim spec values, exact skeleton match, check the stream (#662)\n\n* fix(spec): trim spec values, exact skeleton match, check the stream\n\nTrim leading and trailing whitespace in spec_get, so a CRLF spec''s\ntrailing \\r no longer garbles any key (otel=yes\\r failed loudly).\nMatch a skeleton by exact equality per name instead of a substring.\nCheck the answer stream''s PIPESTATUS in scaffold_from_spec. Say in the\n--dev --clean notice that the printed path is deleted on exit.\n\nAdd witnesses: CRLF trim, the y/n keys the emitters read versus the\nkey map, exact skeleton match, a failing answer stream, and the --dev\ntemp path lying under the sandbox. Widen the spec-answers hook''s\nfiles: to what the suite exercises. Document the unconditional refusal\nof an unmapped skeleton as a decision.\n\nCloses #636\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(spec): resolve answers before the scaffold runs\n\nThe stream status was read only after the scaffold had consumed an empty\nstdin, and a scaffold exiting early could surface the writer''s SIGPIPE as a\nfailure. Resolve the answers into a file first, then redirect it in. The\ntest now asserts the scaffold never ran, the drift test fails on call sites\nits regex cannot parse, the docs say values (not keys) are trimmed, and the\npre-commit trigger covers every python scaffold.\n\n* test(spec): skip comment lines in the spec_yn drift check\n\nA commented example such as ''# spec_yn \"$file\" key y'' was read both as an\nunparseable call site and as a real caller, failing the test for no\ndefect. Drop comment lines in both the guard and the key extraction.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxuHcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiO4QAAJQxMH5bWRI7XTVrk/wnxfx\n6I1+m6iHCV8DlMSdU4NUNzakaxmySi55hnfDiB/sR7S02SL61C0FSn72tajtidz/\nJZR7/9pjrAoqDCIJnrjIiCIEZtB/8sv9PwbQK9JfMjPqZCXz1C8XWdbRMtOP87n0\nWbD+HA0xJyV89UzvODO9/GvRknZFBsK4Q2C+LDHpY6mj7nAQw+Os/vOldE88LkIW\ntCrogT7lqxT9CGlpc11fZiMIzzNm+03JG830fD6QUE8opJDtW5hKPUHGyYd4pgum\nsVstvEMeCKmyvnAocwOBFOaGaiLM4nl0SLrypOoGrqS5qg3GpKEUX2PESqEX4hE5\nNeGg7CFopKZwCLL7YT6HaWSN8Ikbc7Y3XYjelwbDo2yJ3KKqcW6O5nq90iY9Mr2d\n1jhxgYY7Nq3lelDb4tB/m8aRknubvyRcbo3ZegxoiCa618OENbnmO29QS8lOtV4F\nq2lExLQdf2SKuIdk0Jo6yQ3CrOlmWjd+2DTdC6X/JdE9fLvc+iVqlew03FLEk4Ng\nKP+92Sjlu8EtZQfe0wtkzDq74ZOUir11JyneIEqGcgr2XwSyW0/edFgYU+AAaPAI\nf1QenvoZOHesbbn3Nq7yno01NefhV/koFVL+2BPyAGqM85xqQTP4ore7fWI8H+9V\nE8dXkblao+Dv7fWRsqAU\n=MlKX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T00:20:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/