b.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): enforce the .specs feature contract, add --root (#583) (#656)\n\n* feat(ci): enforce the .specs feature contract, add --root (#583)\n\nReject type-folders (bugfix/, chore/, ...) under features/, recognise\npr.md and pr-<N>-<slug>.md without letting them satisfy the floor,\ncheck the [ ] / [~] <branch> / [x] vocabulary in tasks.md, tolerate a\n.gitkeep in features/, and take --root <dir> so one implementation\nserves this repo and a generated project. A missing --root fails.\n\nAdd tests/test_check_specs_structure.sh: 15 cases, each rule with a\npassing control; every new rule was mutation-checked against it.\n\nRefs #583\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* ci(specs): run the specs-structure gate with --root and its tests\n\nPoint the pre-commit hook and the CI step at --root ., and run\ntests/test_check_specs_structure.sh from both (a new hook and a new step\nin the existing job). Scaffolds are not wired yet; that waits on the\nowner''s .specs/ layout decision.\n\nRefs #583\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(ci): close false passes in the specs-structure gate\n\nWiden the pr file glob to pr[-_0-9]*.md and guard with -f. Count\n+ and ordered task bullets. Track fences by character and length and\nfail on an unclosed one. Accept a tab after [~] and require a\n<type>/<name> branch. Add tests to the type list, the common.sh\npre-commit trigger, and reword the stale scaffold and tests/ claims.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0aa173a74242db15d3d794f14d5902234040c64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/a0aa173a74242db15d3d794f14d5902234040c64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/85d1f6581e67a3a8ed2f5f1efb1c8f27b3c13899","verification":{"payload":"tree a0aa173a74242db15d3d794f14d5902234040c64\nparent e663e007589958d78a81549d