/api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/489c29b1185105e2fa2ed187429aa64ac3c53fde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:48:43Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:48:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(joblib): confine artifact paths to the store directory (#645) (#648)\n\n* fix(joblib): confine every artifact path to the store directory\n\nread, delete and _verify built the path from an unvalidated record_id, and\ncreate from an unvalidated _name, so a caller-chosen ''../'' id reached\njoblib.load or unlink outside the store (blueprintx#645).\n\nFull-match the documented id shape and the kebab name charset before any\npath is built, and check resolve().is_relative_to() as defence in depth.\nShould-fail witnesses for read, delete, absolute ids, a slash in _name\nand a symlink out of the store ship with the opt-in.\n\n* docs(joblib): document the id rule and the update() contract\n\nChose to type and document the factory''s return rather than split the\nDatabaseHandler port: a read-only port would touch every handler, the\nfactory and every caller, to fix a failure that only happens when update()\nis called on the one immutable backend. The port''s update() and the\nfactory''s Notes now say it raises NotImplementedError there.\n\nShip the new joblib test with the storage opt-in in the three tiers that\noffer it, and state the record_id and _name rules in the tier docs.\n\n* fix(joblib): check the sidecar before unlinking, fix en-US and docs\n\nReview of #648 at 298c9f31:\n- delete() unlinked the artifact and only then resolved the .sig path, so a\n  sidecar refused by the confinement check left the store half-deleted.\n  Resolve both paths first; two witnesses cover the refusal and that the\n  artifact survives it (red before this change).\n- honour, normalised and Defence become en-US spellings.\n- Docs: create() turns ''_'' in _name into ''-'' before validating, and the\n  accepted and rejected characters are now listed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d830a82e82347020e87ba75caf26658a30ddcbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/3d830a82e82347020e87ba75caf26658a30ddcbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/489c29b1185105e2fa2ed187429aa64ac3c53fde","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d830a82e82347020e87ba75caf26658a30ddcbe\nparent 002432ccb13b0f6dd307ec39d623c5931875d22e\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791395323 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791395323 -0300\n\nfix(joblib): confine artifact paths to the store directory (#645) (#648)\n\n* fix(joblib): confine every artifact path to the store directory\n\nread, delete and _verify built the path from an unvalidated record_id, and\ncreate from an unvalidated _name, so a caller-chosen ''../'' id reached\njoblib.load or unlink outside the store (blueprintx#645).\n\nFull-match the documented id shape and the kebab name charset before any\npath is built, and check resolve().is_relative_to() as defence in depth.\nShould-fail witnesses for read, delete, absolute ids, a slash in _name\nand a symlink out of the store ship with the opt-in.\n\n* docs(joblib): document the id rule and the update() contract\n\nChose to type and document the factory''s return rather than split the\nDatabaseHandler port: a read-only port would touch every handler, the\nfactory and every caller, to fix a failure that only happens when update()\nis called on the one immutable backend. The port''s update() and the\nfactory''s Notes now say it raises NotImplementedError there.\n\nShip the new joblib test with the storage opt-in in the three tiers that\noffer it, and state the record_id and _name rules in the tier docs.\n\n* fix(joblib): check the sidecar before unlinking, fix en-US and docs\n\nReview of #648 at 298c9f31:\n- delete() unlinked the artifact and only then resolved the .sig path, so a\n  sidecar refused by the confinement check left the store half-deleted.\n  Resolve both paths first; two witnesses cover the refusal and that the\n  artifact survives it (red before this change).\n- honour, normalised and Defence become en-US spellings.\n- Docs: create() turns ''_'' in _name into ''-'' before validating, and the\n  accepted and rejected characters are now listed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxoX7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkE8QAHCD4qVrmvfehh/tGCX5NIfQ\nLB2035f2aX66FcbJgqNPsSQAfIG4X+DEbGMuDCKj1Ai0OAHCnHyMFJU+weLQZhvB\nQpxUhYjn1yorjUx38Aax5BtoblVqhRNnQ2fdw2ZW31ZWJFDrSJfVMk9J25AkQo6s\ngHGhudwAXKqyuha/hRgr3i+5JeAKW33oltIJAjuRwbB3lV7RGJWXgKw31WjHdB6m\njU4Cq4bvsPNUR7XPU8J5ciHmA9UDBWtHCHCiHyTPnEsjOHY3w0fBtWmNGyqGzkF0\noQhycW+sO3MFaO/mf2sa7+KN3DMG3ndCBC7o4K3i2P0GlZdLm67aatUAazXPg0VA\nPGqen43JiX7Vef5eVveM52SrPLTcpOLzt7lAE0tKOqJobiCgoacCht6iAEe6qtL3\nknbZ8X4AIh/ozvNeGmH+s3JaIDF4Hr7QtAVz7NHwhuArBsb4Q3trn9RfeLi8Tv7G\nk6H+xRAFsKOBnw