on locale'' prompt to bin/blueprintx.sh (en default,\npt-BR) and pass it to every scaffold as DOCS_LOCALE, next to LICENSE_CHOICE.\nThe six MkDocs-bearing Python skeletons render it into theme.language, with\nan en fallback when a scaffold script is run without the menu.\n\nThe choice describes the generated project''s README/docs only: code comments\nand docstrings stay English in every locale, and BlueprintX''s own prose stays\nen-US (blueprintx#194).\n\n* test(scaffold): pin the docs-locale choice, fix prompt stderr (#247)\n\ntests/test_docs_locale_prompt.sh asserts the prompt mapping, the placeholder\nin every templates/*/mkdocs.yml, the envsubst list in every MkDocs scaffold,\nand the en fallback when DOCS_LOCALE is unset. bin/blueprintx.sh gains a\nsource guard so the test can load the prompt helpers without the menu.\n\nThe test found a latent defect shared by every prompt helper: print_status\nwrites warnings to stdout, so an invalid answer inside $(prompt_...) leaked\n''Invalid option. Try again.'' into the captured value (LICENSE_CHOICE too).\nThe five in-prompt warnings now go to stderr.\n\ncheck_comment_language.py gains --root <dir>, the seam check_function_length\nalready exposes, so BlueprintX can run the shipped gate over its own tree\n(measured: 538 files, 0 findings). Its docstring and failure message no\nlonger hardcode Portuguese docs. docs/cli-reference.md documents the choice\nand what it does not change.\n\n* fix(gates): reject a bare --root instead of checking nothing (#247)\n\nReview on #571 found that `check_comment_language.py --root` exits 0.\nReproduced: the flag fell through to the filename list, file_problems\nignored its unsupported extension, and the gate printed\n\"documentation-language boundary OK (1 file(s) checked)\".\n\nA gate that reports success for having checked nothing is the exact\nfailure this repo''s gate family exists to prevent, and it had a\nsibling to copy: check_function_length.py, which this seam''s own\ndocstring says it mirrors, already rejects the same argv with\n\"--root needs a directory\". The two had drifted.\n\nsplit_root_option now raises ValueError, main catches it and returns 1.\nBoth directions verified: `--root` exits 1 naming the reason, `--root .`\nstill checks 538 files and exits 0.\n\nRegression test calibrated against the pre-fix file extracted from\nHEAD, not an in-place revert: the new case fails there and passes here.\nIt asserts the message, not just the exit code — a crash also exits\nnon-zero.\n\n* fix(tests): collapse a bare-root assert to the shape ruff format wants\n\nThe scaffold-tier lint step failed on ruff format re-wrapping this\nassert onto one line. Formatting only; the assertion is unchanged.\n\n* docs(cli): say the locale choice does not translate shipped pages\n\nThe prompt and CLI reference implied README.md and docs/ are written\nin the chosen locale. The templates ship in English; the choice sets the\nMkDocs UI language only. Reworded to match (ladder finding).\n\n* fix(docs-locale): wire its test, reject a misplaced --root, fix wording\n\nLadder review of f0cbe844, findings that held:\n- tests/test_docs_locale_prompt.sh ran nowhere; add the pre-commit hook\n  and the scaffold_checks.yml step, like test_validate_meta.sh\n- check_comment_language.py accepted --root only as argv[0]; an empty\n  value, --root=x and a later --root fell through to a vacuous success\n- the summary printed Docs locale for skeletons that ignore it\n- cli-reference said Two things above three bullets\n- the gate message pointed at a CLAUDE.md section that does not exist\n\n* fix(gates): resolve named files against --root, not the caller''s cwd\n\nCodeRabbit rung on b56a1b1b: main() resolved a relative filename after\n--root against the process cwd, so the audit read a different file than\nthe chosen root. Without --root the cwd base is kept for pre-commit.\nNew test pins it and restores the rebound module root on teardown.\n\n* fix(gates): dedent three docstring lines the re-indent left too wide\n\nConverting this file''s tabs to 4 spaces turned three over-indented\ndocstring continuation lines (3 tabs, narrow under the old tab width)\ninto 12 columns, pushing two past 99 and failing E501 in five tier\njobs. Match main''s 8-column rendering of the same lines.\n\n* fix(spec): honor docs_locale in --spec, reject a missing --root\n\n--spec never read a docs locale, so a spec-driven scaffold always got\nthe default. Read docs_locale (en or pt-BR, default en), validate it\nbefore anything is created, pass DOCS_LOCALE to the scaffold, and\ndocument the key.\n\ncheck_comment_language.py accepted --root <missing dir>: each named\nfile failed to read, no problem was reported and the gate exited 0\nhaving checked nothing. It now fails naming the directory.\n\nBoth have a should-fail test that fails on the previous code.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ff735157a53ad903ab3cab5509d58bf4e10b622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/2ff735157a53ad903ab3cab5509d58bf4e10b622"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/68c8c12b80b5538bcf3ff7e4555a92b7880e79c5","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ff735157a53ad903ab3cab5509d58bf4e10b622\nparent f4b59b9624a9d3e038a73470cc44e1220104349e\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791364511 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791364511 -0300\n\nfeat(templates): make the docs locale a scaffold choice (#247) (#571)\n\n* feat(scaffold): make the docs locale a scaffold choice (#247)\n\nAdd a ''Select documentation locale'' prompt to bin/blueprintx.sh (en default,\npt-BR) and pass it to every scaffold as DOCS_LOCALE, next to LICENSE_CHOICE.\nThe six MkDocs-bearing Python skeletons render it into theme.language, with\nan en fallback when a scaffold script is run without the menu.\n\nThe choice describes the generated project''s README/docs only: code comments\nand docstrings stay English in every locale, and BlueprintX''s own prose stays\nen-US (blueprintx#194).\n\n* test(scaffold): pin the docs-locale choice, fix prompt stderr (#247)\n\ntests/test_docs_locale_prompt.sh asserts the prompt mapping, the placeholder\nin every templates/*/mkdocs.yml, the envsubst list in every MkDocs scaffold,\nand the en fallback when DOCS_LOCALE is unset. bin/blueprintx.sh gains a\nsource guard so the test can load the prompt helpers without the menu.\n\nThe test found a latent defect shared by every prompt helper: print_status\nwrites warnings to stdout, so an invalid answer inside $(prompt_...) leaked\n''Invalid option. Try again.'' into the captured value (LICENSE_CHOICE too).\nThe five in-prompt warnings now go to stderr.\n\ncheck_comment_language.py gains --root <dir>, the seam check_function_length\nalready exposes, so BlueprintX can run the shipped gate over its own tree\n(measured: 538 files, 0 findings). Its docstring and failure message no\nlonger hardcode Portuguese docs. docs/cli-reference.md documents the choice\nand what it does not change.\n\n* fix(gates): reject a bare --root instead of checking nothing (#247)\n\nReview on #571 found that `check_comment_language.py --root` exits 0.\nReproduced: the flag fell through to the filename list, file_problems\nignored its unsupported extension, and the gate printed\n\"documentation-language boundary OK (1 file(s) checked)\".\n\nA gate that reports success for having checked nothing is the exact\nfailure this repo''s gate family exists to prevent, and it had a\nsibling to copy: check_function_length.py, which this seam''s own\ndocstring says it mirrors, already rejects the same argv with\n\"--root needs a directory\". The two had drifted.\n\nsplit_root_option now raises ValueError, main catches it and returns 1.\nBoth directions verified: `--root` exits 1 naming the reason, `--root .`\nstill checks 538 files and exits 0.\n\nRegression test calibrated against the pre-fix file extracted from\nHEAD, not an in-place revert: the new case fails there and passes here.\nIt asserts the message, not just the exit code — a crash also exits\nnon-zero.\n\n* fix(tests): collapse a bare-root assert to the shape ruff format wants\n\nThe scaffold-tier lint step failed on ruff format re-wrapping this\nassert onto one line. Formatting only; the assertion is unchanged.\n\n* docs(cli): say the locale choice does not translate shipped pages\n\nThe prompt and CLI reference implied README.md and docs/ are written\nin the chosen locale. The templates ship in English; the choice sets the\nMkDocs UI language only. Reworded to match (ladder finding).\n\n* fix(docs-locale): wire its test, reject a misplaced --root, fix wording\n\nLadder review of f0cbe844, findings that held:\n- tests/test_docs_locale_prompt.sh ran nowhere; add the pre-commit hook\n  and the scaffold_checks.yml step, like test_validate_meta.sh\n- check_comment_language.py accepted --root only as argv[0]; an empty\n  value, --root=x and a later --root fell through to a vacuous success\n- the summary printed Docs locale for skeletons that ignore it\n- cli-reference said Two things above three bullets\n- the gate message pointed at a CLAUDE.md section that does not exist\n\n* fix(gates): resolve named files against --root, not the caller''s cwd\n\nCodeRabbit rung on b56a1b1b: main() resolved a relative filename after\n--root against the process cwd, so the audit read a different file than\nthe chosen root. Without --root the cwd base is kept for pre-commit.\nNew test pins it and restores the rebound module root on teardown.\n\n* fix(gates): dedent three docstring lines the re-indent left too wide\n\nConverting this file''s tabs to 4 spaces turned three over-indented\ndocstring continuation lines (3 tabs, narrow under the old tab width)\ninto 12 columns, pushing two past 99 and failing E501 in five tier\njobs. Match main''s 8-column rendering of the same lines.\n\n* fix(spec): honor docs_locale in --spec, reject a missing --root\n\n--spec never read a docs locale, so a spec-driven scaffold always got\nthe default. Read docs_locale (en or pt-BR, default en), validate it\nbefore anything is created, pass DOCS_LOCALE to the scaffold, and\ndocument the key.\n\ncheck_comment_language.py accepted --root <missing dir>: each named\nfile failed to read, no problem was reported and the gate exited 0\nhaving checked nothing. It now fails naming the directory.\n\nBoth have a should-fail test that fails on the previous code.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxg2fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0G8QAESPYraTkvaOG8qOU+4JYJmN\n0ue9sz3wx7x0RS4Ksv7KkLGpGtGRXp8+pTO5RV+gNmTliS9g+DJu+97jgbdVaPhq\nM5m1zdR0qrcqyxf/DIOFpUCBrPGIPcCxQ+gIPir9x6tm/d8p11p/1vRYkKxAHY5h\nNGHfO0x4PUeuED5lXLMn0ZTqn9GrGOqDsGkKsu9lT9qsrNP1CEHdvoiEmvady24U\ns2/HGky/jK2ly4eh344EYhfw30AHYdi4dKkINe9bWZRe4cAnHZOahnJAQ8CZTr/S\nGfbN+UPcNmXgCvQY7AlBkim01eE4RXLmekzn5Xh0irwpFpymEiIaLv2vIQDDTowa\n8Zt3Oaw/NKQGLCt8LsI98kwf+oo7wMEFB3ROP1M+ExGO6fQdTdBSQtD+LTv+HllG\nglM1gUPI8HqNenFx3kQjKuPyLUepNYzyHQpQSeuG8W0aG9u16ESyJxwLqoguLlvh\n10QUq/GXvRy0ly0E6RrFeLX+b0Oa2WIK+DyiqJLKac7yTNrr1FQ/S0r2Jqo9DxPl\nfl2CR5DE3nfc5rGltu1Q7kCLM+OcmC10cDZEK2EWsJMhQvBvSxwZoMlKM19uuA12\nkCUzIPjqi2VNgzdC6505c/RE3jK++AblM0ScZOQg5tBn08Il/lxc6X45yJ7uZiAS\nLRGdOGSjs9b4cihwe587\n=Biep\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:15:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","