ermegor/blueprintx/commits/f85ddc3e929a49b5a694e4d438fd38522eb4835f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/35e9ce124ab1e1720305d7df9973fe2b0311545d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:08:04Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:08:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): docs-gap gate for orphan docs pages (#340) (#542)\n\n* feat(ci): add docs-gap gate for orphan docs pages (blueprintx#340)\n\nMeasures published docs/ pages that MkDocs builds but that never reached\nmkdocs.yml nav (and, where a repo carries one, its docs/CLAUDE.md file\nindex) — Layer 1 always runs, Layer 2 auto-skips when no file-index table\nexists (every generated project''s docs/CLAUDE.md is prose-only).\n\nAlso, required to get this commit''s pre-commit hooks green:\n- bin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py: record test_docs_gap_gate.py as a\n  deliberate DICT_EXPECTED_ABSENT exclusion across the 5 Python scaffolds\n  (bin/scaffold/*.sh is held by another open PR), mirroring #308''s own\n  test_migration_graph_gate.py entries.\n- tests/unit/test_migration_graph_gate.py: drop two decorative banner\n  comments the comment-budget gate flagged (pre-existing, from #537,\n  unrelated to this change, blocking every commit repo-wide).\n\n* fix(ci): gitignore semantics and a zero-discovery guard (#340)\n\nTwo review findings on #542, both reproduced.\n\nexclude_docs is read gitignore-style by MkDocs, and the matcher handled\nonly exact names and trailing-slash prefixes. Measured on the shipped\nconfigs: every template mkdocs.yml carries COMMENT lines inside the\nblock, and each became a literal pattern. Harmless only by luck — no\npage is named \"# work-to-do backlogs\" — but a real page matching a\ncommented-out rule would have been scanned as published.\n\nNow: comments dropped, globs via fnmatch, a leading \"!\" re-includes\nwith the last matching rule winning, and a leading \"/\" anchors to the\ndocs root. Six cases verified — folder prefix, comment, glob, negation,\nglob-still-excludes-others, anchored.\n\nZero discovery returned success. Reproduced: an empty docs/ with a\nvalid mkdocs.yml exited 0 having checked nothing. The file already had\nexactly this guard one branch above for an empty mkdocs.yml; the page\nlist had none. A scan that finds nothing has not passed, it failed to\nrun. Now exits 1 with the same wording as its sibling.\n\nVerified no regression: the gate still reports its two real findings\nagainst this repo''s own docs/.\n\n* fix(ci): match MkDocs publish rules in the docs-gap gate\n\nUse MkDocs'' own gitignore engine (pathspec) for exclude_docs, the implicit\ndot-path and templates/ excludes, and draft_docs, so the gate and the\nbuild agree on which pages are published.\n\nResolve docs_dir from mkdocs.yml instead of assuming docs/. Treat a File\nindex heading with no table as absent, keeping Layer 2 optional.\n\nRecord the api-service scaffold in the test-copy exemption table, like\nits four sibling scaffolds, so the copy-list gate passes on this branch.\n\n* fix(ci): wrap an over-long docs-gap docstring line\n\nruff E501 in a generated project, caught by the lib-minimal scaffold lint run.\n\n* feat(ci): wire the docs-gap gate, register the 6 pages it found (#340)\n\nThe gate was merged-in but called by nothing, and run over this repo it\nreported 6 real orphans: decision-records, issue-scope,\nquality-gate-blind-spots, required-status-checks, skeletons and\nskeletons/bash-cli were built by MkDocs but absent from nav and from the\ndocs/CLAUDE.md file index. All six are live pages (linked from code or\nCONTRIBUTING), so register them rather than delete.\n\nRun the shared gate over this repo from a pre-commit hook and a\nscaffold_checks.yml job (timeout-minutes 10).\n\n* fix(ci): install pathspec and pyyaml for the docs-gap gate\n\nThe gate imports both, and a bare CI runner or an isolated hook env has\nneither, so the new docs-gap job and hook died on ModuleNotFoundError.\nInstall them in the job and carry them in the hook''s environment.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e3bf6c16228d98f66e1418ea8072cdab906a79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/4e3bf6c16228d98f66e1418ea8072cdab906a79f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/35e9ce124ab1e1720305d7df9973fe2b0311545d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e3bf6c16228d98f66e1418ea8072cdab906a79f\nparent aafa6d05de0464904499fa7ca7212b4a4c4b3c21\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791328084 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791328084 -0300\n\nfeat(ci): docs-gap gate for orphan docs pages (#340) (#542)\n\n* feat(ci): add docs-gap gate for orphan docs pages (blueprintx#340)\n\nMeasures published docs/ pages that MkDocs builds but that never reached\nmkdocs.yml nav (and, where a repo carries one, its docs/CLAUDE.md file\nindex) — Layer 1 always runs, Layer 2 auto-skips when no file-index table\nexists (every generated project''s docs/CLAUDE.md is prose-only).\n\nAlso, required to get this commit''s pre-commit hooks green:\n- bin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py: record test_docs_gap_gate.py as a\n  deliberate DICT_EXPECTED_ABSENT exclusion across the 5 Python scaffolds\n  (bin/scaffold/*.sh is held by another open PR), mirroring #308''s own\n  test_migration_graph_gate.py entries.\n- tests/unit/test_migration_graph_gate.py: drop two decorative banner\n  comments the comment-budget gate flagged (pre-existing, from #537,\n  unrelated to this change, blocking every commit repo-wide).\n\n* fix(ci): gitignore semantics and a zero-discovery guard (#340)\n\nTwo review findings on #542, both reproduced.\n\nexclude_docs is read gitignore-style by MkDocs, and the matcher handled\nonly exact names and trailing-slash prefixes. Measured on the shipped\nconfigs: every template mkdocs.yml carries COMMENT lines inside the\nblock, and each became a literal pattern. Harmless only by luck — no\npage is named \"# work-to-do backlogs\" — but a real page matching a\ncommented-out rule would have been scanned as published.\n\nNow: comments dropped, globs via fnmatch, a leading \"!\" re-includes\nwith the last matching rule winning, and a leading \"/\" anchors to the\ndocs root. Six cases verified — folder prefix, comment, glob, negation,\nglob-still-excludes-others, anchored.\n\nZero discovery returned success. Reproduced: an empty docs/ with a\nvalid mkdocs.yml exited 0 having checked nothing. The file already had\nexactly this guard one branch above for an empty mkdocs.yml; the page\nlist had none. A scan that finds nothing has not passed, it failed to\nrun. Now exits 1 with the same wording as its sibling.\n\nVerified no regression: the gate still reports its two real findings\nagainst this repo''s own docs/.\n\n* fix(ci): match MkDocs publish rules in the docs-gap gate\n\nUse MkDocs'' own gitignore engine (pathspec) for exclude_docs, the implicit\ndot-path and templates/ excludes, and draft_docs, so the gate and the\nbuild agree on which pages are published.\n\nResolve docs_dir from mkdocs.yml instead of assuming docs/. Treat a File\nindex heading with no table as absent, keeping Layer 2 optional.\n\nRecord the api-service scaffold in the test-copy exemption table, like\nits four sibling scaffolds, so the copy-list gate passes on this branch.\n\n* fix(ci): wrap an over-long docs-gap docstring line\n\nruff E501 in a generated project, caught by the lib-minimal scaffold lint run.\n\n* feat(ci): wire the docs-gap gate, register the 6 pages it found (#340)\n\nThe gate was merged-in but called by nothing, and run over this repo it\nreported 6 real orphans: decision-records, issue-scope,\nquality-gate-blind-spots, required-status-checks, skeletons and\nskeletons/bash-cli were built by MkDocs but absent from nav and from the\ndocs/CLAUDE.md file index. All six are live pages (linked from code or\nCONTRIBUTING), so register them rather than delete.\n\nRun the shared gate over this repo from a pre-commit hook and a\nscaffold_checks.yml job (timeout-minutes 10).\n\n* fix(ci): install pathspec and pyyaml for the docs-gap gate\n\nThe gate imports both, and a bare CI runner or an isolated hook env has\nneither, so the new docs-gap job and hook died on ModuleNotFoundError.\nInstall them in the job and carry them in the hook''s environment.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxX9UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACTQQAG+/xlfNkV4i99v1Zh/4kRwq\n+CBc8D3/UqRASUUfaqk6KjwEbpr9eD0QjWy0j+cj7pbVKO3xeiygezEXspnFQZ1p\noOI6gaP1INSgj21p4qtlylH5c8UHVHv4vkCTxUBkTJzVwWkbcBKPwWGmo4C1A+K3\nHSwZzryUn+vIacFGJ8DW9zzXcflZHjhGSCm9xIlj8dEi57zv/yXTjSMC6PHxDgnh\nVmWA969a9xSRGZ7kUKpUC2/MHFoJcybV7EasKU6oVFeJYc6TZYJJ5Sl4Bq7md/LG\ngrhbVovoaANFcdoA4WVJ8