tion. Not yet wired into any pyproject.toml, pre-commit\nconfig, or CI — resolve_vulture() treats an absent vulture as an\nexpected skip.\n\nFixes a #331-shaped regression caught while writing this gate: the\nfirst draft filtered discovered files by every ancestor path\ncomponent, which zeroed out the scan whenever --root pointed at a\ncheckout living under .claude/worktrees/agent-* (this repo''s own\nlayout). Pinned by\ntest_discover_python_files_ignores_skip_dir_named_ancestor.\n\nRecords the new test as a deliberate DICT_EXPECTED_ABSENT exclusion\nin bin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py (all 5 Python tiers) so the\nshared-test-copy-list gate does not flag it: the gate itself is not\nyet copied by any scaffold either, for the same reason.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* fix(ci): exclude test_dead_code_gate from the api-service copy list\n\nmain gained the python_api_service.sh tier after this branch was written,\nso the copy-list gate flagged it for never copying the new shared test.\nRecord the same deliberate exclusion the other four scaffolds carry.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tg7pRKKVCMeVgKKNtbue5G\n\n* fix(gates): fail the dead-code gate on a file vulture cannot scan\n\nvulture records an InvalidInput exit code for an unreadable or\nunparsable file and carries on, so run_vulture returned the other\nfiles'' findings and main() printed the all-clear over a file nobody had\nscanned. Raise on InvalidInput and make main() exit 1 naming the cause.\n\nAlso skip the vulture-dependent tests when vulture is not installed, as\nthe gate itself already skips, instead of failing them. New should-fail\ntest covers the unparsable file; it fails with the guard removed.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(gates): split run_gate out of main to stay under PLR0911\n\nThe InvalidInput guard added a seventh return to main(), over the\nscaffolded project''s ruff cap of 6, so the lint step of all 7 scaffold\ntier jobs failed on check_dead_code.py:209. The template root never\nlints bin/ with that config, which is why it passed here. Move the\nscan, report and exit-code stage into run_gate(); behaviour unchanged,\n10 tests pass, ruff clean under the python-common config.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d9ec60f306ad4a44d976fa6e75f6c57bc8ce6b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/3d9ec60f306ad4a44d976fa6e75f6c57bc8ce6b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/aafa6d05de0464904499fa7ca7212b4a4c4b3c21","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d9ec60f306ad4a44d976fa6e75f6c57bc8ce6b9\nparent 8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791273178 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791273178 -0300\n\nfeat(templates): add a two-tier dead-code gate (vulture, blueprintx#332) (#541)\n\n* feat(templates): add a two-tier dead-code gate (vulture, blueprintx#332)\n\nMeasured the cliff in vulture''s own confidence score over\ntemplates/python-common/src/: 2 findings at >=80% confidence (both\nreal, both unused parameters), 63-66 at 60-79% (almost all a\ndeliberately-shipped, not-yet-called scaffold seam like mask_cnpj).\n\ncheck_dead_code.py gates only the >=80% tier and reports the 60-79%\ntier as non-blocking information, per the issue''s own measured\nrecommendation. Not yet wired into any pyproject.toml, pre-commit\nconfig, or CI — resolve_vulture() treats an absent vulture as an\nexpected skip.\n\nFixes a #331-shaped regression caught while writing this gate: the\nfirst draft filtered discovered files by every ancestor path\ncomponent, which zeroed out the scan whenever --root pointed at a\ncheckout living under .claude/worktrees/agent-* (this repo''s own\nlayout). Pinned by\ntest_dis