ZGUwNDY0OTA0NDk5ZmE3Y2E3MjEyYjRhNGM0YjNjMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845","sha":"8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845"}],"sha":"aafa6d05de0464904499fa7ca7212b4a4c4b3c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/aafa6d05de0464904499fa7ca7212b4a4c4b3c21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:47:29Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:47:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(python-common): build the offline wheelhouse (#299) (#531)\n\n* feat(python-common): build the offline wheelhouse (#299)\n\nAdd bin/build_wheelhouse.sh + bin/lib/wheelhouse_select.py: export locked\ndeps, select requirements by evaluating PEP 508 markers against a TARGET\nenv (not the build machine''s), prune the unused DB_BACKEND driver, then\npack a manifest + split-zip payload that the assemble step verifies and\nrefuses on any part-count/sha256 mismatch. Wires poe wheelhouse /\nwheelhouse_assemble and documents the workflow.\n\n* fix(python-common): shfmt-format build_wheelhouse.sh''s case statement\n\npoe lint''s shfmt pass reformats a case-arm indent that differs from\nshfmt''s default (no extra indent under `case ... in`), which failed\nscaffold_lint_test.sh''s \"lint must be a no-op\" assertion in all 5 tiers.\n\n* docs: register offline-wheelhouse.md in nav and the docs file index\n\nOne-line addition to each of two files held by concurrent PRs\n(#476/#503/#508/#523) — mkdocs.yml nav and docs/CLAUDE.md''s file index,\nboth required by docs/CLAUDE.md''s own maintenance rule for a new page.\n\n* fix(wheelhouse): canonical impl names, manifest containment, count check\n\nFive review findings on #299, all reproduced before fixing.\n\n`\"cpython\".capitalize()` is `Cpython`, so the PEP 508 marker\n`platform_python_implementation == \"CPython\"` evaluated False and every\nCPython-only requirement silently left the default wheelhouse. Replaced\nwith an explicit mapping that returns an unknown key unchanged rather\nthan guessing a spelling.\n\n`verify_parts` never compared `len(parts)` against `part_count` — and\nits own docstring already promised that check, so a reader had no reason\nto look. Added it.\n\nManifest paths were joined onto `dir_source` unchecked. `Path(base) /\n\"/etc/passwd\"` discards the base and `../../x` walks out of it; the\nsha256 fields authenticate content, never paths, so a crafted manifest\ncould read, overwrite or unlink outside the transfer directory. Every\nmanifest-supplied name now resolves through a containment check.\n\nAdds the module''s first test suite: 56 unit test files existed and none\ncovered this one. Calibrated against the pre-fix code — 9 of 10 fail,\nthe tenth being the negative control that must pass either way.\n\n* fix(python-common): clear 3 ruff findings in the wheelhouse files\n\nE501 in wheelhouse_select.py, unused json import and untyped\n**kwargs in its test; also apply ruff format.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tg7pRKKVCMeVgKKNtbue5G\n\n* fix(python-common): keep the right DB driver, refuse zero parts\n\nMatch DB_BACKEND case-insensitively and map mariadb to the mysql driver\nso the wheelhouse never drops the configured backend''s driver, and\nrefuse a non-positive part size instead of writing an empty manifest.\n\n* fix(python-common): Bash 3.2-safe driver pruning, fix offline install\n\ndriver_prune_list used an associative array and ${var,,}, neither of\nwhich exists in macOS bash 3.2; use a case on a tr-lowercased value and\na set -u-safe empty-array expansion. Document that a DB_BACKEND build\nmust install from the wheel set, not the full lock file.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(python-common): wheelhouse trap, sdists, stale parts, assemble order\n\nExpand the EXIT trap''s temp dir at set time (it leaked and exited\nnon-zero under set -u), refuse non-wheel downloads, extract nested\nhand-made zips flat, drop stale parts on rebuild, reject a zip_name\nthat collides with an input, and let loose wheels shadow the payload\nonly when they match its wheel_count. Warn on an unknown DB_BACKEND.\nDocs: assemble without poe, witness env var on the pip line.\n\n* docs(python-common): point the DB_BACKEND caveat at the build message\n\nPrint the wheel-set install alternative after a build, and use the\nconcrete wheels path in the should-fail witness.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd75558cc1312a58b772acbfaf1e4c64643d04ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/dd75558cc1312a58b772acbfaf1e4c64643d04ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845","verification":{"payload":"tree dd75558cc1312a58b772acbfaf1e4c64643d04ee\nparent 4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791272849 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272849 -0300\n\nfeat(python-common): build the offline wheelhouse (#299) (#531)\n\n* feat(python-common): build the offline wheelhouse (#299)\n\nAdd bin/build_wheelhouse.sh + bin/lib/wheelhouse_select.py: export locked\ndeps, select requirements by evaluating PEP 508 markers against a TARGET\nenv (not the build machine''s), prune the unused DB_BACKEND driver, then\npack a manifest + split-zip payload that the assemble step verifies and\nrefuses on any part-count/sha256 mismatch. Wires poe wheelhouse /\nwheelhouse_assemble and documents the workflow.\n\n* fix(python-common): shfmt-format build_wheelhouse.sh''s case statement\n\npoe lint''s shfmt pass reformats a case-arm indent that differs from\nshfmt''s default (no extra indent under `case ... in`), which failed\nscaffold_lint_test.sh''s \"lint must be a no-op\" assertion in all 5 tiers.\n\n* docs: register offline-wheelhouse.md in nav and the docs file index\n\nOne-line addition to each of two files held by concurrent PRs\n(#476/#503/#508/#523) — mkdocs.yml nav and docs/CLAUDE.md''s file index,\nboth required by docs/CLAUDE.md''s own maintenance rule for a new page.\n\n* fix(wheelhouse): canonical impl names, manifest containment, count check\n\nFive review findings on #299, all reproduced before fixing.\n\n`\"cpython\".capitalize()` is `Cpython`, so the PEP 508 marker\n`platform_python_implementation == \"CPython\"` evaluated False and every\nCPython-only requirement silently left the default wheelhouse. Replaced\nwith an explicit mapping that returns an unknown key unchanged rather\nthan guessing a spelling.\n\n`verify_parts` never compared `len(parts)` against `part_count` — and\nits own docstring already promised that check, so a reader had no reason\nto look. Added it.\n\nManifest paths were joined onto `dir_source` unchecked. `Path(base) /\n\"/etc/passwd\"` discards the base and `../../x` walks out of it; the\nsha256 fields authenticate content, never paths, so a crafted manifest\ncould read, overwrite or unlink outside the transfer directory. Every\nmanifest-supplied name now resolves through a containment check.\n\nAdds the module''s first test suite: 56 unit test files existed and none\ncovered this one. Calibrated against the pre-fix code — 9 of 10 fail,\nthe tenth being the negative control that must pass either way.\n\n* fix(python-common): clear 3 ruff findings in the wheelhouse files\n\nE501 in wheelhouse_select.py, unused json import and untyped\n**kwargs in its test; also apply ruff format.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tg7pRKKVCMeVgKKNtbue5G\n\n* fix(python-common): keep the right DB driver, refuse zero parts\n\nMatch DB_BACKEND case-insensitively and map mariadb to the mysql driver\nso the wheelhouse never drops the configured backend''s driver, and\nrefuse a non-positive part size instead of writing an empty manifest.\n\n* fix(python-common): Bash 3.2-safe driver pruning, fix offline install\n\ndriver_prune_list used an associative array and ${var,,}, neither of\nwhich exists in macOS bash 3.2; use a case on a tr-lowercased value and\na set -u-safe empty-array expansion. Document that a DB_BACKEND build\nmust install from the wheel set, not the full lock file.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(python-common): wheelhouse trap, sdists, stale parts, assemble order\n\nExpand the EXIT trap''s temp dir at set time (it leaked and exited\nnon-zero under set -u), refuse non-wheel downloads, extract nested\nhand-made zips flat, drop stale parts on rebuild, reject a zip_name\nthat collides with an input, and let loose wheels shadow the payload\nonly when they match its wheel_count. Warn on an unknown DB_BACKEND.\nDocs: assemble without poe, witness env var on the pip line.\n\n* docs(python-common): point the DB_BACKEND caveat at the build message\n\nPrint the wheel-set install alternative after a build, and use the\nconcrete wheels path in the should-fail witness.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKeRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3noQABSsdG7AnckDKP4k4jeFWLAE\nTZkVo3pP+AOHAwLScZe3/CTAf5Jw0RfEnBma05xX0dWgLLx6fpWMM5erUsyYYqHr\nt4zGEvxhfmJmKCge9iD+ATIIO3M9dTguNPrzAJR56xdsLLXmQZRY1h//jGXjUA2S\nJGlKCeh2/cpZE4n7KJHroWSIerQj77OlhUwPmL4eIHDu4HK2SK5vDLfRjakTC9bI\n4PDhN5mp4OVz5CGtTxIzoDdpe1CmPH1xfILfn/Yuccm4WfI3SwamYdVQwkme1Pe0\n2/+2cR4GpaMLlrLkycMmYHAP4cp/JcUdsqRTR3P98VIWZjBBv2eiyzX3svQ9/wE1\nRQToZDaXCTcBqmR9+4moXmngCQpEr+Jx60EscuMJlzy+EFhvUXbkVQy4RD92vHc1\nCstAVDc+lanfUqFqE4c6NWwCBMEuWhszk3jwyvuBQv7j4tpQHZ/pQpLsDhk25Zao\nCgM6wmkgV3paquY6UkntqP1lXxqEr3+BVg+m2ZXbefIeUdsKrCYwCey9HosIcQQ2\nif/VVE/zszbW2cz8er9R9OxeylW5gWAMOEqWhPEqCZwq4b7oQo//VJN7iPJ69xDY\nsCSy1Fri0QVTpe7xd7ZqDq346nWWAREgsOON2boFTgjLGSiAlsHBKRmnO61moZJk\n5Ihj5C0rFONOXzF+HAqn\n=u9tc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:47:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDhlMDZlOTU1MzA4MDY0NzUzNmEwOTFjNTdiYTMzOTk4ZGVmYzY4NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36","sha":"4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36"}],"sha":"8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/8e06e9553080647536a091c57ba33998defc6845"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:42:12Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:42:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(templates): REQUIRED_CHECKS — add the pr-gate name, reach non-Python tiers (#585)\n\n* feat(templates): require the pr-gate check, and make the list data\n\nREQUIRED_CHECKS was a literal in enable_repo_rules.sh, seeded with one name. It\nnow loads bin/required-checks.txt, so the qualifying set can differ per template\nfamily — rule 4 of the qualification test in blueprintx#565 is precisely that a\nshared script cannot require a name only one tier emits.\n\nPython tiers gain ''Classify and gate this PR'' (pr-gate.yaml, jobs.gate.name):\non: pull_request with types including opened, no branches/paths filter, and a\njob-level if that is true for every one of those events. Verified by reading the\nshipped workflow, not guessed.\n\nA missing file means an empty list, which is the pre-existing safe state: no\nrequired_status_checks rule at all.\n\nRefs #564\n\n* feat(templates): ship branch protection to the TS and bash tiers\n\nreact-spa-webpack, ts-lib and bash-cli had no branch-protection provisioning at\nall — REQUIRED_CHECKS there was not one entry, it was zero, and every qualifying\nname those tiers emit was required by nothing.\n\ncopy_repo_rules_provisioner in bin/lib/common.sh is the one seam all three call:\nit ships enable_repo_rules.sh plus the tier''s own required-checks.txt, so a\nshared script never requires a name only one tier emits.\n\nQualifying names, re-measured against the shipped workflows:\n- TS: ''Review threads answered'' only. webpack, eslint, stylelint, jest,\n  type-check, build and pack-smoke all trigger on pull_request with a\n  branches: [main] filter, so they are absent on a PR targeting anything else,\n  and an absent required check reads as permanently pending.\n- bash-cli: ''Lint - shellcheck + shfmt'' and ''Test - bats'' (ci.yml, bare\n  pull_request, literal job names, no job-level if). It ships no review-threads\n  workflow; recorded in its required-checks.txt as an accepted exception.\n\nEntry points: npm run repo:rules for the TS tiers, make repo_rules for bash-cli.\n\ngate-change-ok: the ''Review threads answered'' literal moved into\nbin/required-checks.txt, it was not dropped — the Python tiers still require it\nand now also require ''Classify and gate this PR''.\n\nCloses #564\n\n* fix(templates): don''t drop required checks, gate exit reflects state\n\n- enable_repo_rules.sh: a missing required-checks.txt is UNKNOWN, not a\n  confirmed empty list. apply_ruleset now skips the PUT against an\n  EXISTING ruleset in that case, instead of silently stripping its\n  required_status_checks rule (review thread on PR #585).\n- pr_gate.py: main() now returns 1 when gate_state() is \"failure\".\n  blueprintx#564 made \"Classify and gate this PR\" a required status\n  check itself; a job that always exits 0 could never fail that check.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b83ab3ec5f4dbeca8cb27e2f7e4d002bfff7aa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/9b83ab3ec5f4dbeca8cb27e2f7e4d002bfff7aa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b83ab3ec5f4dbeca8cb27e2f7e4d002bfff7aa9\nparent e20afdb8159101796651b5c0fbd443db44f156c8\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791272532 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272532 -0300\n\nfeat(templates): REQUIRED_CHECKS — add the pr-gate name, reach non-Python tiers (#585)\n\n* feat(templates): require the pr-gate check, and make the list data\n\nREQUIRED_CHECKS was a literal in enable_repo_rules.sh, seeded with one name. It\nnow loads bin/required-checks.txt, so the qualifying set can differ per template\nfamily — rule 4 of the qualification test in blueprintx#565 is precisely that a\nshared script cannot require a name only one tier emits.\n\nPython tiers gain ''Classify and gate this PR'' (pr-gate.yaml, jobs.gate.name):\non: pull_request with types including opened, no branches/paths filter, and a\njob-level if that is true for every one of those events. Verified by reading the\nshipped workflow, not guessed.\n\nA missing file means an empty list, which is the pre-existing safe state: no\nrequired_status_checks rule at all.\n\nRefs #564\n\n* feat(templates): ship branch protection to the TS and bash tiers\n\nreact-spa-webpack, ts-lib and bash-cli had no branch-protection provisioning at\nall — REQUIRED_CHECKS there was not one entry, it was zero, and every qualifying\nname those tiers emit was required by nothing.\n\ncopy_repo_rules_provisioner in bin/lib/common.sh is the one seam all three call:\nit ships enable_repo_rules.sh plus the tier''s own required-checks.txt, so a\nshared script never requires a name only one tier emits.\n\nQualifying names, re-measured against the shipped workflows:\n- TS: ''Review threads answered'' only. webpack, eslint, stylelint, jest,\n  type-check, build and pack-smoke all trigger on pull_request with a\n  branches: [main] filter, so they are absent on a PR targeting anything else,\n  and an absent required check reads as permanently pending.\n- bash-cli: ''Lint - shellcheck + shfmt'' and ''Test - bats'' (ci.yml, bare\n  pull_request, literal job names, no job-level if). It ships no review-threads\n  workflow; recorded in its required-checks.txt as an accepted exception.\n\nEntry points: npm run repo:rules for the TS tiers, make repo_rules for bash-cli.\n\ngate-change-ok: the ''Review threads answered'' literal moved into\nbin/required-checks.txt, it was not dropped — the Python tiers still require it\nand now also require ''Classify and gate this PR''.\n\nCloses #564\n\n* fix(templates): don''t drop required checks, gate exit reflects state\n\n- enable_repo_rules.sh: a missing required-checks.txt is UNKNOWN, not a\n  confirmed empty list. apply_ruleset now skips the PUT against an\n  EXISTING ruleset in that case, instead of silently stripping its\n  required_status_checks rule (review thread on PR #585).\n- pr_gate.py: main() now returns 1 when gate_state() is \"failure\".\n  blueprintx#564 made \"Classify and gate this PR\" a required status\n  check itself; a job that always exits 0 could never fail that check.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKZUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABEwQAIS5MqWG50SJ9NtG9S4E7Sbm\nbXX3W5SS9qBnFYswcNx2dqvvdEthMoAz+RXjfz73pna/qHT2cQCBcaczGGlsgq9M\nZKdjqg9GkruEVcLAcjlrD1v9HNyssnZ8hPSNWMXWnbkaUcq+rm1/bdO8J7YaS9hD\nDuHELbVRphLl5QpJADqw/qt8OJpxhEAe8HRuBdet1LDaXeCgYZDxP0jUPd1tIIcZ\nB+yCqhIDYF1uePOY4pIV2GAGQDCYu/VSyKTduy2FIS1/5AXbSlbWcKOk1lClUEeI\n9tY7FFr3vuvCE18076EwisdLhyX9SO2RvdELBw+eAbxjbhlMpF8WzMGG7ikW4gZp\n1HutdzNhYMzIfxBuaV6RPnNZWR+/sQkLEJw/DTiLvrpohvUQKZHl2fXVL7onMzkc\nS9xroQIt+9CFQZjBY/i35gRWVZH9o7SaDI+u0ETlQYiu1vOxXRlHY+iUCfA5Nj22\nwk7Ug8Qjy8y61czPlVcXgXGx9nlaUd+RKu/ydjy8zANsatI4MGjGTaYutGeFgTmX\nsDCAZ6dXyP+aEuvoJja1uOZIB8UPIjLpJ+Q274HWusFVUpiUs1HTNUgruPWJOOC9\npPWiJolaQo9/sIG/FahUIVn+Ab3k7WnX129XmzTJDrBS34GDxWBa5V4Cd9OoRgQS\n1QTm4x/w53gc/lv8l82k\n=c1bZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:42:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDRkMzYxYzljYTEzNjczNTFkM2ZmMTE4MDk0MTg2NmZjOGIzMTdlMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/e20afdb8159101796651b5c0fbd443db44f156c8","sha":"e20afdb8159101796651b5c0fbd443db44f156c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/e20afdb8159101796651b5c0fbd443db44f156c8"}],"sha":"4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4d361c9ca1367351d3ff1180941866fc8b317e36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/e20afdb8159101796651b5c0fbd443db44f156c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:08:06Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T03:08:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(spec): validate y/n, honor --dev/--clean, refuse unmapped tiers (#634)\n\n* fix(spec): validate y/n, honor --dev/--clean, refuse unmapped tiers\n\nspec_yn turned any unrecognised value into n, so a typo silently\nanswered no. It now accepts y/yes/true and n/no/false in any case and\nfails naming the key; spec_validate_answers reports every bad key in\nthe main shell before anything is created.\n\n--spec returned before the --dev branch, so --dev and --clean were\nignored and the project landed in project_root. Both flows now share\nselect_dev_project_root and print_dev_mode_notice.\n\nA skeleton with no prompt map ran its scaffold with interactive\nprompts, hanging an unattended run; it is now refused before anything\nis created. The CI harness checks SCAFFOLD_SPEC_FILE is readable.\n\nCloses #629\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* test(spec): generate the typescript language instead of sed -i\n\nsed -i differs between GNU and BSD sed; write_spec now takes the\nlanguage from SPEC_LANGUAGE, so the unmapped-skeleton case needs no\nin-place edit and runs the same on macOS and Linux.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(ci): reject a directory spec override, assert dev-mode exit\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* test(ci): refusal tests assert a nonzero exit\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"78647ca1a7f09d4c0ad89af70b799790d4afbafd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/78647ca1a7f09d4c0ad89af70b799790d4afbafd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/e20afdb8159101796651b5c0fbd443db44f156c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 78647ca1a7f09d4c0ad89af70b799790d4afbafd\nparent f8febda69981ecee72efc53b41b261febc2d5d83\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791256086 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791256086 -0300\n\nfix(spec): validate y/n, honor --dev/--clean, refuse unmapped tiers (#634)\n\n* fix(spec): validate y/n, honor --dev/--clean, refuse unmapped tiers\n\nspec_yn turned any unrecognised value into n, so a typo silently\nanswered no. It now accepts y/yes/true and n/no/false in any case and\nfails naming the key; spec_validate_answers reports every bad key in\nthe main shell before anything is created.\n\n--spec returned before the --dev branch, so --dev and --clean were\nignored and the project landed in project_root. Both flows now share\nselect_dev_project_root and print_dev_mode_notice.\n\nA skeleton with no prompt map ran its scaffold with interactive\nprompts, hanging an unattended run; it is now refused before anything\nis created. The CI harness checks SCAFFOLD_SPEC_FILE is readable.\n\nCloses #629\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* test(spec): generate the typescript language instead of sed -i\n\nsed -i differs between GNU and BSD sed; write_spec now takes the\nlanguage from SPEC_LANGUAGE, so the unmapped-skeleton case needs no\nin-place edit and runs the same on macOS and Linux.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* fix(ci): reject a directory spec override, assert dev-mode exit\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSNxnx3xHEyT49GBNg6XF6\n\n* test(ci): refusal tests assert a nonzero exit\n\nClaude-Session: