/blueprintx/commits/d7fa89d58b8f457f983abf80efa986c9c3ac37ef"}],"sha":"f8febda69981ecee72efc53b41b261febc2d5d83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/f8febda69981ecee72efc53b41b261febc2d5d83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d7fa89d58b8f457f983abf80efa986c9c3ac37ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:46:08Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:46:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(specs): move the backlog out of docs/ to .specs/ (#575) (#580)\n\n* chore(ci): let check_specs_structure accept tasks.md and .specs/backlog/\n\nPrepares the guard for blueprintx#575: a feature directory may qualify on\ntasks.md alone (work can be tracked before a design is written), and\n.specs/backlog/ becomes a recognised top-level entry for a multi-step\neffort that maps to no single feature.\n\nRule 7 checks the <kebab-topic>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md filename the same way\nrule 6 checks kebab-case feature names -- .specs/CLAUDE.md states the\npattern, so the gate checks it rather than claiming it.\n\nRefs #575\n\n* chore(specs): move the 44 backlog records to .specs/backlog/\n\ndocs/ is solely for published documentation, yet docs/backlog/ held 44\ntracked files that mkdocs'' exclude_docs hid from the site -- hiding the\nboundary violation rather than resolving it.\n\nEvery file is moved with git mv, so history follows and nothing is\ndeleted: CLAUDE.md is explicit that a completed backlog file is a\npermanent, team-reviewable record.\n\nNone of the 44 maps onto an existing .specs/features/<name>/ directory,\nand they are timestamped historical records rather than live per-feature\ntrackers, so they all land in .specs/backlog/ -- the home the issue\nreserves for an effort that maps to no single feature. Per-feature\ntasks.md is the convention for new work, not a retrofit onto closed\nrecords whose only date lives in the filename.\n\nrepo_rules_self_audit_164_20260904_062813.md is renamed to\nrepo-rules-self-audit-164_... -- the only one of the 44 whose name part\nwas not kebab-case, which the structure guard now checks.\n\nRefs #575\n\n* docs(specs): rewrite the backlog mandate to point at .specs/ (#575)\n\nThe instruction is the half that had to change. CLAUDE.md mandated\ndocs/backlog/<topic>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md while the same file states that\ndocs/ is solely for published documentation — so every session that\nfollowed the rule recreated the violation, and mkdocs'' exclude_docs hid\nit rather than resolving it.\n\nNow: an effort that maps to one feature goes to\n.specs/features/<feature-name>/tasks.md; anything broader to\n.specs/backlog/<kebab-topic>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md. .specs/CLAUDE.md gains\nthe tasks.md shape and the three markers — [ ] to-do, [~] <branch>\ndoing, [x] done — with the branch carried on [~] because an agent id\ndies with its session and \"doing\" without \"by whom\" re-creates the\ncollision the tracker exists to expose.\n\nRescued from an agent killed mid-edit by a session limit; the two\npreceding commits (the 44-file move and the gate change) had already\nlanded on the branch.\n\n* chore: widen #575 surface to the docs/ link fixes\n\nsurface-override: docs/CLAUDE.md, required-status-checks.md,\nskeletons/bash-cli.md and versioning.md only repoint dead\ndocs/backlog/ links at .specs/backlog/; they are the same move.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tg7pRKKVCMeVgKKNtbue5G\n\n* docs(docs): drop the backlog/ rows left in docs/CLAUDE.md (#575)\n\nThe subdirectory table and exclude_docs example still listed backlog/\nas a docs/ folder; backlogs now live in .specs/backlog/.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tg7pRKKVCMeVgKKNtbue5G\n\n* docs(specs): fix review findings on the backlog move (#575)\n\nRecord the 45 moved files (was 44), guard the empty backlog/ glob in\ncheck_specs_structure.sh, repoint the service-tag-changelog plan at\n.specs/backlog/, and mark the old lesson slug as pre-move.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7851a9c6f3edbc1f8656ec6b49cd735266d4180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/d7851a9c6f3edbc1f8656ec6b49cd735266d4180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/d7fa89d58b8f457f983abf80efa986c9c3ac37ef","verification":{"payload":"tree d7851a9c6f3edbc1f8656ec6b49cd735266d4180\nparent b55b045c170630737640cd960e6d3149b768c9c9\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791215168 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791215168 +0000\n\nchore(specs): move the backlog out of docs/ to .specs/ (#575) (#580)\n\n* chore(ci): let check_specs_structure accept tasks.md and .specs/backlog/\n\nPrepares the guard for blueprintx#575: a feature directory may qualify on\ntasks.md alone (work can be tracked before a design is written), and\n.specs/backlog/ becomes a recognised top-level entry for a multi-step\neffort that maps to no single feature.\n\nRule 7 checks the <kebab-topic>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md filename the same way\nrule 6 checks kebab-case feature names -- .specs/CLAUDE.md states the\npattern, so the gate checks it rather than claiming it.\n\nRefs #575\n\n* chore(specs): move the 44 backlog records to .specs/backlog/\n\ndocs/ is solely for published documentation, yet docs/backlog/ held 44\ntracked files that mkdocs'' exclude_docs hid from the site -- hiding the\nboundary violation rather than resolving it.\n\nEvery file is moved with git mv, so history follows and nothing is\ndeleted: CLAUDE.md is explicit that a completed backlog file is a\npermanent, team-reviewable record.\n\nNone of the 44 maps onto an existing .specs/features/<name>/ directory,\nand they are timestamped historical records rather than live per-feature\ntrackers, so they all land in .specs/backlog/ -- the home the issue\nreserves for an effort that maps to no single feature. Per-feature\ntasks.md is the convention for new work, not a retrofit onto closed\nrecords whose only date lives in the filename.\n\nrepo_rules_self_audit_164_20260904_062813.md is renamed to\nrepo-rules-self-audit-164_... -- the only one of the 44 whose name part\nwas not kebab-case, which the structure guard now checks.\n\nRefs #575\n\n* docs(specs): rewrite the backlog mandate to point at .specs/ (#575)\n\nThe instruction is the half that had to change. CLAUDE.md mandated\ndocs/backlog/<topic>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md while the same file states that\ndocs/ is solely for published documentation — so every session that\nfollowed the rule recreated the violation, and mkdocs'' exclude_docs hid\nit rather than resolving it.\n\nNow: an effort that maps to one feature goes to\n.specs/features/<feature-name>/tasks.md; anything broader to\n.specs/backlog/<kebab-topic>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md. .specs/CLAUDE.md gains\nthe tasks.md shape and the 