","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/b55b045c170630737640cd960e6d3149b768c9c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:42:13Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:42:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(ci): pin every shipped action by commit SHA and enforce it (#369) (#572)\n\n* feat(ci): fail an action reference not pinned to a commit SHA (#369)\n\ncheck_actions.sh gains check_action_pins over the template workflows it\nalready walks: every remote `uses:` must be\n`<owner>/<repo>@<40-hex sha> # vX.Y.Z`, the shape Dependabot''s\ngithub-actions ecosystem keeps current. Root workflows stay out of the\ncheck until the follow-up that pins them lands.\n\n* chore(ci): pin every template workflow action by commit SHA (#369)\n\n83 references across 25 workflows (python-common 22, lib-minimal 23,\nts-lib 18, ts-common 12, bash-cli 4, react-spa-webpack optional/deploy\n4), 12 distinct action@tag pairs. Each SHA is the peeled commit of the\nreal tag from `git ls-remote --tags`, annotated with the exact semver\ntag that points at the same commit so Dependabot keeps the pin current.\n\nOne commit rather than one per tier: the lint-actions pre-commit hook\nruns the new pin check over every template on any workflow touch, so a\npartially pinned tree cannot be committed green.\n\n* docs(ci): write the action-pinning rule down, with its witness (#369)\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md states the rule (full SHA + `# vX.Y.Z` comment, first\nparty included) and the count that justified it: 83 references across\n25 template workflows, 12 distinct action@tag pairs, 0 pinned.\ntests/test_check_actions_pins.sh is the should-fail witness: tag,\nbranch, bare SHA and short SHA fail naming the reference; full SHA with\nits version comment and a local reusable workflow pass.\n\n* fix(ci): pin the 4 checkout refs that landed after the pin sweep\n\nMerging main brought in four actions/checkout@v4 references added by\nother PRs; check_actions.sh rejects them. Same SHA as the rest of the\nsweep (v4.4.0, verified against the tag).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBgHFvpjdYVYC8bPoRhpsY\n\n* ci(actions): run the check_action_pins regression suite\n\ntests/test_check_actions_pins.sh was added but never invoked, so a\nregression in the gate gave no signal. Wire it into scaffold_checks and\npre-commit, mirroring validate_meta''s test.\n\n* fix(ci): portable mktemp in pin test, fail on zero template workflows\n\nReview findings on b008edcd, both valid: mktemp --suffix is GNU-only,\nand an empty template list reached check_action_pins as zero arguments\nand printed a vacuous OK. Use a temp dir with a fixed .yml name, and\nassert the template count before running the gate.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"729f86dc0e62a0653207587267cfd5695a0033c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/729f86dc0e62a0653207587267cfd5695a0033c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/b55b045c170630737640cd960e6d3149b768c9c9","verification":{"payload":"tree 729f86dc0e62a0653207587267cfd5695a0033c8\nparent 361db0bf594f686d960c50edfa351b8a0b3d8707\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791214933 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791214933 +0000\n\nchore(ci): pin every shipped action by commit SHA and enforce it (#369) (#572)\n\n* feat(ci): fail an action reference not pinned to a commit SHA (#369)\n\ncheck_actions.sh gains check_action_pins over the template workflows it\nalready walks: every remote `uses:` must be\n`<owner>/<repo>@<40-hex sha> # vX.Y.Z`, the shape Dependabot''s\ngithub-actions ecosystem keeps current. Root workflows stay out of the\ncheck until the follow-up that pins them lands.\n\n* chore(ci): pin every template workflow action by commit SHA (#369)\n\n83 references across 25 workflows (python-common 22, lib-minimal 23,\nts-lib 18, ts-common 12, bash-cli 4, react-spa-webpack optional/deploy\n4), 12 distinct action@tag pairs. Each SHA is the peeled commit of the\nreal tag from `git ls-remote --tags`, annotated with the exact semver\ntag that points at the same commit so Dependabot keeps the pin current.\n\nOne commit rather than one per tier: the lint-actions pre-commit hook\nruns the new pin check over every template on any workflow touch, so a\npartially pinned tree cannot be committed green.\n\n* docs(ci): write the action-pinning rule down, with its witness (#369)\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md states the rule (full SHA + `# vX.Y.Z` comment, first\nparty included) and the count that justified it: 83 references across\n25 template workflows, 12 distinct action@tag pairs, 0 pinned.\ntests/test_check_actions_pins.sh is the should-fail witness: tag,\nbranch, bare SHA and short SHA fail naming the reference; full SHA with\nits version comment and a local reusable workflow pass.\n\n* fix(ci): pin the 4 checkout refs that landed after the pin sweep\n\nMerging main brought in four actions/checkout@v4 references added by\nother PRs; check_actions.sh rejects them. Same SHA as the rest of the\nsweep (v4.4.0, verified against the tag).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBgHFvpjdYVYC8bPoRhpsY\n\n* ci(actions): run the check_action_pins regression suite\n\ntests/test_check_actions_pins.sh was added but never invoked, so a\nregression in the gate gave no signal. Wire it into scaffold_checks and\npre-commit, mirroring validate_meta''s test.\n\n* fix(ci): portable mktemp in pin test, fail on zero template workflows\n\nReview findings on b008edcd, both valid: mktemp --suffix is GNU-only,\nand an empty template list reached check_action_pins as zero arguments\nand printed a vacuous OK. Use a temp dir with a fixed .yml name, and\nassert the template count before running the gate.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8VVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1NUQAGUzXly0joliHwP/8LlPJLMS\n9D3SpIRiu9/msJOsYZK9YNWgSdXbQGot4ZQ4BRnZwPKWiDPwPuulrv+FnacajAj+\nspbMrV73tNvGc4AHjUOgCZ1QbvXloMx0bvSupy7jA95vJSUpe4+gaZGSNN9M6ZZQ\n2vqgvWlyamXDfP31y3Fik1p/JTPPY2f/FRaKTHmUWjn9TuAHcPwAPiMOCkkkOZqa\nmF2M5FXgYSw2H9DzrfMroiy7VFxEGQsUizwmDiZV8Mh+2VYZ9xOKNntIcUl2F5Y+\nE/IHXjnzmPzQ7uxaKDiqc/WNj2ElTrLTVQbLF76bwNIAJL6tr5drLalCtZ7SHpoo\nE8HwZpmCrv+OUkIuYmGZekg5Y1D32jUV2AEgdRCOJQjJoqukD5UD7ceeMurW3QDP\nubjimwVo2K0aY3uGIVwJmYViI867c1TcOfvFUgjr+X2jl2i2TcmYB8rsRUFhWcpy\nTr16J2nKVNjIcYkOZ3jXLSXQEo1VJwfdSnaNiZgztee2C92zXIKVWPlIzYqfqekF\n28ksVwrtUofDDC2TTqzj7i0O3ydgcXSbkVj/48exQDWGsUtg1cwQ1lmScDDR4b1G\nWsfZglf6dWemMVo+tezjKr0nBrYTMBhrhXZ9lA7DsHsYwF8jgR+g86craXRriZX+\nU7sbU951GW8FoseaDDAl\n=Wt9Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T15:42:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/