r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/361db0bf594f686d960c50edfa351b8a0b3d8707/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:31:07Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:31:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(templates): declare @eslint/js in the TS skeletons that import it (#620)\n\n* fix(templates): declare @eslint/js in the TS skeletons that import it\n\nBoth eslint configs import @eslint/js, which resolved only as a transitive\ndependency of eslint. Declare it at ^9.39.4, the same major as eslint, in\nts-common (react-spa-webpack) and ts-lib. Only ts-common ships a lockfile,\nso only its root devDependencies entry changes there.\n\n* fix(templates): keep @eslint/js beside eslint, sort it in ts-lib\n\nDeclared directly, @eslint/js no longer rides along with a solo eslint\nmajor bump, which would leave it a major behind. Group the two in\ndependabot ahead of the catch-all. Also move the ts-lib entry to its\nalphabetical slot so the first npm install does not rewrite\npackage.json.\n\n* revert(templates): drop the dependabot group, outside #614''s surface\n\nThe issue declares only the ts-common and ts-lib manifests; the scope\ngate rejects .github/dependabot.yml. The eslint + @eslint/js grouping\nmoves to its own issue.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"c726b4f1d39c142ff8a7976c092e106c2e4d2355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/c726b4f1d39c142ff8a7976c092e106c2e4d2355"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/361db0bf594f686d960c50edfa351b8a0b3d8707","verification":{"payload":"tree c726b4f1d39c142ff8a7976c092e106c2e4d2355\nparent a1e2f78dadf6528ac8e96c1e98614eaa9c63d44e\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791214267 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791214267 +0000\n\nfix(templates): declare @eslint/js in the TS skeletons that import it (#620)\n\n* fix(templates): declare @eslint/js in the TS skeletons that import it\n\nBoth eslint configs import @eslint/js, which resolved only as a transitive\ndependency of eslint. Declare it at ^9.39.4, the same major as eslint, in\nts-common (react-spa-webpack) and ts-lib. Only ts-common ships a lockfile,\nso only its root devDependencies entry changes there.\n\n* fix(templates): keep @eslint/js beside eslint, sort it in ts-lib\n\nDeclared directly, @eslint/js no longer rides along with a solo eslint\nmajor bump, which would leave it a major behind. Group the two in\ndependabot ahead of the catch-all. Also move the ts-lib entry to its\nalphabetical slot so the first npm install does not rewrite\npackage.json.\n\n* revert(templates): drop the dependabot group, outside #614''s surface\n\nThe issue declares only the ts-common and ts-lib manifests; the scope\ngate rejects .github/dependabot.yml. The eslint + @eslint/js grouping\nmoves to its own issue.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8K7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJt0QAF4QxDBF4NeSFjx78AT7+E3v\no732M9d6g6YvR0KZ3O6o2oC00DoPmdvTNKxcvS/KicNymNV0Nr5sa498krbethfK\n9YHvsxlwPGF8Sxh0pI7RMdE+tAXCiAz+alRXWkl5uACXwWrEB/oEhkgJg38ytkcV\nNPiZRlmNpUs0RtfhQA23RY14YsVXTocdGIhbtf1zGO6vJFgOqpoNstUSDn+uAEYh\nUGlvX1wLJgMzcV0lEFdh+I8g/zYmjXzVfw/K84tKhrpy/9mcjwhZ6DKGIz3R8fna\nE0W8R9t8cZsQPCK2rbhmQfxxF1/KwHNtfqGFo0eKk3W6PcgfXJJRwBLpiyzJmRYG\n+SCIcZkaGoYqMTDMg3CQ0isqp3PNiglUMNeZYoeKsQtb//pw6MNB/CgGN8fm1EMC\ngykcwz1warutW7j1GQwi4jy+UJWdAUjS8nJq+WeMTrT3xgSzsRtmgzNzIyX