.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/a1e2f78dadf6528ac8e96c1e98614eaa9c63d44e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:26:24Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:26:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(specs): dehydrate the 31 .git/ bodies into .specs/features/ (#584) (#591)\n\n* chore(specs): audit the 37 .git/ PR/issue bodies, 0 orphaned (#584)\n\nInventoried every *.md/msg*.txt in the main checkout''s .git/, matched each\nby content against gh pr list / gh issue list, and recorded the verdict in\n.specs/features/dehydrate-git-bodies-584/design.md: 34 shipped, 3 superseded,\n0 orphaned, 0 UNKNOWN. Nothing was filed as pr.md because nothing was orphaned.\n\n* docs(specs): clarify the topic-match vs exact-diff tiers in the audit\n\nCodeRabbit flagged that gh pr/issue list only fetches number+title, so\n\"matched by content\" was ambiguous for the 34 files not spot-verified\nby full-body diff. Record the actual list counts (315 PRs, 280 issues,\nboth under the 400 cap) and spell out that those 34 were matched by\ntopic + issue-number cross-reference, not byte-for-byte diff -- with\npr240.md/msg531.txt as worked examples of a correct match that isn''t\nan exact-text match.\n\n* docs(specs): stop a PR number opening a line as an ATX heading\n\nA reflowed sentence began with #589, which markdownlint MD018\nreads as a heading with no space after the hash. Move it off the\nline start.\n\n* docs(specs): state the limits of the .git bodies audit\n\nName the search scope, the topic-match verdict strength and the date\nof the status cells, and require a text diff before any deletion.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"1be37ef3f0b8ade7d567dc8207a9e9248bac62c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/1be37ef3f0b8ade7d567dc8207a9e9248bac62c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/a1e2f78dadf6528ac8e96c1e98614eaa9c63d44e","verification":{"payload":"tree 1be37ef3f0b8ade7d567dc8207a9e9248bac62c8\nparent 28bac0a8c73619cfc5fdc01667c589532ed63d94\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791213984 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791213984 +0000\n\nchore(specs): dehydrate the 31 .git/ bodies into .specs/features/ (#584) (#591)\n\n* chore(specs): audit the 37 .git/ PR/issue bodies, 0 orphaned (#584)\n\nInventoried every *.md/msg*.txt in the main checkout''s .git/, matched each\nby content against gh pr list / gh issue list, and recorded the verdict in\n.specs/features/dehydrate-git-bodies-584/design.md: 34 shipped, 3 superseded,\n0 orphaned, 0 UNKNOWN. Nothing was filed as pr.md because nothing was orphaned.\n\n* docs(specs): clarify the topic-match vs exact-diff tiers in the audit\n\nCodeRabbit flagged that gh pr/issue list only fetches number+title, so\n\"matched by content\" was ambiguous for the 34 files not spot-verified\nby full-body diff. Record the actual list counts (315 PRs, 280 issues,\nboth under the 400 cap) and spell out that those 34 were matched by\ntopic + issue-number cross-reference, not byte-for-byte diff -- with\npr240.md/msg531.txt as worked examples of a correct match that isn''t\nan exact-text match.\n\n* docs(specs): stop a PR number opening a line as an ATX heading\n\nA reflowed sentence began with #589, which markdownlint MD018\nreads as a heading with no space after the hash. Move it off the\nline start.\n\n* docs(specs): state the limits of the .git bodies audit\n\nName the search scope, the topic-match verdict strength and the date\nof the status cells, and require a text diff before any deletion.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8GhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArawQAD9c1RHjWOV+4KaTqbm+7T5i\nXdxIzK0vnsqevSL1w7IRCPh2hbcw61sa9YXUXU8tlyud5To4WmtH/RYrSB5Otm0v\nKUgQkUl6BOSFko7Tpwd68T0aOSky9KoAI9BolcsKYOfQeFTgs3D1fOLhEE21x5k0\nYP3xcp8XMjSs2ESq8tIuVIBuWZXLtiH6UW1DrLElGlbA8nlCpXaFBllDh0VQNKpZ\nPCFLlvW1prRJk/q2p3kW9oB/0pegCkc53ahsQC7v3OGcyw1FcLGPdmLEAyXpGWhs\nej81BIlAWU2X6pp5A90IvReyRtWhi+srOr1B6/HG1FFrHjP7rc2+w1DV+q1T3e74\nsAp2AJYckIIkD37Wkr5vLbht0Mk0aDUbRhNSDg1K/zL7TgHXEk9vfsZ42h0TAXe+\nlr1zBgjQMaXRrLBE/yq7O9ilDa9xaC7WA/ZjxY2s1XxGOYiyNpRKkbB9afi57/iz\nYe9yqqiJhftm0txauyrVWuhz+YAQ3H8gLlU5XRSfEjNIbimeGTHHFX1OJ+JSzdRZ\n9TTTlvEVkE0PypEA8LWX30mB26GkZRD1mBhAKenntI9vkrqNRnsI3E3CgByNcd/8\nA9h0au8Nhtj/CbWAPsBXu4nqew7DqirIRQKMrPOH2Z8wV90aojzgwRGdXhVLGNoB\nLbmc51MGBwKl72McXJBL\n=z9p0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T15:26:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/a1e2f78dadf6528ac8e96c1e98614eaa9c63d44e","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKGExZTJmNzhkYWRmNjUyOGFjOGU5NmMxZTk4NjE0ZWFhOWM2M2Q0NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/28bac0a8c73619cfc5fdc01667c589532ed63d94","sha":"28bac0a8c73619cfc5fdc01667c589532ed63d94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/28bac0a8c73619cfc5fdc01667c589532ed63d94"}],"sha":"a1e2f78dadf6528ac8e96c1e98614eaa9c63d44e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/a1e2f78dadf6528ac8e96c1e98614eaa9c63d44e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/28bac0a8c73619cfc5fdc01667c589532ed63d94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:50:31Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:50:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): ORM model-definition guards gate (Refs #361) (#514)\n\n* wip(ci): ORM model-definition guards (#361)\n\nRescued from an agent worktree after two consecutive quota kills. This\nfile was the agent''s only work and existed nowhere but local disk; the\nagent was told twice to commit and push first and did not.\n\nCommitted with --no-verify. The pre-commit function-length hook fails\non this branch for a reason unrelated to this file: main() is 61 lines\nin the four bin/scaffold/python_*_service*.sh scripts, a pre-existing\nfailure on main that open PR #486 fixes. Blocking a rescue on it would\nhave meant losing the file instead.\n\nUnverified in every other respect too: the agent was mid-refactor,\nsplitting the gate for the function-length and complexity ceilings, and\nhad not re-run its checks. Treat this as a snapshot to build on, not a\nfinished gate.\n\nRefs #361\n\n* test(ci): unit tests + copy-list wiring for ORM model guards (Refs #361)\n\n18 tests for check_orm_model_guards.py, both directions per guard.\nWire test_orm_model_guards_gate.py into both copy-list homes so it\nships to all five Python tiers, mirroring test_sql_guards_gate.py:\nthe shared bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh (covers ddd/mvc,\nnative and ORM, without touching the ORM scaffold scripts directly)\nand lib-minimal''s own inline list.\n\nSKIP=function-length: main() at 61 lines in the four\npython_*_service*.sh scaffold scripts is pre-existing on main,\nfixed by open PR #486, unrelated to this diff.\n\n* feat(ci): wire the ORM model-definition guards gate (Refs #361)\n\nAdd check-orm-model-guards to .pre-commit-config.yaml, an explicit\nCI step in tests.yaml (CI runs gates explicitly, not via\npre-commit), and bin/lint.sh, mirroring how the other full-tree\nPython gates (check-layer-imports, check-dtypes, ...) are wired.\n\nSKIP=function-length: pre-existing on main (fixed by open PR #486),\nunrelated to this diff.\n\n* fix(ci): UP038 isinstance union syntax in ORM model guards (Refs #361)\n\nruff UP038 in a real scaffolded project: isinstance(x, (A, B)) ->\nisinstance(x, A | B). Found by bin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh\nddd-service-orm-db.\n\n* fix(ci): ruff-format the ORM model guards test file (Refs #361)\n\npoe lint''s ruff format joins two adjacent string literals onto one\nline once they fit under 99 cols; the test file wrote them\npre-split. Verified with the root venv''s ruff (0.11.13, matches\nbin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh) against both new files: 0 findings,\nalready formatted.\n\n* fix(orm-guards): __table_args__ shadows, it does not concatenate\n\nThe guard was built on a false premise stated in its own docstring:\nSQLAlchemy does not concatenate __table_args__ across the MRO. It is an\nordinary class attribute, so lookup takes the first declaration and\ndiscards the rest whole.\n\nConsequences fixed: the duplicate check unioned every base, inventing\ncollisions between a live declaration and a dead one -- renaming the dead\none ''resolved'' a finding by editing code that never runs. It now examines\nonly the effective declaration. The real defect, a shadowed\n__table_args__ whose constraints are silently absent from the table, is\nnow reported in its own right.\n\nDeclaration presence is tracked separately from the name list, so an\nempty __table_args__ still counts as shadowing.\n\nTwo existing tests encoded the false premise and were rewritten; one had\nasserted that distinct names across mixins ''compose without collision'',\nwhich is exactly the belief that let this through review.\n\nAlso: the no-sqlalchemy-import fixture used filter(items=a & b). The\nscanner reads positional arguments only, so it passed with the import\ngate deleted. Proven both ways with the probe neutered -- old fixture\npassed, positional fixture fails.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* fix(tests): reword a comment ruff ERA001 read as code\n\nThe ORM guards test comment tripped ERA001 in all five generated\ntiers. Reword it as prose; no behavior change.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBgHFvpjdYVYC8bPoRhpsY\n\n* fix(ci): ORM guards skip pandas masks and mapped parents\n\nDo not flag & / | in .where()/.filter() on a df_/series_ receiver, and\ndo not report a __table_args__ as shadowed when its class maps its own\ntable (__tablename__); only table-less mixins are shadowed.\n\n* fix(ci): ORM guards use the real MRO and accept composed table args\n\nResolve in-file bases with Python''s own C3 order, treat a declaration\nthat reads <Base>.__table_args__ as consuming that base, see\n@declared_attr __table_args__, skip create_all under the __main__\nguard, collect positional Index names, and report a shadowed mixin\nonce. Only module-level classes are models; DeclarativeBaseNoMeta and\ngenerate_base() count as a Base. Fix the vacuous import-scope test\nand assert both Base sites are named.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"12abdcd8a2f45c16bf98cd1b59f12dc92b6a6cf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/12abdcd8a2f45c16bf98cd1b59f12dc92b6a6cf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/28bac0a8c73619cfc5fdc01667c589532ed63d94","verification":{"payload":"tree 12abdcd8a2f45c16bf98cd1b59f12dc92b6a6cf8\nparent adf63548edb653652411827d2f70f2bae476ceb3\nauthor Guilherme R