e-existing on main (fixed by open PR #486),\nunrelated to this diff.\n\n* fix(ci): UP038 isinstance union syntax in ORM model guards (Refs #361)\n\nruff UP038 in a real scaffolded project: isinstance(x, (A, B)) ->\nisinstance(x, A | B). Found by bin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh\nddd-service-orm-db.\n\n* fix(ci): ruff-format the ORM model guards test file (Refs #361)\n\npoe lint''s ruff format joins two adjacent string literals onto one\nline once they fit under 99 cols; the test file wrote them\npre-split. Verified with the root venv''s ruff (0.11.13, matches\nbin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh) against both new files: 0 findings,\nalready formatted.\n\n* fix(orm-guards): __table_args__ shadows, it does not concatenate\n\nThe guard was built on a false premise stated in its own docstring:\nSQLAlchemy does not concatenate __table_args__ across the MRO. It is an\nordinary class attribute, so lookup takes the first declaration and\ndiscards the rest whole.\n\nConsequences fixed: the duplicate check unioned every base, inventing\ncollisions between a live declaration and a dead one -- renaming the dead\none ''resolved'' a finding by editing code that never runs. It now examines\nonly the effective declaration. The real defect, a shadowed\n__table_args__ whose constraints are silently absent from the table, is\nnow reported in its own right.\n\nDeclaration presence is tracked separately from the name list, so an\nempty __table_args__ still counts as shadowing.\n\nTwo existing tests encoded the false premise and were rewritten; one had\nasserted that distinct names across mixins ''compose without collision'',\nwhich is exactly the belief that let this through review.\n\nAlso: the no-sqlalchemy-import fixture used filter(items=a & b). The\nscanner reads positional arguments only, so it passed with the import\ngate deleted. Proven both ways with the probe neutered -- old fixture\npassed, positional fixture fails.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* fix(tests): reword a comment ruff ERA001 read as code\n\nThe ORM guards test comment tripped ERA001 in all five generated\ntiers. Reword it as prose; no behavior change.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBgHFvpjdYVYC8bPoRhpsY\n\n* fix(ci): ORM guards skip pandas masks and mapped parents\n\nDo not flag & / | in .where()/.filter() on a df_/series_ receiver, and\ndo not report a __table_args__ as shadowed when its class maps its own\ntable (__tablename__); only table-less mixins are shadowed.\n\n* fix(ci): ORM guards use the real MRO and accept composed table args\n\nResolve in-file bases with Python''s own C3 order, treat a declaration\nthat reads <Base>.__table_args__ as consuming that base, see\n@declared_attr __table_args__, skip create_all under the __main__\nguard, collect positional Index names, and report a shadowed mixin\nonce. Only module-level classes are models; DeclarativeBaseNoMeta and\ngenerate_base() count as a Base. Fix the vacuous import-scope test\nand assert both Base sites are named.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6snCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATYEQAFZYMIuHQ3RdrEgxHIClmJcC\nKo42ZNl5V8BY+4RrXy7UZFA/OjlAs7awjOKa2u0ezv/g+3TVTD+AJEhjbxonsss3\nqeFhRu1TJ4sM1iGFIJG+c/1m/282uwMi/nFYccdglUyUflGXQg/FNiBRT+ntR7dQ\nsQvrlTVGTCxzESDxNUTNgbB+CM//1jM0+BNy44ZoAdDUxijjexch+yy1wZCEemp/\nB35iNKx36mPAxA/YA0mvQWlc+YK8WIH5Xwna18WCH4vHJJefa4AENoj7N9JZcW0X\ng/EIW7os/5vvjtyeCFQoJtYV15eiea0ilZw19Q/+DM+aWmjHnhGq2uuEFImhN6Lf\naLNnuMYthi8dDh7Ket2DeuQ7jMopAW6dTabC//LG3ns3SOgRgkRdsWssEX2UYk/e\nOSoq50lztn61PyFpgPuvIpguZgfGfNqDjJtOzA2d9hGdDOABxw5pEEee6RM5gFcc\nDFThbHh8rJklbpNhqMxUWOFAy41RW6fGBUUsjTK9bIZxy4vSyqZynCYFVHiPHuIu\nPpTwMyc0mzFAMeHHdkZR+E6FfeB2/otW252HZC58da0uKOm9YT0mQFExr6Gnk7rf\nn+fMTf/kOBhr8i57juBA0ZDlprN/3EpRxDaU5TLwxD9Pc0R7iS71itZeIQlVXrDZ\nQZrYz9syls2G1QiGpDln\n=0UKo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13: