MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/665000e6e5f5bbf22d4b970bb8aaced7095f8e4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:11:46Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:11:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(templates): editor rulers and the content half of #419 (1/4) (#552)\n\n* chore(templates): editor rulers and the content half of #419\n\nSplit out of #424, which is 241 files and exceeds CodeRabbit''s 100-file\ncap — it has been unreviewable since 2026-09-06.\n\nThese are the 18 files whose diff survives `git diff -w`: real content\nchanges (editor rulers in the two .vscode/settings.json, .editorconfig,\nruff.toml, and prose in the CLAUDE.md set), bundled into the reindent\nPR but independent of it.\n\nThis is the half that actually needs review. The other 223 files are\nwhitespace-only and ship separately.\n\n* docs(tests): reindent the four Python examples with spaces (#419)\n\nReview on #552 flagged the load_gate example (lines 95-107) as still\ntab-indented against the documented indent-style = \"space\" rule. It was\none of four Python examples in this file with the same problem; all 23\ntab-led lines are expanded here, since the rule does not apply to one\nblock. `git diff -w` is empty: whitespace only.\n\n* fix(docs): restore bash-cli rows in CLAUDE.md dropped by the merge\n\nvalidate_meta.sh requires every skeleton named in CLAUDE.md; take main''s\nfile and keep only the 4-space indent wording.\n\n* chore(ruff): transitional W191/D206 and format exemption for #419\n\nUntil the reindent chain lands, tab-indented files remain in the tree and\nfail lint under indent-style = space. Exempt only W191/D206 and the\nformatter; every other rule stays on. Removed by the last PR (#555).\n\ngate-change-ok: transitional W191/D206 exemption, 419 reindent chain, until #555\n\n* fix(vscode): keep the Ruff comment next to the [python] block\n\nThe rulers block had been inserted between the Ruff comment and the\n[python] key it describes; move it above.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9e97659f5a6146153a98a4ab433a89924c8f6c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/f9e97659f5a6146153a98a4ab433a89924c8f6c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/665000e6e5f5bbf22d4b970bb8aaced7095f8e4b","verification":{"payload":"tree f9e97659f5a6146153a98a4ab433a89924c8f6c7\nparent d2e5b2ef4dca470dd4dade5bc2f10b039c9c40fc\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791191506 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791191506 -0300\n\nchore(templates): editor rulers and the content half of #419 (1/4) (#552)\n\n* chore(templates): editor rulers and the content half of #419\n\nSplit out of #424, which is 241 files and exceeds CodeRabbit''s 100-file\ncap — it has been unreviewable since 2026-09-06.\n\nThese are the 18 files whose diff survives `git diff -w`: real content\nchanges (editor rulers in the two .vscode/settings.json, .editorconfig,\nruff.toml, and prose in the CLAUDE.md set), bundled into the reindent\nPR but independent of it.\n\nThis is the half that actually needs review. The other 223 files are\nwhitespace-only and ship separately.\n\n* docs(tests): reindent the four Python examples with spaces (#419)\n\nReview on #552 flagged the load_gate example (lines 95-107) as still\ntab-indented against the documented indent-style = \"space\" rule. It was\none of four Python examples in this file with the same problem; all 23\ntab-led lines are expanded here, since the rule does not apply to one\nblock. `git diff -w` is empty: whitespace only.\n\n* fix(docs): restore bash-cli rows in CLAUDE.md dropped by the merge\n\nvalidate_meta.sh requires every skeleton named in CLAUDE.md; take main''s\nfile and keep only the 4-space indent wording.\n\n* chore(ruff): transitional W191/D206 and format exemption for #419\n\nUntil the reindent chain lands, tab-indented files remain in the tree and\nfail lint under indent-style = space. Exempt only W191/D206 and the\nformatter; every other rule stays on. Removed by the last PR (#555).\n\ngate-change-ok: transitional W191/D206 exemption, 419 reindent chain, until #555\n\n* fix(vscode): keep the Ruff comment next to the [python] block\n\nThe rulers block had been inserted between the Ruff comment and the\n[python] key it describes; move it above.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2nSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiKYQAKSpJOX3m0huJ15O9IiAJbtI\nYzTvG0kqaYcm6tKpTPcVU0Brt6lFSgviY/WsX+1SuakMVDB/7XkCMz2XfqXLrdYm\nm+my2LFl55QdEPrXwCQ/YlDxrC18ojxlsn0+EuWZqdrGLvRvikd3Qt2wiBOaAHCM\nYFAbnqsqrTYvykwa0PnFyJ27SwzI9wzM3zJfiC+YsYj441HcuiAUtH159kzRxjFq\nU3r8J4OCtzk0srKAcQCgiARcMgmeiK1fV9QE52SB0BTq/zy+a9oFxHYl9rSVogR8\nDKp8NsVlojg0ll+AsdLO43IyJz0plJmujdp09WvVMKvcV4vqkyKH6J+/Ay2uzT6C\n5hWH7Nkbklh823iRsK1dII1O5NN0+eEgxNG/MXMZo6neafOUOLQRlGsFUPjMxMJR\nEpvWo0lIzc+zOVW2jwvIeWkH2H0kVk7s4n/OO4JM1rHtcz8K6fpKc2Gi/HuBGAT0\n6i1BG3FoDIyZskkfJKIBX8F1iqlZZGY60Zxkv30ly5ne4GM/rQr7oFxr21gqA1W0\nkembHf2vW+9ENeUw7jLqX5pVYm4RyxJ3D9SjrbVBS27Apl7EpXLqXN2TsKolEHe6\nY6CKE4VZYabMy86r6HlHV46dlpWzuq1R2Xrpq389wnYULLpYMGBCySnHpM+ggTmS\nRMYnL5Ozx+AiG/aj+SoJ\n=ZzOt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026