EwYjAzOWM5YzQwZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f","sha":"f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f"}],"sha":"d2e5b2ef4dca470dd4dade5bc2f10b039c9c40fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d2e5b2ef4dca470dd4dade5bc2f10b039c9c40fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:35:11Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:35:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(chassis): reject dashed database names in dump backup() (#607)\n\n* fix(chassis): reject dashed database names in dump backup()\n\nmysqldump/mariadb-dump/pg_dump use getopt-style parsing, so a bare\npositional dbname starting with \"-\" (e.g. --file=/tmp/pwned) is read\nas an option flag instead of a database name, letting a malicious DSN\nredirect where the backup dump is written. Confirmed locally against\npg_dump 18.6.\n\nAdd validate_not_flag() to the shared chassis/db helpers and call it\nonce, at handler construction, in the mysql/mariadb/postgres handlers\nof both api-service-native-db and ddd-service-native-db (the only\ntiers/handlers that shell out for backup()). One regression test per\nhandler family asserts the value is rejected before subprocess.run is\never invoked.\n\nCloses #600\n\n* fix(chassis): guard pg_dump positional in db.sh, flatten new tests\n\ndb.sh passed DB_NAME from .env to pg_dump as a bare positional, the same\noption-injection shape as the handlers; add the ''--'' terminator\n(verified: pg_dump then rejects --file=... instead of honouring it).\n\nThe regression tests used try/except/else, which is complexity 2 and\nbreaks the tests/ ceiling of 1 in a generated project; use\npytest.raises so a missing rejection fails the test.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBgHFvpjdYVYC8bPoRhpsY\n\n* fix(chassis): export validate_not_flag from chassis.db.infrastructure\n\nThe tier scaffold''s __all__ completeness gate rejects a public helper\ndefined in helpers.py but missing from the package''s __all__; that was\nthe failure in the ddd-service-native-db tier job.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"fad88bce2bf59a836560e67729fe8e8f96baf5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/fad88bce2bf59a836560e67729fe8e8f96baf5f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f","verification":{"payload":"tree fad88bce2bf59a836560e67729fe8e8f96baf5f2\nparent 94d3301101ba85f8794f33eda228fc19ee333b09\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791156911 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791156911 +0000\n\nfix(chassis): reject dashed database names in dump backup() (#607)\n\n* fix(chassis): reject dashed database names in dump backup()\n\nmysqldump/mariadb-dump/pg_dump use getopt-style parsing, so a bare\npositional dbname starting with \"-\" (e.g. --file=/tmp/pwned) is read\nas an option flag instead of a database name, letting a malicious DSN\nredirect where the backup dump is written. Confirmed locally against\npg_dump 18.6.\n\nAdd validate_not_flag() to the shared chassis/db helpers and call it\nonce, at handler construction, in the mysql/mariadb/postgres handlers\nof both api-service-native-db and ddd-service-native-db (the only\ntiers/handlers that shell out for backup()). One regression test per\nhandler family asserts the value is rejected before subprocess.run is\never invoked.\n\nCloses #600\n\n* fix(chassis): guard pg_dump positional in db.sh, flatten new tests\n\ndb.sh passed DB_NAME from .env to pg_dump as a bare positional, the same\noption-injection shape as the handlers; add the ''--'' terminator\n(verified: pg_dump then rejects --file=... instead of honouring it).\n\nThe regression tests used try/except/else, which is complexity 2 and\nbreaks the tests/ ceiling of 1 in a generated project; use\npytest.raises so a missing rejection fails the test.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBgHFvpjdYVYC8bPoRhpsY\n\n* fix(chassis): export validate_not_flag from chassis.db.infrastructure\n\nThe tier scaffold''s __all__ completeness gate rejects a public helper\ndefined in helpers.py but missing from the package''s __all__; that was\nthe failure in the ddd-service-native-db tier job.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwuKvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvtgQAKLZ4UYXDoBWCJFx3DIG+njs\n4rszIHq4z70uTnlOL2IQUqrr30BWOJL9EI5BJoP6hE6LFk0+pqZaX+It51V8pxkj\neXunlLt+L3Grys/I5MF9QErOeURscMs