.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/94d3301101ba85f8794f33eda228fc19ee333b09"}],"sha":"f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/f93cd47b5ad18dbda08098682a95309c995d3d3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/94d3301101ba85f8794f33eda228fc19ee333b09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T21:16:41Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T21:16:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(python-common): branch coverage, floor measured then set (#488)\n\n* feat(python-common): branch coverage, floor measured then set (#427)\n\nMeasured statement vs --cov-branch in a real scaffold per tier before\ntouching anything: ddd tiers and lib-minimal sit at 100/100 (no\ncapability code ships outside .coveragerc''s omit list), mvc-native\nrises 80->81, mvc-orm stays flat at 76 (already below the old 80 floor,\na pre-existing gap this line does not create). branch = True plus a\nfail_under of 76 - the tightest floor with zero current violations -\nland in one commit so the metric and its floor never disagree.\n\nCloses #427\n\n* fix(python-common): keep the coverage floor at 80, document the gap\n\nReview findings on the branch-coverage PR:\n- #427 forbids lowering the floor to fit branch = True, and the shared\n  floor of 76 would loosen it for four tiers. Restore 80 and record\n  the mvc-service-orm-db gap as a pre-existing finding.\n- Move the measurement table and rationale out of .coveragerc into\n  docs/coverage-floor.md; leave a one-line pointer.\n- Enable branch = True in lib-minimal''s own .coveragerc so the metric\n  means the same thing in every tier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5bba8df1cc9d2f20562bf06ec52e6a8deb91b0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/a5bba8df1cc9d2f20562bf06ec52e6a8deb91b0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/94d3301101ba85f8794f33eda228fc19ee333b09","verification":{"payload":"tree a5bba8df1cc9d2f20562bf06ec52e6a8deb91b0f\nparent 23a2432536c1e2747b790bdf1471e2b577067291\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791148601 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791148601 +0000\n\nfeat(python-common): branch coverage, floor measured then set (#488)\n\n* feat(python-common): branch coverage, floor measured then set (#427)\n\nMeasured statement vs --cov-branch in a real scaffold per tier before\ntouching anything: ddd tiers and lib-minimal sit at 100/100 (no\ncapability code ships outside .coveragerc''s omit list), mvc-native\nrises 80->81, mvc-orm stays flat at 76 (already below the old 80 floor,\na pre-existing gap this line does not create). branch = True plus a\nfail_under of 76 - the tightest floor with zero current violations -\nland in one commit so the metric and its floor never disagree.\n\nCloses #427\n\n* fix(python-common): keep the coverage floor at 80, document the gap\n\nReview findings on the branch-coverage PR:\n- #427 forbids lowering the floor to fit branch = True, and the shared\n  floor of 76 would loosen it for four tiers. Restore 80 and record\n  the mvc-service-orm-db gap as a pre-existing finding.\n- Move the measurement table and rationale out of .coveragerc into\n  docs/coverage-floor.md; leave a one-line pointer.\n- Enable branch = True in lib-minimal''s own .coveragerc so the metric\n  means the same thing in every tier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwsI5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxiQQALFh6LJAlgUSED/4fXHT/1i4\nbxKg9R2Z2X2IZWG/P6+i+ZLOaAG9ycS3d4OWlqVCJDFBxCouHOaNHJ0b5z+1Iaes\nlFctxs0r9XNZoNiR7vQxNvcY3lGorEite2D/FdVQqETzmBlspyLP2ZsUeSmWoHRq\nzlTifrXZ9j591D7bCITP05QXOjCMh4AUQUBrVuk2B5lbNNCxJ7BjdO2kp99PAZbk\nAQrGzAVluTcx9/VlKnuNneUZshDURiuWnrWQutZyFkOZYyMLJD2liM/XP8i1VVbL\nbnr0vqJ+J0eRehKGKnPyxqJQHGag3ky+jlsHZy/N9/ratJfMGjR+Tr05AFOKgM/1\npX//kpKv8kWV7h/DXQO+uPdmcbTVrtCUDCWLzx33k02+76EMuY/CxA+U7HldDmVi\n00ku+Mr2mhFKCdhKq+lH2WRkYMe0x5jmkEGsnvEybJgwWuvDY0RALfsbncmUhwsS\nlYKzgnfpIfleiUQ7RmVU/QNsMy2GzNp+7UPGAdo5ooLru/gPDuC/EjCU2HJ+CBY9\nw+hRwrqraY8NdefAzb5VaJ7ER8B5Q8eKJDIlrVfP0ECvwm3VWJHtgL7BlOfGLYmH\neQz57p+OCuFNLCpRM4CfJUU81sa/rpkBTLcHqYy/mXbU/Shop4NCHIAl3eWdpwxb\nw09ICS2JSVJFx3AnTwWq\n=EH9g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T21:16:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/w