https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/23a2432536c1e2747b790bdf1471e2b577067291/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:48:31Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:48:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(ci): measure why complexity ceilings are 1/2/8, not radon''s scale (#476)\n\n* docs(ci): measure why complexity ceilings are 1/2/8, not radon''s scale\n\nAdds docs/complexity-ceilings-measured.md with a reproduced per-construct\nruff C901 table (and/or, try/except, if-in-for, nested if, assert-only,\nwith+assert) confirming mccabe and radon count different things under\nthe same name, so a radon grade cannot justify or challenge a ruff\nceiling. Registers the page in mkdocs.yml nav.\n\nCloses #425\n\n* docs(ci): sequential ifs also trip the src complexity ceiling\n\nReview showed two flat sequential ifs report 3 > 2 under ruff C901, so\nnesting is not the only constraint the page described.\n\n* docs(ci): index the complexity page and point the gate at #425\n\nAdd the docs/CLAUDE.md file-index row for the new page and a one-line\npointer to blueprintx#425 in check_complexity.sh and the python-common\nCLAUDE.md, as the issue asked.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"0049d1e6a9b578d7517c42a2cc303054da2efd0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/0049d1e6a9b578d7517c42a2cc303054da2efd0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/23a2432536c1e2747b790bdf1471e2b577067291","verification":{"payload":"tree 0049d1e6a9b578d7517c42a2cc303054da2efd0d\nparent 8791e5f560ccbd9ba0cec1bd88598db42aeee873\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@u