eived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/8791e5f560ccbd9ba0cec1bd88598db42aeee873","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDg3OTFlNWY1NjBjY2JkOWJhMGNlYzFiZDg4NTk4ZGI0MmFlZWU4NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b","sha":"bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b"}],"sha":"8791e5f560ccbd9ba0cec1bd88598db42aeee873","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/8791e5f560ccbd9ba0cec1bd88598db42aeee873"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:00:40Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:00:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): ignore incoming main files in pr-file-count mid-merge (#611)\n\n* fix(ci): ignore the incoming side''s files in pr-file-count mid-merge\n\nWhile a merge of main into a branch is in progress the index already holds\nmain''s files, but the base came from the pre-merge HEAD, so main''s delta was\ncharged to the branch: 186 files reported for a real 69.\n\nResolve the base against the merge commit about to be created when MERGE_HEAD\nexists. Adds should-pass and should-fail mid-merge regression cases.\n\n* fix(ci): count every incoming head of an octopus merge in pr-file-count\n\nrev-parse MERGE_HEAD resolves only the first line of the file, so an\noctopus merge left the other incoming heads'' files charged to the\nbranch. Read all heads from the MERGE_HEAD file and pass them to\nmerge-base. Adds an octopus mid-merge regression case (fails when only\nthe first head is used).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ba830659beeb10694fc33d53ad66a6562d10d4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/0ba830659beeb10694fc33d53ad66a6562d10d4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ba830659beeb10694fc33d53ad66a6562d10d4a\nparent 53ff992ed24e81fb8445a751a2efc73b3b57f1da\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791129640 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791129640 +0000\n\nfix(ci): ignore incoming main files in pr-file-count mid-merge (#611)\n\n* fix(ci): ignore the incoming side''s files in pr-file-count mid-merge\n\nWhile a merge of main into a branch is in progress the index already holds\nmain''s files, but the base came from the pre-merge HEAD, so main''s delta was\ncharged to the branch: 186 files reported for a real 69.\n\nResolve the base against the merge commit about to be created when MERGE_HEAD\nexists. Adds should-pass and should-fail mid-merge regression cases.\n\n* fix(ci): count every incoming head of an octopus merge in pr-file-count\n\nrev-parse MERGE_HEAD resolves only the first line of the file, so an\noctopus merge left the other incoming heads'' files charged to the\nbranch. Read all heads from the MERGE_HEAD file and pass them to\nmerge-base. Adds an octopus mid-merge regression case (fails when only\nthe first head is used).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwngoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVmYQAFiorzLVu0k7xDwsgexhyPDq\nW3or1ghzwXfdMpx9mHuFXExZ2vQ7da8fAnoKQjH4m4PEu/ifAtTRGpnzW6d7Pdlm\n4faj6cdZjWT6VV3HkbPSNWBXPV83dANHHMZ90l9wIaAucqhPJllq70uYv+6IcG5g\nN+c/ASdnj2XkzVMPjspZQoT70tVGpQs+OUOfOl2D7RiaHcne/lx9Wxq5KFYoekrB\nJuN+rq/5uYeEGpI2TqwDacw3B3IrAYymSxBrs71wrqyMDmtGGDfO2XOkIRh2c6QY\nVyz5w/6z+xX/3sb+ujvGm4Ol9oPlpWiS672cFNKQLtZDfOrCIf10mKeu61HwAUim\npRUPgkDTgrAWfDlRLuwha3axP5sY1Q+WeyMyuXsF04YIUqJ8u7Pg8yB2n6f90e9e\nRf+mHxjBQlJzLQGV2dWUHP5AmX7GvAWajlAd4tWdVnXBwrhdrvHUXVqjNdDhz6Us\nwO/Cxgvh0W0arN0WKoaBdTTRCMG5/3MRUK3Le0eXPcxRgsA7PkAgFjYeOX3Zhoi7\nQFbfUKH5IRwueP4WRrUvh7dqBy7O8T1exng8YG9KyhcZIpuhfLwfz4p8IQbF8b5+\nzaMnp/hk3CDLNEzXGPjlNfDQYYjFODIJUXN/eC8pbf+aF04XhSrqr58EEk2Beg9O\n8OVoFbXGg0/XzuamEYWc\n=ZCd0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T16:00:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKGJmOGNhZGYyMTAwZTY2YmI4ZjEyMDgwOTY4MDkzMjdiODY0Y2ViMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/53ff992ed24e81fb8445a751a2efc73b3b57f1da","sha":"53ff992ed24e81fb8445a751a2efc73b3b57f1da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/53ff992ed24e81fb8445a751a2efc73b3b57f1da"}],"sha":"bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/bf8cadf2100e66bb8f1208096809327b864ceb1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/53ff992ed24e81fb8445a751a2efc73b3b57f1da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:47:41Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:47:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(python-common): ship contracts/CLAUDE.md into scaffolded projects (#325) (#569)\n\n* docs(python-common): ship the leaf CLAUDE.md docs into scaffolds\n\nsrc/config/contracts/CLAUDE.md and src/utils/CLAUDE.md existed in\ntemplates/python-common/ but no scaffold copy list reached them, so no\ngenerated project ever received either doc.\n\nCloses #325\n\n* feat(ci): gate leaf CLAUDE.md docs as a third copy-list asset class\n\ncheck_test_copy_lists.py now compares every python-common leaf doc\nagainst each scaffold''s reachable set, next to tests and workflows.\nKeyed by relative path (every doc is named CLAUDE.md); a wholesale\ndirectory copy counts for the docs under it. Mutation witness: dropping\nthe contracts/CLAUDE.md cp line flags all five service tiers.\n\nRefs #325\n\n* fix(ci): require a doc cp to land inside the project (#569)\n\nreachable_docs credited a doc from the cp SOURCE alone, so a cp\nwriting outside the project still counted as delivered. Parse the\ndestination too: it must be variable-rooted, free of .., and keep\nthe source''s name.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"4345e6e058ba3ac33340da626f2e290f29cbdb6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/4345e6e058ba3ac33340da626f2e290f29cbdb6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/53ff992ed24e81fb8445a751a2efc73b3b57f1da","verification":{"payload":"tree 4345e6e058ba3ac33340da626f2e290f29cbdb6c\nparent 7432bf34891d3442d46b69e09865654c3cfe06b2\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1791110861 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791110861 +0000\n\ndocs(python-common): ship contracts/CLAUDE.md into scaffolded projects (#325) (#569)\n\n* docs(python-common): ship the leaf CLAUDE.md docs into scaffolds\n\nsrc/config/contracts/CLAUDE.md and src/utils/CLAUDE.md existed in\ntemplates/python-common/ but no scaffold copy list reached them, so no\ngenerated project ever received either doc.\n\nCloses #325\n\n* feat(ci): gate leaf CLAUDE.md docs as a third copy-list asset class\n\ncheck_test_copy_lists.py now compares every python-common leaf doc\nagainst each scaffold''s reachable set, next to tests and workflows.\nKeyed by relative path (every doc is named CLAUDE.md); a wholesale\ndirectory copy counts for the docs under it. Mutation witness: dropping\nthe contracts/CLAUDE.md cp line flags all five service tiers.\n\nRefs #325\n\n* fix(ci): require a doc cp to land inside the project (#569)\n\nreachable_docs credited a doc from the cp SOURCE alone, so a cp\nwriting outside the project still counted as delivered. Parse the\ndestination too: it must be variable-rooted, free of .., and keep\nthe source''s name.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwi7NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW1wQAHkcts+Qvdy3e3UIrhK/cFib\nbmY1ubTo3wMxovp8jU3yyYBLIjTXnQuJZpPOdw5q3fA924vbZtPlUJr/hKHnPWfl\nuD5DXYk0pVrIg7nZl9CFjJuoIiYEF6J5xx3PVnpAOTxMmOTMfOVe2AU+nw5viqMa\nJw5oDAIZe9tccdRbbGSsUXV+C+d7wE7w5weFkIp3yb1/uXdbTpqXDTNXrV0zTlGD\nUV2eK5bn52amA9Po324xABEi2+ZmJXofiGha82yK/1rWN3Mezo3+vBSG+OwtHtid\nRsvmvgYn/9s9OcjQN2WA7fo2kSrqPUk0WkfKSzGRC/8H8d1JLbR1qtN7+U7tWNjc\nWer7KrZTVdibOfV8BUYli1vf6J9WCH6olOSfhY6zS/mSwplhG2ViJa+k9f9nw7NF\ncWd115