.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/7432bf34891d3442d46b69e09865654c3cfe06b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:11:25Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:11:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(templates): Alembic parity for mvc-service-orm-db + migrate_* tasks (#545)\n\n* feat(templates): ship Alembic migrations for mvc-service-orm-db\n\nAdd alembic.ini and migrations/{env.py,script.py.mako,CLAUDE.md,\nversions/.gitkeep} to templates/mvc-service-orm-db, mirroring\nddd-service-orm-db with compare_type/render_as_batch already set and\nenv.py reusing config.connection_db.build_database_url instead of\nduplicating DSN composition. Declares the alembic dependency and its\ndeptry DEP002 ignore. Also documents the idempotent-migration\nconvention (DDL+DML allowed, guarded/backfilled DML, documented\nrefusal for a lossy downgrade) in both tiers'' migrations/CLAUDE.md.\n\nAlso drops two decorative banners in test_migration_graph_gate.py\nthat tripped the comment-budget pre-commit hook on the whole tree,\nunrelated to this change but blocking every commit.\n\n* feat(templates): add migrate_* poe tasks (online + offline)\n\npoe_tasks.toml previously mentioned Alembic only inside db_up''s help\ntext, with no way to run/generate/export a migration through the\nproject''s own command interface (blueprintx#381). Adds migrate_new,\nmigrate_up, migrate_down, migrate_current, migrate_history and\nmigrate_sql (offline --sql, for a DBA) — shared across every Python\ntier since poe_tasks.toml is single-sourced, so ddd-service-orm-db\ngets the same fix.\n\n* fix(templates): stop .env overriding deployment DB, quote poe args\n\nAlembic''s env.py called load_dotenv(override=True), so a .env value beat\nthe real deployment environment. The application side calls plain\nload_dotenv(), where the environment wins -- so the app and its\nmigrations could resolve DIFFERENT databases from the same checkout, and\nalembic would migrate the one nobody is serving.\n\nThe review flagged the mvc tier; the ddd tier had the same line. Parity\nacross the ORM tiers is this change''s subject, so both are fixed.\n\npoethepoet splits whitespace in an unquoted parameter expansion, so\n''poe migrate_new \"add status column\"'' reached alembic as three\narguments instead of one -m value. The review flagged migrate_new; the\nsame shape was in commit_msg_check''s --commit-msg-filename, where a path\ncontaining a space breaks identically.\n\n* fix(templates): address review on mvc alembic parity\n\nScaffold alembic.ini + migrations/, space path separator, auto-import\nmodel modules in env.py, SQLite-safe view DDL, no log+pass downgrade,\nmigrate_sql help states it is base-to-head.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd99f6840dd2459707a930d4085b7e9b4ecda783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/bd99f6840dd2459707a930d4085b7e9b4ecda783"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/7432bf34891d3442d46b69e09865654c3cfe06b2","verification":{"payload":"tree bd99f6840dd2459707a930d4085b7e9b4ecda783\nparent 60bac148d8e58eadaf80fcfb06aec942b95567b3\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790943085 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790943085 +0000\n\nfeat(templates): Alembic parity for mvc-service-orm-db + migrate_* tasks (#545)\n\n* feat(templates): ship Alembic migrations for mvc-service-orm-db\n\nAdd alembic.ini and migrations/{env.py,script.py.mako,CLAUDE.md,\nversions/.gitkeep} to templates/mvc-service-orm-db, mirroring\nddd-service-orm-db with compare_type/render_as_batch already set and\nenv.py reusing config.connection_db.build_database_url instead of\nduplicating DSN composition. Declares the alembic dependency and its\ndeptry DEP002 ignore. Also documents the idempotent-migration\nconvention (DDL+DML allowed, guarded/backfilled DML, documented\nrefusal for a lossy downgrade) in both tiers'' migrations/CLAUDE.md.\n\nAlso drops two decorative banners in test_migration_graph_gate.py\nthat tripped the comment-budget pre-commit hook on the whole tree,\nunrelated to this change but blocking every commit.\n\n* feat(templates): add migrate_* poe tasks (online + offline)\n\npoe_tasks.toml previously mentioned Alembic only inside db_up''s help\ntext, with no way to run/generate/export a migration through the\nproject''s own command interface (blueprintx#381). Adds migrate_new,\nmigrate_up, migrate_down, migrate_current, migrate_history and\nmigrate_sql (offline --sql, for a DBA) — shared across every Python\ntier since poe_tasks.toml is single-sourced, so ddd-service-orm-db\ngets the same fix.\n\n* fix(templates): stop .env overriding deployment DB, quote poe args\n\nAlembic''s env.py called load_dotenv(override=True), so a .env value beat\nthe real deployment environment. The application side calls plain\nload_dotenv(), where the environment wins -- so the app and its\nmigrations could resolve DIFFERENT databases from the same checkout, and\nalembic would migrate the one nobody is serving.\n\nThe review flagged the mvc tier; the ddd tier had the same line. Parity\nacross the ORM tiers is this change''s subject, so both are fixed.\n\npoethepoet splits whitespace in an unquoted parameter expansion, so\n''poe migrate_new \"add status column\"'' reached alembic as three\narguments instead of one -m value. The review flagged migrate_new; the\nsame shape was in commit_msg_check''s --commit-msg-filename, where a path\ncontaining a space breaks identically.\n\n* fix(templates): address review on mvc alembic parity\n\nScaffold alembic.ini + migrations/, space path separator, auto-import\nmodel modules in env.py, SQLite-safe view DDL, no log+pass downgrade,\nmigrate_sql help states it is base-to-head.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv59tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp+UQADi0N3btpIgj6PT/nk93AHW7\nI/BOHZm0cGHBWnnEIGFPUKelG3W5F2PXnOT6AtIXCCkZfbsTmLXVkwO21WJveAfd\nFTiMq8WRygaaC1bxU5phrZZ77ogHqlwp2AGKcNLAzvT1ngwPcnDn21aEeERKF1JM\nR+9k1SCP6FuS2F9jmIOtE6rg/0XiiVg5uDGEIq3XqrQACsCDG6G9VEr4B1dXy8F+\nWRbcVrqjIq61ofY9OeL0NBfGFcTlll6Pf87l49EwM7oMvsdqR75JtMFeANtR4xrL\neDoiyRq7W/+sDROf/2AXALpgzwO8CNqa4vBZUf6BzZJrl9wapACc7LqJE4ej+c4G\nZc+iIVkMv8AJ9ZeAWVpI4zJaAj7D7BV5EHAlX+FiGshLYBYyDg3fNaW69j5+wd/9\nE4Adm/oHjVt8CypYO0i5CcRpYh2WqsFdT7iZnESXeMQhi/PUWgFvEKicoXpC9MlO\nOYO34Jg6PlV+PccayJ2WmLUD4RVQEiRnKOwXTQUqMDZFN+GAo05Xo7qHdNxmRedZ\n7Q6wPh8X6LCjq63j/ftH3wFrnTC6gL+0N4tNuiPYRIZmMzUejTIQ6BXY2vm7mI5s\nzymUsYgyL7wzc91wb3cMLC9+FLfI0eaRADvbK0clnHhsfr3qcTl6eYYHoqWijA32\nbMtSjCuQ6ZYEj5awa0Wk\n=SMbt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T12:11:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.co