72b7fcec67e5"}],"sha":"60bac148d8e58eadaf80fcfb06aec942b95567b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/60bac148d8e58eadaf80fcfb06aec942b95567b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d7ed6bcbd34e7bbbd5a487d63a3372b7fcec67e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:54:44Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:54:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ts-common): add missing eslint-plugin-jest to the lockfile (#533)\n\n* fix(ts-common): add missing eslint-plugin-jest to the lockfile\n\n`eslint-plugin-jest` is declared in templates/ts-common/package.json\n(`^29.0.0`) but was absent from package-lock.json, so the `npm ci` step\nthe TypeScript typecheck job runs fails before typechecking anything:\n\n    npm error code EUSAGE\n    npm error Missing: eslint-plugin-jest@29.16.6 from lock file\n\n⚠️ That job is red on EVERY open PR, and the failure has nothing to do\nwith any of their diffs — it is inherited from the default branch, and\nthe check''s name (\"TypeScript typecheck\") actively misdirects, since\ntsc never runs. Measured this round on PR #530, whose entire diff is\none JSON config and one workflow comment.\n\nRegenerated the lockfile the same way CI builds its workspace\n(envsubst-render package.json, then `npm install --package-lock-only`),\nthen restored the lockfile''s root `name` to\n`react-spa-webpack-template` — the render sets it to the CI workspace''s\n`ci-typecheck`, which must not leak into the template. CI does not\ncompare that field (its own comment says so); the template''s own name\nis the correct value to commit.\n\nDiff is 31 insertions, 0 deletions — one added dependency, 1160 -> 1161\npackages, nothing else moved.\n\nVerified with the exact failing command: envsubst-render + `npm ci`\nagainst this committed file exits 0, \"added 1124 packages\".\n\n* fix(deps): pin handlebars 4.7.9 via overrides, clearing 7 alerts\n\nSeven of the repo''s ten open Dependabot alerts — including the only\ncritical one — are `handlebars` in this lockfile. Measured before\nchoosing a fix, because the obvious options were both wrong:\n\n- the lockfile holds **4.7.8**; the advisories'' `first_patched_version`\n  is **4.7.9**, which IS published on npm;\n- a plain `npm install --package-lock-only` refresh leaves it at 4.7.8;\n- the reason: `@boundaries/elements` declares `\"handlebars\": \"4.7.8\"` —\n  an EXACT pin, not a range, so npm has no room to resolve higher.\n\nSo a refresh cannot clear them, and dropping the parent would mean\nremoving a webpack-toolchain dependency to fix a lockfile — changing\nwhat the React skeleton IS, to satisfy an advisory.\n\n`overrides` is the remaining option and the right one: one line,\nreversible, and it expresses exactly the claim being made — this tree\ntakes 4.7.9 regardless of what a transitive parent pinned.\n\n⚠️ It is a standing cost, paid by every future scaffold: an override\ngoes stale silently when the parent eventually widens its range. Same\nhazard as the pinned `pymarkdownlnt` in #530 — revisit both together.\n\nVerified with the exact command CI runs: envsubst-render + `npm ci`\nagainst this committed lockfile exits 0, \"added 1124 packages\", and\n`node_modules/handlebars` resolves to **4.7.9**.\n\nStacked onto this PR rather than opened separately because it edits the\nsame two files — a sibling PR would have collided by construction.\n\nCloses #529\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8029f62c60bd393a9c41b1d8025a83f2cf65d70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/c8029f62c60bd393a9c41b1d8025a83f2cf65d70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/d7ed6bcbd34e7bbbd5a487d63a3372b7fcec67e5","verification":{"payload":"tree c8029f62c60bd393a9c41b1d8025a83f2cf65d70\nparent d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790938484 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790938484 +0000\n\nfix(ts-common): add missing eslint-plugin-jest to the lockfile (#533)\n\n* fix(ts-common): add missing eslint-plugin-jest to the lockfile\n\n`eslint-plugin-jest` is declared in templates/ts-common/package.json\n(`^29.0.0`) but was absent from package-lock.json, so the `npm ci` step\nthe TypeScript typecheck job runs fails before typechecking anything:\n\n    npm error code EUSAGE\n    npm error Missing: eslint-plugin-jest@29.16.6 from lock file\n\n⚠️ That job is red on EVERY open PR, and the failure has nothing to do\nwith any of their diffs — it is inherited from the default branch, and\nthe check''s name (\"TypeScript typecheck\") actively misdirects, since\ntsc never runs. Measured this round on PR #530, whose entire diff is\none JSON config and one workflow comment.\n\nRegenerated the lockfile the same way CI builds its workspace\n(envsubst-render package.json, then `npm install --package-lock-only`),\nthen restored the lockfile''s root `name` to\n`react-spa-webpack-template` — the render sets it to the CI workspace''s\n`ci-typecheck`, which must not leak into the template. CI does not\ncompare that field (its own comment says so); the template''s own name\nis the correct value to commit.\n\nDiff is 31 insertions, 0 deletions — one added dependency, 1160 -> 1161\npackages, nothing else moved.\n\nVerified with the exact failing command: envsubst-render + `npm ci`\nagainst this committed file exits 0, \"added 1124 packages\".\n\n* fix(deps): pin handlebars 4.7.9 via overrides, clearing 7 alerts\n\nSeven of the repo''s ten open Dependabot alerts — including the only\ncritical one — are `handlebars` in this lockfile. Measured before\nchoosing a fix, because the obvious options were both wrong:\n\n- the lockfile holds **4.7.8**; the advisories'' `first_patched_version`\n  is **4.7.9**, which IS published on npm;\n- a plain `npm install --package-lock-only` refresh leaves it at 4.7.8;\n- the reason: `@boundaries/elements` declares `\"handlebars\": \"4.7.8\"` —\n  an EXACT pin, not a range, so npm has no room to resolve higher.\n\nSo a refresh cannot clear them, and dropping the parent would mean\nremoving a webpack-toolchain dependency to fix a lockfile — changing\nwhat the React skeleton IS, to satisfy an advisory.\n\n`overrides` is the remaining option and the right one: one line,\nreversible, and it expresses exactly the claim being made — this tree\ntakes 4.7.9 regardless of what a transitive parent pinned.\n\n⚠️ It is a standing cost, paid by every future scaffold: an override\ngoes stale silently when the parent eventually widens its range. Same\nhazard as the pinned `pymarkdownlnt` in #530 — revisit both together.\n\nVerified with the exact command CI runs: envsubst-render + `npm ci`\nagainst this committed lockfile exits 0, \"added 1124 packages\", and\n`node_modules/handlebars` resolves to **4.7.9**.\n\nStacked onto this PR rather than opened separately because it edits the\nsame two files — a sibling PR would have collided by construction.\n\nCloses #529\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv410CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA97kQACq5GoaO8KsO+hmnUcdHQMyG\n3tVR2a/6GuTdHK7V704+gqcexch/6KueqxH3Q6yzJhFs9i2gFIzEgYVsXZcmm9ij\nxb3FOSAHiR4ex8EXSOH4VpggmZY/p3FWWqW11OU7tQ2FKaN4ch323pGwMGVHGYc4\ncncJZw3OC/Jly751ovv3aPo51ymSuB0bUWMCwEQBBZZ3cX852SfHuYLh2pRZOsyR\n62I/P7aHm0dMSDg8usSK/PWc/zHakhqcAO8QQt8VEAz/cvbyHi2mqEocfj53Vu7w\nRY7HyC+jKEPHvRtDtz+DornBTDnch0j6UxsoHGrf9C7/AR3trl1vY8jJ7hY1Iym2\n87+VbrGgvmhNzAqtNCzXYtoyD25c8u1vLLo3ogdhSR4LXTXTVTGKwTUVlOkMec3n\nOk7VmnjnAwpXY5tdNadBBZMGQUF97GeA8IdnEu8o6UFB/7yTLzj77pPzDRAkHBJf\n50GFJf9US02W5djz9htsuNeXRiLVH0CEoobzM3SHDUT4wLlaZ70ZKDPy9Ofomv0X\nCulQh+vv1ySS2fglVI22iH7hsNOq30Yc5y2ALdjsxdTMkkN76mBrBaNllOsWd0i2\nILISmAUrbWs+OkH+W4ASOqyEsNDTdOlzANq+6fsl6CvEH+25L8yJFPaWxRUon2wp\ncWkH50xTHKdvtagqjPdq\n=ssyS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T10:54:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/d7ed6bcbd34e7bbbd5a487d63a3372b7fcec67e5","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKGQ3ZWQ2YmNiZDM0ZTdiYmJkNWE0ODdkNjNhMzM3MmI3ZmNlYzY3ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f","sha":"d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f"}],"sha":"d7ed6bcbd34e7bbbd5a487d63a3372b7fcec67e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d7ed6bcbd34e7bbbd5a487d63a3372b7fcec67e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:47:32Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:47:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): run the SQL guards gate in CI, not only pre-commit (#355) (#574)\n\nPR #509 shipped check_sql_guards.py and wired it into the scaffolded\nproject''s pre-commit, but never into that project''s tests.yaml. It also\nmerged with an empty closingIssuesReferences, so #355 stayed open and\nthe gap stayed invisible.\n\nMeasured against origin/main before this change:\n\n  WHERE-less mutations   pre-commit yes   CI 0 refs\n  WITH (NOLOCK)          pre-commit yes   CI 0 refs\n  unnormalised CPF/CNPJ  pre-commit yes   CI yes\n\nA gate that runs only in pre-commit is bypassed by --no-verify and by\nany contributor who never installed the hooks, so a DELETE with no\nWHERE could reach a generated project''s main branch with nothing red.\nThat is the one-leg defect blueprintx#510 exists to prevent, in the\ntier the repo ships to everyone else.\n\nThe step mirrors the Identifier Masking Gate immediately above it --\nsame job, same `if: runner.os == ''Linux''`, same reason written at the\nsite. The two gates come from the same PR and had no reason to differ.\n\nactionlint: the two SC2181 findings in this file are pre-existing on\nmain (verified against origin/main:tests.yaml, same count), untouched\nhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2e3ca50063fd63344ef4ec49517778c46d4bfd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/b2e3ca50063fd63344ef4ec49517778c46d4bfd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f","verification":{"payload":"tree b2e3ca50063fd63344ef4ec49517778c46d4bfd5\nparent 2471a1677aa3756f3de37299d4cf6bdbb7ba5c9b\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790502452 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790502452 +0000\n\nfix(ci): run the SQL guards gate in CI, not only pre-commit (#355) (#574)\n\nPR #509 shipped check_sql_guards.py and wired it into the scaffolded\nproject''s pre-commit, but never into that project''s tests.yaml. It also\nmerged with an empty closingIssuesReferences, so #355 stayed open and\nthe gap stayed invisible.\n\nMeasured against origin/main before this change:\n\n  WHERE-less mutations   pre-commit yes   CI 0 refs\n  WITH (NOLOCK)          pre-commit yes   CI 0 refs\n  unnormalised CPF/CNPJ  pre-commit yes   CI yes\n\nA gate that runs only in pre-commit is bypassed by --no-verify and by\nany contributor who never installed the hooks, so a DELETE with no\nWHERE could reach a generated project''s main branch with nothing red.\nThat is the one-leg defect blueprintx#510 exists to prevent, in the\ntier the repo ships to everyone else.\n\nThe step mirrors the Identifier Masking Gate immediately above it --\nsame job, same `if: runner.os == ''Linux''`, same reason written at the\nsite. The two gates come from the same PR and had no reason to differ.\n\nactionlint: the two SC2181 findings in this file are pre-existing on\nmain (verified against origin/main:tests.yaml, same count), untouched\nhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquOY0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALcIQAD1ObUj6CtClJfWS2Piq8c2Y\nW0oOXE/YAeswDrGWydfmPMP2DuhJRH5jMII54lHoih6tfL1/TVCXVlM1+w0ACNah\nZCyVAxA6xRaEqAw5qGy7Q3TUsTVeb59BuEUm6tciX8qUZOqjCfGon//GmHS5R9GG\nuZB/0XRQ2vBj0Qtt8czC7NYUBm2NB2sjXITLfzvUqh4puEZCpgIkoTm/Cqhp26kX\nSkZaF+9xnRDF4XffFnPLXc3oqW4K4c8644Dkdr8GndLT1G4ZBhqBOioWlRAVpC2l\niLEhDpUuYOUUebb3qUgqQgMIR55DhciH2YWM5izLl1BaYXNh7huXKI2Yrs0MHs9A\nQGuts5XSTqzBeuMbu6+qeCn2H/t4mtPxfnofzZMfBly+hatkRbBaxIpDaiWWkwkN\nKHeuczQyH4fP3aRc9e2IUURgGYaTJTTfWrFfLEX19uqxJe1ewOTbRHn/xZdSzOXm\npAlNMZRl/dWx1W/9u6uVbyQhG/gPk0N+Z0ehTo/+a4tRrh1OLg13ydmH3yAdYlQ8\n5AG0NvaDB/wQp1iHkCASaIwitIBdXXEasfYwtLawuZEKQmneVVjC7Y8e7t+M0fEI\nNhE9X3rD7Z1eFwyTXsLb/rj6zd9YxQ9DZkHnhSeRCnR4g69ZZfNKUUavLTXArHOF\n8M6xXTGnCXmby8QbGXqP\n=gNd2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T09:47:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKGQ4MDMyMDBhMTZlZGE2YWUzZWMyMzEzODJmOGM3M2NmNzA2ZmRkNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/2471a1677aa3756f3de37299d4cf6bdbb7ba5c9b","sha":"2471a1677aa3756f3de37299d4cf6bdbb7ba5c9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/2471a1677aa3756f3de37299d4cf6bdbb7ba5c9b"}],"sha":"d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d803200a16eda6ae3ec231382f8c73cf706fdd5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/2471a1677aa3756f3de37299d4cf6bdbb7ba5c9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T06:55:50Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T06:55:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(templates): gitleaks secret scan for TS and bash-cli tiers (#155) (#563)\n\n* feat(templates): gitleaks secret scan for TS and bash-cli tiers (#155)\n\nOnly templates/python-common/ shipped any secret scanning; the TypeScript\n(ts-common -> react-spa-webpack, ts-lib) and bash-cli tiers shipped none.\n\nUses gitleaks, not GitGuardian''s ggshield: ggshield needs a hosted API key\nthat a freshly scaffolded project does not have, and with none it exits 3\nhaving scanned nothing. gitleaks needs no key or account, so it is the only\nscanner that can be on by default in a generated project.\n\nSame pinned + checksum-verified install as .github/workflows/secret_scan.yml\n(gitleaks 8.30.1), fetch-depth 0 so history is scanned and not just the tip,\nand no .gitleaks.toml -- an allowlist is added only for a measured false\npositive.\n\n* docs: record the measured gitleaks vs GitGuardian delta (#155)\n\nThe page assumed GitGuardian was the scanner. It is not the default and\ncannot be: measured on this tree, gitleaks 8.30.1 scans 4.76 MB in 1.52 s\nwith no key and trips on planted synthetic credentials, while ggshield\n1.54.0 cannot run at all (exit 3, no resolvable key; BlueprintX''s own key\nfails auth). GitGuardian''s measurable delta here is zero.\n\nAlso records a should-fail lesson: the first probe used AWS''s documented\nexample access key and gitleaks reported no leaks -- it allowlists that\nvalue, so a should-fail test built on a documented example proves nothing.\n\nAdds the per-tier coverage table now that the TypeScript and bash-cli tiers\nscan too.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"3187cab2d8617b5327d2a7d4a5bfa895b0e69a58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/3187cab2d8617b5327d2a7d4a5bfa895b0e69a58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/2471a1677aa3756f3de37299d4cf6bdbb7ba5c9b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3187cab2d8617b5327d2a7d4a5bfa895b0e69a58\nparent 4e3d5c67286cc3de19b13acad868c4e21bc42474\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790492150 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790492150 +0000\n\nfeat(templates): gitleaks secret scan for TS and bash-cli tiers (#155) (#563)\n\n* feat(templates): gitleaks secret scan for TS and bash-cli tiers (#155)\n\nOnly templates/python-common/ shipped any secret scanning; the TypeScript\n(ts-common -> react-spa-webpack, ts-lib) and bash-cli tiers shipped none.\n\nUses gitleaks, not GitGuardian''s ggshield: ggshield needs a hosted API key\nthat a freshly scaffolded project does not have, and with none it exits 3\nhaving scanned nothing. gitleaks needs no key or account, so it is the only\nscanner that can be on by default in a generated project.\n\nSame pinned + checksum-verified install as .github/workflows/secret_scan.yml\n(gitleaks 8.30.1), fetch-depth 0 so history is scanned and not just the tip,\nand no .gitleaks.toml -- an allowlist is added only for a measured false\npositive.\n\n* docs: record the measured gitleaks vs GitGuardian delta (#155)\n\nThe page assumed GitGuardian was the scanner. It is not the default and\ncannot be: measured on this tree, gitleaks 8.30.1 scans 4.76 MB in 1.52 s\nwith no key and trips on planted synthetic credentials, while ggshield\n1.54.0 cannot run at all (exit 3, no resolvable key; BlueprintX''s own key\nfails auth). GitGuardian''s measurable delta here is zero.\n\nAlso records a should-fail lesson: the first probe used AWS''s documented\nexample access key and gitleaks reported no leaks -- it allowlists that\nvalue, so a should-fail test built on a documented example proves nothing.\n\nAdds the per-tier coverage table now that the TypeScript and bash-cli tiers\nscan too.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquL32CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ7QQADeem+o1x913MpQ+/51Mh90B\nBZ6R0BnwIRvTNPJpkRdsO2HdlgayCxpAHkV2FKPdLKo6FWM+q8y+obX1HNkNpjbv\nL17We50ZCGazzGGmLnZp6uTQ65pk1PTLuKQVu17FSF/DaVRWR4POf1bvP2j67P2/\n+mU+cWVP/QPTD7G+ngYiVAMgFKouQVf+t54DduGcOmbKM7fJ9DDEMaxxrQf5Mau6\n492UO5URP28ZAaCEprAUwq1ToeSRvYsyoGwm8v1hXJdd7ZX+AdYcBFG8eS9aSt2K\n+m0IzrOmV1+REao4ql0wjjiQXKhUXixZ8zGWH3EtKwhx00o0RpY2szF/bdvUTJOd\nyaG12r76RdHu64yMl6jdCKcZ3TN9Tp4ZtWjbNg04gSa0B6qp1CaZ3aIG5oAmhbRs\ndcZWF0yGScz9EURuXxCxz/7b4tbd2VPWRVMciCv7EuTS6MPoDaiPMSEDsizzQMt+\nlRobRzD7TKcF8jfKiRfPwsXsaGRLlOjlk7CCZwuBVYZXBSTtO17pjmijVpuB+URy\nb66V9tIFuVLXLSkXpYdCtZrY1mxcEl94MCqao87995tNceLmrdPdlZ7tiZcxJnGN\nYXkacKuhyOXsQORx+Hw0IkcFs/64tvpqTQNF0t5ah28ol6FKcjrBGV1apEZ3eV1B\n7/01R+VWXQLaYxXxASmF\n=j7hz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:55:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f