rules, data\nguardrails, naming and file-naming tables, tooling summary, project-memory\nrule and (MVC pair) runtime type-checking notes. They now live once in\ntemplates/common/CLAUDE.md, shipped as .claude/CLAUDE.md; each skeleton\nfile keeps a four-line pointer plus what is tier-specific.\n\n* docs(contributing): record the shared CLAUDE.md source (#549)\n\nThe one-implementation rule now covers the skeleton CLAUDE.md family;\nthe before/after duplication ratios are the reason it was worth doing.\n\n* fix(scaffold): copy shared CLAUDE.md into .claude/ dir\n\nEvery skeleton''s root CLAUDE.md (and docs/contributing.md) points readers at\n.claude/CLAUDE.md for conventions shared across all skeletons, but neither\nscaffold_copy_common_templates (the five service tiers) nor lib-minimal''s\ncopy_templates ever wrote that file — the pointer dangled in every\ngenerated project. Copy templates/common/CLAUDE.md to .claude/CLAUDE.md in\nboth paths.\n\nAddresses a CodeRabbit finding on PR #573.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ab61e4624d9c185f9b1d2559b348e5b2669e871","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/9ab61e4624d9c185f9b1d2559b348e5b2669e871"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/28c09538d5ae220ea9b7a055bd82ca2e6c04f4c2","verification":{"payload":"tree 9ab61e4624d9c185f9b1d2559b348e5b2669e871\nparent 663906cb232c848947ed2fe5b7c16c183b22f515\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790476363 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790476363 +0000\n\nchore(templates): dedup six skeleton CLAUDE.md files into templates/common (#549) (#573)\n\n* chore(templates): dedup skeleton CLAUDE.md into common (#549)\n\nSix Python skeleton root files carried the same boundary rules, data\nguardrails, naming and file-naming tables, tooling summary, project-memory\nrule and (MVC pair) runtime type-checking notes. They now live once in\ntemplates/common/CLAUDE.md, shipped as .claude/CLAUDE.md; each skeleton\nfile keeps a four-line pointer plus what is tier-specific.\n\n* docs(contributing): record the shared CLAUDE.md source (#549)\n\nThe one-implementation rule now covers the skeleton CLAUDE.md family;\nthe before/after duplication ratios are the reason it was worth doing.\n\n* fix(scaffold): copy shared CLAUDE.md into .claude/ dir\n\nEvery skeleton''s root CLAUDE.md (and docs/contributing.md) points readers at\n.claude/CLAUDE.md for conventions shared across all skeletons, but neither\nscaffold_copy_common_templates (the five service tiers) nor lib-minimal''s\ncopy_templates ever wrote that file — the pointer dangled in every\ngenerated project. Copy templates/common/CLAUDE.md to .claude/CLAUDE.md in\nboth paths.\n\nAddresses a CodeRabbit finding on PR #573.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquIBLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5a4QAFtPe+zYxsKUoNc8aRa8Ay53\n4PD/nRlNg1LoCI6szYTYXWo8uMDx0sN/3RcyqUXUirhApy6V6KpclQ7SIntQmFbM\n95Nu6de228QFZe7uvIEU/0IuR+HRuYxGi/rBnne0uCurJIDediQPsiH4UUMXZeHW\nd9RNESySHb6PAWvMUyssVE6zWqFF8zA5uIMIwMorRCdz9J75TEvgtBmXHL3D9pPq\nheJF4g63iHD3bHRDv4fOEFWzw4Y2NHL2Zz3Xd4ADpKBecDM0KTFYLeXXvisFEBH6\nqxCiBFbZ/Igb3SsOQGK7KxgnEAz/Kea5qHS333OKtVN8Gtb+El3AKddvVMPqKR/C\natdTsggRhsVzp6+iXveH7C0ORJab3fIofAW27WRuL9wKv7kDmBYVE7H7xbSeWDUX\nEiLYAopPfzrKhLabs3rcYRVvm2m07uIN6Sv0qKhG1vMqbfLW9Zt0y6TWPC4D814B\nMHFyG79nPpCm86vujkuVucHSkwnQjH2sTjLTssIInnh2zC7nIKiLvc5i4T7CKacr\n5DsJ2u92hYjCS9B9QEe7LRfLo7ibmW9lkp8RQdQmDYVHvi8acUKHQYyRqXbXERNh\nAZZN3tPF0Jb6rnKKx1fwXs3B6ETT3xLHZEhg4mqMRurGPgmJVSiJaLPggQ9eh5I0\n04XezFISPeBy2W+StrW/\n=8yFy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T02:32:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/28c09538d5ae220ea9b7a055bd82ca2e6c04f4c2","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDI4YzA5NTM4ZDVhZTIyMGVhOWI3YTA1NWJkODJjYTJlNmMwNGY0YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/663906cb232c848947ed2fe5b7c16c183b22f515","sha":"663906cb232c848947ed2fe5b7c16c183b22f515","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/663906cb232c848947ed2fe5b7c16c183b22f515"}],"sha":"28c09538d5ae220ea9b7a055bd82ca2e6c04f4c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/28c09538d5ae220ea9b7a055bd82ca2e6c04f4c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/663906cb232c848947ed2fe5b7c16c183b22f515/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:34:53Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:34:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(ci): measure the open-time review ask, keep `opened` (#567) (#577)\n\n* docs(ci): measure the open-time review ask, keep `opened` (#567)\n\nWidened the attribution measurement behind #567 from n=10/15h to 244 asks\nover 15 days (656 comments, 7 pages, 2026-09-06 -> 2026-09-20), attributing\neach CodeRabbit verdict to the ask that preceded it on the same PR.\n\nOn-open asks are 45% of everything spent but win 26% of the reviews that\nhappen. They are kept anyway: a refused ask costs nothing, and the on-open\nask is the enrolment step for review_retry.yml, which only adopts a PR whose\nnewest reviewer comment is a rate-limit notice.\n\n* docs(ci): record this PR''s own refused on-open ask (#567)\n\nOpening #577 reproduced the pattern in 13 seconds: the window was already\ndeclared shut at 17:19:58Z, the on-open ask went out at 17:20:05Z and was\nrefused at 17:20:11Z.\n\nRecorded because the obvious reading is wrong. The ask took nothing from\nanybody -- the window was shut before it. The refusal is now the PR''s newest\nreviewer comment, which is exactly the condition review_retry.yml needs to\nadopt it, so this is the enrolment step working, not a leak.\n\n* fix(docs): correct accept-rate denominator and PR #577 attribution\n\nRecalculate the on-open/tick/retry accept rates in the coderabbit\nopen-trigger measurement to exclude \"other\" from the denominator, as\nthe method section already specifies (20.7/45.1/50.6 -> 22.1/46.9/51.9\nfor the 15-day table, 15.0/52.9 -> 16.1/56.3 for the 7-day table), and\nmirror the corrected 15-day figures in the workflow header comment.\n\nDocument that PR #577''s rate-limit refusal happened after the\nmeasured comment stream ended, so it is a later example and not one\nof the 81 counted refusals. Add a reconciliation note showing the\ncontent-based on-open attribution (111) closely tracks the workflow''s\nown successful \"Request the review\" runs (109) for this window.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ed358808185bb5de8221a2f07114716e4d894a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/7ed358808185bb5de8221a2f07114716e4d894a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/663906cb232c848947ed2fe5b7c16c183b22f515","verification":{"payload":"tree 7ed358808185bb5de8221a2f07114716e4d894a7\nparent c431e81703766b32e4148eba644c781f8d86d0aa\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790462093 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790462093 +0000\n\ndocs(ci): measure the open-time review ask, keep `opened` (#567) (#577)\n\n* docs(ci): measure the open-time review ask, keep `opened` (#567)\n\nWidened the attribution measurement behind #567 from n=10/15h to 244 asks\nover 15 days (656 comments, 7 pages, 2026-09-06 -> 2026-09-20), attributing\neach CodeRabbit verdict to the ask that preceded it on the same PR.\n\nOn-open asks are 45% of everything spent but win 26% of the reviews that\nhappen. They are kept anyway: a refused ask costs nothing, and the on-open\nask is the enrolment step for review_retry.yml, which only adopts a PR whose\nnewest reviewer comment is a rate-limit notice.\n\n* docs(ci): record this PR''s own refused on-open ask (#567)\n\nOpening #577 reproduced the pattern in 13 seconds: the window was already\ndeclared shut at 17:19:58Z, the on-open ask went out at 17:20:05Z and was\nrefused at 17:20:11Z.\n\nRecorded because the obvious reading is wrong. The ask took nothing from\nanybody -- the window was shut before it. The refusal is now the PR''s newest\nreviewer comment, which is exactly the condition review_retry.yml needs to\nadopt it, so this is the enrolment step working, not a leak.\n\n* fix(docs): correct accept-rate denominator and PR #577 attribution\n\nRecalculate the on-open/tick/retry accept rates in the coderabbit\nopen-trigger measurement to exclude \"other\" from the denominator, as\nthe method section already specifies (20.7/45.1/50.6 -> 22.1/46.9/51.9\nfor the 15-day table, 15.0/52.9 -> 16.1/56.3 for the 7-day table), and\nmirror the corrected 15-day figures in the workflow header comment.\n\nDocument that PR #577''s rate-limit refusal happened after the\nmeasured comment stream ended, so it is a later example and not one\nof the 81 counted refusals. Add a reconciliation note showing the\ncontent-based on-open attribution (111) closely tracks the workflow''s\nown successful \"Request the review\" runs (109) for this window.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEiNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATBUQAC3wCKqfkOqt76b64U+6phrW\nO+AzBX2H851btc0oOm//OvFuR2ir/VJjJyyH8o+pwXltBF66hXrjBhSF94mdgKji\nXTwaIG47/aXS519f+yJbz6M2TkNZpIT0bmoizzt83q5JOXgRChqBEtnukEC7krE/\npx0PHGElbtZemz0JuYvnN3WakAd46zzMAy5Lq7USUBkFpcZR8Kc8XVIHyhL3R65W\np6n2l1DWi1QLXemNvDmwEF2FFgOBqSigMLkKRL1M8HUv6zxyUOu6pGcfF6V2I72Q\n6DbOvp3+OmslzZThK6U+jy47HhxvzWdqZ+XC4plNIzFfYPXRlgp3ncb4IT8MV/5R\n3UuFkvBHWtT+bTsOCO3zaYJ8p7BfoYyRtDPINql6o0rp+jws4FKjdqRmgwHgvz82\nWpT/byQHFV21o2tn8zJVxOfFlWUeMNzF0HuYpZ/8H1ohcWnBIct3jFQwF+ftGu00\nuJ/Mkz4kSg6bDMpiKD+3BRFvx1r53enIaU+lZSVX10bRZFt4W6buFx6DjGwFB9CU\nT13iugw0Yk1MkY+eaIuj0JbIXKn4G