ollowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/c431e81703766b32e4148eba644c781f8d86d0aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:26:54Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:26:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: measure REQUIRED_CHECKS against what each tier''s CI emits (#164) (#565)\n\n* docs: measure required status checks per scaffolded tier (#164)\n\nAnswers the question in #164 by reading every job name and trigger in\ntemplates/*/.github/workflows/. Records the four-rule qualification\ntest, the per-tier inventory, and why four candidates are disqualified\n- including pr-reconcile.yaml, which runs on types [closed] and would\ndeadlock every PR if it were required.\n\n* docs: add required-status-check provisioning to the parity table (#164)\n\nThe Python tiers provision a pr-quality-gate ruleset from\nREQUIRED_CHECKS; the TypeScript and bash tiers ship no equivalent\nscript, so the check names they do emit are required by nothing.\nThat is a cross-language parity gap, so it gets a row in the\nsnapshot table rather than only a paragraph.\n\n* docs(required-status-checks): fix rule-2 branch-filter inconsistency\n\nCodeRabbit review on PR #565 found the doc''s own qualification rule 2\ndisqualified any pull_request branches:/paths: filter, yet the\nTypeScript inventory table still marked webpack/eslint/stylelint/jest/\ntype-check/docs/pack-smoke as qualifying despite all of them triggering\non pull_request: branches: [main] — the same filter that already\ndisqualifies Python''s Run Automated Tests row. Reclassify those TS rows\nas non-qualifying, tighten rule 2''s wording to explicitly reject\nbranches-ignore/paths/paths-ignore too, and note in rule 1 that a\nmatrix job''s emitted check-run name is the per-leg interpolated name,\nnot the raw jobs.<id>.name template string.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae8b8dcd5698572422655fbc16797d0201af3c05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/ae8b8dcd5698572422655fbc16797d0201af3c05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/c431e81703766b32e4148eba644c781f8d86d0aa","verification":{"payload":"tree ae8b8dcd5698572422655fbc16797d0201af3c05\nparent aae9a90f3ac08527d6a809f69fe1190e7655043e\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1790458014 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790458014 +0000\n\ndocs: measure REQUIRED_CHECKS against what each tier''s CI emits (#164) (#565)\n\n* docs: measure required status checks per scaffolded tier (#164)\n\nAnswers the question in #164 by reading every job name and trigger in\ntemplates/*/.github/workflows/. Records the four-rule qualification\ntest, the per-tier inventory, and why four candidates are disqualified\n- including pr-reconcile.yaml, which runs on types [closed] and would\ndeadlock every PR if it were required.\n\n* docs: add required-status-check provisioning to the parity table (#164)\n\nThe Python tiers provision a pr-quality-gate ruleset from\nREQUIRED_CHECKS; the TypeScript and bash tiers ship no equivalent\nscript, so the check names they do emit are required by nothing.\nThat is a cross-language parity gap, so it gets a row in the\nsnapshot table rather than only a paragraph.\n\n* docs(required-status-checks): fix rule-2 branch-filter inconsistency\n\nCodeRabbit review on PR #565 found the doc''s own qualification rule 2\ndisqualified any pull_request branches:/paths: filter, yet the\nTypeScript inventory table still marked webpack/eslint/stylelint/jest/\ntype-check/docs/pack-smoke as qualifying despite all of them triggering\non pull_request: branches: [main] — the same filter that already\ndisqualifies Python''s Run Automated Tests row. Reclassify those TS rows\nas non-qualifying, tighten rule 2''s wording to explicitly reject\nbranches-ignore/paths/paths-ignore too, and note in rule 1 that a\nmatrix job''s emitted check-run name is the per-leg interpolated name,\nnot the raw jobs.<id>.name template string.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquDieCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA96IQABsgi4F0uxxatQ6etSFSmGMz\nDwvyG3eVmJablMPMHlAjzdlRKeSkw8fnHdQwKPDc4NNbUIIRNUU1quTnm7hi1sY0\nu7mt9+kWSnaWBjZLm/l/SV/741Uc27HcrCmARYtUTRQ31mvM7I400fzI2L6CjBMU\ni8qu+UVYveAKiED4F6pFcfv4uEBjWnGU/0dy60C5S3QZbOZaSqKjz0ct/GbvwAKv\n9i5WIbueeCPd9oBnDu4ncUe4fjLZ1Fz/9VpAfVm6y8FdlYKsCSmWMO9ix8Wopesq\nTG+yMBCKRJ67K7XsX2bQ5DX+L/hlY2mLspQ+GGe9suMl02ZXRhD1gTt89fRBoDpU\nrd+DnyeeqAQwlq+TWjrzBmIu94TtoPDiNOswiwqftELZya+g/aV+gtM/RPbpF4JW\nHJkHxuOKZng3gboFfWt0VSLh4VXJE3RMTO1c7/m0YapMGcFYa1kveVWtTbO03Jgz\neZfyhfZUU5k4XAAO7jX5lE3BWc7j5InAe87k/CdA2DDaDVZ03j2vFOp4OXcd0O8j\ndpUFi85y/Epu6Js9F1LWU9rNg2TxHOPlLg/ruADDSQfOuWQbyAl1oPg19NSXGpEa\nGbrD0dFgIYrgd1kt8uOL6DqtfNd+tmDbbNUyerwmAtWTDE+aiiNHN//Uabibhxjn\nqZSXWv5Szz9fvJjN2hne\n=12qz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:26:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuser