/c53304c26843de232b0daf687d9bac85553514a6","sha":"c53304c26843de232b0daf687d9bac85553514a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/c53304c26843de232b0daf687d9bac85553514a6"}],"sha":"249efa3c62a3dc679c3241df36d70f5409e51f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/249efa3c62a3dc679c3241df36d70f5409e51f10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/c53304c26843de232b0daf687d9bac85553514a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T20:57:25Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T20:57:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(versioning): re-measure the v1.0.0 entry bar, 4 rows were stale (#534)\n\nThe entry-bar checklist opens with \"every row is decidable — yes/no, not\na feeling\", and four rows had gone stale against `main`. A stale entry\nbar under-reports readiness in the direction that costs the most: it\nmakes 1.0.0 look blocked when it is not.\n\nRe-measured 2026-09-18, every row against current state:\n\n- **published + linked from README** -> [x]. README references\n  `versioning`; the page is in the mkdocs nav.\n- **docs/README audited (#242) — BLOCKER** -> [x]. #242 is closed.\n- **should-fail regression tests (#111)** -> [x]. The row was reopened\n  on 2026-09-04 because the merge-blocking `validate-meta` job had no\n  case in `tests/`. `tests/test_validate_meta.sh` now exists on `main`\n  and is wired as a pre-commit hook — the cited absence is gone.\n- **Wave D (ts-lib)** -> [x]. `templates/ts-lib/` ships with its own\n  `skeleton.meta`, and #135, the one issue the row named as open, is\n  closed. The sign-off it asked for is moot: parity is met, not waived.\n\nTwo rows correctly stay unchecked, and they are now the whole entry bar:\n\n- **Wave C prose** — #195/#197/#241/#245 closed, **#194 and #247 still\n  open**; recorded so the row names what it waits on.\n- **post-1.0 breaking-change policy** — owner sign-off, unchecked on\n  purpose by the page''s own design.\n\nEach flipped row carries the measurement and its date rather than just\na tick, so the next reader can contradict it instead of trusting it.\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"dacdad178eef916719eb31abf6f1f6450e4842a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/dacdad178eef916719eb31abf6f1f6450e4842a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/c53304c26843de232b0daf687d9bac85553514a6","verification":{"payload":"tree dacdad178eef916719eb31abf6f1f6450e4842a7\nparent 57b48e494eaf82f8d9417172ae43c434b5ab4fea\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789937845 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789937845 +0000\n\ndocs(versioning): re-measure the v1.0.0 entry bar, 4 rows were stale (#534)\n\nThe entry-bar checklist opens with \"every row is decidable — yes/no, not\na feeling\", and four rows had gone stale against `main`. A stale entry\nbar under-reports readiness in the direction that costs the most: it\nmakes 1.0.0 look blocked when it is not.\n\nRe-measured 2026-09-18, every row against current state:\n\n- **published + linked from README** -> [x]. README references\n  `versioning`; the page is in the mkdocs nav.\n- **docs/README audited (#242) — BLOCKER** -> [x]. #242 is closed.\n- **should-fail regression tests (#111)** -> [x]. The row was reopened\n  on 2026-09-04 because the merge-blocking `validate-meta` job had no\n  case in `tests/`. `tests/test_validate_meta.sh` now exists on `main`\n  and is wired as a pre-commit hook — the cited absence is gone.\n- **Wave D (ts-lib)** -> [x]. `templates/ts-lib/` ships with its own\n  `skeleton.meta`, and #135, the one issue the row named as open, is\n  closed. The sign-off it asked for is moot: parity is met, not waived.\n\nTwo rows correctly stay unchecked, and they are now the whole entry bar:\n\n- **Wave C prose** — #195/#197/#241/#245 closed, **#194 and #247 still\n  open**; recorded so the row names what it waits on.\n- **post-1.0 breaking-change policy** — owner sign-off, unchecked on\n  purpose by the page''s own design.\n\nEach flipped row carries the measurement and its date rather than just\na tick, so the next reader can contradict it instead of trusting it.\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsEi1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhxcQAGY/0gN00szkYNxrfAdavadt\nLJb9T8ZAZ1MUySHrJ9q/ehFqWipmpNMn+90fbuUy7RKKwpasD7HLsu6JY/f1ps/F\n98yb6H9Q4B18f84hRPZSzYmBxbeTplR/woRHCM9uNqU/z9Y5HaqwCeVJRysguKRo\nOYDM1YBOBXfuXXlkrtJc3e10+6/slGwMPV2nMzQnp2TlAVUHv+tbM/uKVazdj7A1\n+2dUdBWQIhVC7S/HaYCPUGzpBZGcyWJtl2+GNOcBvzo34LMTvq+APuGXVF51AQkj\nTcZTkyHatmoHlOmREr6Mpbi/RrbHITD5NKJn1maLf2km1KV/W3uKnkLqNIU2o2+m\nAkoJtxshDP18s1909eOBaepCLoqL/q+OBK4PQMy38B2sNu+b6w4NOZgWqaViyXzD\nkCpD3KuN00esJx4eokP