88?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/57b48e494eaf82f8d9417172ae43c434b5ab4fea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:19:26Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:19:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): validate release version input before pushing a tag (#557)\n\n* fix(ci): validate release version input before pushing a tag\n\nFive workflow_dispatch release workflows (BlueprintX''s own release.yml,\npython-common/release.yaml, ts-lib/release-npm.yml, and lib-minimal''s\nrelease-pypi.yaml/release-test-pypi.yaml) took a free-text version\ninput straight into a tag with no validation. A malformed value (a\nstray slash, a leading v, shell metacharacters) could create the tag\nbefore the packaging step failed, leaving a pushed tag with no\nmatching artifact.\n\nAdds a Validate version step ahead of tag creation in each, using two\npatterns instead of one: the semver-with-separator form already proven\nin bash-cli''s release.yml (root release.yml, the generic service\nrelease.yaml, and ts-lib, whose version must match package.json) and a\nPEP 440-lenient form for the two PyPI workflows, whose own documented\nexamples (1.2.3a1, 1.2.3rc1) have no separator before the suffix.\n\nNotes the accepted format in each tier''s CLAUDE.md and workflow input\ndescription.\n\n* fix(ci): one real grammar per ecosystem in release validators (#548)\n\nReview on #557 found three defects in the version gate. All three\nreproduce against the shipped patterns.\n\nSemVer side (.github/workflows/release.yml,\npython-common/release.yaml, ts-lib/release-npm.yml) — the pattern\n^[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+([.-][0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$ accepts a dot-introduced\nsuffix, empty prerelease identifiers and leading zeroes. Measured: it\naccepts 1.2.3.rc, 1.2.3-rc..1, 1.2.3-rc., 01.2.3 and 1.2.3-rc.01. The\nroot and Python workflows push the input as a tag immediately after\nvalidating it, so each of those becomes an invalid release tag.\n\nReplaced with the SemVer 2.0.0 grammar: numeric identifiers with no\nleading zeroes, prerelease introduced by a hyphen and composed of\ndot-separated NON-EMPTY identifiers.\n\nPEP 440 side (lib-minimal/release-pypi.yaml, release-test-pypi.yaml) —\nthe validator and the suffix extractor were two different grammars, and\nthe gap is the dangerous part. Measured: 1.2.3-rc.1 passes validation\nand extracts an EMPTY suffix, so the `suffix == ''''` branch treats a\nprerelease as a final release and moves the `latest` docs alias.\n1.2.3foo1 passes too, then reaches the build.\n\nBoth now use one grammar, written once and read back by the extractor:\nrelease plus at most one of a<N>/b<N>/rc<N>, .post<N> or .dev<N>, no\nleading zeroes anywhere. Verified round-trip — every accepted value\nextracts the suffix it was accepted for, and a bare release extracts ''''.\n\n⚠️ The extractor existed in FOUR places, not the two the review named.\nThe fourth (release-test-pypi.yaml''s CLEAN_TAG branch) was found only\nbecause each replacement asserted its needle; a blanket edit would have\nleft it behind and the mismatch would have survived the fix.\n\nAlso quoted three unquoted expansions in the blocks touched here\n(SC2086). actionlint on release-pypi.yaml: 3 findings before, 2 after —\nthe remaining pair is in a different step and predates this change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cdab6aa2e0dba06d245b48daaedd4b6672684a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/3cdab6aa2e0dba06d245b48daaedd4b6672684a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/57b48e494eaf82f8d9417172ae43c434b5ab4fea","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cdab6aa2e0dba06d245b48daaedd4b6672684a7\nparent 6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789928366 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789928366 +0000\n\nfix(ci): validate release version input before pushing a tag (#557)\n\n* fix(ci): validate release version input before pushing a tag\n\nFive workflow_dispatch release workflows (BlueprintX''s own release.yml,\npython-common/release.yaml, ts-lib/release-npm.yml, and lib-minimal''s\nrelease-pypi.yaml/release-test-pypi.yaml) took a free-text version\ninput straight into a tag with no validation. A malformed value (a\nstray slash, a leading v, shell metacharacters) could create the tag\nbefore the packaging step failed, leaving a pushed tag with no\nmatching artifact.\n\nAdds a Validate version step ahead of tag creation in each, using two\npatterns instead of one: the semver-with-separator form already proven\nin bash-cli''s release.yml (root release.yml, the generic service\nrelease.yaml, and ts-lib, whose version must match package.json) and a\nPEP 440-lenient form for the two PyPI workflows, whose own documented\nexamples (1.2.3a1, 1.2.3rc1) have no separator before the suffix.\n\nNotes the accepted format in each tier''s CLAUDE.md and workflow input\ndescription.\n\n* fix(ci): one real grammar per ecosystem in release validators (#548)\n\nReview on #557 found three defects in the version gate. All three\nreproduce against the shipped patterns.\n\nSemVer side (.github/workflows/release.yml,\npython-common/release.yaml, ts-lib/release-npm.yml) — the pattern\n^[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+([.-][0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$ accepts a dot-introduced\nsuffix, empty prerelease identifiers and leading zeroes. Measured: it\naccepts 1.2.3.rc, 1.2.3-rc..1, 1.2.3-rc., 01.2.3 and 1.2.3-rc.01. The\nroot and Python workflows push the input as a tag immediately after\nvalidating it, so each of those becomes an invalid release tag.\n\nReplaced with the SemVer 2.0.0 grammar: numeric identifiers with no\nleading zeroes, prerelease introduced by a hyphen and composed of\ndot-separated NON-EMPTY identifiers.\n\nPEP 440 side (lib-minimal/release-pypi.yaml, release-test-pypi.yaml) —\nthe validator and the suffix extractor were two different grammars, and\nthe gap is the dangerous part. Measured: 1.2.3-rc.1 passes validation\nand extracts an EMPTY suffix, so the `suffix == ''''` branch treats a\nprerelease as a final release and moves the `latest` docs alias.\n1.2.3foo1 passes too, then reaches the build.\n\nBoth now use one grammar, written once and read back by the extractor:\nrelease plus at most one of a<N>/b<N>/rc<N>, .post<N> or .dev<N>, no\nleading zeroes anywhere. Verified round-trip — every accepted value\nextracts the suffix it was accepted for, and a bare release extracts ''''.\n\n⚠️ The extractor existed in FOUR places, not the two the review named.\nThe fourth (release-test-pypi.yaml''s CLEAN_TAG branch) was found only\nbecause each replacement asserted its needle; a blanket edit would have\nleft it behind and the mismatch would have survived the fix.\n\nAlso quoted three unquoted expansions in the blocks touched here\n(SC2086). actionlint on release-pypi.yaml: 3 findings before, 2 after —\nthe remaining pair is in a different step and predates this change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsCOvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAUwQAKyC6H83DZ0LQc45/HBli09Y\n+8ViKBRiRFAiev6l5FcLRCPLF0huNiigvqKJWd8vpQ+32kezTSrn7RnUEuu9zrT/\nXKYRJQyo8no+O62dCmG/WGlPh9gd4kx3vp+OcRZ/Eqz+sEn8psNP3sPyJ0bKFQvh\nrIrtIc0VRx7Dn28HubW6q30XzfZU0ZZbqcCZWHMgP7mYoKgKdQXWWtHWL+Z4PS7S\nXwsGt0rkzKvgijXH8I6pIeC9+BFAgLZ6M3X563pkEP6SjJVGtCkf+uWZdea8cZmC\nHT7Oyi8R7zMLk4EAamFGDcDhB6uiSlK+lGb+IloVjSQwhtRjW7omzJyseEotjX6K\nR13MeR+nJsUD0jG96O9bW6+hjzPA2dceJy1roThEPkxTudV8Y3YjFKMsa5C77qYA\nAn0m/tdvgr6KHzriE+X3XBPCrvWl4x9csmJeRlXkE4jU39CLhHznx50QqcdgOFNh\nr6TIOTCgo0mUvbGj3j5PddBb0NTqkR054Q8UOT8AhuC7Oh0EXlXzWok9Cv4T3WPc\nYQX6tx+LXXRzMsI2ZYPcRSpkJZWOvG/PNR7X1D+bkHd1P32sW4vgZBYNR2mq62N5\ns80jW21i0kbv/5XXUpRlSKjVFp4g00Eavq462CYFl5DRDOHriz/9E2/C/nXsDbT/\nUzcHApx0YM0cjPzAiv31\n=3PHC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:19:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/57b48e494eaf82f8d9417172ae43c434b5ab4fea","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDU3YjQ4ZTQ5NGVhZjgyZjhkOTQxNzE3MmFlNDNjNDM0YjVhYjRmZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b","sha":"6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b"}],"sha":"57b48e494eaf82f8d9417172ae43c434b5ab4fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/57b48e494eaf82f8d9417172ae43c434b5ab4fea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T16:52:33Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T16:52:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(chassis): make update() atomic across the six native-driver handlers (#566)\n\n* fix(chassis): make update() atomic with row locking across six handlers\n\nEvery SQL DatabaseHandler.update() did a read-modify-write across two\nconnections (self.read then self.create), so two callers updating different\nfields of one record both read the pre-state and the later write silently\ndropped the earlier one.\n\nRead and write now share ONE transaction per handler, with the row held by a\npessimistic lock: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on PostgreSQL/MySQL/MariaDB/Oracle,\nWITH (UPDLOCK, ROWLOCK) on SQL Server, BEGIN IMMEDIATE on SQLite.\n\nApplied to all six handlers in both native-driver tiers rather than to the two\nthat review flagged, so the copies cannot drift.\n\nRefs #561\n\n* docs(chassis): state the update() atomicity guarantee\n\nRecords the decision (pessimistic row locking over an optimistic version\ncolumn) with the reason, on the DatabaseHandler ABC docstring and in\ntemplates/python-common/CLAUDE.md: the per-dialect lock form, and why SQLite\nneeds BEGIN IMMEDIATE rather than the driver''s deferred transaction.\n\nRefs #561\n\n* test(chassis): pin the lost-update race for all six handlers\n\nSQLite is raced for real: two threads write different fields of one record\nwith json.loads stalled, so the windows overlap in both the broken and the\nfixed implementation. The five server-backed handlers use a recording fake\ndriver asserting the two properties a real race would test - read and write\non ONE connection, and the read carrying that dialect''s row lock.\n\nCalibrated: with the six update() bodies reverted to the pre-fix version all\n6 tests fail, the SQLite one by losing the ''beta'' field exactly as reported;\nrestoring the fix returns 6 passed, and the race test is stable over 10 runs.\n\nRefs #561\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"736427de4501b160c5cb22b78aaf88e968329e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/736427de4501b160c5cb22b78aaf88e968329e39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b","verification":{"payload":"tree 736427de4501b160c5cb22b78aaf88e968329e39\nparent 67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789923153 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789923153 +0000\n\nfix(chassis): make update() atomic across the six native-driver handlers (#566)\n\n* fix(chassis): make update() atomic with row locking across six handlers\n\nEvery SQL DatabaseHandler.update() did a read-modify-write across two\nconnections (self.read then self.create), so two callers updating different\nfields of one record both read the pre-state and the later write silently\ndropped the earlier one.\n\nRead and write now share ONE transaction per handler, with the row held by a\npessimistic lock: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on PostgreSQL/MySQL/MariaDB/Oracle,\nWITH (UPDLOCK, ROWLOCK) on SQL Server, BEGIN IMMEDIATE on SQLite.\n\nApplied to all six handlers in both native-driver tiers rather than to the two\nthat review flagged, so the copies cannot drift.\n\nRefs #561\n\n* docs(chassis): state the update() atomicity guarantee\n\nRecords the decision (pessimistic row locking over an optimistic version\ncolumn) with the reason, on the DatabaseHandler ABC docstring and in\ntemplates/python-common/CLAUDE.md: the per-dialect lock form, and why SQLite\nneeds BEGIN IMMEDIATE rather than the driver''s deferred transaction.\n\nRefs #561\n\n* test(chassis): pin the lost-update race for all six handlers\n\nSQLite is raced for real: two threads write different fields of one record\nwith json.loads stalled, so the windows overlap in both the broken and the\nfixed implementation. The five server-backed handlers use a recording fake\ndriver asserting the two properties a real race would test - read and write\non ONE connection, and the read carrying that dialect''s row lock.\n\nCalibrated: with the six update() bodies reverted to the pre-fix version all\n6 tests fail, the SQLite one by losing the ''beta'' field exactly as reported;\nrestoring the fix returns 6 passed, and the race test is stable over 10 runs.\n\nRefs #561\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsA9RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ8EQAJxNf2dQmINaioAxL+o0UYxN\ns2qB2bY0w+slziNnhflR8bdrCjZJXtAHNLMbAZVXi8A/CqFRKKvV06KjVvMzx2q4\ngAevU8fGOsMOnm36GVGDK3leEEUHi+TxkUZQh8QxBPES1CKKcCBxJtNWdeQqbX9v\nhXB6w+TEAiqLZ4LBszt74STeEHgiN/xN4nPrSBd1qJg1qKuDpyMdL0Gs0k5yjQa/\nsAQPZZo3bf6BV7wO9A8/dZoiBNEHdKSieBDgioZX0swOmOFvajZJXm7OcynJBfum\nS//SL29jeIKVJ5gAX7a+FbN5PDy45sqWlcnwtmE+Tp8NIcCBX1oqS/i0+b2R3lE+\nPalzIWZ6A7xg5Y49s3ewQgSAud7AQAOd5HX1LSDO9rXk3Tnk+hMFtJc1lByJTNrL\nW9MxX2ElSfunuiiUz0uyDNqXKX7O4yJ9aunVvthFohDe5VKJsSpYYliW/src0wxw\nQ85LILLbwcoRoHzrHUBZPHD7LXJaJbkIKjKQjuGw4IIHgZYi00/XvfviyfkAetFo\n1exi8gs1jBXapGwsK9Pdv4PCRxQg7LySNpms0cpFqrVhT/O418ija1KJj59B8Mvz\nJn2j+i55Yx3Z8Kr+M1xawiW49lEZ55Taz/nLqmyKFOVqXxJsiY31tb/qbAWL1zfy\nJ4nG2YnOeBT6L2QGkr1g\n=RkTX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T16:52:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDZhY2Q4ZGI4YjFlZDRlOTVkM2M0MDAwYmI4MGI2MDA0ZDg4NzUyNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e","sha":"67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e"}],"sha":"6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/6acd8db8b1ed4e95d3c4000bb80b6004d887524b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T10:17:53Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T10:17:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): fail a PR above 90 changed files (#560)\n\n* feat(ci): add PR file-count ceiling gate (#551)\n\nCodeRabbit hard-refuses to review a PR above 100 changed files, so such a\nPR can never merge. Fail at 90 (calibrated: 1 violation in the last 100\nPRs, largest legitimate PR is 59 files) instead of discovering it after\nthe PR is already open and unreviewable.\n\n* fix(ci): resolve the file-count gate''s merge-base against origin/main\n\nA bare local branch name can sit dozens of commits stale in a long-lived\nworktree without anyone noticing (measured here: local main was 45\ncommits behind origin/main, which inflated a 3-file change to 213).\nResolve against origin/<branch> when that ref exists, falling back to\nthe local name only when there is no origin remote at all.\n\n* chore(ci): wire the PR file-count gate into pre-commit and CI (#551)\n\nAttempted as two separate commits, one per file, so a rebase past\n#503/#528 (.pre-commit-config.yaml) or #489/#492/#503/#530\n(scaffold_checks.yml) touches only its own hunk. This repo''s own\nprecommit-ci-parity hook refuses a commit that wires a script into only\none side (it stashes unstaged changes before running, so a\npre-commit-only or CI-only intermediate state fails loudly) --\ncombined here instead of using --no-verify. Both hunks stay small and\nindependent; a conflict on either file''s own content still rebases\ncleanly, it is only the two-commit split that was not possible.\n\n* docs: document the PR file-count ceiling gate (#551)\n\nAdd the gate to CLAUDE.md''s gate-family list and to CONTRIBUTING.md''s\nPR process, so the 90-file ceiling and its calibration are findable\nwithout reading the gate script itself.\n\n* fix(ci): count the index on a branch with no commit of its own (#551)\n\nThe no-op guard was `merge-base(HEAD, <default>) == HEAD`, read as \"we\nare on the default branch\". It is also true of a feature branch BEFORE\nits first commit — HEAD still points at the branch point — which is\nexactly the state pre-commit runs in, with the whole change staged.\n\nReproduced on a throwaway repo: fresh branch, no commit, 91 staged\nfiles, gate exit 0. The cap was bypassable by every branch''s first\ncommit, which is the most common way a large change arrives.\n\nThe gate now asks the question it meant to ask: is the CURRENT CHECKOUT\nthe default branch (by name, or by tip when detached, as CI is)? The\nmerge-base is still used for the diff, and an unresolvable one (shallow\nclone, unrelated history) still no-ops.\n\nThe existing regression suite could not see this: its fixture made an\nempty commit right after `checkout -b`, with a comment calling that\ncommit load-bearing. It was — it moved HEAD off the branch point and\nhid the hole. The fixture now builds both states and asserts the same\n91-file message in each. Calibrated against the pre-fix gate: the new\ncase fails there and passes here.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c7ae2ebf5885d94e0a8c2d0e89f33671ed4a7fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/9c7ae2ebf5885d94e0a8c2d0e89f33671ed4a7fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c7ae2ebf5885d94e0a8c2d0e89f33671ed4a7fa\nparent cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789899473 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789899473 +0000\n\nfeat(ci): fail a PR above 90 changed files (#560)\n\n* feat(ci): add PR file-count ceiling gate (#551)\n\nCodeRabbit hard-refuses to review a PR above 100 changed files, so such a\nPR can never merge. Fail at 90 (calibrated: 1 violation in the last 100\nPRs, largest legitimate PR is 59 files) instead of discovering it after\nthe PR is already open and unreviewable.\n\n* fix(ci): resolve the file-count gate''s merge-base against origin/main\n\nA bare local branch name can sit dozens of commits stale in a long-lived\nworktree without anyone noticing (measured here: local main was 45\ncommits behind origin/main, which inflated a 3-file change to 213).\nResolve against origin/<branch> when that ref exists, falling back to\nthe local name only when there is no origin remote at all.\n\n* chore(ci): wire the PR file-count gate into pre-commit and CI (#551)\n\nAttempted as two separate commits, one per file, so a rebase past\n#503/#528 (.pre-commit-config.yaml) or #489/#492/#503/#530\n(scaffold_checks.yml) touches only its own hunk. This repo''s own\nprecommit-ci-parity hook refuses a commit that wires a script into only\none side (it stashes unstaged changes before running, so a\npre-commit-only or CI-only intermediate state fails loudly) --\ncombined here instead of using --no-verify. Both hunks stay small and\nindependent; a conflict on either file''s own content still rebases\ncleanly, it is only the two-commit split that was not possible.\n\n* docs: document the PR file-count ceiling gate (#551)\n\nAdd the gate to CLAUDE.md''s gate-family list and to CONTRIBUTING.md''s\nPR process, so the 90-file ceiling and its calibration are findable\nwithout reading the gate script itself.\n\n* fix(ci): count the index on a branch with no commit of its own (#551)\n\nThe no-op guard was `merge-base(HEAD, <default>) == HEAD`, read as \"we\nare on the default branch\". It is also true of a feature branch BEFORE\nits first commit — HEAD still points at the branch point — which is\nexactly the state pre-commit runs in, with the whole change staged.\n\nReproduced on a throwaway repo: fresh branch, no commit, 91 staged\nfiles, gate exit 0. The cap was bypassable by every branch''s first\ncommit, which is the most common way a large change arrives.\n\nThe gate now asks the question it meant to ask: is the CURRENT CHECKOUT\nthe default branch (by name, or by tip when detached, as CI is)? The\nmerge-base is still used for the diff, and an unresolvable one (shallow\nclone, unrelated history) still no-ops.\n\nThe existing regression suite could not see this: its fixture made an\nempty commit right after `checkout -b`, with a comment calling that\ncommit load-bearing. It was — it moved HEAD off the branch point and\nhid the hole. The fixture now builds both states and asserts the same\n91-file message in each. Calibrated against the pre-fix gate: the new\ncase fails there and passes here.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr7LRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6fYQAJzgBIRatSnwVA8fZReI4hsu\nJ+28GLCu2WE3UOUJVAQ7Kof9aGuUrxYyQ2fH9eh7I2hImFuM28dc63K4xtBKUcjJ\nH9Uy4qWA24kXA1b1DJtoKYFN0AADnGfwnNDAGJa7STiVvpL2nsh+NLelyiMLA0dC\nTAsjVnCjYOwDJ444tiuwzOvq8/USria6/61bSiAw5YaknqUNp//nDdPawPo8Kszx\ngZHJKJCFph77T7YufF1NQDRNbJE5I0Ntr8/YYmGVWXm02fZPxR1GOiSJu+IHLytY\nwD0Gb36NyeeY1k3aR1e4Seu9xbfbaIUk1XeSRQgY+CmjmbdCqDXehzQvkGYsf9XB\nkmb2Kx2B/S+NAs1Z9JWHVha3pyHmeIEhrRG8kKtv9fCWUhDajKu+0w/jgbpPjViO\nT4luW8vMAEEoWijTlJjLN92ciSIz4jztn7Jbzp3nqk5DdxQlSgd3LmgXA5CuhmjG\nZEvABBCx9j8fJLijRlN1D0U+qhGZM52GP5uamoi3acIkoHzlQTdBvCySeNallCT3\nZkzdUHiZAmzd2I9sZ+62jM8ikeXz4OvoLrimPZmV4gWZfc7nWpPigusinOB75Bsd\nINFuxJSNBzn8IvZ8SiaCc1st9clp0Te1bh0Nv0qr+jUPeCs85qpUc+7EbjJlxJMD\n/geZi/CHqc0G728oOvA5\n=dQ+8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T10:17:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDY3YWQ1MjE2OTRlMjEzNTI3NWY5ZTMzNDBkMzVmZTNhOTdlNjQ1MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee","sha":"cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee"}],"sha":"67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/67ad521694e2135275f9e3340d35fe3a97e6451e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:52:51Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:52:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(templates): add API service skeleton (hexagonal + FastAPI transport) (#532)\n\n* feat(templates): add api-service skeleton (#482)\n\nNew templates/api-service-native-db/ skeleton: hexagonal DDD layers plus\na FastAPI transport layer (capabilities/*/transport/routers.py, app/api.py),\nnamed for the role (API service) not the framework. bin/scaffold/\npython_api_service.sh follows the existing Python scaffold sequence.\nNo registry/publish workflow — a service is deployed, not published.\n\nDiscovered automatically by bin/blueprintx.sh''s skeleton.meta scan; no\nchange to that script. bin/preview.sh gets a matching preview function.\ndocs/skeletons.md is the skeleton''s own docs page. One-line addition to\nthe root CLAUDE.md architecture tree (validate_meta.sh requires every\nskeleton dir name to appear there). check_test_copy_lists.py gets the\nsame schemas/-not-yet-wired exclusion the other four service scaffolds\ncarry for test_config_schemas_example.py.\n\n* fix(templates): fit router builder under complexity ceiling\n\nbuild_example_feature_router() had two nested route-handler defs, which\nmccabe counts as branches of the enclosing function (complexity 3 > the\nsrc/ ceiling of 2). Move the handlers to a small _ExampleFeatureEndpoints\nclass (constructor-injected callables — a legitimate DI class per\ncommon.md), registered via add_api_route instead of nested @decorators.\n\nVerified: bash bin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh api-service-native-db passes\nend to end (lint, 818 unit + 85 integration tests). Also manually\nscaffolded, ran uvicorn, and curled /health, POST /notes, GET /notes —\nall real HTTP responses (200/201/200).\n\n* fix(api-service): nine review findings — DSN forms, races, stale docs\n\nAll ten findings on #532 reproduced against current code; none was\nstale. Nine are fixed here. The tenth is filed as #561 — see below.\n\nScaffold (2):\n- Four `cp -r src dest` calls nested the package on a re-run\n  (`src/chassis/db/db/`), so a second scaffold silently stopped updating\n  those files. Reproduced, then switched to `mkdir -p dest && cp -r\n  src/. dest/`, matching the two sites that already did it.\n- `test_migration_graph_gate.py` was never copied, so the gate shipped\n  with no test in any generated project. `check_test_copy_lists.py` now\n  reports 56 tests reachable from all 6 scaffolds.\n\nConnection strings (1, and it makes two backends unusable):\n- This is the NATIVE-driver tier, but `_compose_dsn` built SQLAlchemy\n  URLs for every backend. MSSQL and Oracle hand the string straight to\n  the driver instead of parsing it, so\n  `pyodbc.connect(\"mssql+pyodbc://…\")` and\n  `oracledb.connect(dsn=\"oracle+oracledb://…\")` both fail — selecting\n  either backend with the documented DB_* variables could never work.\n  MSSQL now gets an ODBC `KEY=VALUE;` string, Oracle an Easy Connect\n  `host:port/service` with credentials passed as arguments.\n- URL-form credentials are percent-encoded. Measured: the password\n  `p@ss/w0rd` re-partitions the URL and the driver connects to host `ss`\n  instead of `db`.\n\nConcurrency (2):\n- One repository is shared by all requests and FastAPI runs sync\n  handlers in worker threads, so `list()` returning a live `dict_values`\n  view let a concurrent `add()` raise `RuntimeError: dictionary changed\n  size during iteration`. Added a lock and a tuple snapshot — the\n  snapshot is the fix, not the lock alone.\n- SQLite `backup()` used `shutil.copy2`. Measured on a WAL database with\n  500 committed rows: the copy is not stale but UNREADABLE\n  (`OperationalError`), while `Connection.backup()` returns all 500.\n\nDocs (4): `uvicorn app.api:app` names a module that exports only\n`create_app()`; Oracle reads `DB_SERVICE`, not `DB_NAME`; the use-case\nexample was wrong in three ways at once (package, call form, argument\ntype); driver names in `architecture.md` and `skeleton.meta` predated\nthe move to psycopg/oracledb/mysql-connector-python.\n\nNot fixed here, deliberately: the read-modify-write `update()` race is\nin 6 handler files across tiers including the already-shipped\nddd-service-native-db, so it is #561 rather than a one-tier patch that\nwould leave five broken and start the drift.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b5dc694948347d40d3992e18f8f322bb02b8239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/5b5dc694948347d40d3992e18f8f322bb02b8239"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b5dc694948347d40d3992e18f8f322bb02b8239\nparent aa7b4f7f56c7f35a8c5464d09317941fdd9161ea\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789897971 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789897971 +0000\n\nfeat(templates): add API service skeleton (hexagonal + FastAPI transport) (#532)\n\n* feat(templates): add api-service skeleton (#482)\n\nNew templates/api-service-native-db/ skeleton: hexagonal DDD layers plus\na FastAPI transport layer (capabilities/*/transport/routers.py, app/api.py),\nnamed for the role (API service) not the framework. bin/scaffold/\npython_api_service.sh follows the existing Python scaffold sequence.\nNo registry/publish workflow — a service is deployed, not published.\n\nDiscovered automatically by bin/blueprintx.sh''s skeleton.meta scan; no\nchange to that script. bin/preview.sh gets a matching preview function.\ndocs/skeletons.md is the skeleton''s own docs page. One-line addition to\nthe root CLAUDE.md architecture tree (validate_meta.sh requires every\nskeleton dir name to appear there). check_test_copy_lists.py gets the\nsame schemas/-not-yet-wired exclusion the other four service scaffolds\ncarry for test_config_schemas_example.py.\n\n* fix(templates): fit router builder under complexity ceiling\n\nbuild_example_feature_router() had two nested route-handler defs, which\nmccabe counts as branches of the enclosing function (complexity 3 > the\nsrc/ ceiling of 2). Move the handlers to a small _ExampleFeatureEndpoints\nclass (constructor-injected callables — a legitimate DI class per\ncommon.md), registered via add_api_route instead of nested @decorators.\n\nVerified: bash bin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh api-service-native-db passes\nend to end (lint, 818 unit + 85 integration tests). Also manually\nscaffolded, ran uvicorn, and curled /health, POST /notes, GET /notes —\nall real HTTP responses (200/201/200).\n\n* fix(api-service): nine review findings — DSN forms, races, stale docs\n\nAll ten findings on #532 reproduced against current code; none was\nstale. Nine are fixed here. The tenth is filed as #561 — see below.\n\nScaffold (2):\n- Four `cp -r src dest` calls nested the package on a re-run\n  (`src/chassis/db/db/`), so a second scaffold silently stopped updating\n  those files. Reproduced, then switched to `mkdir -p dest && cp -r\n  src/. dest/`, matching the two sites that already did it.\n- `test_migration_graph_gate.py` was never copied, so the gate shipped\n  with no test in any generated project. `check_test_copy_lists.py` now\n  reports 56 tests reachable from all 6 scaffolds.\n\nConnection strings (1, and it makes two backends unusable):\n- This is the NATIVE-driver tier, but `_compose_dsn` built SQLAlchemy\n  URLs for every backend. MSSQL and Oracle hand the string straight to\n  the driver instead of parsing it, so\n  `pyodbc.connect(\"mssql+pyodbc://…\")` and\n  `oracledb.connect(dsn=\"oracle+oracledb://…\")` both fail — selecting\n  either backend with the documented DB_* variables could never work.\n  MSSQL now gets an ODBC `KEY=VALUE;` string, Oracle an Easy Connect\n  `host:port/service` with credentials passed as arguments.\n- URL-form credentials are percent-encoded. Measured: the password\n  `p@ss/w0rd` re-partitions the URL and the driver connects to host `ss`\n  instead of `db`.\n\nConcurrency (2):\n- One repository is shared by all requests and FastAPI runs sync\n  handlers in worker threads, so `list()` returning a live `dict_values`\n  view let a concurrent `add()` raise `RuntimeError: dictionary changed\n  size during iteration`. Added a lock and a tuple snapshot — the\n  snapshot is the fix, not the lock alone.\n- SQLite `backup()` used `shutil.copy2`. Measured on a WAL database with\n  500 committed rows: the copy is not stale but UNREADABLE\n  (`OperationalError`), while `Connection.backup()` returns all 500.\n\nDocs (4): `uvicorn app.api:app` names a module that exports only\n`create_app()`; Oracle reads `DB_SERVICE`, not `DB_NAME`; the use-case\nexample was wrong in three ways at once (package, call form, argument\ntype); driver names in `architecture.md` and `skeleton.meta` predated\nthe move to psycopg/oracledb/mysql-connector-python.\n\nNot fixed here, deliberately: the read-modify-write `update()` race is\nin 6 handler files across tiers including the already-shipped\nddd-service-native-db, so it is #561 rather than a one-tier patch that\nwould leave five broken and start the drift.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr6zzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARtEQAGXDY0/7DCpLh4OQ7DzhVeju\nHSWJzS3SwEgjalcCLBPM3/h3H9KhZoFlYr/bGyDDRc22SvNN/obSaE2qz6TXlWVZ\n+QlrnWPyxafTYVY09ByxhH3gzQBGA3eD8XGSy2R50prjhm69Lu/WAfrTotzXe9ZC\n8qyjbxfVqAQCCKIQOBEZzunFvB1xkQQBX3HIQTKIULWF8uA5WQl