,"sha":"cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/cfe36cc23bdc4183b0a70aa2a5ec6ed098c684ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/aa7b4f7f56c7f35a8c5464d09317941fdd9161ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T01:37:47Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T01:37:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(markdownlint): pin pymarkdownlnt, close the rule-enumeration hole (#530)\n\nThe gate''s own failure message says \"only MD018/019/020/021/023, MD047,\nMD009 are enabled\" — and that was false. `.pymarkdown.json` enumerates\nrules md001-md048 one by one, so every rule a NEWER pymarkdownlnt adds\nis enabled by default and silently joins the gate.\n\nMeasured 2026-09-18: CI installed pymarkdownlnt unpinned and got\n0.9.40, which added MD049 (emphasis-style), MD050 and MD051\n(link-fragments). 15 violations appeared across three files nobody had\ntouched, turning 9 open PRs red. Locally the same script passed,\nbecause this machine has 0.9.39 — a gate whose verdict depends on the\nday its runner installed a dependency.\n\nThe MD051 hits are the clearest sign the rules were never chosen: they\nflag `[Page placeholder 1](#)` in the React SPA README, deliberate\nplaceholder anchors a scaffolded project fills in.\n\nTwo changes, one defect:\n- disable md049/md050/md051 explicitly, so the config matches the set\n  the gate claims to enforce;\n- pin `pymarkdownlnt==0.9.40` in CI, so the enumeration cannot go stale\n  behind an implicit upgrade. Bump it deliberately, re-measuring.\n\nVerified against the exact CI version: a throwaway venv with\npymarkdownlnt==0.9.40 runs `bin/ci/check_markdown.sh` to\n\"pymarkdownlnt OK\", exit 0. The failing half is already evidenced by\nCI''s own job log on PR #528.\n\ngate-change-ok: md049/050/051 were never in the measured set; they\narrived enabled-by-default via an unpinned upstream bump, not by\ndecision. This restores the documented set and pins the version.\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2688a4b4d944cce4f2cdf6e3e0c91da0d2b5f93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/e2688a4b4d944cce4f2cdf6e3e0c91da0d2b5f93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/aa7b4f7f56c7f35a8c5464d09317941fdd9161ea","verification":{"payload":"tree e2688a4b4d944cce4f2cdf6e3e0c91da0d2b5f93\nparent 80053287143d4c4ec4b0760b61fc33522a5701b5\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789868267 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789868267 +0000\n\nfix(markdownlint): pin pymarkdownlnt, close the rule-enumeration hole (#530)\n\nThe gate''s own failure message says \"only MD018/019/020/021/023, MD047,\nMD009 are enabled\" — and that was false. `.pymarkdown.json` enumerates\nrules md001-md048 one by one, so every rule a NEWER pymarkdownlnt adds\nis enabled by default and silently joins the gate.\n\nMeasured 2026-09-18: CI installed pymarkdownlnt unpinned and got\n0.9.40, which added MD049 (emphasis-style), MD050 and MD051\n(link-fragments). 15 violations appeared across three files nobody had\ntouched, turning 9 open PRs red. Locally the same script passed,\nbecause this machine has 0.9.39 — a gate whose verdict depends on the\nday its runner installed a dependency.\n\nThe MD051 hits are the clearest sign the rules were never chosen: they\nflag `[Page placeholder 1](#)` in the React SPA README, deliberate\nplaceholder anchors a scaffolded project fills in.\n\nTwo changes, one defect:\n- disable md049/md050/md051 explicitly, so the config matches the set\n  the gate claims to enforce;\n- pin `pymarkdownlnt==0.9.40` in CI, so the enumeration cannot go stale\n  behind an implicit upgrade. Bump it deliberately, re-measuring.\n\nVerified against the exact CI version: a throwaway venv with\npymarkdownlnt==0.9.40 runs `bin/ci/check_markdown.sh` to\n\"pymarkdownlnt OK\", exit 0. The failing half is already evidenced by\nCI''s own job log on PR #528.\n\ngate-change-ok: md049/050/051 were never in the measured set; they\narrived enabled-by-default via an unpinned upstream bump, not by\ndecision. This restores the documented set and pins the version.\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrzjrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJREQAC3cjcQdjoee7kChmqCWefJF\neQ0u2iEMr5z0lwmRjf1bUXSbKCKuL4nILUAEyrbALjj+RD1xL+4bAr2HlId5O6M7\nv76UHqjEiiOhQaYt2Tm1IkfSsIrMPhEd74YD+zGI5vmBN4Xgzvb5Th+q0WNurXcu\n7r4BvfbGZ4WzkjjsYi/P7MbC5PMpLFEiuqUv8sRgTItNVeQLK86Fjox5zg5YNxj7\nt4XCG3DU3AjEiw+tZbHCZkxUqZs71x1XBlgh+kst6IQ+UDPn9U9FquogqDT/7RWb\ndO5cua+ShctavX+pTYAE2Q8xMmxwaYJjATS9q03ItNpMqpf60HBOpv82PQoG+27S\niK7axbKJEc2B9fzEsUcdM4SI8Lc2vhMI0fAfAGSUy/QYK2ypJjSvoTSpZvl5TgVj\nc/99urhAh80V24AYrgdq05K3axm3hWqV9o5PWPJTVUwp