les) - annotate with noqa: BLE001\npointing at the existing docstring rather than duplicate it.\n\n* docs(contributing): record BLE adoption + TS catch-safety parity\n\nblueprintx#440: measured Ruff Rule Adoption Log entry for BLE (the\nexcept-Exception gap E722 does not cover) and the explicit decision\nnot to adopt RUF yet (150 findings, real cost, deferred). Adds the\nmissing \"Broad-except / catch-safety\" row to the cross-language\nparity snapshot, noting the TS half already shipped in #443 and\ndiffers by construction (no typed catch clause to mirror BLE).\n\n* feat(ruff): select BLE (flake8-blind-except) in python-common\n\nblueprintx#440. E722 (already selected via E) only catches a bare\nexcept:; BLE001 is the gap above it - except Exception:/except\nBaseException: names a type but says nothing. Measured 0 net-new\ncost: the two live findings were fixed in a prior commit on this\nbranch, and this is a separate, final commit because ruff.toml is\nalso held by open PR #486 (pep8-naming) - both touch the same\nselect/config block and should not race.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c4dc02d92e72590e11f98c33c6bff9ab1e09ed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/7c4dc02d92e72590e11f98c33c6bff9ab1e09ed8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/1ce1be57e7c13b1593265dd19da70f98a692973c","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c4dc02d92e72590e11f98c33c6bff9ab1e09ed8\nparent 125cbf5cd358c2a4e31b05ab13908183a3a82d61\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789818005 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789818005 +0000\n\nfeat(ruff): forbid a broad except (BLE) + TS catch-safety parity (#511)\n\n* fix(templates): suppress the two live BLE001 sites in _pipeline.py\n\nblueprintx#440: turning on ruff''s BLE (blind-except) rule in a\nfollowing commit flags these as the only two unsuppressed broad\nexcepts in templates/. Both are the same documented five-mode\ndegradation (mvc-service-native-db and mvc-service-orm-db,\nbyte-identical _pipeline.py files) - annotate with noqa: BLE001\npointing at the existing docstring rather than duplicate it.\n\n* docs(contributing): record BLE adoption + TS catch-safety parity\n\nblueprintx#440: measured Ruff Rule Adoption Log entry for BLE (the\nexcept-Exception gap E722 does not cover) and the explicit decision\nnot to adopt RUF yet (150 findings, real cost, deferred). Adds the\nmissing \"Broad-except / catch-safety\" row to the cross-language\nparity snapshot, noting the TS half already shipped in #443 and\ndiffers by construction (no typed catch clause to mirror BLE).\n\n* feat(ruff): select BLE (flake8-blind-except) in python-common\n\nblueprintx#440. E722 (already selected via E) only catches a bare\nexcept:; BLE001 is the gap above it - except Exception:/except\nBaseException: names a type but says nothing. Measured 0 net-new\ncost: the two live findings were fixed in a prior commit on this\nbranch, and this is a separate, final commit because ruff.toml is\nalso held by open PR #486 (pep8-naming) - both touch the same\nselect/config block and should not race.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrnSVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+xQQAJffIjmiR5i2udEFsKz9+g8P\n8cTZsnLtTidYHFCxVNriifgEOvBhQY7A7pmjXmzdbPCYILaE5qiox3DSx1qSr5Ki\nc2DmLvqGS/Q7LpVHQ0S7xdtyXnoOMFZXz4Iut9b7Qnvfjt2aZzXY+tQFULBO04NC\nOVQWmJgspM30ZEcF5zt0j5zm3Y9eU/13bL2Ve02aIyvXrvpv7X2D9vtE1KFXV66E\nOv4UwkFhNkQeAFF73K0Fy98fllhRcpcy0ZXKFHxQzY+gYtoT8wOE9+I1UpGDqHgu\nq6LXjHVQsyY6C3d+licv4uHM9j7gM2qcsDRQItqsRLUV+5K8Wvc0pb9Gmy0pzZQO\nqavZDiKjU/CVtccYqb4vPoCMeZBVMkbtg7uAmXQ4XaEtGAl3WgrJ+9AMI+Na0egl\nDginzx7HesB+z9QP+DT2/Ly+t+cSUB89Uda0R4hlsaLcaaitddoIAkPB7AkPEmT9\nZiCmNmbwWXF/T5FSr+7JNJMOaDOZGFyJmJSJXF6QfuLIaPjClkKBIOe7/mjyDtXs\narkmYsAjTGihe4iN+k7+4UjEx/1vHKz/QUhha1mCYWaF66kmDOr5+GPlqSi5P5yB\nzhwNjKUvZmX7emB3U/2D