uilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/125cbf5cd358c2a4e31b05ab13908183a3a82d61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:39:39Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:39:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): Alembic migration-graph gate (#308) (#537)\n\n* feat(ci): add migration-graph gate (#308)\n\nAlembic migrations form a linked list via down_revision. Two PRs that\neach add a migration off the same base clean-merge on the Git side\n(two new files, no textual overlap) while the migration graph\nsilently branches into two heads — discovered only when someone runs\n`alembic upgrade head` against a real database.\n\nAdd check_migration_graph.py: a structural, DB-free gate that reads\nevery revision/down_revision header via ast (never imports the\nmigration module, since it imports alembic.op) and rejects a\nduplicate revision id, a dangling down_revision, a self-referencing\ndown_revision, or more than one head. Self-skips when\nmigrations/versions/ is absent or empty; an unparsable file is a\nfinding, never a silent skip.\n\nManually verified the should-fail witness: two synthetic revisions\nsharing a parent report \"2 head revisions present\" and exit 1; adding\nthe merge revision (down_revision as a tuple of both parents) then\nreports a single head and exits 0. 11 unit tests cover both, plus\nduplicate/dangling/self-reference/unparsable/missing-header cases.\n\nRecords the new test as a deliberate, honest gap in\nbin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py''s DICT_EXPECTED_ABSENT: no\nbin/scaffold/*.sh cp line yet, since that copy list is held by\nanother open PR. Wiring the cp line is a follow-up (see PR body).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* ci(templates): wire the migration-graph gate into tests.yaml (#308)\n\nRescued from a session-limit kill: the gate and its tests were committed,\nthis CI wiring step was still uncommitted in the worktree.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* fix(ci): reject unverifiable down_revision, detect cycles per component\n\nTwo review findings, both confirmed against the branch head.\n\ndown_revision: .get() collapsed ''absent'', ''None'' and ''not a literal'' into\none value, so an unreadable file became a root and shifted the head count.\nDistinct _MISSING/_UNSUPPORTED sentinels keep the three apart, and a tuple\nholding a non-string is now reported instead of having that element\nsilently dropped.\n\nCycles: head-counting only fired when the WHOLE graph had no head, so a\ntwo-node cycle beside a valid chain left the count at 1 and went unseen.\nKahn''s algorithm now peels from every root and names whatever will not\npeel. All four regression tests verified failing against the old gate.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2623bbfd90bd31e9e7659263692a9ef5c41d4e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/f2623bbfd90bd31e9e7659263692a9ef5c41d4e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/125cbf5cd358c2a4e31b05ab13908183a3a82d61","verification":{"payload":"tree f2623bbfd90bd31e9e7659263692a9ef5c41d4e8\nparent 3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789814379 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789814379 -0300\n\nfeat(ci): Alembic migration-graph gate (#308) (#537)\n\n* feat(ci): add migration-graph gate (#308)\n\nAlembic migrations form a linked list via down_revision. Two PRs that\neach add a migration off the same base clean-merge on the Git side\n(two new files, no textual overlap) while the migration graph\nsilently branches into two heads — discovered only when someone runs\n`alembic upgrade head` against a real database.\n\nAdd check_migration_graph.py: a structural, DB-free gate that reads\nevery revision/down_revision header via ast (never imports the\nmigration module, since it imports alembic.op) and rejects a\nduplicate revision id, a dangling down_revision, a self-referencing\ndown_revision, or more than one head. Self-skips when\nmigrations/versions/ is absent or empty; an unparsable file is a\nfinding, never a silent skip.\n\nManually verified the should-fail witness: two synthetic revisions\nsharing a parent report \"2 head revisions present\" and exit 1; adding\nthe merge revision (down_revision as a tuple of both parents) then\nreports a single head and exits 0. 11 unit tests cover both, plus\nduplicate/dangling/self-reference/unparsable/missing-header cases.\n\nRecords the new test as a deliberate, honest gap in\nbin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py''s DICT_EXPECTED_ABSENT: no\nbin/scaffold/*.sh cp line yet, since that copy list is held by\nanother open PR. Wiring the cp line is a follow-up (see PR body).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* ci(templates): wire the migration-graph gate into tests.yaml (#308)\n\nRescued from a session-limit kill: the gate and its tests were committed,\nthis CI wiring step was still uncommitted in the worktree.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n* fix(ci): reject unverifiable down_revision, detect cycles per component\n\nTwo review findings, both confirmed against the branch head.\n\ndown_revision: .get() collapsed ''absent'', ''None'' and ''not a literal'' into\none value, so an unreadable file became a root and shifted the head count.\nDistinct _MISSING/_UNSUPPORTED sentinels keep the three apart, and a tuple\nholding a non-string is now reported instead of having that element\nsilently dropped.\n\nCycles: head-counting only fired when the WHOLE graph had no head, so a\ntwo-node cycle beside a valid chain left the count at 1 and went unseen.\nKahn''s algorithm now peels from every root and names whatever will not\npeel. All four regression tests verified failing against the old gate.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrmZrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsk4QAI27K441LB/5fC2cvFFNoNa9\nKjaRrXPl8ZbhrhxQYiB3S82pUgzWwBhp+fO4mbolXxJCtuDUGHn9pacxcvwxKa5w\ndoRrWp6Upi7YlKJu+JAW+DOzClPUyhKYjA6po0S8VR06gould8D1/XBc0QwOx56W\nDbrtLY9B/0lLCxVVrPLbLj8GfMfwiNn636QRf5wnJvrbnQ9IOPA3DDErrsTXvbFV\nH11E4ziIXPyZNrfsQclAZLD2NZm6X19YFxzFktCGR32UCOo4iDdYhGQbH3N40i6k\nSpOD0ERV9gfud2C9EGGLocE+qVnf6VwwvjzUUy6eTGEYzVGLE2pUblmY9QxipOoV\nufvw5TvJT786vDbLcaLg4Mq6dMFfWMqV9n0DPmeQniG4v7sPDSkEYuRaOkNpaGn8\nMpwMSBWLM8MMp+XZKIDVSPvWpXvke15CshzJBSk73rpyEMBjztgS2UvWuVVDv91H\nFwXuu4iHebuNJXOBMD3OFVUg49mr2lCM5CAwlapw+3L/V6FvUAnL8MWhtcpO4IoZ\nwAH01tCilB1nMMGgGUUSh+kaY2p6Wf+uDIY4fGlZ2SnlXipgVPrdTRzBSOUJUYr+\nDkHn3F4eaIh9MKs4H963bv/qE28hvYtp5Z3AirzAA54Qa48Xh6NnrzfOkpL6m05g\nNtDRkOxTyNo/9tIWEM/d\n=gb7d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T10:39:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/125cbf5cd358c2a4e31b05ab13908183a3a82d61","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDEyNWNiZjVjZDM1OGMyYTRlMzFiMDVhYjEzOTA4MTgzYTNhODJkNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f","sha":"3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f"}],"sha":"125cbf5cd358c2a4e31b05ab13908183a3a82d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/125cbf5cd358c2a4e31b05ab13908183a3a82d61"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:21:12Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:21:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(react-spa-webpack): wire OTLP log export opt-in (#504) (#519)\n\n* feat(react-spa-webpack): wire OTLP log export opt-in (#504)\n\nAdds prompt_otel() and conditional_copy_otel() to ts_react_app.sh,\nmirroring ts_lib.sh''s version added by PR #505. On opt-in, copies\notel-log-emitter.ts (+ test) into src/shared/utils/, the OTel\ncollector docker-compose/config, patches package.json with the 5\npinned @opentelemetry/* deps, and appends the env fragment to both\n.env and .env.example (react-spa-webpack ships both, unlike ts-lib).\nNo webpack.config.js change needed - DefinePlugin already inlines\nevery .env key dynamically.\n\nVerified by scaffolding a real project with the prompt answered y:\nnpm ci is clean and every copied/patched artifact lands as coded.\ntsc --noEmit fails inside otel-log-emitter.ts itself (BatchLogRecord-\nProcessorOptions / Logger type mismatch against the pinned\n@opentelemetry/* versions) - pre-existing in ts-common''s shared file,\nreproducible identically for ts-lib (same tsconfig strictness), and\noutside this file''s scope; noted in the PR for follow-up.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(scaffold): guard the OTEL prompt on a tty, and actually wire it in\n\nread consumes piped stdin, so a non-interactive run holding a stray ''y''\nline enabled OTEL -- dependencies, env vars and a composition-root edit\nnobody asked for. With no terminal the answer is now the default.\n\nThe bigger one: conditional_copy_otel printed ''wrap your composition\nroot yourself'' and stopped. An enabled scaffold therefore exported\nnothing until a human edited application code -- dependencies installed,\nenv vars set, module present, no logs leaving the browser. An opt-in\nthat ships inert is worse than one that is absent, because everything\nvisible says it is on.\n\nwire_otel_composition_root now patches context.tsx via sed_inplace, and\ndegrades loudly rather than silently when the file is missing or does\nnot match the expected shape. Verified on a real copy of the template:\nimport added, new ConsoleNotifier(withOtelLogExport(CONSOLE_EMITTER));\nboth warning paths and the tty guard exercised.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"40fdb05a625ec0d90ff70b02136714bbab290470","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/40fdb05a625ec0d90ff70b02136714bbab290470"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f","verification":{"payload":"tree 40fdb05a625ec0d90ff70b02136714bbab290470\nparent 050525cc668bf13f15b15d337d0b085ed151d45c\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789813272 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789813272 +0000\n\nfeat(react-spa-webpack): wire OTLP log export opt-in (#504) (#519)\n\n* feat(react-spa-webpack): wire OTLP log export opt-in (#504)\n\nAdds prompt_otel() and conditional_copy_otel() to ts_react_app.sh,\nmirroring ts_lib.sh''s version added by PR #505. On opt-in, copies\notel-log-emitter.ts (+ test) into src/shared/utils/, the OTel\ncollector docker-compose/config, patches package.json with the 5\npinned @opentelemetry/* deps, and appends the env fragment to both\n.env and .env.example (react-spa-webpack ships both, unlike ts-lib).\nNo webpack.config.js change needed - DefinePlugin already inlines\nevery .env key dynamically.\n\nVerified by scaffolding a real project with the prompt answered y:\nnpm ci is clean and every copied/patched artifact lands as coded.\ntsc --noEmit fails inside otel-log-emitter.ts itself (BatchLogRecord-\nProcessorOptions / Logger type mismatch against the pinned\n@opentelemetry/* versions) - pre-existing in ts-common''s shared file,\nreproducible identically for ts-lib (same tsconfig strictness), and\noutside this file''s scope; noted in the PR for follow-up.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(scaffold): guard the OTEL prompt on a tty, and actually wire it in\n\nread consumes piped stdin, so a non-interactive run holding a stray ''y''\nline enabled OTEL -- dependencies, env vars and a composition-root edit\nnobody asked for. With no terminal the answer is now the default.\n\nThe bigger one: conditional_copy_otel printed ''wrap your composition\nroot yourself'' and stopped. An enabled scaffold therefore exported\nnothing until a human edited application code -- dependencies installed,\nenv vars set, module present, no logs leaving the browser. An opt-in\nthat ships inert is worse than one that is absent, because everything\nvisible says it is on.\n\nwire_otel_composition_root now patches context.tsx via sed_inplace, and\ndegrades loudly rather than silently when the file is missing or does\nnot match the expected shape. Verified on a real copy of the template:\nimport added, new ConsoleNotifier(withOtelLogExport(CONSOLE_EMITTER));\nboth warning paths and the tty guard exercised.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrmIYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqp8QADxoX1m1HkkU9KrTZAxYorFt\nAQA7P7Zzk8KX4d407iSnQkETuMoYow41ACrdBNb5YUO/iUG+IYrE3eNUxveoRJcG\nriqksekmz3QUQj1xevBBLMmEHyTRezkTk/2TsOgGaoD5+9LWnpE/W9RrK3Fd+jq+\nSBmdft/8qhZlLOuRWOwcyKPewZmP6a9qutIZWKRlMh/wY4RLGEFIvCflTvCyJW6f\nTSEDwJyVB+9lJbelgDPwftCqhXpnMvgAP9RFI8LHDDBe8Y410S/vPXjDzRJ+Sxn0\nl7wKkWikKp7iILK4sNiZ8Q3n4S0g1SU3spJbifWVz1AosAQR9oQdU3+7u9YyZkpx\n6nVU1sF9fEHJWz76K3Jk+bsfEgthuKXBpHJvjvS/ab0i4swlIsN51x+I3ocnzaBe\nkmTQTj1DCZLWwwmrjRvNHvol78kKm5TGo67OnY5WuRK3yJpytOW/RliIfHFF4wem\n7s+WWwZwPVfROfEP6GoXyerTDGLFs/a6az4TDYKTMnv+1dluHstKnr4oOoXcYnKh\nqhicwpEpzRcjpypX1s/4CjoDw/QY6Zb/fp+JgfVfpWTOT4+siage0ekIB1rGh6Z/\n3uyIhh6bmwNjG2WJfV+ERndjsoGMeJZQYlVq89IYKMLoCaG36PTm0J8WYJnV3UQw\n0HbzTY8DMqQFeLelH7f0\n=QGJ0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T10:21:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDNmMGE2NWQ0MDFhOGEyODYyYzk4ZjAwODc1MzYzYTYzZjFmNzE3M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/050525cc668bf13f15b15d337d0b085ed151d45c","sha":"050525cc668bf13f15b15d337d0b085ed151d45c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/050525cc668bf13f15b15d337d0b085ed151d45c"}],"sha":"3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/3f0a65d401a8a2862c98f00875363a63f1f7173f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/050525cc668bf13f15b15d337d0b085ed151d45c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:17:28Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T10:17:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(specs): a .specs/ root with its own CLAUDE.md, a structure guard, and the lessons mirrors (#517)\n\n* feat(specs): add .specs/CLAUDE.md\n\nDocuments the .specs/ convention (features/<name>/{design,plan}.md and\nthe git-ignored _lessons/ mirror) so future spec/plan output lands here\ninstead of docs/superpowers/. Part of blueprintx#447.\n\n* feat(specs): migrate docs/superpowers specs+plans into .specs/features/\n\nMoves all 10 pre-existing spec/plan docs from docs/superpowers/{specs,plans}/\ninto .specs/features/<name>/{design.md,plan.md}, following the new .specs/\nconvention (see .specs/CLAUDE.md). docs/superpowers/ is now empty; a later\ncommit drops its exclude_docs entry. Part of blueprintx#447.\n\n* chore(scaffold): pull in origin/main''s function-length fix (#486)\n\nCherry-picks the already-merged main() line-count fix for the 4\nbin/scaffold/python_*_service*.sh scripts into this branch so the\nwhole-repo function-length pre-commit hook can pass while adding the\n.specs/ structure guard below. No functional change vs origin/main.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* docs(backlog): track .specs/ directory organization (blueprintx#447)\n\nRecords what shipped in this PR and what''s deliberately deferred\n(mkdocs.yml exclude_docs + docs/CLAUDE.md cleanup, blocked on several\nother open PRs holding those files).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(ci): scan dot-prefixed specs entries, enforce the kebab-case rule\n\nBash does not expand * to dot-prefixed entries, so both directory scans\nwalked past a stray .specs/.notes and a hidden feature directory -- the\nscans reported clean on exactly the entries least expected to be there.\ndotglob plus nullglob before the loops.\n\nThe kebab-case rule was stated in .specs/CLAUDE.md and in this script''s\nown header, and never checked: .specs/features/447/ passed. A gate that\nnames a rule and does not enforce it is worse than one that never\nclaimed to.\n\nThe first pattern still accepted a bare 447, because [a-z0-9] includes\ndigits -- the exact case the check was added for. Caught by the fixture,\nnot by re-reading the regex. Verified: 447, Specs_Directory,\nmy--feature, -lead and trail- all rejected; a valid layout still passes.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c02ec53aff19c54a630d316edde457ae21e3c33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/9c02ec53aff19c54a630d316edde457ae21e3c33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/050525cc668bf13f15b15d337d0b085ed151d45c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c02ec53aff19c54a630d316edde457ae21e3c33\nparent 72647c30709151b50fb6d64025c89a88630d7436\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789813048 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789813048 +0000\n\nfeat(specs): a .specs/ root with its own CLAUDE.md, a structure guard, and the lessons mirrors (#517)\n\n* feat(specs): add .specs/CLAUDE.md\n\nDocuments the .specs/ convention (features/<name>/{design,plan}.md and\nthe git-ignored _lessons/ mirror) so future spec/plan output lands here\ninstead of docs/superpowers/. Part of blueprintx#447.\n\n* feat(specs): migrate docs/superpowers specs+plans into .specs/features/\n\nMoves all 10 pre-existing spec/plan docs from docs/superpowers/{specs,plans}/\ninto .specs/features/<name>/{design.md,plan.md}, following the new .specs/\nconvention (see .specs/CLAUDE.md). docs/superpowers/ is now empty; a later\ncommit drops its exclude_docs entry. Part of blueprintx#447.\n\n* chore(scaffold): pull in origin/main''s function-length fix (#486)\n\nCherry-picks the already-merged main() line-count fix for the 4\nbin/scaffold/python_*_service*.sh scripts into this branch so the\nwhole-repo function-length pre-commit hook can pass while adding the\n.specs/ structure guard below. No functional change vs origin/main.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* docs(backlog): track .specs/ directory organization (blueprintx#447)\n\nRecords what shipped in this PR and what''s deliberately deferred\n(mkdocs.yml exclude_docs + docs/CLAUDE.md cleanup, blocked on several\nother open PRs holding those files).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(ci): scan dot-prefixed specs entries, enforce the kebab-case rule\n\nBash does not expand * to dot-prefixed entries, so both directory scans\nwalked past a stray .specs/.notes and a hidden feature directory -- the\nscans reported clean on exactly the entries least expected to be there.\ndotglob plus nullglob before the loops.\n\nThe kebab-case rule was stated in .specs/CLAUDE.md and in this script''s\nown header, and never checked: .specs/features/447/ passed. A gate that\nnames a rule and does not enforce it is worse than one that never\nclaimed to.\n\nThe first pattern still accepted a bare 447, because [a-z0-9] includes\ndigits -- the exact case the check was added for. Caught by the fixture,\nnot by re-reading the regex. Verified: 447, Specs_Directory,\nmy--feature, -lead and trail- all rejected; a valid layout still passes.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7P96vZzPgCW7PdAjHZCPj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrmE4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzmIQAAstzgRmacI0BnuuPF8J/YAJ\nT10t/UsaG0vlBfMygto2rkHTamutEEOqJot0A3HwW7ws6CPnzXimKnxdU9kf1BrR\nymJ8tnHwRyjousgL6UwP7fYLPxzZF2xM89YrgFISvVnwh/BSCuOsSyLBDt9oVDa7\nxVL0TP42KkMZiFisDETd8Bt6PVA3e24SoWOfzWog127hTuUtZBDUnaM/j5T8ysQL\nhuy04D7IEWHug8bbSLMWxd401NIWDiASDVimRmIPC6UsRjAslRAbz2q3maGals6H\neftXCQ6sV+sNQBzduBiW6i/HfLG6ojaWEybTrG/gpaOY7chO9Cd189fOb4oVMuua\nGtODMcqOWQBpqNSVvuPACD5Ikw3IxoFecGwFAJMXviJieq0IxQB+/GJp6ZiIylyl\nluZyU0dSEX3yRyRDhTh1UlerUDcDlE5xC5RgvBWjxJ1z9llM5IQ1AjwFVWt9KsAs\nwqLL28q