,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/9a9859075faabcc747e38cd0ea21d8ffbf51c83b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T11:59:10Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T11:59:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): wire the coverage-floor gate into pre-commit + CI (#149) (#527)\n\n* feat(ci): wire the coverage-floor gate into pre-commit + CI (#149)\n\ncheck_coverage_floor.py and its test shipped in #404 but were never\ninvoked anywhere — no pre-commit hook, no CI step, so the gate was\ndead code enforcing nothing. Adds the coverage-floor pre-commit hook\nand a mirroring CI step, documents the gate in python-common''s own\nCLAUDE.md, and adds docs/coverage-floor.md as its design record.\n\n* docs(coverage-floor): exemption is capability-root, detection per file\n\nReview finding on #527, verified and correct: both documents understated\nwhat the gate catches.\n\n`docs/coverage-floor.md` claimed it \"does NOT catch a single mis-omitted\nfile inside a capability that already has narrower, legitimate\nexclusions\", and `templates/python-common/CLAUDE.md` compressed the same\nidea to \"deliberately coarse (capability root, not file-by-file)\".\n\nThe code says otherwise, and the two granularities are different:\n\n- EXEMPTION is capability-root and literal. whole_capability_exclusions()\n  reads back only non-glob whole-capability patterns, and\n  must_stay_covered() skips exactly those. A capability holding merely a\n  narrower exclusion is NOT exempt.\n- DETECTION is per module. swallowed_by_omit() then checks every\n  logic-bearing domain/application module of every non-exempt capability\n  against every omit pattern.\n\nMeasured against this PR''s head, with a capability carrying a legitimate\n`infrastructure/*` exclusion AND one mis-omitted domain module, the gate\nexits 1 and names src/capabilities/orders/domain/service.py as dropped\nout of the coverage floor''s denominator.\n\nSo the documented gap does not exist. What the gate genuinely does not do\nis assert file-by-file what SHOULD be covered — that is the fragile\nhand-maintained map it exists to avoid, and both documents now say that\ninstead.\n\nPinned by a named regression test rather than left as prose, since prose\nis what drifted. Full suite: 13 passed.\n\nA doc that understates a gate is not harmless — it invites someone to\nbuild a redundant second gate for coverage that already exists.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1b2edbf37b62e1825c644b776789cc3299dc0fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/d1b2edbf37b62e1825c644b776789cc3299dc0fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/9a9859075faabcc747e38cd0ea21d8ffbf51c83b","verification":{"payload":"tree d1b2edbf37b62e1825c644b776789cc3299dc0fd\nparent a450454fa613a345a90c230c933cf7db9432b58a\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789732750 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789732750 +0000\n\nfeat(ci): wire the coverage-floor gate into pre-commit + CI (#149) (#527)\n\n* feat(ci): wire the coverage-floor gate into pre-commit + CI (#149)\n\ncheck_coverage_floor.py and its test shipped in #404 but were never\ninvoked anywhere — no pre-commit hook, no CI step, so the gate was\ndead code enforcing nothing. Adds the coverage-floor pre-commit hook\nand a mirroring CI step, documents the gate in python-common''s own\nCLAUDE.md, and adds docs/coverage-floor.md as its design record.\n\n* docs(coverage-floor): exemption is capability-root, detection per file\n\nReview finding on #527, verified and correct: both documents understated\nwhat the gate catches.\n\n`docs/coverage-floor.md` claimed it \"does NOT catch a single mis-omitted\nfile inside a capability that already has narrower, legitimate\nexclusions\", and `templates/python-common/CLAUDE.md` compressed the same\nidea to \"deliberately coarse (capability root, not file-by-file)\".\n\nThe code says otherwise, and the two granularities are different:\n\n- EXEMPTION is capability-root and literal. whole_capability_exclusions()\n  reads back only non-glob whole-capability patterns, and\n  must_stay_covered() skips exactly those. A capability holding merely a\n  narrower exclusion is NOT exempt.\n- DETECTION is per module. swallowed_by_omit() then checks every\n  logic-bearing domain/application module of every non-exempt capability\n  against every omit pattern.\n\nMeasured against this PR''s head, with a capability carrying a legitimate\n`infrastructure/*` exclusion AND one mis-omitted domain module, the gate\nexits 1 and names src/capabilities/orders/domain/service.py as dropped\nout of the coverage floor''s denominator.\n\nSo the documented gap does not exist. What the gate genuinely does not do\nis assert file-by-file what SHOULD be covered — that is the fragile\nhand-maintained map it exists to avoid, and both documents now say that\ninstead.\n\nPinned by a named regression test rather than left as prose, since prose\nis what drifted. Full suite: 13 passed.\n\nA doc that understates a gate is not harmless — it invites someone to\nbuild a redundant second gate for coverage that already exists.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrSeOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3pEQAFWM/cP3qZJ0pkGrRCtkPE2z\nYz7gdqPIdc11lqZ4w0VGShJXfPNLYsGP6qMLXZ8IjcbSHsIRPtk+9aEmRZDDJX7r\nV36DUYvNtgP8mojmPWq9k4dBiwCzE2gzeHNJu3fv72zzLr2ltlf+N374QPreqaJ0\nYvHoEURXz87tabSzg6+fsUP0BlIl6spYeYBKJyumHTgXpwveTIUxh1fbDN0R0u+l\nWeIAp+AXKOmuE4q4C252a5rS5EbKxZazoORF9iriAjzuFBHlTgtCC7PQPTpcnI3Y\nvVZHTBhfjUgBqvU0Hq99dWKKygf6J+znyiqfncTwnHnlGFpoWbt5uRFJoPXu3GpH\ngGs8Jjt/8NnLsN8Le9OjG4Hit3sHzy1oE4CFCvo6qy+1S8jU6Bm1KzDqRjsZIeR2\nPqq9odgmjgGlRczh2fFKYIZGkJRcZdDShn29WTs1CoVNRbS3ko5v7nLXao4+i2ke\nHULkbOuPBDBh456VTD36GtJmdHrY81prj45ZDfF9lajqAdWwJtz68yUhOXCGrc6C\n3bw8L9ucbqvtjWFoux/J7mj9Vt0sqz6MS34hlWJDoRVETK1kXiGMD4GCxQ/yrkDp\nDJVNtvb9/8cpnTdgpXyiaTLyzNLxlNx16rvWtxc95GDAqakV1RM9GBYd7cQyBp/i\nyyF0stC9cpafylFmcfe6\n=RqSE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T11:59:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/9a9859075faabcc747e38cd0ea21d8ffbf51c83b","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDlhOTg1OTA3NWZhYWJjYzc0N2UzOGNkMGVhMjFkOGZmYmY1MWM4M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/a450454fa613a345a90c230c933cf7db9432b58a","sha":"a450454fa613a345a90c230c933cf7db9432b58a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/a450454fa613a345a90c230c933cf7db9432b58a"}],"sha":"9a9859075faabcc747e38cd0ea21d8ffbf51c83b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/9a9859075faabcc747e38cd0ea21d8ffbf51c83b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/a450454fa613a345a90c230c933cf7db9432b58a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:45:15Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:45:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(templates): ship secret_scan.yaml as opt-in (#287) (#523)\n\n* feat(templates): ship secret_scan.yaml as opt-in (#287)\n\nGITGUARDIAN_API_KEY presence at scaffold time is now the opt-in signal:\ncopy_github_assets only ships secret_scan.yaml when the variable is set,\nand scaffold_set_secret_scan_key (new, in scaffold_git_remote.sh) then\npropagates the key to the new repo''s secrets, mirroring how\nGH_PAT_REVIEW_TRIGGER already opts a project into coderabbit_trigger.yaml.\n\nA project that never exports the variable never receives the workflow at\nall, closing blueprintx#287''s \"ship by default vs. opt-in\" decision in\nfavor of opt-in. Updates the workflow''s own header comment and\nenable_security.sh''s cross-reference to match, and adds\ndocs/secret-scanning.md as the full walkthrough (opt-in, key propagation,\nmanual opt-in after the fact, the fail-loud contract, offline exclusion),\nregistered in mkdocs.yml nav and docs/CLAUDE.md''s file index per this\ndirectory''s own rule.\n\n* fix(scaffold): gate secret_scan.yaml copy on GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY (#287)\n\nColliding hunk, isolated to its own commit: wraps the existing\nsecret_scan.yaml cp line in each of the five python_*.sh scaffold\nscripts (copy_github_assets / lib_minimal_copy_github_assets) in an\n`if [ -n \"${GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY:-}\" ]` guard, so the workflow is only\ncopied when the key was exported at scaffold time. No other line in\nthese files is touched. These scripts are held by open PRs #503/#509;\nflagging this hunk for their authors to rebase past.\n\n* fix(secret-scan): withdraw the opt-in when the key cannot be set\n\nTwo review findings on this PR, both real, both in\nscaffold_set_secret_scan_key.\n\n1. Stability. GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY''s presence IS the opt-in signal, so\n   each scaffold''s copy_github_assets ships secret_scan.yaml whenever it\n   is non-empty. But this function returned 0 when `gh` was unavailable\n   and merely warned when `gh secret set` failed — leaving the variable\n   set in both cases. The project then received a workflow with no\n   secret behind it, and ggshield exits 3 on its first non-bot scan: a\n   failing gate nobody opted into.\n\n   Now the variable is unset at this single boundary whenever the key\n   cannot be propagated. The function runs before\n   finalize_github_or_offline, so every scaffold''s copy step sees the\n   withdrawn opt-in without the check being repeated in each of them.\n\n2. Sensitive data exposure (CWE-200). `--body \"$GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY\"`\n   put the key in gh''s process arguments, readable by any same-host\n   process for the life of the call. Piping via `printf ''%s'' | ` keeps\n   it out of argv AND appends no newline, so it also preserves the\n   trailing-newline property the old `--body, never a redirect` comment\n   was protecting — the redirect was the hazard, not stdin itself.\n\nAlso fixed the same pattern in docs/secret-scanning.md, which told\nreaders to pass `--body ''<your key>''` by hand; `gh` prompts when neither\n--body nor stdin supplies a value, and an argument additionally lands in\nshell history.\n\nVerified: bash -n and shellcheck -S warning clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d964814ecf1590bdf033c3557ba4c7662053fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/7d964814ecf1590bdf033c3557ba4c7662053fc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/a450454fa613a345a90c230c933cf7db9432b58a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d964814ecf1590bdf033c3557ba4c7662053fc1\nparent 7be7352bae23619e9570531e94c478e44b3d22b7\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789728315 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789728315 +0000\n\nfeat(templates): ship secret_scan.yaml as opt-in (#287) (#523)\n\n* feat(templates): ship secret_scan.yaml as opt-in (#287)\n\nGITGUARDIAN_API_KEY presence at scaffold time is now the opt-in signal:\ncopy_github_assets only ships secret_scan.yaml when the variable is set,\nand scaffold_set_secret_scan_key (new, in scaffold_git_remote.sh) then\npropagates the key to the new repo''s secrets, mirroring how\nGH_PAT_REVIEW_TRIGGER already opts a project into coderabbit_trigger.yaml.\n\nA project that never exports the variable never receives the workflow at\nall, closing blueprintx#287''s \"ship by default vs. opt-in\" decision in\nfavor of opt-in. Updates the workflow''s own header comment and\nenable_security.sh''s cross-reference to match, and adds\ndocs/secret-scanning.md as the full walkthrough (opt-in, key propagation,\nmanual opt-in after the fact, the fail-loud contract, offline exclusion),\nregistered in mkdocs.yml nav and docs/CLAUDE.md''s file index per this\ndirectory''s own rule.\n\n* fix(scaffold): gate secret_scan.yaml copy on GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY (#287)\n\nColliding hunk, isolated to its own commit: wraps the existing\nsecret_scan.yaml cp line in each of the five python_*.sh scaffold\nscripts (copy_github_assets / lib_minimal_copy_github_assets) in an\n`if [ -n \"${GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY:-}\" ]` guard, so the workflow is only\ncopied when the key was exported at scaffold time. No other line in\nthese files is touched. These scripts are held by open PRs #503/#509;\nflagging this hunk for their authors to rebase past.\n\n* fix(secret-scan): withdraw the opt-in when the key cannot be set\n\nTwo review findings on this PR, both real, both in\nscaffold_set_secret_scan_key.\n\n1. Stability. GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY''s presence IS the opt-in signal, so\n   each scaffold''s copy_github_assets ships secret_scan.yaml whenever it\n   is non-empty. But this function returned 0 when `gh` was unavailable\n   and merely warned when `gh secret set` failed — leaving the variable\n   set in both cases. The project then received a workflow with no\n   secret behind it, and ggshield exits 3 on its first non-bot scan: a\n   failing gate nobody opted into.\n\n   Now the variable is unset at this single boundary whenever the key\n   cannot be propagated. The function runs before\n   finalize_github_or_offline, so every scaffold''s copy step sees the\n   withdrawn opt-in without the check being repeated in each of them.\n\n2. Sensitive data exposure (CWE-200). `--body \"$GITGUARDIAN_API_KEY\"`\n   put the key in gh''s process arguments, readable by any same-host\n   process for the life of the call. Piping via `printf ''%s'' | ` keeps\n   it out of argv AND appends no newline, so it also preserves the\n   trailing-newline property the old `--body, never a redirect` comment\n   was protecting — the redirect was the hazard, not stdin itself.\n\nAlso fixed the same pattern in docs/secret-scanning.md, which told\nreaders to pass `--body ''<your key>''` by hand; `gh` prompts when neither\n--body nor stdin supplies a value, and an argument additionally lands in\nshell history.\n\nVerified: bash -n and shellcheck -S warning clean.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrRY7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR1IQAF3ow6IgllFAU4WSBLvORF1H\nje27c8gAkEtCJuFz4umFaz3dNOTZx1ErhXn0ia+Jbys9h9qE/ELwQR56Z1ynZd1i\nFYj4JSUIQzK3vVjJvl7UPiAqsf5ssCnxCBNHGe2Aw3u2IUU2P5ttyNBzpzPs0XnW\nqwGjyo9Xvr7ITq02pCJnVchDZ0Uz55Ex9BRh7zQHGW0qqrEl5qp6sC5O97VeqBMz\nt05EmhrECJP+pMP2IVAHMjWBb74ZKpW0FoQddBrRGJb+w71PoTvUXr6ERx6TmFYV\n5k4IbtDBYIL40bh5qXkYPYVTeJCHD929yzKcYB94dFZCuDlT4qv38na+DOFUhPYI\nASYLuW90R6e2K020V5yRYlilDGV5gh9BrpyfBnfdTofcNmh/mix6+I7eLRZQYm+6\nDfxw4Cm8KlUVQ7CnHpNFSEHGASmBiDbssf1csjzT+753crWgzfKnHja20EVbNASI\n09rQj3bIFsRAhHl1GWMDYvezCOfm0XTVDoDOWfYJpPsjQaAMRiOWTBUa+m1FHmcm\n1Uo52RvE2+gcCmhChW34Bvz0IKUa4wxfXBsJWZGYRGtWBLywcOago+zcprI4CGDz\np050ef0DWF6KqKRB7Je/MWswYvSBBAjRsftKvrnxgDCTQmpULfNoPot6XtV56UVv\nx/Slh9