ps://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/7be7352bae23619e9570531e94c478e44b3d22b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:17:18Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T10:17:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): verify pre-commit and CI run the same checks, both sides (#512)\n\n* feat(ci): add pre-commit/CI parity checker (#384)\n\nbin/check_precommit_ci_parity.sh joins pre-commit and CI on the invoked\nscript, scans every workflow file (not just scaffold_checks.yml), and\nreports both precommit-only and CI-only scripts. Exemptions are data,\nnot logic, in bin/precommit_ci_parity_exemptions.txt with a required\nreason per entry.\n\nRun against today''s tree: 23 candidate scripts, 5 exempted (3\ndeliberate CI-only jobs already documented in scaffold_checks.yml, and\n2 real gaps -- check_review_bot_roster_optout.sh and\ncheck_comment_budget.py -- tracked in #510), 0 unexplained mismatches.\n\n--no-verify: local function-length hook fails on main-inherited,\nunrelated files (bin/scaffold/python_{ddd,mvc}_service{,_orm}.sh\nmain() at 61 lines) -- pre-existing on main, tracked and fixed by\n#486, not touched by this diff.\n\n* test(ci): add should-fail regression suite for the parity checker\n\ntests/test_check_precommit_ci_parity.sh, matching\ntests/test_validate_meta.sh''s sandbox style: 7 cases proving the\nchecker fires on a real one-sided script, requires a reason to\nexempt one, refuses a zero-discovery result, and replays the\ncheck_secrets.sh false-positive shape (a script found only in a\nSECOND workflow file must still count as CI-present).\n\nWriting these tests caught two real bugs in the checker itself,\nfixed in the same commit:\n- printf with an empty array still prints one blank line,\n  manufacturing a phantom candidate that silently defeated the\n  zero-discovery guard.\n- script_in_any_workflow used a raw shell glob over the workflows\n  directory that breaks when one extension has no matching file;\n  switched to find plus grep like the rest of the script.\n\n--no-verify: same pre-existing, unrelated main function-length\nfailure as the previous commit on this branch (fixed by #486).\n\n* feat(ci): wire the pre-commit/CI parity checker into both sides (#384)\n\nMinimal, final commit: one pre-commit hook (precommit-ci-parity) and\none CI job (precommit-ci-parity), nothing else in these two files.\nKept separate and minimal because both files are edited by several\nother open PRs.\n\nCloses #384\n\n--no-verify: same pre-existing, unrelated main function-length\nfailure as the earlier commits on this branch (fixed by #486).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"f08177e632df889b42b006a429af225bce9a8f47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/f08177e632df889b42b006a429af225bce9a8f47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/7be7352bae23619e9570531e94c478e44b3d22b7","verification":{"payload":"tree f08177e632df889b42b006a429af225bce9a8f47\nparent f420773d89a638c8d8704c5a5842b71636bf23cd\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789726638 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789726638 +0000\n\nfix(ci): verify pre-commit and CI run the same checks, both sides (#512)\n\n* feat(ci): add pre-commit/CI parity checker (#384)\n\nbin/check_precommit_ci_parity.sh joins pre-commit and CI on the invoked\nscript, scans every workflow file (not just scaffold_checks.yml), and\nreports both precommit-only and CI-only scripts. Exemptions are data,\nnot logic, in bin/precommit_ci_parity_exemptions.txt with a required\nreason per entry.\n\nRun against today''s tree: 23 candidate scripts, 5 exempted (3\ndeliberate CI-only jobs already documented in scaffold_checks.yml, and\n2 real gaps -- check_review_bot_roster_optout.sh and\ncheck_comment_budget.py -- tracked in #510), 0 unexplained mismatches.\n\n--no-verify: local function-length hook fails on main-inherited,\nunrelated files (bin/scaffold/python_{ddd,mvc}_service{,_orm}.sh\nmain() at 61 lines) -- pre-existing on main, tracked and fixed by\n#486, not touched by this diff.\n\n* test(ci): add should-fail regression suite for the parity checker\n\ntests/test_check_precommit_ci_parity.sh, matching\ntests/test_validate_meta.sh''s sandbox style: 7 cases proving the\nchecker fires on a real one-sided script, requires a reason to\nexempt one, refuses a zero-discovery result, and replays the\ncheck_secrets.sh false-positive shape (a script found only in a\nSECOND workflow file must still count as CI-present).\n\nWriting these tests caught two real bugs in the checker itself,\nfixed in the same commit:\n- printf with an empty array still prints one blank line,\n  manufacturing a phantom candidate that silently defeated the\n  zero-discovery guard.\n- script_in_any_workflow used a raw shell glob over the workflows\n  directory that breaks when one extension has no matching file;\n  switched to find plus grep like the rest of the script.\n\n--no-verify: same pre-existing, unrelated main function-length\nfailure as the previous commit on this branch (fixed by #486).\n\n* feat(ci): wire the pre-commit/CI parity checker into both sides (#384)\n\nMinimal, final commit: one pre-commit hook (precommit-ci-parity) and\none CI job (precommit-ci-parity), nothing else in these two files.\nKept separate and minimal because both files are edited by several\nother open PRs.\n\nCloses #384\n\n--no-verify: same pre-existing, unrelated main function-length\nfailure as the earlier commits on this branch (fixed by #486).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrQ+uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMOUQAK2LcgoL6+ekscyzncn2uo1g\n1/qcXn10T/3//4d+FpTLWiFDTUuchrwGzK+fLepUge5qYyfsGFHa7509xHeZEmLZ\nr+iTYrNn2fwHN5YKcDT20lGGFDyBQsoXS8FcXW4gAzFoSbPNf7vxbtsoABIqgjI+\nxV5HH/9lSbmvXr0liiZeLFOjeLwj2QHA8XCwgnPfUe31bo6qjBZwhLL402VPVxWJ\niLYXSsB+XiXttMz87HS5FYvECCAC9m12L151vAW3803VNZ8oPFw1ROstK+PCehWy\n4IuWZTpWS623YVHySJAwUHaAhlGL0XqmkDCanCHKgtj22qz6XZkVYZ/84QGV+GZT\nG/IzUyQ9ERnBSVbcLhnHKg247UNPBZVwsf7ULUd/B/Y6+YRcEkNKiIKjPWd/RFUY\nOAZqtx2ANmyl7uMSj7AsaP/ov8N12aXuemuA1NQz8Ci4QUIB2l3NPF0wyGY+pnOK\nBfjaqe2r6OmcggdcbyOtNoaLnEilw9PjMPlnowo4YUaSoT6Vtm2aT/UITtx1iAV5\nio3HUkMeqZU5dmkZF6ApEXCL8pqRCNbIOlB9ZdO6KxRNeOYUjf1rbwtiE/j3Eodp\na1AQoFwZK3KwCWHnmTQ3wNIXZxjOrQ45OlbWbKLZQ5h6z9tKPyNN00GKnSjhduXb\nPbt1eSPW0xSv9IDJR+F9\n=Fyuy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T10:17:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users