ns_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/f420773d89a638c8d8704c5a5842b71636bf23cd","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKGY0MjA3NzNkODlhNjM4YzhkODcwNGM1YTU4NDJiNzE2MzZiZjIzY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/9ea2bf262c5899afdf97af1a6aa9c704d86e39ed","sha":"9ea2bf262c5899afdf97af1a6aa9c704d86e39ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/9ea2bf262c5899afdf97af1a6aa9c704d86e39ed"}],"sha":"f420773d89a638c8d8704c5a5842b71636bf23cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/f420773d89a638c8d8704c5a5842b71636bf23cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/9ea2bf262c5899afdf97af1a6aa9c704d86e39ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T00:46:52Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T00:46:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): declare issue file surface, enforce it at PR time (#520)\n\n* feat(ci): declare issue file surface, enforce it at PR time\n\nAdds bin/ci/check_issue_scope.py + .github/workflows/issue_scope.yml:\nan issue declares its expected file surface as a fenced ```surface```\nblock in its body, and the PR-time gate checks that the PR''s changed\nfiles (via closingIssuesReferences) stay inside the declared union.\n\nReplaces the hand-written collision map every dispatched agent used\nto get, reconstructed from memory and never checked, which already\nfailed once (dotfiles-dev#162: two worktree agents collided, one\nagent''s files wiped, an empty commit reported success).\n\nDesign in docs/issue-scope.md: fenced block over a scope:* label (no\ntaxonomy file to maintain, opt-in per issue instead of a 40-issue\nbackfill), one gh pr view call for files+closingIssuesReferences+\ncommits plus one REST call per linked issue (quota was exhausted 3x\ntoday by chattier checks), payable strictness (undeclared surface\nwarns, does not block), surface-override: commit trailer for a PR\nthat must legitimately widen its surface, and UNKNOWN — never a\nsilent pass — when the API is unreadable.\n\nCloses #314\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* test(ci): should-fail regression suite for check_issue_scope.py\n\nFake gh binary on PATH, 6 cases: no linked issue, files within a\ndeclared surface, a file outside it with no override (must fail and\nname the file), the same with a surface-override: trailer (must\npass), a linked issue with no declared surface (must warn, not\nblock), and gh itself failing (must report UNKNOWN, never a silent\npass).\n\nRefs #314\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(ci): answer three review findings on the issue-scope gate\n\n1. An empty or comment-only surface fence was read as a declaration of NOTHING,\n   so every changed file fell outside it and the PR failed. That is the opposite\n   of the documented non-blocking behaviour for an undeclared surface, and it is\n   the exact shape the issue template shipped. Now UNDECLARED. The template''s\n   placeholder is commented out so a templated issue declares nothing until the\n   author writes a real pattern. Measured against the pre-fix code: the\n   template-shaped issue FAILS; with the fix it passes. Both are tests.\n\n2. The job ran the gate from the PR''s own merge-ref checkout, so a PR could\n   rewrite check_issue_scope.py and judge itself. It now checks out\n   pull_request.base.sha, applying the rule already on the base branch.\n\n3. An issue edited after the job passed left a green status describing an older\n   declaration; no pull_request event fires for an issue edit. A second job now\n   runs on issues:[edited], re-checks every OPEN PR whose\n   closingIssuesReferences name that issue, and posts its verdict as a commit\n   status under its own context. The context is deliberately distinct from the\n   PR job''s check name: a status and a check run sharing one name is ambiguous\n   for branch protection.\n\nVerified: bash tests/test_check_issue_scope.sh green, and red when the fix in\n(1) is reverted; bin/ci/check_actions.sh OK over 38 workflows, 76 bounded jobs;\nshellcheck clean on the new script.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3b63e2612c12476fe8641bc84877fbe456d8fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/c3b63e2612c12476fe8641bc84877fbe456d8fa0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/9ea2bf262c5899afdf97af1a6aa9c704d86e39ed","verification":{"payload":"tree c3b63e2612c12476fe8641bc84877fbe456d8fa0\nparent 1a17a8b9ba33017216f6983185c939f834b88e82\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789692412 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789692412 +0000\n\nfeat(ci): declare issue file surface, enforce it at PR time (#520)\n\n* feat(ci): declare issue file surface, enforce it at PR time\n\nAdds bin/ci/check_issue_scope.py + .github/workflows/issue_scope.yml:\nan issue declares its expected file surface as a fenced ```surface```\nblock in its body, and the PR-time gate checks that the PR''s changed\nfiles (via closingIssuesReferences) stay inside the declared union.\n\nReplaces the hand-written collision map every dispatched agent used\nto get, reconstructed from memory and never checked, which already\nfailed once (dotfiles-dev#162: two worktree agents collided, one\nagent''s files wiped, an empty commit reported success).\n\nDesign in docs/issue-scope.md: fenced block over a scope:* label (no\ntaxonomy file to maintain, opt-in per issue instead of a 40-issue\nbackfill), one gh pr view call for files+closingIssuesReferences+\ncommits plus one REST call per linked issue (quota was exhausted 3x\ntoday by chattier checks), payable strictness (undeclared surface\nwarns, does not block), surface-override: commit trailer for a PR\nthat must legitimately widen its surface, and UNKNOWN — never a\nsilent pass — when the API is unreadable.\n\nCloses #314\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* test(ci): should-fail regression suite for check_issue_scope.py\n\nFake gh binary on PATH, 6 cases: no linked issue, files within a\ndeclared surface, a file outside it with no override (must fail and\nname the file), the same with a surface-override: trailer (must\npass), a linked issue with no declared surface (must warn, not\nblock), and gh itself failing (must report UNKNOWN, never a silent\npass).\n\nRefs #314\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(ci): answer three review findings on the issue-scope gate\n\n1. An empty or comment-only surface fence was read as a declaration of NOTHING,\n   so every changed file fell outside it and the PR failed. That is the opposite\n   of the documented non-blocking behaviour for an undeclared surface, and it is\n   the exact shape the issue template shipped. Now UNDECLARED. The template''s\n   placeholder is commented out so a templated issue declares nothing until the\n   author writes a real pattern. Measured against the pre-fix code: the\n   template-shaped issue FAILS; with the fix it passes. Both are tests.\n\n2. The job ran the gate from the PR''s own merge-ref checkout, so a PR could\n   rewrite check_issue_scope.py and judge itself. It now checks out\n   pull_request.base.sha, applying the rule already on the base branch.\n\n3. An issue edited after the job passed left a green status describing an older\n   declaration; no pull_request event fires for an issue edit. A second job now\n   runs on issues:[edited], re-checks every OPEN PR whose\n   closingIssuesReferences name that issue, and posts its verdict as a commit\n   status under its own context. The context is deliberately distinct from the\n   PR job''s check name: a status and a check run sharing one name is ambiguous\n   for branch protection.\n\nVerified: bash tests/test_check_issue_scope.sh green, and red when the fix in\n(1) is reverted; bin/ci/check_actions.sh OK over 38 workflows, 76 bounded jobs;\nshellcheck clean on the new script.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrIn8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnv8QAIGiW2eEuB34ts450Gie4ldm\nMoeG9wNV+mNdvAfJPMmSANH+e33J6pzNqHe+RxaVSNv4mxgKBg91akOC+2IyaAsm\nMcycY3AfK38gTHlZ+m4bpG21GgMw/hA074XkJU4UQPA7ZTGRme2uyovXd/g+GBLC\n+Jpdc1a1eD2NJSeYp52U7ef5fgKO4C91Rq4eea2p9qFTQjrsgNABTyDVRciXe7T6\nKiplbnm+FvQl7RbojlKbASnwnbP1L3xYaEGvysFjaCmMXS6VnafG4sAGc7jWL+B4\nKPAbBa7XQpoB3ZAk2ZNOzj4AwpQoF6+HwzQldHrewvvFt/v1o/ws990nwwGYJvAk\n8GiFP9r4lf688TW+L3wDsoBzDlIQ+OLFMjDap+SJ9Wy1Hl8uZA1NfvuwkROZfFfa\nrjkUdaxkCe2SP