55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/1a17a8b9ba33017216f6983185c939f834b88e82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T23:58:39Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T23:58:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): identifier-masking gate for #355 (unnormalised CPF/CNPJ) (#509)\n\n* chore(scaffold): wire test_identifier_masking_gate.py copy lists\n\nWires the new gate''s test into both scaffold-tier test copy lists\n(bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh for the four service tiers,\nbin/scaffold/python_lib_minimal.sh for lib-minimal) ahead of the\ngate itself, so check_test_copy_lists.py never sees an unreachable\nshared test. Isolated because both files are also touched by open\nPRs #502/#319/#316 - kept minimal to reduce rebase conflict surface.\n\nSKIP=function-length: main already fails this hook on 4 pre-existing\nscaffold main() functions (bin/scaffold/python_{ddd,mvc}*service*.sh)\nunrelated to this diff, tracked by #486.\n\n* feat(ci): identifier-masking gate for blueprintx#355\n\nAdds check_identifier_masking.py, a structural gate flagging a\nmasked CPF/CNPJ literal compared directly in SQL text or an ORM\ncomparison/keyword - a masked value never equals the unmasked\nvalue stored in the column, so the query silently matches zero\nrows and raises nothing.\n\nThis covers only the \"unnormalised formatted values\" slice of\n#355. WHERE-less DELETE/UPDATE and WITH (NOLOCK) are already\nshipped on main via check_sql_guards.py (PR #403); that gate''s own\ndocstring explicitly excludes CPF/CNPJ normalisation as its own\nrule with its own false-positive shape, per the issue''s \"ship one\nper PR\" instruction.\n\nScope deliberately narrow per the issue''s own warning against\nbuilding a maintainer-needed registry first: CPF and CNPJ only,\nthe two identifiers br_identifiers.py ships unmask_* helpers for.\nCNH, SELECT *, DDL-in-app-code and float-for-money remain out of\nscope, same as the sibling gate.\n\n13 unit tests: dangerous form fails naming file/line/value/hatch,\nsafe form (unmask_cpf/digits-only) passes, false positives (masked\nvalue vs unrelated column) stay clean, both escape-hatch\ndirections, and the zero-discovery guard.\n\n* fix(gates): scan a SQL-only src tree instead of failing it\n\nThe discovery guard checked only list_py, so a tree holding just .sql files\nreported ''checked NOTHING'' and exited 1 while every file in it was scannable.\nMeasured on the pre-fix file: a compliant src/query.sql exits 1; with the fix\nit exits 0, and a masked comparison in the same tree still exits 1. Both are\nnow tests. The guard still fires when BOTH lists are empty, the case it\nexists for.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(gates): wire identifier masking into the enforced lint paths\n\nThe gate shipped but ran nowhere: no entry in bin/lint.sh, no pre-commit hook\nand no CI step, so poe lint omitted it entirely. A gate nobody runs is the\nfailure this repo writes gates to prevent. Added to all three, mirroring the\nsibling gates: files \\.(py|sql)$ with pass_filenames false, since the gate\ndoes its own discovery and must fail when it finds nothing.\n\nVerified with bin/ci/check_actions.sh: 37 workflows, job timeouts OK.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"d351d323155aeba5b96b8758ab34d7532b4902da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/d351d323155aeba5b96b8758ab34d7532b4902da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/1a17a8b9ba33017216f6983185c939f834b88e82","verification":{"payload":"tree d351d323155aeba5b96b8758ab34d7532b4902da\nparent 19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789689519 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789689519 +0000\n\nfeat(ci): identifier-masking gate for #355 (unnormalised CPF/CNPJ) (#509)\n\n* chore(scaffold): wire test_identifier_masking_gate.py copy lists\n\nWires the new gate''s test into both scaffold-tier test copy lists\n(bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh for the four service tiers,\nbin/scaffold/python_lib_minimal.sh for lib-minimal) ahead of the\ngate itself, so check_test_copy_lists.py never sees an unreachable\nshared test. Isolated because both files are also touched by open\nPRs #502/#319/#316 - kept minimal to reduce rebase conflict surface.\n\nSKIP=function-length: main already fails this hook on 4 pre-existing\nscaffold main() functions (bin/scaffold/python_{ddd,mvc}*service*.sh)\nunrelated to this diff, tracked by #486.\n\n* feat(ci): identifier-masking gate for blueprintx#355\n\nAdds check_identifier_masking.py, a structural gate flagging a\nmasked CPF/CNPJ literal compared directly in SQL text or an ORM\ncomparison/keyword - a masked value never equals the unmasked\nvalue stored in the column, so the query silently matches zero\nrows and raises nothing.\n\nThis covers only the \"unnormalised formatted values\" slice of\n#355. WHERE-less DELETE/UPDATE and WITH (NOLOCK) are already\nshipped on main via check_sql_guards.py (PR #403); that gate''s own\ndocstring explicitly excludes CPF/CNPJ normalisation as its own\nrule with its own false-positive shape, per the issue''s \"ship one\nper PR\" instruction.\n\nScope deliberately narrow per the issue''s own warning against\nbuilding a maintainer-needed registry first: CPF and CNPJ only,\nthe two identifiers br_identifiers.py ships unmask_* helpers for.\nCNH, SELECT *, DDL-in-app-code and float-for-money remain out of\nscope, same as the sibling gate.\n\n13 unit tests: dangerous form fails naming file/line/value/hatch,\nsafe form (unmask_cpf/digits-only) passes, false positives (masked\nvalue vs unrelated column) stay clean, both escape-hatch\ndirections, and the zero-discovery guard.\n\n* fix(gates): scan a SQL-only src tree instead of failing it\n\nThe discovery guard checked only list_py, so a tree holding just .sql files\nreported ''checked NOTHING'' and exited 1 while every file in it was scannable.\nMeasured on the pre-fix file: a compliant src/query.sql exits 1; with the fix\nit exits 0, and a masked comparison in the same tree still exits 1. Both are\nnow tests. The guard still fires when BOTH lists are empty, the case it\nexists for.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n* fix(gates): wire identifier masking into the enforced lint paths\n\nThe gate shipped but ran nowhere: no entry in bin/lint.sh, no pre-commit hook\nand no CI step, so poe lint omitted it entirely. A gate nobody runs is the\nfailure this repo writes gates to prevent. Added to all three, mirroring the\nsibling gates: files \\.(py|sql)$ with pass_filenames false, since the gate\ndoes its own discovery and must fail when it finds nothing.\n\nVerified 