com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/1a17a8b9ba33017216f6983185c939f834b88e82","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDFhMTdhOGI5YmEzMzAxNzIxNmY2OTgzMTg1YzkzOWY4MzRiODhlODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903","sha":"19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903"}],"sha":"1a17a8b9ba33017216f6983185c939f834b88e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/1a17a8b9ba33017216f6983185c939f834b88e82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:32:53Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:32:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ruff): adopt pep8-naming (N) minus N802 in tests (#486)\n\n* fix(scaffold): main() back under the 60-line function-length ceiling\n\nThe four service scaffolds'' main() sat at 61 lines (one over\ncheck_function_length.py''s ceiling), blocking every commit''s\npre-commit run repo-wide regardless of what changed. Extract the\nGitHub-remote-vs-offline-mode branch into finalize_github_or_offline,\nmatching the file''s existing named-helper style; no behaviour change.\n\n* feat(ruff): adopt pep8-naming (N) minus N802 in tests\n\nRe-measured (ruff 0.11.13): 9 findings across N802/N806/N813 in\nsrc/ bin/ tests/ optional/. N802 (5) is a false-positive family, every\none a test name using upper-case for deliberate semantic emphasis\n(tests/CLAUDE.md), so it is ignored only in tests/**. N806 (3) is a\nreal finding shape (a local ALL-CAPS constant inside a function) and\nis fixed by hoisting each to module scope. N813 (1) is a deliberate\ndefusedxml alias, kept via a targeted per-file-ignore. Case-by-case\ndetail lands in CONTRIBUTING.md''s Ruff Rule Adoption Log.\n\nCloses #422\n\n* docs(contributing): record the pep8-naming (N) adoption rationale\n\nDocuments why N is adopted with two per-file-ignores rather than whole:\n\n- N802 (5 findings) ignored in tests/** only — every one is a test name\n  using upper-case for semantic emphasis on the behaviour under test,\n  which is what tests/CLAUDE.md asks a test name to describe.\n- N806 (3 findings) fixed, not ignored — local _ALL_CAPS constants\n  hoisted to module scope, which is the PEP-8 rule seen from the other\n  side.\n- N813 (1 finding) kept via a per-file-ignore — the lowercase\n  defused_et alias is deliberate and reads as \"the defused one\" at\n  every call site.\n\nAlso fills the casing row in the cross-language parity table: no\nlike-for-like TS gap, because a JS/TS test name is a string literal\npassed to it()/describe(), not a function identifier.\n\nRefs #422\n\n* docs(contributing): date the re-measured parity row, not the table\n\nThe casing row was measured 2026-09-13; every other row still dates from\nthe 2026-09-06 snapshot in the heading. Bumping the heading would assert\na whole-table re-measurement that never happened, so the row carries its\nown date instead, and the staleness note now says which date governs\nwhat.\n\n* fix(ruff): mirror the N813 exemption for lib-minimal''s layout\n\nper-file-ignores keys are path-relative, and lib-minimal re-roots src/utils/\nunder src/<pkg>/_internal/utils/. The N813 entry added for xml_reader.py\nmatched only the template layout, so ''Scaffold + lint + test — lib-minimal''\nwas the one tier that went red. Two sibling entries (tabular_reader,\nconfig/contracts) already carry the same mirror; this one was missing it.\n\nVerified with bin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh lib-minimal: scaffolds clean,\nlints clean, 85 tests pass.\n\n* chore(ruff): record why pep8-naming adds per-file-ignores\n\nThe PR-body justification was overwritten when the reviewer bot\nregenerated the description, so gate integrity kept failing. A commit\ntrailer survives. Exemptions: N802 in tests (5 mixed-case behaviour\nnames) and N813 on the deliberate defusedxml alias in xml_reader.py,\ntemplate and lib-minimal layouts. N was not enabled before this PR.\n\ngate-change-ok: pep8-naming adoption, 3 measured exemptions (see body)\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"df566ae9dcad9a101597c47be905ec4922210075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/df566ae9dcad9a101597c47be905ec4922210075"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903","verification":{"payload":"tree df566ae9dcad9a101597c47be905ec4922210075\nparent d9a4d27aaf011ea82e97f5c3030a87d9205b67f3\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789659173 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789659173 +0000\n\nfeat(ruff): adopt pep8-naming (N) minus N802 in tests (#486)\n\n* fix(scaffold): main() back under the 60-line function-length ceiling\n\nThe four service scaffolds'' main() sat at 61 lines (one over\ncheck_function_length.py''s ceiling), blocking every commit''s\npre-commit run repo-wide regardless of what changed. Extract the\nGitHub-remote-vs-offline-mode branch into finalize_github_or_offline,\nmatching the file''s existing named-helper style; no behaviour change.\n\n* feat(ruff): adopt pep8-naming (N) minus N802 in tests\n\nRe-measured (ruff 0.11.13): 9 findings across N802/N806/N813 in\nsrc/ bin/ tests/ optional/. N802 (5) is a false-positive family, every\none a test name using upper-case for deliberate semantic emphasis\n(tests/CLAUDE.md), so it is ignored only in tests/**. N806 (3) is a\nreal finding shape (a local ALL-CAPS constant inside a function) and\nis fixed by hoisting each to module scope. N813 (1) is a deliberate\ndefusedxml alias, kept via a targeted per-file-ignore. Case-by-case\ndetail lands in CONTRIBUTING.md''s Ruff Rule Adoption Log.\n\nCloses #422\n\n* docs(contributing): record the pep8-naming (N) adoption rationale\n\nDocuments why N is adopted with two per-file-ignores rather than whole:\n\n- N802 (5 findings) ignored in tests/** only — every one is a test name\n  using upper-case for semantic emphasis on the behaviour under test,\n  which is what tests/CLAUDE.md asks a test name to describe.\n- N806 (3 findings) fixed, not ignored — local _ALL_CAPS constants\n  hoisted to module scope, which is the PEP-8 rule seen from the other\n  side.\n- N813 (1 finding) kept via a per-file-ignore — the lowercase\n  defused_et alias is deliberate and reads as \"the defused one\" at\n  every call site.\n\nAlso fills the casing row in the cross-language parity table: no\nlike-for-like TS gap, because a JS/TS test name is a string literal\npassed to it()/describe(), not a function identifier.\n\nRefs #422\n\n* docs(contributing): date the re-measured parity row, not the table\n\nThe casing row was measured 2026-09-13; every other row still dates from\nthe 2026-09-06 snapshot in the heading. Bumping the heading would assert\na whole-table re-measurement that never happened, so the row carries its\nown date instead, and the staleness note now says which date governs\nwhat.\n\n* fix(ruff): mirror the N813 exemption for lib-minimal''s layout\n\nper-file-ignores keys are path-relative, and lib-minimal re-roots src/utils/\nunder src/<pkg>/_internal/utils/. The N813 entry added for xml_reader.py\nmatched only the template layout, so ''Scaffold + lint + test — lib-minimal''\nwas the one tier that went red. Two sibling entries (tabular_reader,\nconfig/contracts) already carry the same mirror; this one was missing it.\n\nVerified with bin/ci/scaffold_lint_test.sh lib-minimal: scaffolds clean,\nlints clean, 85 tests pass.\n\n* chore(ruff): record why pep8-naming adds per-file-ignores\n\nThe PR-body justification was overwritten when the reviewer bot\nregenerated the description, so gate integrity kept failing. A commit\ntrailer survives. Exemptions: N802 in tests (5 mixed-case behaviour\nnames) and N813 on the deliberate defusedxml alias in xml_reader.py,\ntemplate and lib-minimal layouts. N was not enabled before this PR.\n\ngate-change-ok: pep8-naming adoption, 3 measured exemptions (see body)\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XivhWbApyVDfvG6GGjo6xK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrAglCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHggQAA0CncpFFiwL9jgqII1nUBBE\nuoEmzxErEq3uk5YT8EeIf27lUjQaRYt3zgD7Xtj/yhTgOPAt+2ailGeHhxhiksF6\n7AQOdxg9+VuSCE0G9wiCcsQgjjBcnAZeoYIknl02s3ydNfq3uM9brAKOQWNn7mrb\nLTAmSQr37JgFyOZ3142bzghpbccA+MQBXrUzq3hJpusTwf+AqMbwtLvdSM/Fi8GF\nPE2WUbXLg6zNT8bq/pJKuxTedLI5HwxJVj37RlTQzI98HuYQbLCGbhrrSg38U3M9\nvcy2qNpuL4chcKOjh