/blueprintx/commits/19ed8bd02a440f8ed29c030022a37da61ae31903"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d9a4d27aaf011ea82e97f5c3030a87d9205b67f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:24:22Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:24:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): adopt markdownlint with a measured rule set (#477)\n\n* feat(ci): add measured pymarkdownlnt rule set (blueprintx#383)\n\nAdopt MD018/019/020/021/023 (malformed-heading family), MD047 and\nMD009 only. MD013 and MD040 stay explicitly disabled; the measured\ncounts behind every enable/disable decision are documented in\nbin/ci/check_markdown.sh (added in a follow-up commit), never as\ncomments inside this JSON file, since check-json requires strict\nJSON and rejects // comments.\n\n* ci(markdown): wire the measured markdownlint gate (blueprintx#383)\n\nRegisters bin/ci/check_markdown.sh as a pre-commit hook (files: \\.md$)\nand a matching scaffold_checks.yml CI job (timeout-minutes: 10,\nMARKDOWNLINT_REQUIRED=1 so a missing pymarkdownlnt hard-fails in CI\ninstead of silently skipping). Minimal, isolated diff to these two\ncollision-prone files per the open-PR note on blueprintx#383.\n\n* feat(ci): add the markdownlint gate wrapper (blueprintx#383)\n\nbin/ci/check_markdown.sh runs pymarkdownlnt over every tracked .md\nfile (root + templates/) using .pymarkdown.json''s measured rule set.\nResolves gracefully when pymarkdownlnt is absent locally; hard-fails\nin CI via MARKDOWNLINT_REQUIRED=1. Fails on zero discovered files.\n\nDeliberately not shipped into templates/python-common/ or any\ngenerated project — same shape as check_actions.sh, which audits\ntemplate text from BlueprintX''s own root without executing it.\n\n* fix(docs): escape bare #NNN refs (blueprintx#383)\n\nWraps the first bare issue/PR reference on 7 lines across 6\ndocs/backlog/ ledgers in backticks (e.g. `#155`), the same fix\nPR #343 already established for this exact MD018 shape. A bare\n#NNN at the start of a block is a possible ATX heading opening to\na strict CommonMark/GFM parser when the # is followed immediately\nby a digit with no space.\n\nVerified: bin/ci/check_markdown.sh went from 7 findings (all MD018)\nto 0 across all 156 tracked .md files.\n\n* fix(ci): run pymarkdownlnt with --strict-config\n\nWithout it a wrong-type setting in .pymarkdown.json is silently replaced by\nits default and the gate still exits 0. Measured: md009.enabled=''yes-please''\n-> lenient exit 0, strict exit 1 (''must be of type bool''). The real config\npasses strict (156 files, OK). Answers the CodeRabbit thread on line 48.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d9a6c401ab48944fa526e42a966c9806598e424","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/0d9a6c401ab48944fa526e42a966c9806598e424"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/d9a4d27aaf011ea82e97f5c3030a87d9205b67f3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d9a6c401ab48944fa526e42a966c9806598e424\nparent 4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789640662 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789640662 +0000\n\nfeat(ci): adopt markdownlint with a measured rule set (#477)\n\n* feat(ci): add measured pymarkdownlnt rule set (blueprintx#383)\n\nAdopt MD018/019/020/021/023 (malformed-heading family), MD047 and\nMD009 only. MD013 and MD040 stay explicitly disabled; the measured\ncounts behind every enable/disable decision are documented in\nbin/ci/check_markdown.sh (added in a follow-up commit), never as\ncomments inside this JSON file, since check-json requires strict\nJSON and rejects // comments.\n\n* ci(markdown): wire the measured markdownlint gate (blueprintx#383)\n\nRegisters bin/ci/check_markdown.sh as a pre-commit hook (files: \\.md$)\nand a matching scaffold_checks.yml CI job (timeout-minutes: 10,\nMARKDOWNLINT_REQUIRED=1 so a missing pymarkdownlnt hard-fails in CI\ninstead of silently skipping). Minimal, isolated diff to these two\ncollision-prone files per the open-PR note on blueprintx#383.\n\n* feat(ci): add the markdownlint gate wrapper (blueprintx#383)\n\nbin/ci/check_markdown.sh runs pymarkdownlnt over every tracked .md\nfile (root + templates/) using .pymarkdown.json''s measured rule set.\nResolves gracefully when pymarkdownlnt is absent locally; hard-fails\nin CI via MARKDOWNLINT_REQUIRED=1. Fails on zero discovered files.\n\nDeliberately not shipped into templates/python-common/ or any\ngenerated project — same shape as check_actions.sh, which audits\ntemplate text from BlueprintX''s own root without executing it.\n\n* fix(docs): escape bare #NNN refs (blueprintx#383)\n\nWraps the first bare issue/PR reference on 7 lines across 6\ndocs/backlog/ ledgers in backticks (e.g. `#155`), the same fix\nPR #343 already established for this exact MD018 shape. A bare\n#NNN at the start of a block is a possible ATX heading opening to\na strict CommonMark/GFM parser when the # is followed immediately\nby a digit with no space.\n\nVerified: bin/ci/check_markdown.sh went from 7 findings (all MD018)\nto 0 across all 156 tracked .md files.\n\n* fix(ci): run pymarkdownlnt with --strict-config\n\nWithout it a wrong-type setting in .pymarkdown.json is silently replaced by\nits default and the gate still exits 0. Measured: md009.enabled=''yes-please''\n-> lenient exit 0, strict exit 1 (''must be of type bool''). The real config\npasses strict (156 files, OK). Answers the CodeRabbit thread on line 48.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq7/WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA23QQAKDqf+Nxxq1Xhv1bF2Cqe9vh\n4uqTHa5uG+b2VLBnJugijp0LU9OG9ylR7180AaY6EcmQcwrLQrwqkp/soln1IlC7\nM9gBrCcHPZc+bzeZO+hRIPYkWQwpLpnihWSt1LaPxZlRubuqosuq6ShgnM1miFuV\nRiFNQ7NF3lkXQwr93nfgBQVkY+HPw/EuQVg9j/u6qVNZHln9wVvG8aF0fSQOKiyP\nQ+iSXPRIjXTAWBeNIYKKDLsIeUchDzAKiQdmERRTGezpmCW+DMKj7a4lZCaIU72x\njTF8eTztYF4NY9t9esqDSRi/SuOu9e6wlGgVLG97huYUFpqVD3F71vffIMCKQbKv\nXDZw401y9Ln+G9O8FNfQWnWkC8VZPoC6uYgJkGIkl8PrlGZE9Rjhz3A02mlqqqMN\nCwCrASqGkLR8sydum3UZF1KFuI+x0slRD8+bMEc9YyQbor1D5LHuv4K8FGz/UTNL\nmT3GbGD+yiJKH9IApn2tPJKwSjQ7NtZQlnxy99tqnLltxWBtvOrc7GCSRgD1d3+o\nGcYu1Lhbao+UMVs2Q0thMU8AWihFxv7CvQfSsd4GTi12n614S7ADDVtpbMpVT9f3\nDPVQZ+OEVB35YUj0SAta/IJIPsV7zUEkC7Bnjk7OqpJ40TS56+0vuS1Q9Z7XNYnO\nIPnbLaXYCueVxrtpVJ8g\n=Dm3v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T10:24:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/d9a4d27aaf011ea82e97f5c3030a87d9205b67f3","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKGQ5YTRkMjdhYWYwMTFlYTgyZTk3ZjVjMzAzMGE4N2Q5MjA1YjY3ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b","sha":"4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b"}],"sha":"d9a4d27aaf011ea82e97f5c3030a87d9205b67f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/d9a4d27aaf011ea82e97f5c3030a87d9205b67f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:09:15Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:09:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ts-common): OTLP log export seam + ts-lib wiring (#438) (#505)\n\n* feat(ts-common): OTLP log emitter seam for TS skeletons (#438)\n\nwithOtelLogExport() wraps a LogEmitter with an OpenTelemetry logs\nexporter, mirroring python-common/optional/otel_logging.py: opt-in,\nadditive (base emitter always still runs), fire-and-forget, and\nrefuses to start when credentials would cross the network in\ncleartext. Ships the local-dev collector compose fragment alongside\npython-common''s own copy.\n\nNot yet wired into ts_lib.sh / ts_react_app.sh - that follows in a\nseparate commit.\n\n* feat(ts-lib): wire OTLP log export opt-in into the scaffold (#438)\n\nprompt_otel + conditional_copy_otel mirror the Python scaffolds:\ncopies otel-log-emitter.ts + its test into src/utils/, adds the\nexact-pinned @opentelemetry/* deps to package.json, re-exports\nwithOtelLogExport from the public barrel, and ships the local-dev\ncollector compose fragment. Documents the new ts-common files.\n\nreact-spa-webpack wiring is deferred to a follow-up issue - #459 is\nactively editing bin/scaffold/ts_react_app.sh''s sed -i calls.\n\n--no-verify: local function-length pre-commit hook scans the whole\nrepo and is already red on main() in the four frozen\npython_*_service*.sh files (fixed by open PR #486, unrelated to this\ndiff) - see CLAUDE.md task brief.\n\n* fix(ts-common): address CodeRabbit findings on the OTLP log seam\n\n- resolveOtlpLogsUrl: append /v1/logs only when the endpoint came\n  from the generic env var; the signal-specific one is used verbatim\n  per the OTel spec. Passing the raw value straight through as the\n  exporter''s url silently targeted / instead of the collector.\n- isCleartextWithCredentials: refuse EVERY credentialed request in a\n  browser runtime, not only cleartext ones. fetch (the only browser\n  transport) follows redirects with no config knob to disable it, so\n  an https:// or loopback endpoint could still 3xx to a cleartext\n  host and forward the headers there.\n- withOtelLogExport: accept an injectable install parameter so its\n  fire-and-forget contract can be tested deterministically, instead\n  of relying on @opentelemetry/* being absent from ts-common''s own\n  devDependencies (false once conditional_copy_otel adds them).\n\nPR #505 review threads PRRT_kwDORFcNJs6jPCdy, PRRT_kwDORFcNJs6jPCd9,\nPRRT_kwDORFcNJs6jPCdu.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4be7b470b254ac8906a5ef9d4eac0d0130d820f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/b4be7b470b254ac8906a5ef9d4eac0d0130d820f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b","verification":{"payload":"tree b4be7b470b254ac8906a5ef9d4eac0d0130d820f\nparent 0802a7d26840c434fce399e13d302071502bb461\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789639755 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789639755 +0000\n\nfeat(ts-common): OTLP log export seam + ts-lib wiring (#438) (#505)\n\n* feat(ts-common): OTLP log emitter seam for TS skeletons (#438)\n\nwithOtelLogExport() wraps a LogEmitter with an OpenTelemetry logs\nexporter, mirroring python-common/optional/otel_logging.py: opt-in,\nadditive (base emitter always still runs), fire-and-forget, and\nrefuses to start when credentials would cross the network in\ncleartext. Ships the local-dev collector compose fragment alongside\npython-common''s own copy.\n\nNot yet wired into ts_lib.sh / ts_react_app.sh - that follows in a\nseparate commit.\n\n* feat(ts-lib): wire OTLP log export opt-in into the scaffold (#438)\n\nprompt_otel + conditional_copy_otel mirror the Python scaffolds:\ncopies otel-log-emitter.ts + its test into src/utils/, adds the\nexact-pinned @opentelemetry/* deps to package.json, re-exports\nwithOtelLogExport from the public barrel, and ships the local-dev\ncollector compose fragment. Documents the new ts-common files.\n\nreact-spa-webpack wiring is deferred to a follow-up issue - #459 is\nactively editing bin/scaffold/ts_react_app.sh''s sed -i calls.\n\n--no-verify: local function-length pre-commit hook scans the whole\nrepo and is already red on main() in the four frozen\npython_*_service*.sh files (fixed by open PR #486, unrelated to this\ndiff) - see CLAUDE.md task brief.\n\n* fix(ts-common): address CodeRabbit findings on the OTLP log seam\n\n- resolveOtlpLogsUrl: append /v1/logs only when the endpoint came\n  from the generic env var; the signal-specific one is used verbatim\n  per the OTel spec. Passing the raw value straight through as the\n  exporter''s url silently targeted / instead of the collector.\n- isCleartextWithCredentials: refuse EVERY credentialed request in a\n  browser runtime, not only cleartext ones. fetch (the only browser\n  transport) follows redirects with no config knob to disable it, so\n  an https:// or loopback endpoint could still 3xx to a cleartext\n  host and forward the headers there.\n- withOtelLogExport: accept an injectable install parameter so its\n  fire-and-forget contract can be tested deterministically, instead\n  of relying on @opentelemetry/* being absent from ts-common''s own\n  devDependencies (false once conditional_copy_otel adds them).\n\nPR #505 review threads PRRT_kwDORFcNJs6jPCdy, PRRT_kwDORFcNJs6jPCd9,\nPRRT_kwDORFcNJs6jPCdu.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq7xLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVZ4QAF2SY+94rxDtE60KAatlRda1\nFva7qPZ+Yf4A/zLqMl5S8kRkVnDHzIY3GQWyVfd27iEFJqK2vCGJ10LeyVGqZQy1\nDIWdPCyCTeqADLnqrJnQ6iSjB8FrOw8IktrpJvlfKJ8SDhJuNz7zBS51OQSlZdS9\njYbWfci2Jl1oV3ZuC57rKXNXXLa0FpTJQpaPq13Ccby0ByYU0+d3MeqAQl4wTp50\nArihToVQxY4abt8gUZAl/uTGasfGihHwtDKBGTlq9vDRdAFjmihRXORhSnw+PUu3\nDe+LTLmqxqfgmq8l4wY9T+THNvCoZpyRz1SuYJ0hmT3iq4achy8uS3MGvvVcb0WD\nDqAtHzPMR1BbCosrji8qUAR1usA4ug3615F63reSuj+1QF0I2DC6bHKAfm8jV9iL\nORisWKX9FKw2NY2uWXHqL5HiWzSdUKdxCZU0BV1I/mUkluaFJOt36LLAgEBao98g\nEPxEke7mzZwVro0vLt/8yeEkES1lzDNdrffn7jSLGpMA5FH8mrT3XSqahVJFAHXv\nQQy5cveF9rPNCU5lLDgbtrXdbioyKY869ZVnlbalsq33K/o6QmfHFnFsak+zEefg\nfMmQOmtvHt9U/+gCDyk3zT8fHm3uZouH7/IZThRZ+UM02RZQOwUAgn5g4l0QQQwA\nJe2iGCXjCjn+jWDN3JsI\n=+HGf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T10:09:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b","node_id":"C_kwDORFcNJtoAKDRmNmM3ODI3NTdhNzc3MzEyYzNjODc1YmI2ZTk3ZmJjMDk0ZTM0MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commit/0802a7d26840c434fce399e13d302071502bb461","sha":"0802a7d26840c434fce399e13d302071502bb461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/0802a7d26840c434fce399e13d302071502bb461"}],"sha":"4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/4f6c782757a777312c3c875bb6e97fbc094e342b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55053188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guilhermegor","id":55053188,"login":"guilhermegor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MDUzMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guilhermegor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/commits/0802a7d26840c434fce399e13d302071502bb461/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:55:29Z","email":"55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guilherme Rodrigues"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:55:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(python-common): gate migration slug verb convention (#375) (#513)\n\n* feat(python-common): gate migration slug verb convention (#375)\n\nAdopts Rails'' <verb>_<object>[_<qualifier>] migration slug shape and\nadds check_migration_slugs.py to enforce it - decidable from the\nfilename alone, no interactive picker needed. Self-skips when\nmigrations/versions/ is absent (only ddd-service-orm-db ships\nmigrations today, #373); escape hatch for alembic merge''s own slug\nshape via \"# migration-slug-ok: <reason>\".\n\nNo existing migration files violate this: migrations/versions/ ships\nonly .gitkeep today.\n\n* chore(templates): copy the migration-slug gate test to every tier (#375)\n\nRequired by the test-copy-lists pre-commit hook: a shipped tests/unit/\nfile needs an active cp line or it is written, committed, and never\nrun in a generated project. Lands in the shared\nscaffold_copy_gate_tests helper (bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh)\nrather than in either per-tier scaffold script, since that helper is\nwhat all five Python scaffolds already call for this test family.\n\n* chore(templates): copy migration-slug gate test in lib-minimal too (#375)\n\nlib-minimal keeps its own hand-maintained copy-list function\n(lib_minimal_copy_gate_tests) rather than calling the shared\nscaffold_copy_gate_tests in bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh, so\nthe earlier fix there did not reach this tier. CI''s\ncheck_test_copy_lists.py caught the gap:\n\"python_lib_minimal.sh: never copies test_migration_slug_gate.py\".\n\nVerified locally: bin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py now reports\n\"copy lists OK: 54 shared test(s) + 9 workflow(s) reachable from all\n5 Python scaffolds.\"\n\n* fix(python-common): escape hatch can''t borrow a reason across lines\n\n_RE_ESCAPE used \\s*, which matches a newline. _has_escape_hatch joins\nthe scanned lines with \\n before searching, so a bare\n\"# migration-slug-ok:\" pragma followed by any non-whitespace on a\nlater line (a docstring, an import) let \\s* consume the newline and\ncapture that later line''s text as the \"reason\" - silencing a\ngenuinely bad slug with no real justification given.\n\nRestrict the match to horizontal whitespace and text on the pragma''s own\nline ([ \\t]* / [^\\r\\n]*), matching CodeRabbit''s review on #513. Added\ntest_a_bare_escape_hatch_cannot_borrow_a_reason_from_the_next_line,\nverified to fail against the old regex before restoring the fix\n(mutation test).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce64785f6dd014f9ca6d0094d1ab226c44dd9bc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/trees/ce64785f6dd014f9ca6d0094d1ab226c44dd9bc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guilhermegor/blueprintx/git/commits/0802a7d26840c434fce399e13d302071502bb461","verification":{"payload":"tree ce64785f6dd014f9ca6d0094d1ab226c44dd9bc3\nparent 975a8ec8fa98d92540774d6b6d6054c46cabb3c6\nauthor Guilherme Rodrigues <55053188+guilhermegor@users.noreply.github.com> 1789638929 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789638929 +0000\n\nfeat(python-common): gate migration slug verb convention (#375) (#513)\n\n* feat(python-common): gate migration slug verb convention (#375)\n\nAdopts Rails'' <verb>_<object>[_<qualifier>] migration slug shape and\nadds check_migration_slugs.py to enforce it - decidable from the\nfilename alone, no interactive picker needed. Self-skips when\nmigrations/versions/ is absent (only ddd-service-orm-db ships\nmigrations today, #373); escape hatch for alembic merge''s own slug\nshape via \"# migration-slug-ok: <reason>\".\n\nNo existing migration files violate this: migrations/versions/ ships\nonly .gitkeep today.\n\n* chore(templates): copy the migration-slug gate test to every tier (#375)\n\nRequired by the test-copy-lists pre-commit hook: a shipped tests/unit/\nfile needs an active cp line or it is written, committed, and never\nrun in a generated project. Lands in the shared\nscaffold_copy_gate_tests helper (bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh)\nrather than in either per-tier scaffold script, since that helper is\nwhat all five Python scaffolds already call for this test family.\n\n* chore(templates): copy migration-slug gate test in lib-minimal too (#375)\n\nlib-minimal keeps its own hand-maintained copy-list function\n(lib_minimal_copy_gate_tests) rather than calling the shared\nscaffold_copy_gate_tests in bin/lib/scaffold_python_templates.sh, so\nthe earlier fix there did not reach this tier. CI''s\ncheck_test_copy_lists.py caught the gap:\n\"python_lib_minimal.sh: never copies test_migration_slug_gate.py\".\n\nVerified locally: bin/ci/check_test_copy_lists.py now reports\n\"copy lists OK: 54 shared test(s) + 9 workflow(s) reachable from all\n5 Python scaffolds.\"\n\n* fix(python-common): escape hatch can''t borrow a reason across lines\n\n_RE_ESCAPE used \\s*, which matches a newline. _has_escape_hatch joins\nthe scanned lines with \\n before searching, so a bare\n\"# migration-slug-ok:\" pragma followed by any non-whitespace on a\nlater line (a docstring, an import) let \\s* consume the newline and\ncapture that later line''s text as the \"reason\" - silencing a\ngenuinely bad slug with no real justification given.\n\nRestrict the match to horizontal whitespace and text on the pragma''s own\nline ([ \\t]* / [^\\r\\n]*), matching CodeRabbit''s review on #513. Added\ntest_a_bare_escape_hatch_cannot_borrow_a_reason_from_the_next_line,\nverified to fail against the old regex before restoring the fix\n(mutation test).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ci-bot <ci-bot@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq7kRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwhIQAKcx072u+QkY+AVDXKUk94tJ\nDeO+v+GhW7pCQM/Ca/gc+f7AXuWsyHd9psBKbHZDN5g78N5OmWvp21t2Ic6Rpy7L\nkI0404Bi91nilBrdCuIRM1fn0Jm/gJ1T8oKYdznrxgkZHDeHOoZ3gAXXzBaatcrS\nLobeYPr2QqQwGbnuagmwJiAaF4wHKyn8T5kaIAJRACYsel5mWYGoHffvrReMUORO\nouwwNkJ4rX3gyqx7Wuf2PHqEKIV8FTUhzvh4aD0cUtRknC73VgvlnA53I5YjkTz8\nTKsqGXsAjJpAcB4t/DEf92Pvn5SSmzTo1OqLr2AwWO7JQZyab0okn/vfmQji5k67\nPdoat/evmFDoKrjXmXRFfqDwW+kj1YkbVh9Im1LL0RV/