ml_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528","sha":"647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528"}],"sha":"e9b0e1047e3dc190c4299ede3285f875c81c8791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/e9b0e1047e3dc190c4299ede3285f875c81c8791"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28598?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rhysyngsun","id":28598,"login":"rhysyngsun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTk4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:09:18Z","email":"nlevesq@mit.edu","name":"Nathan Levesque"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:45:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(settings): restore the celery task routing settings production.py owned\n\nThis affects deployed environments, not just local-dev.\n\n`lms/envs/common.py` (and the CMS twin) wires the custom router\nunconditionally -- CELERY_ROUTES = \"openedx.core.lib.celery.routers.\nroute_task\" -- but route_task reads EXPLICIT_QUEUES and\nALTERNATE_ENV_TASKS, and both are defined only in production.py: the\nmodule aqueduct replaces. Overlaying onto common.py therefore leaves the\nrouter installed with its inputs missing, so every apply_async dies with\n\n    AttributeError: ''Settings'' object has no attribute ''EXPLICIT_QUEUES''\n\nThat is not a narrow break. Enrolling a learner through the enrollment\nAPI hits it (ENROLLMENT_TRACK_UPDATED -> grade recalculation ->\napply_async) and returns a 500, which is how it was found; anything else\nthat queues a task fails the same way.\n\nSupply both as empty dicts rather than copying upstream''s task -> queue\ntable. Empty makes route_task return None, which is its documented \"use\ncelery''s default routing\" answer, so every task lands on\nCELERY_TASK_DEFAULT_QUEUE -- the one queue a worker started without -Q\nactually consumes. Transcribing production.py''s table instead would pin\n~25 task names that drift with edx-platform, and would route work onto\n*.high / *.high_mem queues that nothing consumes unless the deployment\nalso runs dedicated workers. A deployment that does run them can set\nEXPLICIT_QUEUES through the YAML tier; setdefault leaves it alone.\n\nIntroduce apply_base_post_configure as the post_configure every entry\nmodule needs, so the four deployment modules stop listing the individual\nfixups and cannot miss the next one.\n\nVerified in a running stack: both settings present, and lms-worker and\ncms-worker come up clean with no restarts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8f9831ad8bc2c03755f89b69be92621a5a29061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/f8f9831ad8bc2c03755f89b69be92621a5a29061"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528","verification":{"payload":"tree f8f9831ad8bc2c03755f89b69be92621a5a29061\nparent 53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049\nauthor Nathan Levesque <nlevesq@mit.edu> 1791230958 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791297919 -0400\n\nfix(settings): restore the celery task routing settings production.py owned\n\nThis affects deployed environments, not just local-dev.\n\n`lms/envs/common.py` (and the CMS twin) wires the custom router\nunconditionally -- CELERY_ROUTES = \"openedx.core.lib.celery.routers.\nroute_task\" -- but route_task reads EXPLICIT_QUEUES and\nALTERNATE_ENV_TASKS, and both are defined only in production.py: the\nmodule aqueduct replaces. Overlaying onto common.py therefore leaves the\nrouter installed with its inputs missing, so every apply_async dies with\n\n    AttributeError: ''Settings'' object has no attribute ''EXPLICIT_QUEUES''\n\nThat is not a narrow break. Enrolling a learner through the enrollment\nAPI hits it (ENROLLMENT_TRACK_UPDATED -> grade recalculation ->\napply_async) and returns a 500, which is how it was found; anything else\nthat queues a task fails the same way.\n\nSupply both as empty dicts rather than copying upstream''s task -> queue\ntable. Empty makes route_task return None, which is its documented \"use\ncelery''s default routing\" answer, so every task lands on\nCELERY_TASK_DEFAULT_QUEUE -- the one queue a worker started without -Q\nactually consumes. Transcribing production.py''s table instead would pin\n~25 task names that drift with edx-platform, and would route work onto\n*.high / *.high_mem queues that nothing consumes unless the deployment\nalso runs dedicated workers. A deployment that does run them can set\nEXPLICIT_QUEUES through the YAML tier; setdefault leaves it alone.\n\nIntroduce apply_base_post_configure as the post_configure every entry\nmodule needs, so the four deployment modules stop listing the individual\nfixups and cannot miss the next one.\n\nVerified in a running stack: both settings present, and lms-worker and\ncms-worker come up clean with no restarts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQl/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIdkQADeNm0brwwB1fWX5a4mPof30\nnbSIXlSwkXrzEclTWrVUGT5rO1indw/dPKVoFbv9UOII5q5+pdhgpz5uFBNOJveK\nyhx70UdXoRf6pYXHJz/pYIeDBNQdjUNTjYnAmoA2ZHX9N5kZIwTZCzD6xz9UnUsG\nTrS4xc0+7ZkzzBaJOpvBnXO+KqVTTA5HGNOS3gDCMYpF8NxttyANviLTiemdqPoK\nFvSIzqVhlDILFChV/m9tz/Bz3Ii3fiULADYh+dYn5DlP0kPisAfhthMYvAydNcTy\n9smCa94J1TKo14jyJ5eFF9yhmepHp8mYPMMrV5lHEhcRuelu09uz/FKf2bD/lGax\nwxtgFNlz+eCMhoP6ISZwyljLns8ufslwMtxkTRZ9q6OzLvBD0z1c790Sr8uSo2Ct\nDR1FMSvPWdBIX4AwMmlVUfBpc3Dqy80Nc+5YZZd0FyxTRkLY56fAyhpJN2V4Qk1o\nVfKIUUsFw9zAL8cKio4ey40ycchPJuywDB0OI6bD7LGmaVU+0Zfk6pMIxukSLmV6\nrK3HwBBz6s3P+sRqoPsDtjFlzeT31k2w9jqdnMXnhIQxW7ByL0X7OVDkPTwAEa3h\nnaN2aFVGe9i8PqItcDVauhAxreUr0TppXfFSCreCvUpet77aFOnS8/XNpr1h5jTb\ne9tl90H6NF3KnHHobBmX\n=D4Ma\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:45:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDY0N2JkZjc1YjIxODRkODE2YjI4Y2IwOTE5MGJkMGRhMTU3ZWQ1Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049","sha":"53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049"}],"sha":"647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/647bdf75b2184d816b28cb09190bd0da157ed528"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:09:11Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:09:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: unbreak Settings Verification and regenerate the master settings models (#307)\n\n* fix: Let verify_settings inject lehrer_bootstrap without an app user\n\ninject_aqueduct_settings has copied lehrer_bootstrap in with\nowner=\"app:app\" since #274. verify_settings calls it on the container from\n_python_only_env, which never creates that user, so every Settings\nVerification cell failed with \"failed to resolve ownership for app:app:\nfind uid: no such user: app\" before reaching any check.\n\nThis adds a bootstrap_owner argument that defaults to \"app:app\" for the\nimage build and is passed as None from verify_settings.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models\n\nedx-platform master replaced drf_yasg with drf_spectacular_sidecar: it\ndropped SWAGGER_SETTINGS from the LMS, added the SIDECAR dist keys to the\nLMS SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS, and gave the CMS a common-level\nSPECTACULAR_SETTINGS. The committed models still carried the old shape, so\nthe drift check fails as soon as it can run again (observed locally on\nmit-ol/master/mitxonline with the ownership fix applied).\n\nRegenerated with `dagger call platform regenerate-aqueduct-settings` for\nmit-ol (mitxonline) and generic.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Derive SERVERS for the Studio Authoring API schema\n\nThe CMS SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS default trims /api/contentstore from the\npublished paths, and upstream only puts it back through the SERVERS that\ncms.envs.production adds. lehrer overlays cms.envs.common, so Swagger''s\n\"Try it out\" at /authoring-api/ui/ requested /v0/xblock/... and got a 404.\nThat was already true of the master cells, and the regenerated model\nextends the default to verawood, whose common.py has no\nSPECTACULAR_SETTINGS of its own.\n\nThis adds a StudioSettingsMixin validator that lists the contentstore\nserver, the CMS root (one documented path sits outside the trimmed\nprefix), and AUTHORING_API_URL when it is set. It assigns the setting\nrather than editing the default in place, because django-aqueduct only\nlets a field the base also defines through when it is in\nmodel_fields_set.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Make the LMS schema SERVERS survive the overlay on master\n\nThe LMS entry modules added SERVERS by editing SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS in\nplace. django-aqueduct only lets a field the base also defines through\nwhen it is in model_fields_set, which an in-place edit does not touch, so\non master (where lms.envs.common defines the setting) the edit was\ndiscarded and the Enrollment API schema had no servers.\n\nThis moves the derivation into spectacular_with_servers, shared with the\nStudio mixin, and assigns its result. The LMS now lists the root URL under\n/api/enrollment first, since every published path has that prefix trimmed\nand upstream''s single root-URL server does not resolve them.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Build the prefixed schema server from SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX\n\nspectacular_with_servers appended SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX_TRIM to the root URL,\nbut drf-spectacular documents that setting as a bool: it only switches\ntrimming on, and the prefix it removes is SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX. edx-platform\nhappens to set both to the same path, so the committed models were\nunaffected, but an operator-supplied SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS with\nSCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX_TRIM set to True or False raised a TypeError while the\nsettings module loaded.\n\nThe prefixed server now uses SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX, and is only listed when\ntrimming is on and the prefix is a non-empty string; otherwise the root\nserver is the only one.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Christopher Patti <feoh@feoh.org>","tree":{"sha":"94284392172c131a28e0af135854ed7dcbbb2771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/94284392172c131a28e0af135854ed7dcbbb2771"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049","verification":{"payload":"tree 94284392172c131a28e0af135854ed7dcbbb2771\nparent db4445b2af6ef53d18b45c495c30d1c9ae6e8384\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1791295751 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791295751 -0400\n\nfix: unbreak Settings Verification and regenerate the master settings models (#307)\n\n* fix: Let verify_settings inject lehrer_bootstrap without an app user\n\ninject_aqueduct_settings has copied lehrer_bootstrap in with\nowner=\"app:app\" since #274. verify_settings calls it on the container from\n_python_only_env, which never creates that user, so every Settings\nVerification cell failed with \"failed to resolve ownership for app:app:\nfind uid: no such user: app\" before reaching any check.\n\nThis adds a bootstrap_owner argument that defaults to \"app:app\" for the\nimage build and is passed as None from verify_settings.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models\n\nedx-platform master replaced drf_yasg with drf_spectacular_sidecar: it\ndropped SWAGGER_SETTINGS from the LMS, added the SIDECAR dist keys to the\nLMS SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS, and gave the CMS a common-level\nSPECTACULAR_SETTINGS. The committed models still carried the old shape, so\nthe drift check fails as soon as it can run again (observed locally on\nmit-ol/master/mitxonline with the ownership fix applied).\n\nRegenerated with `dagger call platform regenerate-aqueduct-settings` for\nmit-ol (mitxonline) and generic.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Derive SERVERS for the Studio Authoring API schema\n\nThe CMS SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS default trims /api/contentstore from the\npublished paths, and upstream only puts it back through the SERVERS that\ncms.envs.production adds. lehrer overlays cms.envs.common, so Swagger''s\n\"Try it out\" at /authoring-api/ui/ requested /v0/xblock/... and got a 404.\nThat was already true of the master cells, and the regenerated model\nextends the default to verawood, whose common.py has no\nSPECTACULAR_SETTINGS of its own.\n\nThis adds a StudioSettingsMixin validator that lists the contentstore\nserver, the CMS root (one documented path sits outside the trimmed\nprefix), and AUTHORING_API_URL when it is set. It assigns the setting\nrather than editing the default in place, because django-aqueduct only\nlets a field the base also defines through when it is in\nmodel_fields_set.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Make the LMS schema SERVERS survive the overlay on master\n\nThe LMS entry modules added SERVERS by editing SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS in\nplace. django-aqueduct only lets a field the base also defines through\nwhen it is in model_fields_set, which an in-place edit does not touch, so\non master (where lms.envs.common defines the setting) the edit was\ndiscarded and the Enrollment API schema had no servers.\n\nThis moves the derivation into spectacular_with_servers, shared with the\nStudio mixin, and assigns its result. The LMS now lists the root URL under\n/api/enrollment first, since every published path has that prefix trimmed\nand upstream''s single root-URL server does not resolve them.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPLwaU8Nv65d2PoJvLhjyq\n\n* fix: Build the prefixed schema server from SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX\n\nspectacular_with_servers appended SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX_TRIM to the root URL,\nbut drf-spectacular documents that setting as a bool: it only switches\ntrimming on, and the prefix it removes is SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX. edx-platform\nhappens to set both to the same path, so the committed models were\nunaffected, but an operator-supplied SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS with\nSCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX_TRIM set to True or False raised a TypeError while the\nsettings module loaded.\n\nThe prefixed server now uses SCHEMA_PATH_PREFIX, and is only listed when\ntrimming is on and the prefix is a non-empty string; otherwise the root\nserver is the only one.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Christopher Patti <feoh@feoh.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQEHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxfoQAJVMKwMdyMpaAErBgVYR1yph\nJmGJ//8Kfmzh/QD7NY0d7lIVIjiw0ct2jrCWJ84abAY11/uIf5wrzMDPrJUflIB8\nwiKPaOPeUp6m9EKaGto23zQyH8ljtGDxPIYqfXdFRLY5osvdnnpGJkUtvbRrs0h9\noM6/yP8NWKziWLGLvBP/6K0VuNeZ+aK65aVJ5OeaXrr88SOHSkGMFzkLtP+HT/ZB\nPaThss7LEc7iJqe+Lfa1/7txmuoupM5C4Ub3z3NFNwfkbMTT2ifU9A790ibCaIsK\nrHhDnSgr4YnR8hg2oc8bOuv2j3eZDKkD4dQkX9TmzTjmV5wwbYJ/UGKvXQDv5WrL\ngk4DAm5iAi0CijUj4TnvcnR02e0ph3nZHIz+W9LAoFlJKRSTkm9AULNB1jhBCwA/\n8n1SrY7BNOB4EEBFToP+zGvxKXuk92G8L69iH3SRutk3ym0Yflk3AP2sPCJbUo/h\nxgjt2rPEScpzPhojotA3ldhHkd3FxY7Agla5mE9/8LzFzhqVBFMll1fsov8YHtn/\nTBrEMre9RCGlwpcVew5tVoOLsIUz00YlqWh8Mb5zmhOurpd+t1PvUjSli3/Bcmn0\n2nwwPzRrDRoTFAMj/5rCNOTnwrB7B7Vkx9qs/T3NUgo2Izly/iXhE+w0hjTvYDsT\nWOZ11klesmZLscLls310\n=XMIw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:09:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/53b822c409f82ae2e163366ded130dc0d7bb3049","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDUzYjgyMmM0MDlmODJhZTJlMTYzMzY2ZGVkMTMwZGMwZDdi