"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhysyngsun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/27600f784667881eef9a0a5fbdc0cc9948fd665d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:47:09Z","email":"nlevesq@mit.edu","name":"Nathan Levesque"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:47:09Z","email":"nlevesq@mit.edu","name":"Nathan Levesque"},"message":"chore: untrack committed __pycache__ and fill out the Python .gitignore\n\n18 .pyc files were tracked, added by d247097 and 30e2190 (#274). The root\n.gitignore covered only `dist/` and `/generated/`, so bytecode outside src/\nwas never ignored -- src/.gitignore has `/**/__pycache__`, which is why only\ntests/ and deployments/ accumulated any.\n\nCompiled names embed both the interpreter and the pytest plugin version\n(cpython-314-pytest-9.1.1), so these churn on every toolchain bump and\nconflict on every merge. Each one''s .py source is tracked; nothing in the\nrepo references the .pyc paths.\n\nAlso adds the entries a Python project normally carries: bytecode, venv,\ntool caches, build output, coverage, .env, editor/OS cruft. The venv and\nthe mypy/pytest/ruff caches are each already self-ignoring via a\ntool-written .gitignore containing `*`, so those lines are a backstop\nrather than a fix.\n\n`dist/` stays unanchored: frontend/shared has no local rule of its own.","tree":{"sha":"447c14b6d625b0534aa3a4efda151562dcf3a015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/447c14b6d625b0534aa3a4efda151562dcf3a015"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/27600f784667881eef9a0a5fbdc0cc9948fd665d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_a