rade prek from 0.5.4 to the previous release, 0.5.3 (2026-09-13), at\nthe repository owner''s request. Where the uv project exempted prek from\nexclude-newer, drop that exemption: it existed only so uv could resolve\n0.5.4, and 0.5.3 is outside the window.\n\nPart of https://github.com/mitodl/ol-infrastructure/issues/5805","tree":{"sha":"09afa58f64fb5599ad257e08057fe7d9e820f3b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/09afa58f64fb5599ad257e08057fe7d9e820f3b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/ceecdd9c76697624e4a7bfa6d09dd093655c3110","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/feoh","id":330070,"login":"feoh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDA3MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/ceecdd9c76697624e4a7bfa6d09dd093655c3110","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKGNlZWNkZDljNzY2OTc2MjRlNGE3YmZhNmQwOWRkMDkzNjU1YzMxMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/94d1e56c97b754e178d4ba8e5209577e65712ecc","sha":"94d1e56c97b754e178d4ba8e5209577e65712ecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/94d1e56c97b754e178d4ba8e5209577e65712ecc"}],"sha":"ceecdd9c76697624e4a7bfa6d09dd093655c3110","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/ceecdd9c76697624e4a7bfa6d09dd093655c3110"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/adf0b3eede4b244a0d1afa578da9a2aa2c092288/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:49:45Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:49:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: Boot-check cells without django-aqueduct against production settings (#291)\n\n* fix(core): boot-check cells without django-aqueduct against production settings\n\nThe post-build boot check ran `manage.py <svc> check --settings=aqueduct`\nfor every cell. ulmo/xpro runs Python 3.11, which django-aqueduct cannot\nresolve on, so the package is not installed there and importing\n`lms.envs.aqueduct` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named\n''django_aqueduct''`. That failed build-ulmo-xpro-edxapp-image.\n\nThe check now uses `aqueduct` when `django_aqueduct` is importable and\nthe upstream `production` settings otherwise.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): pick the boot-check settings from the cell, not an import probe\n\nThe import probe fell back to production settings on any import failure,\nso a cell that declares django-aqueduct but ships a broken install would\npass the boot gate without importing lms.envs.aqueduct. Decide from the\ncell''s declared packages instead, via Cell.uses_aqueduct(), which\nreplaces the duplicate predicate in cli/compat.py.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* doc: Point the compat test comment at Cell.uses_aqueduct\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): give the production-settings boot check a stub config\n\nulmo''s lms/envs/production.py loads the YAML at LMS_CFG and iterates its\ntop-level mapping. The shipped env.yml is empty at build time (real config\nis mounted at runtime), so it parses to None and the check died with\nAttributeError: ''NoneType'' object has no attribute ''items''. The\ncommon_initialization system check then also requires LMS_ROOT_URL.\n\nPoint LMS_CFG/CMS_CFG at a stub mapping with a placeholder LMS_ROOT_URL for\ncells on production settings. Set inline on the check command so it does not\nleak into the image env. A local ulmo/xpro build now passes both boot checks.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): remove the boot-check stub config after the check\n\nThe stub env file written for production-settings boot checks stayed in\n/tmp of the shipped image. Remove it once the check passes, and cover the\naqueduct and production command shapes with a unit test.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): decide aqueduct from the effective requirements, by distribution name\n\nReview feedback on #291. The substring match on \"django-aqueduct\" counted\ninline comments, missed normalized spellings (Django_Aqueduct), and ignored\npackages_to_remove. Match PEP 503-normalized distribution names via the\nparser the plugin import check already uses, and exclude removed packages.\n\nbuild_platform also consulted the manifest cell even when explicit\n--pip-package-lists/--pip-package-overrides won over it, so an override\nthat installs django-aqueduct on a cell without it was only checked against\nproduction settings. Read the same requirement files install_deps used.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi","tree":{"sha":"2e3edb08e609a28ad099694533424fe370a22874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/2e3edb08e609a28ad099694533424fe370a22874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/adf0b3eede4b244a0d1afa578da9a2aa2c092288","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e3edb08e609a28ad099694533424fe370a22874\nparent 30e21900dcbd4a341882fe5f45798e46ae3bf1ef\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1790862585 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790862585 -0400\n\nfix: Boot-check cells without django-aqueduct against production settings (#291)\n\n* fix(core): boot-check cells without django-aqueduct against production settings\n\nThe post-build boot check ran `manage.py <svc> check --settings=aqueduct`\nfor every cell. ulmo/xpro runs Python 3.11, which django-aqueduct cannot\nresolve on, so the package is not installed there and importing\n`lms.envs.aqueduct` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named\n''django_aqueduct''`. That failed build-ulmo-xpro-edxapp-image.\n\nThe check now uses `aqueduct` when `django_aqueduct` is importable and\nthe upstream `production` settings otherwise.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): pick the boot-check settings from the cell, not an import probe\n\nThe import probe fell back to production settings on any import failure,\nso a cell that declares django-aqueduct but ships a broken install would\npass the boot gate without importing lms.envs.aqueduct. Decide from the\ncell''s declared packages instead, via Cell.uses_aqueduct(), which\nreplaces the duplicate predicate in cli/compat.py.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* doc: Point the compat test comment at Cell.uses_aqueduct\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): give the production-settings boot check a stub config\n\nulmo''s lms/envs/production.py loads the YAML at LMS_CFG and iterates its\ntop-level mapping. The shipped env.yml is empty at build time (real config\nis mounted at runtime), so it parses to None and the check died with\nAttributeError: ''NoneType'' object has no attribute ''items''. The\ncommon_initialization system check then also requires LMS_ROOT_URL.\n\nPoint LMS_CFG/CMS_CFG at a stub mapping with a placeholder LMS_ROOT_URL for\ncells on production settings. Set inline on the check command so it does not\nleak into the image env. A local ulmo/xpro build now passes both boot checks.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): remove the boot-check stub config after the check\n\nThe stub env file written for production-settings boot checks stayed in\n/tmp of the shipped image. Remove it once the check passes, and cover the\naqueduct and production command shapes with a unit test.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi\n\n* fix(core): decide aqueduct from the effective requirements, by distribution name\n\nReview feedback on #291. The substring match on \"django-aqueduct\" counted\ninline comments, missed normalized spellings (Django_Aqueduct), and ignored\npackages_to_remove. Match PEP 503-normalized distribution names via the\nparser the plugin import check already uses, and exclude removed packages.\n\nbuild_platform also consulted the manifest cell even when explicit\n--pip-package-lists/--pip-package-overrides won over it, so an override\nthat installs django-aqueduct on a cell without it was only checked against\nproduction settings. Read the same requirement files install_deps used.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UwC8kVguhgMxwUDHcsN1Fi","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmT5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAANAQABzigWuSYstv41AbzDupQfU9\nMgRqnvemKYw3mtwseBmxM2ZRwiQVFNjgLYwSnEdw1lsQ75mbWTSkYUcYFyzdaAqa\nvy0iwX5rD08Xosna6pFrWfl36KQCfozrgYGNi5no+77KCh7s4EeGjrPpCKVfLTjy\nk41KgzeCtbpNGeuehKg0y1qF7p9XZxBx0zu05JIR1Bje4oRF/C9y+bEU+gMj1D7C\ngi6Hw2OE1xHTZSVNNRcloAJJ0lyYhDYQQN8em9h0vAZwcbue7IVlplhuSiJ/oyXc\niije1iLrDpMqoV7JHTOv1UvovnIeDwc+FSEcd5iL7mJK9zypTyC62GC2ukh/mE+A\nuGYiOWVdorz/4cHFbsEWwL+jOFfZ+2d2oiu8XttEt9dcX6GEs4OLMFtYG0mUiB4m\nMv73SFgBHvGmedgvpjyWouDYLna5xAFCoa4QZyqHDDs9vOSqr83mXTBYUhB/3Dcn\nBCyIa+dKm6SOcaK71WUoSEETFZFFtTcTdcyw1vDb9pA2JrtL7dURaei66ARM24cX\nK1z1aOwSm+kQbcocvtpB/DzyiJy+K6FFTEWWL2y+y+AU/yRBm8On1wZGQBZjxuXy\nPMPuVko49IfTSGiaY4DBvZjznnpaSdrAs4tetB55WlJ0JGkhiEgvpqgbUOwZKmI0\nYqARFvM86zokEG9T9L6w\n=VcK5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T13:49:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred