,"sha":"94d1e56c97b754e178d4ba8e5209577e65712ecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/94d1e56c97b754e178d4ba8e5209577e65712ecc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/feoh","id":330070,"login":"feoh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDA3MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/82906863bd5d00f1f6813d5d035ec854f03db135/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T23:23:10Z","email":"feoh@feoh.org","name":"Christopher Patti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T23:23:10Z","email":"feoh@feoh.org","name":"Christopher Patti"},"message":"ci: run hooks with prek and autofix.ci\n\nPin prek 0.5.4 in its own dependency group, included by dev, and copy the autofix.ci uv workflow with the full project environment for the schema generators. Switch the three fast-checks hook commands and developer instructions to prek.\n\nRemove the unused ci block and packer_fmt hook (no .pkr.hcl files). Keep every other hook unchanged, including bootstrap-schema.\n\nPart of https://github.com/mitodl/ol-infrastructure/issues/5805","tree":{"sha":"898cbd0c753efb2d0fa1d8c44eb871d1662b8afc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/898cbd0c753efb2d0fa1d8c44eb871d1662b8afc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/82906863bd5d00f1f6813d5d035ec854f03db135","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330070?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/feoh","id":330070,"login":"feoh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDA3MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feoh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/82906863bd5d00f1f6813d5d035ec854f03db135","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDgyOTA2ODYzYmQ1ZDAwZjFmNjgxM2Q1ZDAzNWVjODU0ZjAzZGIxMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/30e21900dcbd4a341882fe5f45798e46ae3bf1ef","sha":"30e21900dcbd4a341882fe5f45798e46ae3bf1ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/30e21900dcbd4a341882fe5f45798e46ae3bf1ef"}],"sha":"82906863bd5d00f1f6813d5d035ec854f03db135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/82906863bd5d00f1f6813d5d035ec854f03db135"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/30e21900dcbd4a341882fe5f45798e46ae3bf1ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:44:05Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:44:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(bootstrap): apply a typed bootstrap spec, and drive edxapp-provision with it (#274)\n\n* feat(bootstrap): apply a typed bootstrap spec, and drive edxapp-provision with it\n\nGetting a fresh install usable was a local-dev-only Django script\n(provision.py) plus a waffle flag argv list, and nothing in either repo\ncreates the OAuth applications a deployed LMS needs. This adds\nlehrer.bootstrap: a Pydantic spec for users, DOT applications (with\ntheir ApplicationAccess scopes) and waffle flags, and a runner the\nplatform image carries as lehrer_bootstrap. Each step converges on the\nspec and prints one JSON line per object. Secrets are named by env var,\nnever inlined, so a spec can live in a ConfigMap.\n\nThe edxapp-provision Job now runs the runner against\nlocal-dev/provision/bootstrap.yaml. Its pod template carries a hash of\nthe spec, so editing the spec replaces the Job and re-runs it; before,\nthe edit only updated the ConfigMap of a Job that had already finished.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015kKXdAfrJrpNfoz9Bh1X5b\n\n* fix(bootstrap): refuse a duplicate app name, take waffle percent as an int\n\nApplications are matched on client_id, so rotating one in the Secret\nwould have created a second row under the same name. edxnotes fetches\nits application by name and would then 500 on MultipleObjectsReturned.\nThe runner now fails on that instead.\n\nwaffle_flag declares --percent with type=int, so a float percent\nfailed every spec that set one. lehrer dev setup now names the problem\nwhen the spec has no superuser or no password_env for it, instead of\nraising StopIteration or printing $None.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015kKXdAfrJrpNfoz9Bh1X5b\n\n* fix(bootstrap): keep an unchanged password, and report its origin as a literal\n\napply_users called set_password on every run. It salts afresh, and Django\nchecks every session against a hash of the stored password, so each run\nlogged the user out everywhere: on every deploy, once ol-infrastructure''s\npre-deploy Job runs the spec. The password is now set only when\ncheck_password says it differs.\n\nlehrer dev setup printed \"$\" + the spec''s password_env, which CodeQL reads\nas a password reaching a print (py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data) and\nfails the PR on. The value was only a variable name, but it is back to one\nof two literals, as the comment above it already says.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Christopher Patti <feoh@feoh.org>","tree":{"sha":"7abe988d8eb614e65286df71bb05de22032cdf95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/7abe988d8eb614e65286df71bb05de22032cdf95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/30e21900dcbd4a341882fe5f45798e46ae3bf1ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 7abe988d8eb614e65286df71bb05de22032cdf95\nparent d674af3a571476ebb660eebc922ed0c6ce288276\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1790775845 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790775845 -0400\n\nfeat(bootstrap): apply a typed bootstrap spec, and drive edxapp-provision with it (#274)\n\n* feat(bootstrap): apply a typed bootstrap spec, and drive edxapp-provision with it\n\nGetting a fresh install usable was a local-dev-only Django script\n(provision.py) plus a waffle flag argv list, and nothing in either repo\ncreates the OAuth applications a deployed LMS needs. This adds\nlehrer.bootstrap: a Pydantic spec for users, DOT applications (with\ntheir ApplicationAccess scopes) and waffle flags, and a runner the\nplatform image carries as lehrer_bootstrap. Each step converges on the\nspec and prints one JSON line per object. Secrets are named by env var,\nnever inlined, so a spec can live in a ConfigMap.\n\nThe edxapp-provision Job now runs the runner against\nlocal-dev/provision/bootstrap.yaml. Its pod template carries a hash of\nthe spec, so editing the spec replaces the Job and re-runs it; before,\nthe edit only updated the ConfigMap of a Job that had already finished.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015kKXdAfrJrpNfoz9Bh1X5b\n\n* fix(bootstrap): refuse a duplicate app name, take waffle percent as an int\n\nApplications are matched on client_id, so rotating one in the Secret\nwould have created a second row under the same name. edxnotes fetches\nits application by name and would then 500 on MultipleObjectsReturned.\nThe runner now fails on that instead.\n\nwaffle_flag declares --percent with type=int, so a float percent\nfailed every spec that set one. lehrer dev setup now names the problem\nwhen the spec has no superuser or no password_env for it, instead of\nraising StopIteration or printing $None.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015kKXdAfrJrpNfoz9Bh1X5b\n\n* fix(bootstrap): keep an unchanged password, and report its origin as a literal\n\napply_users called set_password on every run. It salts afresh, and Django\nchecks every session against a hash of the stored password, so each run\nlogged the user out everywhere: on every deploy, once ol-infrastructure''s\npre-deploy Job runs the spec. The password is now set only when\ncheck_password says it differs.\n\nlehrer dev setup printed \"$\" + the spec''s password_env, which CodeQL reads\nas a password reaching a print (py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data) and\nfails the PR on. The value was only a variable name, but it is back to one\nof two literals, as the comment above it already says.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Christopher Patti <feoh@feoh.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRIlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGNQQAH0uw0KT6+duc8dVE7JolXF6\nTMH13dJs4QisICNVPLnr6H8g77z2NSPp7IZWYGdeovlSG8r7TpUMjmOqqIj0DWLV\nYHZyoNez9ZvWEQbi4wFUP6k6zlfSQM1lmBuSo8MmEsKLJjnuq+1vcN5phMG6C5cO\nCYyEkUGE5pGxgC4JHALUpdkadfMCkW4N9LVIQSd/g/hRAeXSdobIWM0XlhI17dhd\nsd4C29v7OjyfUBuzmYY4iNTsOBhZeKJwbTEnr1vwBPvwxWvq3CpCMTMl6oKKIWQm\n92vue5Osv9KPz//8Q7sQObz4C4dUFg3QRtFn3U/TFWGp+0coonNA4DZrHnfnMB4K\nvWi6E4sod4QhdHTR2j9/gstjtuphDxeSs+FPPRWVyeq3q20b8z7G/asOJiE79Gz9\nlZodfw7btuH0uLPaLg6P6n8cNr0fm52Izsbi2YDtKeaUrmIog1iXhLewA3bDfejo\njPQEGMTewTh8sqFb7VqsLqZNdE5Lu46Uu+SCvKJBVvXhpYMHgB3eDJbuKsh2awwt\n2YcwMBKubDQp2eoyzgwV4/8Zv/h7MkGGFQr1y/m79++PNGy54/zVZGzuN27R9DUM\neAe8bJwW0zIJ4WSGFzplU8mVn50RIJNSl2159TVl78uG2gW7r+Ts8zIu5/LYNime\nLLPBSI9h2di4jKgiwe/k\n=Xe0c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:44:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/