ebb660eebc922ed0c6ce288276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/d674af3a571476ebb660eebc922ed0c6ce288276"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/a6dd1ebdd63856c216bee5e47c2a0075a388b723/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:38:32Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:38:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mit-ol): read learning MFE course data from React Query on master (#287)\n\nThe course tab bar is missing for learners on the mitxonline course outline and\ncourseware (https://github.mit.edu/mitxonline/mitxonline-issues/issues/1591).\nResponsiveCourseTabs read the tabs through useModel(''courseHomeMeta''), and\nopenedx/frontend-app-learning#2110 stopped mirroring that query into the model\nstore, so useModel returns {} and the component renders nothing. mitxonline\nbuilds the learning MFE from master in every environment.\n\nThis moves the remaining model store readers in the legacy slot config onto the\nqueries for master, with the previous code kept as a verawood variant selected\nthrough build_config.yaml:\n\n- ResponsiveCourseTabs reads its tabs through a per-release useCourseTabs hook.\n  It is imported for every deployment, so ulmo gets the model store variant too.\n  Tabs are keyed by tabId (openedx/frontend-app-learning#2099 dropped the slug\n  the normalizer used to add), and the Course tab is active on the outline page\n  the same way upstream''s isActiveTab handles it.\n- useFeedbackEnrichment reads the course title and unit title from the course\n  home metadata and sequence queries, since #2110 and #2128 left both models\n  empty and feedback submissions went out without them.\n- The unit title override passes sequenceId to BookmarkButton, which #2128 made\n  required so the button can patch the cached sequence.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"188e30144d381ea0b6c92ddfbd314ca5f72004e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/188e30144d381ea0b6c92ddfbd314ca5f72004e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/a6dd1ebdd63856c216bee5e47c2a0075a388b723","verification":{"payload":"tree 188e30144d381ea0b6c92ddfbd314ca5f72004e5\nparent 3460b902cb9d9d8ffccd01df96c853ae7dad73e3\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1790696312 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790696312 -0400\n\nfix(mit-ol): read learning MFE course data from React Query on master (#287)\n\nThe course tab bar is missing for learners on the mitxonline course outline and\ncourseware (https://github.mit.edu/mitxonline/mitxonline-issues/issues/1591).\nResponsiveCourseTabs read the tabs through useModel(''courseHomeMeta''), and\nopenedx/frontend-app-learning#2110 stopped mirroring that query into the model\nstore, so useModel returns {} and the component renders nothing. mitxonline\nbuilds the learning MFE from master in every environment.\n\nThis moves the remaining model store readers in the legacy slot config onto the\nqueries for master, with the previous code kept as a verawood variant selected\nthrough build_config.yaml:\n\n- ResponsiveCourseTabs reads its tabs through a per-release useCourseTabs hook.\n  It is imported for every deployment, so ulmo gets the model store variant too.\n  Tabs are keyed by tabId (openedx/frontend-app-learning#2099 dropped the slug\n  the normalizer used to add), and the Course tab is active on the outline page\n  the same way upstream''s isActiveTab handles it.\n- useFeedbackEnrichment reads the course title and unit title from the course\n  home metadata and sequence queries, since #2110 and #2128 left both models\n  empty and feedback submissions went out without them.\n- The unit title override passes sequenceId to BookmarkButton, which #2128 made\n  required so the button can patch the cached sequence.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu9t4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq+IQAAOdFIjcoUJPVXs7ym1SZiAu\nme1/tO9NzDuKMXU6zW8s6gLQUNfDP2hWeDSGCbuzHrZUiszthTe4k4VyDq/ST1jv\nmoGXpTW5ZEuWAB31EtH66K9Zq/MARjKorQ1OG4c+p+/Bb0A+Yf2FNOl1FjaJauK4\niTs8zmYiwj1M8SnOrebEYZ7LAVzAU5DTZT23XtqODmrPTiosvehr73utD8Hd9OOL\nb5yGypK/hYxn3rGVuFvU90Zydw944I3a+SrGfAljAq1ZXuI/Di1OdR32FTdK40hN\nDen16yF6aPDzwzMkBZrdi2Ys1jCnFYG/hA7Er2xhdbF2Bi719Zoxg01gUycFy0iD\nqGtuVQRFiHkVhfuFBQYIPsdofUC6L/DpqZwmPiLhuPs63Zm8+OPVMTWUfLOtFozF\n1S58EAajh5NQiIywB6rkLt/wflwJM2pGvuz2Yt8tTVVMaAcD3ZTvOPgVjiQ931Lg\nx0F8JJHLTNLCChjhhfQu/4z4jt3v++5ee3Na0HnJTyKUUKQUgMc6mafKSUFbY+W9\n5U0sqGuppXsHiNmlKHA5OPyfNGGMMxUFV9CeQXeoupRRi3aB4DnKVpNbsSrMigQ3\nbALZcjRV8gdCSy0/M4ymN6IwMV9p3I7qQNrYArMm1vW3GucCno8XBs+U5AF1yLjM\ntO7ZzHv+XRx6nKqQmQK0\n=2w5v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:38:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/a6dd1ebdd63856c216bee5e47c2a0075a388b723","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKGE2ZGQxZWJkZDYzODU2YzIxNmJlZTVlNDdjMmEwMDc1YTM4OGI3MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/3460b902cb9d9d8ffccd01df96c853ae7dad73e3","sha":"3460b902cb9d9d8ffccd01df96c853ae7dad73e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/3460b902cb9d9d8ffccd01df96c853ae7dad73e3"}],"sha":"a6dd1ebdd63856c216bee5e47c2a0075a388b723","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/a6dd1ebdd63856c216bee5e47c2a0075a388b723"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/3460b902cb9d9d8ffccd01df96c853ae7dad73e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:31:13Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:31:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mitxonline): serve admin-console and gradebook from the Site Project (#285)\n\n* feat(mitxonline): serve admin-console and gradebook from the Site Project\n\nUpstream landed the frontend-base conversions of frontend-app-admin-console and\nfrontend-app-gradebook, and mitxonline''s legacy builds of both now run from the\nlegacy-mfe branch (ol-infrastructure #6058). This adds both module libraries to\nthe mitxonline Site Project so the legacy builds can be retired.\n\nThey are registered as-is rather than through wrapWithAppsPath. Both declare\nabsolute route paths (/admin-console/authz/*, /gradebook/:courseId), which React\nRouter will not nest under the relative \"apps\" parent, and admin-console builds\nits own links from that absolute base. Those are the URLs the legacy MFEs served\nand the LMS already links to, so Fastly routes those paths to the Site Project\ninstead (ol-infrastructure change to follow) and no LMS setting changes.\n\nadmin-console''s error page links \"back\" to whatever resolves\norg.openedx.frontend.role.courseAuthoring. Nothing here registers that role, so\nthis adds an externalRoutes entry with the production Studio authoring URL, the\nsame target as the legacy build''s COURSE_AUTHORING_MICROFRONTEND_URL.\nFRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG supplies each environment''s own URL at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FP7D3ULwwxXhgN8hFfb8DF\n\n* fix(mitxonline): take the course authoring route from runtime config only\n\nThe static externalRoutes entry pinned the production Studio URL into a bundle\nthat is promoted CI -> QA -> Production. A relative URL cannot replace it,\nbecause authoring is served from the Studio host and the Site Project from the\nLMS host. FRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG already supplies each environment''s\nhttps://<studio>/authoring (mitodl/ol-infrastructure#6064), so this drops the\nstatic fallback. Doing so also removes the need to keep two lists in the same\norder for the by-index merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FP7D3ULwwxXhgN8hFfb8DF\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca69e3f032053b1e7fa7ff65836de3b7704b29dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/ca69e3f032053b1e7fa7ff65836de3b7704b29dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/3460b902cb9d9d8ffccd01df96c853ae7dad73e3","verification":{"payload":"tree ca69e3f032053b1e7fa7ff65836de3b7704b29dd\nparent a9ffbbc964ff7cb07cae830ebc9baf90a9f948fb\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1790623873 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790623873 -0400\n\nfeat(mitxonline): serve admin-console and gradebook from the Site Project (#285)\n\n* feat(mitxonline): serve admin-console and gradebook from the Site Project\n\nUpstream landed the frontend-base conversions of frontend-app-admin-console and\nfrontend-app-gradebook, and mitxonline''s legacy builds of both now run from the\nlegacy-mfe branch (ol-infrastructure #6058). This adds both module libraries to\nthe mitxonline Site Project so the legacy builds can be retired.\n\nThey are registered as-is rather than through wrapWithAppsPath. Both declare\nabsolute route paths (/admin-console/authz/*, /gradebook/:courseId), which React\nRouter will not nest under the relative \"apps\" parent, and admin-console builds\nits own links from that absolute base. Those are the URLs the legacy MFEs served\nand the LMS already links to, so Fastly routes those paths to the Site Project\ninstead (ol-infrastructure change to follow) and no LMS setting changes.\n\nadmin-console''s error page links \"back\" to whatever resolves\norg.openedx.frontend.role.courseAuthoring. Nothing here registers that role, so\nthis adds an externalRoutes entry with the production Studio authoring URL, the\nsame target as the legacy build''s COURSE_AUTHORING_MICROFRONTEND_URL.\nFRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG supplies each environment''s own URL at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FP7D3ULwwxXhgN8hFfb8DF\n\n* fix(mitxonline): take the course authoring route from runtime config only\n\nThe static externalRoutes entry pinned the production Studio URL into a bundle\nthat is promoted CI -> QA -> Production. A relative URL cannot replace it,\nbecause authoring is served from the Studio host and the Site Project from the\nLMS host. FRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG already supplies each environment''s\nhttps://<studio>/authoring (mitodl/ol-infrastructure#6064), so this drops the\nstatic fallback. Doing so also removes the need to keep two lists in the same\norder for the by-index merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FP7D3ULwwxXhgN8hFfb8DF\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqusCBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb68QAFP3OVETp0b0llw7mG21P2Vf\naFZ9nzvl2gldZks1n68jj1gjJNu6W3vsrYLRCMpUdLvfckGHuCwXlcICwVY/jlr4\njr8MRdeQ7ESMosyU9bzufmaJ0P8x5aBke7Ny6XJCmOk4Wjba9Oh0OcIQhTbiwGcs\nI3bDR2I0FQZu/8fIV2GQT6evrzAv+6NQL+uaFGelAKCFEACcGVhbvYr