/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/d6f7a3ec5a859ccd223eb326ecea549fc9507ba5","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKGQ2ZjdhM2VjNWE4NTljY2QyMjNlYjMyNmVjZWE1NDlmYzk1MDdiYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e","sha":"14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e"}],"sha":"d6f7a3ec5a859ccd223eb326ecea549fc9507ba5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/d6f7a3ec5a859ccd223eb326ecea549fc9507ba5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:42:58Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:42:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Route local dev by port and make a fresh stack able to log in to the LMS and Studio (#242)\n\n* fix(local-dev): drop the notes port-forward and point the notes public API at notes.localhost\n\nThe notes resource forwarded host port 8001, which the k3d loadbalancer\nalready binds, so the forward never bound and Tilt retried it in a loop\nfor the life of the session (\"bind: address already in use\").\n\nHost port 8001 reaches notes only through Traefik''s notes.localhost\nIngress rule. A bare localhost:8001 matches no rule and 404s, so\nEDXNOTES_PUBLIC_API now names notes.localhost:8001.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): say the loadbalancer ports route by host, not by port\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): route by port, and make a fresh stack able to log in to the LMS and Studio\n\nOn a fresh standalone stack nothing could be logged in to. Every\nloadbalancer port landed on Traefik''s one host-routed entrypoint, which\nmatched only lms./studio./notes.localhost, while every configured URL\n(and dev-hosts.json: localhost for generic, local.openedx.io for mit-ol)\nnamed something else, so LMS, Studio and notes all 404ed. Behind that,\nthree more gaps:\n\n- CACHES was never set, so every alias pointed at a memcached on\n  localhost:11211 that nothing runs, and the cache-backed session engine\n  could not create a session.\n- JWT_AUTH had no signing key, so every login failed minting its JWT\n  cookie (json.loads(None) in _encode_and_sign).\n- Studio had no SSO client, no SOCIAL_AUTH_EDX_OAUTH2_* settings, and\n  shared the `sessionid` cookie name with the LMS on the same host.\n\nThis gives LMS (8000), Studio (8010) and notes (8001) a Traefik\nentrypoint each, applied to k3s''s bundled Traefik by `lehrer dev setup`,\nso the port picks the service and any hostname resolving to 127.0.0.1\nworks. k3d fixes port mappings at create time, so an existing cluster\nmust be recreated; setup and start warn when one no longer matches\nk3d-config.yaml. The k3s image is pinned so the bundled chart''s values\nschema can''t drift.\n\nSettings: CACHE_REDIS_URL builds CACHES on the stack''s Valkey (DB 1);\nJWT_PRIVATE_SIGNING_JWK / JWT_PUBLIC_SIGNING_JWK_SET are merged into\nJWT_AUTH by a post_configure hook, since JWT_AUTH is a common.py dict a\nvalidator cannot see; StudioSettingsMixin declares the Studio SSO\nsettings so they can arrive from env. All of them no-op when unset, so\ndeployments that supply CACHES/JWT_AUTH/SSO through YAML are unaffected.\n\nedxapp-provision now registers the cms-sso application (redirect URI\nfrom CMS_ROOT_URL, user_id scope), and secret-defaults.yaml carries its\ncredentials and a committed local-dev JWK pair.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): put caches on the broker host, declare the broker fields, and stop the workers flapping\n\nReview follow-ups to the previous commit, plus what the rebuilt stack\nturned up.\n\nCACHES now builds on CELERY_BROKER_HOSTNAME (CACHE_REDIS_DB picks the\nDB) instead of a URL of its own. ol-infrastructure''s local-dev repoints\nthe broker at a shared Valkey and does not run redis-valkey.openedx, and\nDjango''s RedisCache raises on an unreachable host where the memcached\ndefault failed silently, so a separate URL would have broken that caller.\n\nDeriving from the broker host exposed that no CELERY_BROKER_* field was\never declared: the env source dropped them all and BROKER_URL was built\nas redis://:@/, which is why the workers never reached the broker. They\nare declared on ProductionSettingsMixin now.\n\nWith the broker reachable, the workers'' liveness probe was what killed\nthem: `celery inspect ping` starts a CLI that loads the Django settings,\nwhich takes about 10s here, against a 10s timeout. It gets 30s.\n\nSOCIAL_AUTH_REDIRECT_IS_HTTPS defaults to True, auth_backends'' own\ndefault, because a field common.py lacks reaches Django at its default\nand None would switch the https rewrite off rather than fall back.\n\nk3d-config.yaml lowers kubelet eviction-minimum-reclaim to 1%. Each\nplatform rebuild leaves a ~6GB image on the host disk; once that disk\ncrossed k3s''s 5% eviction line, the default 10% reclaim kept both nodes\ntainted until 15% was free, and nothing could reschedule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): build the cache URL from the broker''s scheme and credentials\n\nThe cache URL hardcoded redis:// and dropped CELERY_BROKER_USER, so a\ncaller pairing CACHE_REDIS_DB with a TLS broker that has an ACL user\n(rediss://default:...@host) would have got a plaintext, userless\nconnection. BROKER_URL and CACHES now share one helper for the server\npart. Also corrects the comment on why the broker fields need\ndeclaring: openedx/envs/common.py does define them, but only through a\nstar import that codegen does not follow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): carry the broker''s TLS options into the derived caches\n\nCelery signals TLS out of band: CELERY_BROKER_TRANSPORT stays \"redis\" and\nCELERY_BROKER_USE_SSL carries the options, which _derive_broker_url hands\nto Celery as BROKER_USE_SSL. The cache LOCATION was built from the\ntransport alone, so against a TLS-only Redis/Valkey the workers would\nconnect and Django''s cache-backed sessions would not.\n\n_derive_caches now maps a TLS broker''s \"redis\" to \"rediss\", which selects\nredis-py''s SSLConnection, and passes the options dict through cache\nOPTIONS. Django''s RedisCacheClient forwards anything beyond pool_class /\nparser_class / serializer to ConnectionPool.from_url, so ssl_cert_reqs\nand friends reach the connection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n* fix(local-dev): warn when a required loadbalancer host port is unmapped\n\nThe stale-cluster check only compared host ports the existing\nloadbalancer already binds, so a cluster created before 8001 and 8010\nexisted at all got no warning even though notes and Studio were\nunreachable. Compare every configured pair and report a missing mapping\nthe same way as a misrouted one.\n\nThe entrypoint agreement test asserted only that each Traefik\nexposedPort appears somewhere on the loadbalancer side, which a swapped\npair (8000:8010, 8010:8000) satisfies while sending every LMS request to\nStudio. It now asserts each entrypoint is mapped from its own host port.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n* fix(local-dev): default the Django caches to Valkey DB 3, not DB 1\n\nThe platform ConfigMaps are applied whole by callers that repoint the\nbroker at a Valkey they share with other applications: ol-infrastructure''s\nlocal-dev passes apply_platform_configmaps and overrides only\nCELERY_BROKER_HOSTNAME, so it inherits this DB onto a server where DB 0-2\nalready hold mit-learn''s cache and the Celery broker and result backend of\nmitxonline, learn-ai and odl-video-service. Django''s RedisCache.clear() is\na FLUSHDB, so an LMS or Studio cache clear there would drop another app''s\nqueues.\n\nDB 3 is unused on that server and equally free on the standalone stack''s\nown Valkey, where only the broker (DB 0) is in play.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n* fix(settings): regenerate the master aqueduct models against upstream\n\nThe generic and mit-ol master cells of Settings Verification have been\nred on main since edx-platform master moved: the committed models predate\nCCX_COACH_MICROFRONTEND_URL and the MAINTENANCE_BANNER_TEXT description,\nand still carry a literal DATA_DIR where COMMON_ROOT, COURSES_ROOT,\nENV_ROOT, MEDIA_ROOT, OPENEDX_ROOT, REPO_ROOT and XMODULE_ROOT are now\nderived. Regenerated with `dagger call platform\nregenerate-aqueduct-settings` for generic/master and mit-ol/master.\n\nNothing in lehrer reads DATA_DIR; the derived roots fall through to the\nlive common.py value under django-aqueduct''s overlay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57e2dd554cdfcf39ddb577356b3d4c5656ad6a59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/57e2dd554cdfcf39ddb577356b3d4c5656ad6a59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e","verification":{"payload":"tree 57e2dd554cdfcf39ddb577356b3d4c5656ad6a59\nparent 484b7afedab046bc7ea0b0e91e3b746b8eb1d050\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1790012578 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790012578 -0400\n\nRoute local dev by port and make a fresh stack able to log in to the LMS and Studio (#242)\n\n* fix(local-dev): drop the notes port-forward and point the notes public API at notes.localhost\n\nThe notes resource forwarded host port 8001, which the k3d loadbalancer\nalready binds, so the forward never bound and Tilt retried it in a loop\nfor the life of the session (\"bind: address already in use\").\n\nHost port 8001 reaches notes only through Traefik''s notes.localhost\nIngress rule. A bare localhost:8001 matches no rule and 404s, so\nEDXNOTES_PUBLIC_API now names notes.localhost:8001.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): say the loadbalancer ports route by host, not by port\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): route by port, and make a fresh stack able to log in to the LMS and Studio\n\nOn a fresh standalone stack nothing could be logged in to. Every\nloadbalancer port landed on Traefik''s one host-routed entrypoint, which\nmatched only lms./studio./notes.localhost, while every configured URL\n(and dev-hosts.json: localhost for generic, local.openedx.io for mit-ol)\nnamed something else, so LMS, Studio and notes all 404ed. Behind that,\nthree more gaps:\n\n- CACHES was never set, so every alias pointed at a memcached on\n  localhost:11211 that nothing runs, and the cache-backed session engine\n  could not create a session.\n- JWT_AUTH had no signing key, so every login failed minting its JWT\n  cookie (json.loads(None) in _encode_and_sign).\n- Studio had no SSO client, no SOCIAL_AUTH_EDX_OAUTH2_* settings, and\n  shared the `sessionid` cookie name with the LMS on the same host.\n\nThis gives LMS (8000), Studio (8010) and notes (8001) a Traefik\nentrypoint each, applied to k3s''s bundled Traefik by `lehrer dev setup`,\nso the port picks the service and any hostname resolving to 127.0.0.1\nworks. k3d fixes port mappings at create time, so an existing cluster\nmust be recreated; setup and start warn when one no longer matches\nk3d-config.yaml. The k3s image is pinned so the bundled chart''s values\nschema can''t drift.\n\nSettings: CACHE_REDIS_URL builds CACHES on the stack''s Valkey (DB 1);\nJWT_PRIVATE_SIGNING_JWK / JWT_PUBLIC_SIGNING_JWK_SET are merged into\nJWT_AUTH by a post_configure hook, since JWT_AUTH is a common.py dict a\nvalidator cannot see; StudioSettingsMixin declares the Studio SSO\nsettings so they can arrive from env. All of them no-op when unset, so\ndeployments that supply CACHES/JWT_AUTH/SSO through YAML are unaffected.\n\nedxapp-provision now registers the cms-sso application (redirect URI\nfrom CMS_ROOT_URL, user_id scope), and secret-defaults.yaml carries its\ncredentials and a committed local-dev JWK pair.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): put caches on the broker host, declare the broker fields, and stop the workers flapping\n\nReview follow-ups to the previous commit, plus what the rebuilt stack\nturned up.\n\nCACHES now builds on CELERY_BROKER_HOSTNAME (CACHE_REDIS_DB picks the\nDB) instead of a URL of its own. ol-infrastructure''s local-dev repoints\nthe broker at a shared Valkey and does not run redis-valkey.openedx, and\nDjango''s RedisCache raises on an unreachable host where the memcached\ndefault failed silently, so a separate URL would have broken that caller.\n\nDeriving from the broker host exposed that no CELERY_BROKER_* field was\never declared: the env source dropped them all and BROKER_URL was built\nas redis://:@/, which is why the workers never reached the broker. They\nare declared on ProductionSettingsMixin now.\n\nWith the broker reachable, the workers'' liveness probe was what killed\nthem: `celery inspect ping` starts a CLI that loads the Django settings,\nwhich takes about 10s here, against a 10s timeout. It gets 30s.\n\nSOCIAL_AUTH_REDIRECT_IS_HTTPS defaults to True, auth_backends'' own\ndefault, because a field common.py lacks reaches Django at its default\nand None would switch the https rewrite off rather than fall back.\n\nk3d-config.yaml lowers kubelet eviction-minimum-reclaim to 1%. Each\nplatform rebuild leaves a ~6GB image on the host disk; once that disk\ncrossed k3s''s 5% eviction line, the default 10% reclaim kept both nodes\ntainted until 15% was free, and nothing could reschedule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): build the cache URL from the broker''s scheme and credentials\n\nThe cache URL hardcoded redis:// and dropped CELERY_BROKER_USER, so a\ncaller pairing CACHE_REDIS_DB with a TLS broker that has an ACL user\n(rediss://default:...@host) would have got a plaintext, userless\nconnection. BROKER_URL and CACHES now share one helper for the server\npart. Also corrects the comment on why the broker fields need\ndeclaring: openedx/envs/common.py does define them, but only through a\nstar import that codegen does not follow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KsDfYZtWMXh4uxGPoJEx91\n\n* fix(local-dev): carry the broker''s TLS options into the derived caches\n\nCelery signals TLS out of band: CELERY_BROKER_TRANSPORT stays \"redis\" and\nCELERY_BROKER_USE_SSL carries the options, which _derive_broker_url hands\nto Celery as BROKER_USE_SSL. The cache LOCATION was built from the\ntransport alone, so against a TLS-only Redis/Valkey the workers would\nconnect and Django''s cache-backed sessions would not.\n\n_derive_caches now maps a TLS broker''s \"redis\" to \"rediss\", which selects\nredis-py''s SSLConnection, and passes the options dict through cache\nOPTIONS. Django''s RedisCacheClient forwards anything beyond pool_class /\nparser_class / serializer to ConnectionPool.from_url, so ssl_cert_reqs\nand friends reach the connection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n* fix(local-dev): warn when a required loadbalancer host port is unmapped\n\nThe stale-cluster check only compared host ports the existing\nloadbalancer already binds, so a cluster created before 8001 and 8010\nexisted at all got no warning even though notes and Studio were\nunreachable. Compare every configured pair and report a missing mapping\nthe same way as a misrouted one.\n\nThe entrypoint agreement test asserted only that each Traefik\nexposedPort appears somewhere on the loadbalancer side, which a swapped\npair (8000:8010, 8010:8000) satisfies while sending every LMS request to\nStudio. It now asserts each entrypoint is mapped from its own host port.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n* fix(local-dev): default the Django caches to Valkey DB 3, not DB 1\n\nThe platform ConfigMaps are applied whole by callers that repoint the\nbroker at a Valkey they share with other applications: ol-infrastructure''s\nlocal-dev passes apply_platform_configmaps and overrides only\nCELERY_BROKER_HOSTNAME, so it inherits this DB onto a server where DB 0-2\nalready hold mit-learn''s cache and the Celery broker and result backend of\nmitxonline, learn-ai and odl-video-service. Django''s RedisCache.clear() is\na FLUSHDB, so an LMS or Studio cache clear there would drop another app''s\nqueues.\n\nDB 3 is unused on that server and equally free on the standalone stack''s\nown Valkey, where only the broker (DB 0) is in play.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n* fix(settings): regenerate the master aqueduct models against upstream\n\nThe generic and mit-ol master cells of Settings Verification have been\nred on main since edx-platform master moved: the committed models predate\nCCX_COACH_MICROFRONTEND_URL and the MAINTENANCE_BANNER_TEXT description,\nand still carry a literal DATA_DIR where COMMON_ROOT, COURSES_ROOT,\nENV_ROOT, MEDIA_ROOT, OPENEDX_ROOT, REPO_ROOT and XMODULE_ROOT are now\nderived. Regenerated with `dagger call platform\nregenerate-aqueduct-settings` for generic/master and mit-ol/master.\n\nNothing in lehrer reads DATA_DIR; the derived roots fall through to the\nlive common.py value under django-aqueduct''s overlay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QE9PZSMAVijFfsyPLf9yiP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsWyiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv60QADLctRt5NUSK7La5LyGBOR1U\nMNFlBwmvxkYoB2aIdJbSdq2jl3mCqrSmlrXolVwbk2oTrL7WQloqpV8oJ0Y7HslH\nfiyWJ/g9LfBrqrew8PNXsO60JsJbVgllRsLiNU7k1CbB9gcX0HNcRblDlnSmgJsL\nmEDUZXkTJ2DyqxMJ/qf5nqr+Oi3XRzOiNZqEK1ANvdfkAFSY8y0SbLBsfRnOazr6\nD1yxTEz5SOexUsfC9t9+8W+HpLoH9rhFKIInSyzANU5F1ttcJ0WDjw7zRI/+H7SI\nTz6JmXXdRRUYuj+j8d5j+uBg1p+3+O/djPy7OIT/OkGU0OzPddAsdfObZ1lnRtg1\n6SIwMAVuMHAmsghePdyutWpD8ZE7AVsjfJ9N8P8V7uvvSBA8SBnhUGyBxeSI7rqp\nWB0QbEJNZJiOyIAYzGMsOzIeeMae+WxicSIjd5ew9RJtu6Z21jG9/E1A8oe5d6oF\nZr+2e2v6DzgFEX+HBG94pqtsBJV//PZPc6+6qnnUrOGUyIiypI4pFh4AuiicK87Y\nDWDUfYTQa7TuNd7GiNR+Vc/GDg47NvnjXzFAJ9tNJqA5vchyF1saHxZXVp/c4wtw\nDIFJsNnSklm7c+1xa34gJE9/Y8XJoOvio8AHIyE5icfVoeKomom7QHzjqUW1FQwx\n7i4Di7F6aSeQCv8TlftO\n=qZ+F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T17:42:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDE0ZTMwZDlkMWRlNjdiMjM0OTRiNGE4OWZkZDkwYWVlMzljMDA1MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/484b7afedab046bc7ea0b0e91e3b746b8eb1d050","sha":"484b7afedab046bc7ea0b0e91e3b746b8eb1d050","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/484b7afedab046bc7ea0b0e91e3b746b8eb1d050"}],"sha":"14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/14e30d9d1de67b23494b4a89fdd90aee39c0050e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52656433?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asadali145","id":52656433,"login":"asadali145","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNjU2NDMz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/484b7afedab046bc7ea0b0e91e3b746b8eb1d050/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:30:05Z","email":"asad.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Asad Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:30:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ol_openedx_course_sync): Course Sync tab for problem actions (#235)\n\n* feat(mitxonline): Course Sync tab for problem actions\n\nRenders the page behind the Course Sync tab that ol_openedx_course_sync adds to\nthe instructor dashboard: pick reset attempts or rescore, give a problem id, and\nthe action fans out to the source course and every course synced from it.\n\nRegistered in the mitxonline Site Project rather than @shared, since\nol_openedx_course_sync is only installed on mitxonline — mitx and xpro keep the\nshared factory''s tab set. Only the route widget is registered here; the nav tab\nitself comes from the LMS filter, so the tab surfaces exactly where the backend\nplugin applies.\n\nROUTES_SLOT_ID and PlaceholderSlot are now exported from the shared factory so a\nSite Project can register its own route widgets. The upstream package defines\nboth but does not re-export them, and its exports map has no subpath, so they\ncannot be deep-imported.\n\nBackend: https://github.com/mitodl/open-edx-plugins/pull/871\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mitxonline): rename Course Sync tab heading, bold higher-score checkbox label\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mitxonline): reset Course Sync page state on course change\n\nReact Router keeps the same CourseSyncPage instance when only :courseId\nchanges, so a stale problem ID and result set carried over into the next\ncourse. Reset all local state on courseId change and ignore any in-flight\nsubmission whose response arrives after the course has already changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mitxonline): rename Course Sync page to Course Sync Actions\n\nAlign the frontend naming with the tab title the plugin emits: rename\nCourseSyncPage to CourseSyncActionsPage (file, component, CSS class),\nthe route widget id, and the README references.\n\nThe `tabId` and the `course_sync/api` URL prefix stay as-is — both are\ncontracts with ol_openedx_course_sync (COURSE_SYNC_TAB_ID and the plugin''s\nLMS URL namespace).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mitxonline): follow the plugin rename of the course sync tab id\n\nTrack the ol_openedx_course_sync rename: the tab id the filter emits is now\n`course_sync_actions`, and the plugin''s LMS URLs moved to\n`/courses/<course>/course_sync_actions/api/`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb1071eba3607658a6d118de6bf8b8aeb9bbd0fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/cb1071eba3607658a6d118de6bf8b8aeb9bbd0fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/484b7afedab046bc7ea0b0e91e3b746b8eb1d050","verification":{"payload":"tree cb1071eba3607658a6d118de6bf8b8aeb9bbd0fd\nparent 93c77a787ff59484d2c0a9ccd7f8152dd9ff426e\nauthor Asad Ali <asad.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789983005 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789983005 +0500\n\nfeat(ol_openedx_course_sync): Course Sync tab for problem actions (#235)\n\n* feat(mitxonline): Course Sync tab for problem actions\n\nRenders the page behind the Course Sync tab that ol_openedx_course_sync adds to\nthe instructor dashboard: pick reset attempts or rescore, give a problem id, and\nthe action fans out to the source course and every course synced from it.\n\nRegistered in the mitxonline Site Project rather than @shared, since\nol_openedx_course_sync is only installed on mitxonline — mitx and xpro keep the\nshared factory''s tab set. Only the route widget is registered here; the nav tab\nitself comes from the LMS filter, so the tab surfaces exactly where the backend\nplugin applies.\n\nROUTES_SLOT_ID and PlaceholderSlot are now exported from the shared factory so a\nSite Project can register its own route widgets. The upstream package defines\nboth but does not re-export them, and its exports map has no subpath, so they\ncannot be deep-imported.\n\nBackend: https://github.com/mitodl/open-edx-plugins/pull/871\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mitxonline): rename Course Sync tab heading, bold higher-score checkbox label\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mitxonline): reset Course Sync page state on course change\n\nReact Router keeps the same CourseSyncPage instance when only :courseId\nchanges, so a stale problem ID and result set carried over into the next\ncourse. Reset all local state on courseId change and ignore any in-flight\nsubmission whose response arrives after the course has already changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mitxonline): rename Course Sync page to Course Sync Actions\n\nAlign the frontend naming with the tab title the plugin emits: rename\nCourseSyncPage to CourseSyncActionsPage (file, component, CSS class),\nthe route widget id, and the README references.\n\nThe `tabId` and the `course_sync/api` URL prefix stay as-is — both are\ncontracts with ol_openedx_course_sync (COURSE_SYNC_TAB_ID and the plugin''s\nLMS URL namespace).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mitxonline): follow the plugin rename of the course sync tab id\n\nTrack the ol_openedx_course_sync rename: the tab id the filter emits is now\n`course_sync_actions`, and the plugin''s LMS URLs moved to\n`/courses/<course>/course_sync_actions/api/`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsPkdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKkYQAFU8qPFIoJFRvB0/dxltS7d1\n94nQTsnlO0oer5O36jXBLqtbiIrSLOfJ0mLa5G5zpnBbfIKP0cnAO7u0AC6kNGoj\nl5HPXjMlfRExdpJdsenmHB/NOCKKQv1jX7U/LnZoCOukoCMu53OxG0uNblcvQYj+\n7mDs6TVZZQ2a1z3aUNgqd9vxJGRZfT2wy5rvmguoqmwGwFyGB/tzbhQWXxbNzfPM\nUPZYS9T2cAvZaOpPrc+0TEwjQFGz5XXlnqkLb9TKGo