","email":"34372316+arslanashraf7@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Arslan Ashraf"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:20:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mit-ol): bump Django-5.2-floor plugin pins for master and verawood cells (#237)\n\nmitodl/open-edx-plugins#845 raised the Django dependency floor to >=5.2\nacross the plugin monorepo and bumped each affected plugin''s minor\nversion accordingly. Bump the corresponding pins in the master and\nverawood build_manifest.yaml cells to match (release/ulmo cells are\nleft untouched).\n\nAlso brings ol-openedx-feedback up from 0.2.1, which was already\nlagging behind the pre-#845 baseline of 0.2.2, and pins\nol-openedx-chat and ol-openedx-uai-content-customization to their\nlatest published PyPI releases (0.6.1 and 0.5.0 respectively), each\none newer than what #845 itself bumped to.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7c5a88e1baf2b5c14de80ef3e23170516f02aab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/f7c5a88e1baf2b5c14de80ef3e23170516f02aab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/fe6c118b53623d7ec98fcd44ec64ee44291856c8","verification":{"payload":"tree f7c5a88e1baf2b5c14de80ef3e23170516f02aab\nparent 02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82\nauthor Arslan Ashraf <34372316+arslanashraf7@users.noreply.github.com> 1789572030 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789572030 -0400\n\nfix(mit-ol): bump Django-5.2-floor plugin pins for master and verawood cells (#237)\n\nmitodl/open-edx-plugins#845 raised the Django dependency floor to >=5.2\nacross the plugin monorepo and bumped each affected plugin''s minor\nversion accordingly. Bump the corresponding pins in the master and\nverawood build_manifest.yaml cells to match (release/ulmo cells are\nleft untouched).\n\nAlso brings ol-openedx-feedback up from 0.2.1, which was already\nlagging behind the pre-#845 baseline of 0.2.2, and pins\nol-openedx-chat and ol-openedx-uai-content-customization to their\nlatest published PyPI releases (0.6.1 and 0.5.0 respectively), each\none newer than what #845 itself bumped to.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrO/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9Y0QAFfCag5lQo8V+eby0Rhk8NTv\nVGPrrHjjeK99dA/VxUMt9A8wcnJbnY8fQzJtJs8539J7BrJybU/weyab9vVJhL+X\nyU5rGAwJWSt4iCJIDI2dsqPa4J5pi5G243prE+gXuLCvfNSGxc3oSVtTiKDlo+D4\nErxeLpLCB1AkHaOh0ray5nh0HVQcb/yo0R57HTRnYKei6dyUIk+IIpRcaHTNtxWa\nkaB7cJpQXZrqcDIlI3VVJWJFVawEvtWeUdppV2+fzKbxgAx5rrmQYK7BcyYQZ8JI\nV61VvUV55hiMuCCzozGlCIbg9blNgSyRRM+UYfeUz+/X+eNydu50mJDOtUq5TojL\nuPzysEcvw2HpKFt5mL1pehWl7EFxKUXJk7DCixlBETZrGDdQdQPjVISgTJaM88oH\nEdo9rCapUCF2vMxUABhE5Pp/Iiuot3hv5CacXDs2RuEo7lrpGrqjXFYZ3NdQAy+b\nb8rFCCYCzmjQFQTj2WWjpdWw5NoueTbAEHfxxP7TPWczc/Kh10Hye6v47LBAsMXR\nWCFaAOgrDIe7NPCA0YjqSgL+KetQ2YLHhm+cBfdvCZqpAlzgYrnpVSIKnrxEt+qm\nr/WbFZbh7XLH05KGSGcimHkAlJaxvn4k2tOJNggrzpU6IQB/ro92Bgw+sTA603em\nSoig0zSs3S8OMDEb9vKn\n=JiHP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T15:20:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/fe6c118b53623d7ec98fcd44ec64ee44291856c8","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKGZlNmMxMThiNTM2MjNkN2VjOThmY2Q0NGVjNjRlZTQ0MjkxODU2Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82","sha":"02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82"}],"sha":"fe6c118b53623d7ec98fcd44ec64ee44291856c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/fe6c118b53623d7ec98fcd44ec64ee44291856c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52656433?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asadali145","id":52656433,"login":"asadali145","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNjU2NDMz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asadali145","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T19:08:04Z","email":"asad.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Asad Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T19:08:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mit-ol): put mitx and xpro on the Verawood dependency line (#234)\n\nmitx and xpro build from edx-platform release/verawood, so they should run the\nfrontend major that release ships. Per OEP-10 ADR 0003, apps built on\nfrontend-base are never branched or tagged for an Open edX release - they\ndeclare openedx.org/release: null and participate by published version only -\nso the major is the release signal. openedx/frontend-template-site is the one\nfrontend repo branched per release, and its release/verawood branch pins\ninstructor-dashboard 1.2.x and frontend-base 1.0.x.\n\nBoth sites now take \"1.x\", the major-line range the upstream README gives as\nthe way for consumers to select a maintained line. 2.x is deliberately out of\nrange: it publishes from the app''s main branch, which takes breaking changes\nwith no DEPR process and is not supported in production, and frontend-base 2\nmoves the whole site to react-intl 10. Updates within 1.x stay ordinary\nreviewable bumps, bounded by a Renovate allowedVersions of <2.\n\nNeither site had a range that said any of this. \"^1.1.0-alpha\" is not a pin at\n1.1: npm expands it to >=1.1.0-alpha <2.0.0, so mitx had been walked to 1.3.0\n(#206) with nothing recording the choice. Resolved versions do not change -\nmitx stays on 1.3.0 and frontend-base on 1.0.1 - so this changes what the\nranges permit, not what ships.\n\nBoth also declare react-intl ^6.8.9, which is what fixes the blank dashboard\nfrom #222. Paragon 23.23.0 widened its react-intl peer range to\n^5.25.1 || ^6.4.0 || ^10.1.20, so npm hoists 10.1.25 for Paragon''s unmet peer\nwhile frontend-base 1.x''s regular dependency react-intl ^6.6.6 nests its own\ncopy; two module instances mean two IntlProvider contexts and every intl-aware\nParagon component throws. Declaring react-intl at the root collapses that to\none 6.8.9 both consumers share. An overrides entry was measured as an\nalternative and touches the identical 28 lockfile entries, so it buys nothing;\nmirroring template-site''s peerDependencies layout was tested and does not fix\nit at all. A Renovate rule keeps react-intl below 7 in these two directories,\nand is dropped alongside the declarations when these sites move to\nfrontend-base 2.\n\nxpro keeps building from the mitodl fork, since upstream\nopenedx/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard#234 is still open, tracking that\nfork''s verawood branch. package-lock.json records the commit it resolved\n(7d6de02), so an install is reproducible, but Renovate''s lock file maintenance\ndeletes the lockfile and re-resolves - so a push to the fork branch is absorbed\nby that run rather than arriving as a deliberate bump. The README says so, and\nsays to treat the branch as frozen or name a commit if that matters.\n\nThe README also gains a \"Version lines\" section, because nothing said which\nversions a site may use or why the three differ: only main (alpha) and stable\n(latest) publish, and frontend-template-site''s release/* branch is the\nauthoritative record of what a release ships, with the master and Verawood rows\nand links to both sources. It states the cost of taking the whole 1.x line\nrather than template-site''s exact 1.2.x - mitx resolves 1.3.0, a minor ahead of\nthat pin, which adds CCX coach pages, the grading policy view and Schedule,\nfeatures calling LMS endpoints release/verawood may not serve. No MIT code\nregisters against them, and narrowing to 1.2.x is the fallback if it matters.\nRange guidance is scoped to stable lines, because a prerelease line has to stay\na caret: npm excludes prereleases from a range that does not name one, so a bare\n2.x matches no published frontend-base version while ^2.0.0-alpha admits the\nalpha line. The xpro fork section is rewritten too - the old revert note named a\n\"^1.0.0-alpha\" range no site uses and treated the upstream merge as the trigger,\nwhen the fixes have to reach npm on a line xpro can install. And the local-dev\nsnapshot command now documents the `rm -rf ./shared` that makes it re-runnable:\na bare `cp -R ../shared ./shared` nests a second copy at ./shared/shared/ once\nthe snapshot exists, leaving stale sources that webpack still resolves.\n\nScope is mitx and xpro only. mitxonline is untouched: #225 moved it to\nfrontend-base 2, which resolves react-intl to a single 10.x on its own.\n\nVerified: both lockfiles resolve a single hoisted react-intl 6.8.9 with\nfrontend-base and paragon deduped onto it; npm ci, tsc --noEmit and a production\n`openedx build` pass for both; and the mitx bundle still carries the\nroutes/tabs/enrollmentActions slots plus the canvas_integration and\nrapid_response route widgets. Those runs predate switching xpro from the commit\nto the branch ref, which resolves the same commit and leaves the dependency tree\nunchanged, so they stand.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7dea66dd6e3abdca0fc1264db0b5c229343b6680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/7dea66dd6e3abdca0fc1264db0b5c229343b6680"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82","verification":{"payload":"tree 7dea66dd6e3abdca0fc1264db0b5c229343b6680\nparent 735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8\nauthor Asad Ali <asad.ali@arbisoft.com> 1789499284 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789499284 +0500\n\nfix(mit-ol): put mitx and xpro on the Verawood dependency line (#234)\n\nmitx and xpro build from edx-platform release/verawood, so they should run the\nfrontend major that release ships. Per OEP-10 ADR 0003, apps built on\nfrontend-base are never branched or tagged for an Open edX release - they\ndeclare openedx.org/release: null and participate by published version only -\nso the major is the release signal. openedx/frontend-template-site is the one\nfrontend repo branched per release, and its release/verawood branch pins\ninstructor-dashboard 1.2.x and frontend-base 1.0.x.\n\nBoth sites now take \"1.x\", the major-line range the upstream README gives as\nthe way for consumers to select a maintained line. 2.x is deliberately out of\nrange: it publishes from the app''s main branch, which takes breaking changes\nwith no DEPR process and is not supported in production, and frontend-base 2\nmoves the whole site to react-intl 10. Updates within 1.x stay ordinary\nreviewable bumps, bounded by a Renovate allowedVersions of <2.\n\nNeither site had a range that said any of this. \"^1.1.0-alpha\" is not a pin at\n1.1: npm expands it to >=1.1.0-alpha <2.0.0, so mitx had been walked to 1.3.0\n(#206) with nothing recording the choice. Resolved versions do not change -\nmitx stays on 1.3.0 and frontend-base on 1.0.1 - so this changes what the\nranges permit, not what ships.\n\nBoth also declare react-intl ^6.8.9, which is what fixes the blank dashboard\nfrom #222. Paragon 23.23.0 widened its react-intl peer range to\n^5.25.1 || ^6.4.0 || ^10.1.20, so npm hoists 10.1.25 for Paragon''s unmet peer\nwhile frontend-base 1.x''s regular dependency react-intl ^6.6.6 nests its own\ncopy; two module instances mean two IntlProvider contexts and every intl-aware\nParagon component throws. Declaring react-intl at the root collapses that to\none 6.8.9 both consumers share. An overrides entry was measured as an\nalternative and touches the identical 28 lockfile entries, so it buys nothing;\nmirroring template-site''s peerDependencies layout was tested and does not fix\nit at all. A Renovate rule keeps react-intl below 7 in these two directories,\nand is dropped alongside the declarations when these sites move to\nfrontend-base 2.\n\nxpro keeps building from the mitodl fork, since upstream\nopenedx/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard#234 is still open, tracking that\nfork''s verawood branch. package-lock.json records the commit it resolved\n(7d6de02), so an install is reproducible, but Renovate''s lock file maintenance\ndeletes the lockfile and re-resolves - so a push to the fork branch is absorbed\nby that run rather than arriving as a deliberate bump. The README says so, and\nsays to treat the branch as frozen or name a commit if that matters.\n\nThe README also gains a \"Version lines\" section, because nothing said which\nversions a site may use or why the three differ: only main (alpha) and stable\n(latest) publish, and frontend-template-site''s release/* branch is the\nauthoritative record of what a release ships, with the master and Verawood rows\nand links to both sources. It states the cost of taking the whole 1.x line\nrather than template-site''s exact 1.2.x - mitx resolves 1.3.0, a minor ahead of\nthat pin, which adds CCX coach pages, the grading policy view and Schedule,\nfeatures calling LMS endpoints release/verawood may not serve. No MIT code\nregisters against them, and narrowing to 1.2.x is the fallback if it matters.\nRange guidance is scoped to stable lines, because a prerelease line has to stay\na caret: npm excludes prereleases from a range that does not name one, so a bare\n2.x matches no published frontend-base version while ^2.0.0-alpha admits the\nalpha line. The xpro fork section is rewritten too - the old revert note named a\n\"^1.0.0-alpha\" range no site uses and treated the upstream merge as the trigger,\nwhen the fixes have to reach npm on a line xpro can install. And the local-dev\nsnapshot command now documents the `rm -rf ./shared` that makes it re-runnable:\na bare `cp -R ../shared ./shared` nests a second copy at ./shared/shared/ once\nthe snapshot exists, leaving stale sources that webpack still resolves.\n\nScope is mitx and xpro only. mitxonline is untouched: #225 moved it to\nfrontend-base 2, which resolves react-intl to a single 10.x on its own.\n\nVerified: both lockfiles resolve a single hoisted react-intl 6.8.9 with\nfrontend-base and paragon deduped onto it; npm ci, tsc --noEmit and a production\n`openedx build` pass for both; and the mitx bundle still carries the\nroutes/tabs/enrollmentActions slots plus the canvas_integration and\nrapid_response route widgets. Those runs predate switching xpro from the commit\nto the branch ref, which resolves the same commit and leaves the dependency tree\nunchanged, so they stand.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqZeUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO20QABiybQpEcYxC4NrrCwcGX8Mj\ns5rHnh6Xni4qiacfZe4/PrNjKa8xMjjgTb8r+C8GxVBMd30Nvsk34inHL5dxJgaF\noVSgmnhu4shDRTQVUfDQ23hLs3jJVA301BNFUDi/+6iYjoEbRAsI8z9yXAOqqfmi\n3XspKsEOMdqSSKPQUW3KHVYP1oNKPWwC3YywdfBQTLm8OckUsDFl7fGQbNi6uFn9\nOlzSjzV/Ud1IuGwjFA32XoB7DUcJeZX6iDMPqW2AkhpSqRyUKWfFuY/gEUFGuWYy\n4gXNw5lpJBisn8I6sa0Hh16C1L760TJfqOCIat3LcFhZ0IzQjWYXkZNZ9jpaJjaj\nNCBXKHaCIf9qsY5kMjsix15FCCFLQfXV/wyufHRYPRJTH23pnnUUt7/n1YjQ3QPK\n3vnsi8CsDKzp/xQKnisN/cmO2Q8fBztJuHZTvL+FlbwmVcfSYSNshp8fCugUdSbH\njZakS24/zdwMmoAK8+2JbsYC+PKx8wPjTw94wSlHqaEXQd4OEU2RMK94zEeRNEis\n7PZI2X5HfWfLM197UUGicV6B19cJ10Zv4migDXfxgJqOkuUEziVuyZxWTJOKpbw2\nWapE2FpMoE92G2Y1NROJJ8Z7uLkMy10e+zYGY5txuT72Y1x1JPNUfKsMmrcKYoIH\n1Ac3CU1fQ0Egcs8z4JvW\n=YMZp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T19:08:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDAyMDAxNDM2ZjEyNGM0NjJiZmNmNTE2ZDlhNzg0OTY2MjUwZDNmODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8","sha":"735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8"}],"sha":"02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/02001436f124c462bfcf516d9a784966250d3f82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88967643?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Anas12091101","id":88967643,"login":"Anas12091101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4OTY3NjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Anas12091101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:04:01Z","email":"88967643+Anas12091101@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Muhammad Anas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:04:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump mitxonline instructor-dashboard to ^2.0.0-alpha (#225)\n\nPicks up openedx/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard#233, which reports\npending enrollments for unregistered email addresses. That fix merged to\nthe app''s main branch and ships only on the alpha dist-tag; it was never\nbackported to stable, so 1.3.0 cannot provide it.\n\n2.0.0-alpha peer-requires @openedx/frontend-base ^2.0.0-alpha.5, so that\npin moves to ^2.0.0-alpha in the same change. Both ranges now match what\nopenedx/frontend-template-site pins on its main branch, which is the\nfrontend set that tracks edx-platform master - the branch mitxonline\nbuilds from.\n\nThis also fixes the duplicate react-intl that has been breaking the\nmitxonline dashboard since #222. frontend-base 1.x depends on react-intl\n^6.6.6 while Paragon 23.23.0 widened its react-intl peer range to admit\n10.x, so npm hoisted 10.1.25 for Paragon''s unmet peer and nested 6.8.9\nunder frontend-base - two module instances, two IntlProvider contexts,\nand ''Could not find required intl object'' on every intl-aware component.\nfrontend-base 2.0.0-alpha.13 depends on react-intl ^10.1.20, which\nParagon''s peer range accepts, so the tree collapses to a single\nreact-intl 10.1.25 with no pin or override needed.\n\nThe lockfile was regenerated by applying the two range changes one at a\ntime, each followed by `npm install --package-lock-only`. Moving both at\nonce makes npm re-resolve far more of the tree than the change requires -\n67 unrelated packages, webpack, sass, typescript-eslint and the rest of\nthe build toolchain - because the instructor dashboard cannot satisfy its\nfrontend-base peer until frontend-base has already moved. Applied in\norder, the diff is the two version changes plus the removal of the 20\nnested @formatjs/react-intl entries frontend-base 1.x required.\n\nScope is mitxonline only: its two manifest files and the one README row\nthat records its version. mitx and xpro are untouched here; #234 moves\nthose onto the Verawood line.\n\nVerified: npm ci, tsc --noEmit and a production `openedx build` all pass;\nexactly one react-intl on disk at 10.1.25 with Paragon deduped onto it;\nand the built bundle still carries the enrollmentActions.mitxonline\nwidget plus the canvas_integration and rapid_response route widgets.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a204ab7f9f43fe869177ceddb4377be5c0949c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/a204ab7f9f43fe869177ceddb4377be5c0949c2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8","verification":{"payload":"tree a204ab7f9f43fe869177ceddb4377be5c0949c2c\nparent a2b303b7314b8d4d50a4b8cce061c1bcd280370a\nauthor Muhammad Anas <88967643+Anas12091101@users.noreply.github.com> 1789495441 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789495441 +0500\n\nchore(deps): bump mitxonline instructor-dashboard to ^2.0.0-alpha (#225)\n\nPicks up openedx/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard#233, which reports\npending enrollments for unregistered email addresses. That fix merged to\nthe app''s main branch and ships only on the alpha dist-tag; it was never\nbackported to stable, so 1.3.0 cannot provide it.\n\n2.0.0-alpha peer-requires @openedx/frontend-base ^2.0.0-alpha.5, so that\npin moves to ^2.0.0-alpha in the same change. Both ranges now match what\nopenedx/frontend-template-site pins on its main branch, which is the\nfrontend set that tracks edx-platform master - the branch mitxonline\nbuilds from.\n\nThis also fixes the duplicate react-intl that has been breaking the\nmitxonline dashboard since #222. frontend-base 1.x depends on react-intl\n^6.6.6 while Paragon 23.23.0 widened its react-intl peer range to admit\n10.x, so npm hoisted 10.1.25 for Paragon''s unmet peer and nested 6.8.9\nunder frontend-base - two module instances, two IntlProvider contexts,\nand ''Could not find required intl object'' on every intl-aware component.\nfrontend-base 2.0.0-alpha.13 depends on react-intl ^10.1.20, which\nParagon''s peer range accepts, so the tree collapses to a single\nreact-intl 10.1.25 with no pin or override needed.\n\nThe lockfile was regenerated by applying the two range changes one at a\ntime, each followed by `npm install --package-lock-only`. Moving both at\nonce makes npm re-resolve far more of the tree than the change requires -\n67 unrelated packages, webpack, sass, typescript-eslint and the rest of\nthe build toolchain - because the instructor dashboard cannot satisfy its\nfrontend-base peer until frontend-base has already moved. Applied in\norder, the diff is the two version changes plus the removal of the 20\nnested @formatjs/react-intl entries frontend-base 1.x required.\n\nScope is mitxonline only: its two manifest files and the one README row\nthat records its version. mitx and xpro are untouched here; #234 moves\nthose onto the Verawood line.\n\nVerified: npm ci, tsc --noEmit and a production `openedx build` all pass;\nexactly one react-intl on disk at 10.1.25 with Paragon deduped onto it;\nand the built bundle still carries the enrollmentActions.mitxonline\nwidget plus the canvas_integration and rapid_response route widgets.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqYiRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2qQQABcSSUwcQeWjggqUAxD1eINv\n+2cI69kM1LfZnzib3q+M6+k8ar7cHRUHYZoiiwc71cNnd+uh3oTACUaxCj0Tyu5p\nx2e2MxMpnsAjNAcgFgmKPPcy58OKGxhZ4DJwGShuvNQvwFTvsTgZMl/HQFXkpvFC\neKbek3NLW1ophmpW93t1zzIxEK7CrjxhYhH/oLnm6MVDnpfGQdzXz25JUWzI9wWU\njxwJL2oPlcDL2wuaYYrxLC18yyohkwZOnfPNAIIsPT4LUu+SqQyeULn/oSRi/kUk\n0xt7468EWQsK1bn0zfNrtrFH6Z9t9Bj0YGIR4uRosuHGCrDxD1r/v3CaFcAU9L+F\nG02PiBRrAIttJMbsUa942NCBF0aBlZQ75sJbGLB1FfUm7KJ2W7FNsxks8pAbQwrx\nls50LlmV2ELYp/XTPX8mxUUvF4esgjL3PJiS4cg8yJumRrVV71WIbKG++O4WMkxV\n8mTMEmlwV5nqESjMfTb5okpgh2VIaak8p6MsknyWFt+34Jqxt93MB5b0VJh97USe\n1MVX87wM5rwbZu7NtV0iKgU0ThXkZu6aJpbdMRjtXSSSYBAmPnvlRiVR4TziRXqi\nL6HAYuzHNO9baBO+e4jhKT2cjiEuX13wlJtxHSevaFG9TDFtsVhWt9BYrX6bNhL4\nFnTunWCzQ+SCNKUWmMmu\n=wD4m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T18:04:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDczNWUzYTliMThlOTMyNTA4OGE2NDVjMGJjNTc5NzEyZTU3NWY0YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/a2b303b7314b8d4d50a4b8cce061c1bcd280370a","sha":"a2b303b7314b8d4d50a4b8cce061c1bcd280370a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/a2b303b7314b8d4d50a4b8cce061c1bcd280370a"}],"sha":"735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/735e3a9b18e9325088a645c0bc579712e575f4a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/a2b303b7314b8d4d50a4b8cce061c1bcd280370a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:25:57Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:25:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(local-dev): live-update platform settings instead of rebuilding the image (#232)\n\n* feat(local-dev): live-update platform settings instead of rebuilding the image\n\nEvery edit to a deployment''s aqueduct settings or lehrer''s base.py ran\nthe full platform custom_build: Dagger export of a ~6 GB image, docker\nload, a push, and a rollout. Measured at 31m26s from tilt up to the LMS\nserving the new image; the same edit through live_update serves in 8s\non the same pod.\n\nThe syncs mirror inject_aqueduct_settings() and a test pins them\ntogether. Build-time inputs (assets.py, i18n.py, *.env.yml,\nbuild_manifest.yaml) match no sync, so Tilt still does the full build\nfor them. base.py reaches CMS through an in-pod cp, because Tilt maps a\nfile to its first matching sync only; --remove-destination is needed\nsince the image''s copy is root-owned and the pod runs as app.\n\nedxapp-migrate and edxapp-provision now wait for a trigger after tilt\nup starts them. Their finished pods cannot be live-updated, and Tilt\nrebuilds the image for any resource whose live update fails, which\nwould undo the change on every edit.\n\nThe build tarballs move under ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}. Where systemd''s\ntmp.mount is active, /tmp is tmpfs, so the ~6 GB platform tarball sat\nin RAM beside the cluster on every rebuild.\n\n`lehrer dev check` now enforces minimum versions rather than presence.\nk3d''s floor is 5.5 (first release reading k3d.io/v1alpha5) and dagger''s\nis read from dagger.json''s engineVersion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUGswrApLsjSWorCwnmeZs\n\n* fix(local-dev): keep Job-run scripts out of live_update, trap-clean tarballs\n\nset_waffle_flags.py is run by the edxapp-provision Job from the image.\nSyncing it into the long-running pods meant an edit skipped the rebuild\nthe Job needs, and nothing long-running uses it or the other two helper\nscripts. The sync table now covers only the settings modules under\n*/envs/, and an edit to a helper script takes the full build.\n\nEach tarball build command now removes its tarball in an EXIT trap, so a\nbuild that fails after the export no longer leaves a multi-GB file in\n$TMPDIR. Teardown expands ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} the way the commands do rather\nthan tempfile.gettempdir(), which also follows $TEMP/$TMP.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUGswrApLsjSWorCwnmeZs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95544ad42f5430d52952279f69c6b7acd0240e42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/95544ad42f5430d52952279f69c6b7acd0240e42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/a2b303b7314b8d4d50a4b8cce061c1bcd280370a","verification":{"payload":"tree 95544ad42f5430d52952279f69c6b7acd0240e42\nparent 554d5236504d687097c5dd18d05e1b78c2a0f5d2\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1789482357 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789482357 -0400\n\nfeat(local-dev): live-update platform settings instead of rebuilding the image (#232)\n\n* feat(local-dev): live-update platform settings instead of rebuilding the image\n\nEvery edit to a deployment''s aqueduct settings or lehrer''s base.py ran\nthe full platform custom_build: Dagger export of a ~6 GB image, docker\nload, a push, and a rollout. Measured at 31m26s from tilt up to the LMS\nserving the new image; the same edit through live_update serves in 8s\non the same pod.\n\nThe syncs mirror inject_aqueduct_settings() and a test pins them\ntogether. Build-time inputs (assets.py, i18n.py, *.env.yml,\nbuild_manifest.yaml) match no sync, so Tilt still does the full build\nfor them. base.py reaches CMS through an in-pod cp, because Tilt maps a\nfile to its first matching sync only; --remove-destination is needed\nsince the image''s copy is root-owned and the pod runs as app.\n\nedxapp-migrate and edxapp-provision now wait for a trigger after tilt\nup starts them. Their finished pods cannot be live-updated, and Tilt\nrebuilds the image for any resource whose live update fails, which\nwould undo the change on every edit.\n\nThe build tarballs move under ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}. Where systemd''s\ntmp.mount is active, /tmp is tmpfs, so the ~6 GB platform tarball sat\nin RAM beside the cluster on every rebuild.\n\n`lehrer dev check` now enforces minimum versions rather than presence.\nk3d''s floor is 5.5 (first release reading k3d.io/v1alpha5) and dagger''s\nis read from dagger.json''s engineVersion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUGswrApLsjSWorCwnmeZs\n\n* fix(local-dev): keep Job-run scripts out of live_update, trap-clean tarballs\n\nset_waffle_flags.py is run by the edxapp-provision Job from the image.\nSyncing it into the long-running pods meant an edit skipped the rebuild\nthe Job needs, and nothing long-running uses it or the other two helper\nscripts. The sync table now covers only the settings modules under\n*/envs/, and an edit to a helper script takes the full build.\n\nEach tarball build command now removes its tarball in an EXIT trap, so a\nbuild that fails after the export no longer leaves a multi-GB file in\n$TMPDIR. Teardown expands ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} the way the commands do rather\nthan tempfile.gettempdir(), which also follows $TEMP/$TMP.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUGswrApLsjSWorCwnmeZs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqVV1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7eYQAHDks2qfEhJHoAIktLhn4Pzs\nx2GMJCk8RTxoI/3E7hber/LhFVt2f5Cl4doNEx3jBfXut4WIAtaH87Qmhm39as7z\nT7V5MiBiuLUx8Z8FNkAAU0OepnVXbC8/0aq48ovJ6FlKxa1Ow9uLd+gyexLOSi52\nO1d26Rmg2pTYwudH3QxSOZL0vCAktqdJ0BTazqq+QSrv+v/3OhJQxT9kFy5vMb4P\n//6ANxKEZaEyuhA8DYhFEtxSkafKa4ER1u5G4qNkR/7cUSzSWMpOZe3fMyPk80Z9\nNvywuGusCbJ2wjjgUqPM+SPy87zXVLl28Ylq/RJbTxR48SnpAG1d2pqpsmd/PPWu\nJGNXMrxyZpXst/9XqO4TaA72bG7NQ/55u8EPYPEllP0XEQsKuKY8VvsE3VghpXz2\nvyNZcfMgmExoRK1B6IQiE8v2lrenKhAQ1+/jrQaj0POCvo4SzKcf30RwrtZH3LvS\nB7sh9D2+OcgMXmTRjjWaUgth9K8KNxECRibiFVqM7XsSinDXGpSSDSNU2ZU5sNIX\n9s0bwkExXFVJ8JmiQApJYej+i6LdvcYlr4y81zW9bNyZ1VspmpoqnEgnPwzF4lSI\nbeE9nrQEu5s4+FD2gIBSwZfy29+hypZHhGU5nHWES02eI0CbmM9kNhb5EbU8XE1X\n55go/dYbTKVaANx91nbr\n=Q8jK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:25:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","grav