f0df9a20579414a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/fe2dbf95c8760f6c9f9f8bf66382fc6d78313fdc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T15:52:36Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T15:52:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(notes): add Meilisearch support and stop installing ES apps when ES is off (#217)\n\nedx-notes-api has supported three search backends since the views/ package\nsplit: Elasticsearch, Meilisearch, and a LIKE query over the Note model.\nnotesapi/v1/views/__init__.py picks between them with ES_DISABLED and\nMEILISEARCH_ENABLED. env_config.py only ever set the first, so Meilisearch was\nunreachable from any deployment driven by this settings module -- setting\nMEILISEARCH_* in the environment did nothing, because getattr(settings,\n\"MEILISEARCH_ENABLED\", False) was always False.\n\nAdds MEILISEARCH_ENABLED, MEILISEARCH_URL, MEILISEARCH_API_KEY and\nMEILISEARCH_INDEX, with the URL and index defaulted to the values notes''\nown Client class already assumes.\n\nTwo related fixes fall out of the same block:\n\nELASTICSEARCH_DSL_HOST is no longer unconditionally required. It is appended to\nREQUIRED_ENV_VARS only when Elasticsearch is actually in use, so a deployment\nrunning without an Elasticsearch domain no longer has to pass a placeholder\nvalue for a variable nothing reads.\n\nWhen ES is disabled the ES apps are now dropped from INSTALLED_APPS. The\nstar-import of notesserver.settings.common runs with common.py''s own\nES_DISABLED = False, so INSTALLED_APPS always carried\nelasticsearch_dsl/django_elasticsearch_dsl/django_elasticsearch_dsl_drf\nregardless, and django_elasticsearch_dsl''s AppConfig.ready() installed\nRealTimeSignalProcessor on Note save and delete. That was inert only because\nNoteDocument is reachable solely through views/elasticsearch.py, which is not\nimported when ES is off -- an accident of import order, not a guarantee, and it\nwould break the moment anything else imported that module.\n\nMEILISEARCH_ENABLED without ELASTICSEARCH_DSL_DISABLED now raises rather than\nbeing ignored: views/__init__.py only consults it inside the ES_DISABLED\nbranch, so that combination silently keeps serving Elasticsearch.\n\nVerified inside the running CI image (mitodl/openedx-notes@sha256:a4f77f8e,\nedx-notes-api 3dab0c9) by importing the patched module as the settings module,\nacross five configurations:\n\n  default, ES enabled     ES apps present, RealTimeSignalProcessor on\n                          post_save, views.elasticsearch. Unchanged.\n  ES off, no Meilisearch  ES apps [], zero post_save receivers, views.common.\n  ES off + Meilisearch    ES apps [], zero receivers, views.meilisearch,\n                          URL http://meilisearch:7700, index student_notes.\n  Meilisearch, ES on      ImproperlyConfigured, names the conflict.\n  Meilisearch, no API key ImproperlyConfigured, names the variable.\n\nThe notes pod reaches the in-namespace Meilisearch service: GET\nhttp://meilisearch:7700/health returns 200 {\"status\":\"available\"}.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018H46AMxaprJ3Ec4Ue96PBT\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf57fe4a68360d85b20de011533f9858f4affa11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/bf57fe4a68360d85b20de011533f9858f4affa11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/fe2dbf95c8760f6c9f9f8bf66382fc6d78313fdc","verification":{"payload":"tree bf57fe4a68360d85b20de011533f9858f4affa11\nparent ee47afba7721b1f1ca1c0e7741c1461109596a18\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788537156 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788537156 -0400\n\nfeat(notes): add Meilisearch support and stop installing ES apps when ES is off (#217)\n\nedx-notes-api has supported three search backends since the views/ package\nsplit: Elasticsearch, Meilisearch, and a LIKE query over the Note model.\nnotesapi/v1/views/__init__.py picks between them with ES_DISABLED and\nMEILISEARCH_ENABLED. env_config.py only ever set the first, so Meilisearch was\nunreachable from any deployment driven by this settings module -- setting\nMEILISEARCH_* in the environment did nothing, because getattr(settings,\n\"MEILISEARCH_ENABLED\", False) was always False.\n\nAdds MEILISEARCH_ENABLED, MEILISEARCH_URL, MEILISEARCH_API_KEY and\nMEILISEARCH_INDEX, with the URL and index defaulted to the values notes''\nown Client class already assumes.\n\nTwo related fixes fall out of the same block:\n\nELASTICSEARCH_DSL_HOST is no longer unconditionally required. It is appended to\nREQUIRED_ENV_VARS only when Elasticsearch is actually in use, so a deployment\nrunning without an Elasticsearch domain no longer has to pass a placeholder\nvalue for a variable nothing reads.\n\nWhen ES is disabled the ES apps are now dropped from INSTALLED_APPS. The\nstar-import of notesserver.settings.common runs with common.py''s own\nES_DISABLED = False, so INSTALLED_APPS always carried\nelasticsearch_dsl/django_elasticsearch_dsl/django_elasticsearch_dsl_drf\nregardless, and django_elasticsearch_dsl''s AppConfig.ready() installed\nRealTimeSignalProcessor on Note save and delete. That was inert only because\nNoteDocument is reachable solely through views/elasticsearch.py, which is not\nimported when ES is off -- an accident of import order, not a guarantee, and it\nwould break the moment anything else imported that module.\n\nMEILISEARCH_ENABLED without ELASTICSEARCH_DSL_DISABLED now raises rather than\nbeing ignored: views/__init__.py only consults it inside the ES_DISABLED\nbranch, so that combination silently keeps serving Elasticsearch.\n\nVerified inside the running CI image (mitodl/openedx-notes@sha256:a4f77f8e,\nedx-notes-api 3dab0c9) by importing the patched module as the settings module,\nacross five configurations:\n\n  default, ES enabled     ES apps present, RealTimeSignalProcessor on\n                          post_save, views.elasticsearch. Unchanged.\n  ES off, no Meilisearch  ES apps [], zero post_save receivers, views.common.\n  ES off + Meilisearch    ES apps [], zero receivers, views.meilisearch,\n                          URL http://meilisearch:7700, index student_notes.\n  Meilisearch, ES on      ImproperlyConfigured, names the conflict.\n  Meilisearch, no API key ImproperlyConfigured, names the variable.\n\nThe notes pod reaches the in-namespace Meilisearch service: GET\nhttp://meilisearch:7700/health returns 200 {\"status\":\"available\"}.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018H46AMxaprJ3Ec4Ue96PBT\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmulECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhncQAA+XDDxKdwvGmb4phpOXM9zo\n2oYVHP8dyqP6bf+yS+B5SOqdOe3yX9OUIwvt+6w0ujEzbWW9yVZOlB5ePdnyzZO0\n2fNZo/HOU73h4vZk0ft+pfxSQZNXFogDR/Wg1d9sjJcVqewdD1AZRm10qvZ8ohQR\nGws7YhFU0rRnjtmj1BkUfmqWoj3yXjc21PAgNZSV