7f6967d40611b6","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDAyZmYwMzNjYWQzNTFhOTU5N2U4MzkyNDUyN2Y2OTY3ZDQwNjExYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8","sha":"8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8"}],"sha":"02ff033cad351a9597e83924527f6967d40611b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/02ff033cad351a9597e83924527f6967d40611b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:15:56Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:15:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make the local-dev stack composable: shared secret defaults and a config-override layer (#210)\n\n* feat(local-dev): share the openedx-secrets defaults with Tilt callers\n\nThe goal is for this stack to compose into a cluster another team already\nruns, rather than each team standing up its own k3d. openedx-secrets was in\nthe way: every manifest here needs it, but only `lehrer dev setup` could\ncreate it, so a Tilt caller composing this stack had to hand-maintain a\nsecond copy of the same key list.\n\nMove the defaults to local-dev/secret-defaults.yaml and read them from both\nconsumers — the CLI, and a new manage_secrets key in setup() that builds the\nSecret from the same file. A composing caller now passes manage_secrets: True\nand gets a Secret identical to the one lehrer''s own cluster gets. secret_manifest()\nis exported so a team that wants only the Secret can call it without setup().\n\nAlso fixes a drift the shared file makes structural: DB_PASSWORD mirrored\nMYSQL_PASSWORD by re-reading os.environ with its own hardcoded \"openedx-dev\"\nfallback, so changing the MYSQL_PASSWORD default would have silently left\nDB_PASSWORD behind. Mirrors now copy the resolved value.\n\nThe Secret is ordered ahead of the MariaDB and MongoDB CRs, which read\nMYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD and MONGO_PASSWORD out of it.\n\nVerified: 278 tests pass; the Starlark path renders all 7 defaults plus the\nmirrored DB_PASSWORD into a valid Secret, and MYSQL_PASSWORD=from-env\npropagates to DB_PASSWORD; CLI and Starlark produce identical key sets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* feat(local-dev): add an optional config-override layer for composing callers\n\napply_platform_configmaps: False was the only way for a caller on its own\ninfrastructure to change a host: it suppressed lms-config/cms-config entirely\nand made the caller supply a complete replacement. That is a copy of this\nrepo''s key set living in another repo, and it silently goes stale every time\na key is added here.\n\nEvery platform manifest now reads an optional <variant>-config-overrides\nConfigMap last in envFrom, so a caller supplies only the keys it changes\n(shared Valkey/OpenSearch hosts, public URLs) and inherits the rest.\n\nTests pin the two things that make the layer work and are easy to get wrong:\nthe override must be last (envFrom resolves in order, so an override placed\nearlier loses to the ConfigMap it overrides) and must match the base\nConfigMap''s variant. job-demo-course.yaml is the trap — it reads cms-config\ndespite its name, so deriving the override name from the filename gets it\nwrong, which is exactly what happened while writing this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* fix(local-dev): compare the root-password warning against the written value\n\n_warn_on_init_only_root_password was still handed\nos.environ.get(\"MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD\", \"openedx-dev\") while the Secret is now\nwritten from the YAML-resolved value — the same two-sources-of-truth bug this\nbranch fixed for DB_PASSWORD, left one line further down.\n\nThe failure mode is the dangerous direction. The function returns early when\nprevious == current, so changing the default in secret-defaults.yaml makes the\nrun that changes it compare the old default against the old default, conclude\nnothing moved, and skip the warning — on exactly the run where root''s password\ndiverges from the initialized datadir and the warning is the only symptom\nbefore Grant/Database reconciliation starts failing on auth.\n\nTests assert the call site reads resolved[\"MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD\"] and that no\nhardcoded password default is left in the module; both fail against the\nprevious code.\n\nReported by Copilot on #210.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* fix(local-dev): roll platform pods when their config changes\n\nenvFrom never triggers a rollout, so an edit to lms-config/cms-config updated\nthe ConfigMap and left every running LMS/CMS/worker pod on the old values with\nnothing reporting it. Only the notes deployment was checksum-annotated; the\nfour platform Deployments were not.\n\nsetup() now hashes the platform ConfigMaps and substitutes the result into a\npod-template annotation, the same __NOTES_CONFIG_CHECKSUM__ pattern already\nused one section below.\n\nThe hash covers a new config_override_paths key as well as our own files. A\ncomposing caller applies its *-config-overrides itself, so hashing only lehrer''s\nConfigMaps would miss exactly the edits that caller makes most often — the\noverride layer would look like it did nothing.\n\nread_file rather than cat: it registers a Tilt watch on each path, so an edit\nre-runs the Tiltfile and recomputes the hash. Hashing via a shell cat would read\nthe file without Tilt ever being told it changed.\n\nReported by Copilot on mitodl/ol-infrastructure#5686.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46ec88468810a82910929d3f07602a9e967d8388","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/46ec88468810a82910929d3f07602a9e967d8388"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 46ec88468810a82910929d3f07602a9e967d8388\nparent 7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788444956 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788444956 -0400\n\nMake the local-dev stack composable: shared secret defaults and a config-override layer (#210)\n\n* feat(local-dev): share the openedx-secrets defaults with Tilt callers\n\nThe goal is for this stack to compose into a cluster another team already\nruns, rather than each team standing up its own k3d. openedx-secrets was in\nthe way: every manifest here needs it, but only `lehrer dev setup` could\ncreate it, so a Tilt caller composing this stack had to hand-maintain a\nsecond copy of the same key list.\n\nMove the defaults to local-dev/secret-defaults.yaml and read them from both\nconsumers — the CLI, and a new manage_secrets key in setup() that builds the\nSecret from the same file. A composing caller now passes manage_secrets: True\nand gets a Secret identical to the one lehrer''s own cluster gets. secret_manifest()\nis exported so a team that wants only the Secret can call it without setup().\n\nAlso fixes a drift the shared file makes structural: DB_PASSWORD mirrored\nMYSQL_PASSWORD by re-reading os.environ with its own hardcoded \"openedx-dev\"\nfallback, so changing the MYSQL_PASSWORD default would have silently left\nDB_PASSWORD behind. Mirrors now copy the resolved value.\n\nThe Secret is ordered ahead of the MariaDB and MongoDB CRs, which read\nMYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD and MONGO_PASSWORD out of it.\n\nVerified: 278 tests pass; the Starlark path renders all 7 defaults plus the\nmirrored DB_PASSWORD into a valid Secret, and MYSQL_PASSWORD=from-env\npropagates to DB_PASSWORD; CLI and Starlark produce identical key sets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* feat(local-dev): add an optional config-override layer for composing callers\n\napply_platform_configmaps: False was the only way for a caller on its own\ninfrastructure to change a host: it suppressed lms-config/cms-config entirely\nand made the caller supply a complete replacement. That is a copy of this\nrepo''s key set living in another repo, and it silently goes stale every time\na key is added here.\n\nEvery platform manifest now reads an optional <variant>-config-overrides\nConfigMap last in envFrom, so a caller supplies only the keys it changes\n(shared Valkey/OpenSearch hosts, public URLs) and inherits the rest.\n\nTests pin the two things that make the layer work and are easy to get wrong:\nthe override must be last (envFrom resolves in order, so an override placed\nearlier loses to the ConfigMap it overrides) and must match the base\nConfigMap''s variant. job-demo-course.yaml is the trap — it reads cms-config\ndespite its name, so deriving the override name from the filename gets it\nwrong, which is exactly what happened while writing this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* fix(local-dev): compare the root-password warning against the written value\n\n_warn_on_init_only_root_password was still handed\nos.environ.get(\"MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD\", \"openedx-dev\") while the Secret is now\nwritten from the YAML-resolved value — the same two-sources-of-truth bug this\nbranch fixed for DB_PASSWORD, left one line further down.\n\nThe failure mode is the dangerous direction. The function returns early when\nprevious == current, so changing the default in secret-defaults.yaml makes the\nrun that changes it compare the old default against the old default, conclude\nnothing moved, and skip the warning — on exactly the run where root''s password\ndiverges from the initialized datadir and the warning is the only symptom\nbefore Grant/Database reconciliation starts failing on auth.\n\nTests assert the call site reads resolved[\"MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD\"] and that no\nhardcoded password default is left in the module; both fail against the\nprevious code.\n\nReported by Copilot on #210.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* fix(local-dev): roll platform pods when their config changes\n\nenvFrom never triggers a rollout, so an edit to lms-config/cms-config updated\nthe ConfigMap and left every running LMS/CMS/worker pod on the old values with\nnothing reporting it. Only the notes deployment was checksum-annotated; the\nfour platform Deployments were not.\n\nsetup() now hashes the platform ConfigMaps and substitutes the result into a\npod-template annotation, the same __NOTES_CONFIG_CHECKSUM__ pattern already\nused one section below.\n\nThe hash covers a new config_override_paths key as well as our own files. A\ncomposing caller applies its *-config-overrides itself, so hashing only lehrer''s\nConfigMaps would miss exactly the edits that caller makes most often — the\noverride layer would look like it did nothing.\n\nread_file rather than cat: it registers a Tilt watch on each path, so an edit\nre-runs the Tiltfile and recomputes the hash. Hashing via a shell cat would read\nthe file without Tilt ever being told it changed.\n\nReported by Copilot on mitodl/ol-infrastructure#5686.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmYEcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxF4QAKEZUbcuZnl5YDzvRd7PrUdZ\nDmQCk8BhMX4im7yLCKnM3ile0jCBOWto7qhf9DvfoJKDWB1f9HBv/FWAa39wpbac\nNevIfe2ZKSXbxW1Kq+jreNuZZOSN8jGkwhrHeO3CIX+tMquldDS5y8GarrCura8y\nePQ/OWnmpMOhHR7t1JcBlQ0yseUw5R3UkuyRmExfRo79Eg/qzFMoJEcuwy2UPaC+\njpqQ2VpgX2oIK90S33yYE/UuDd50dfj6kF9XSwmt4Q9fQjllMMAkItxnaszQC/T0\n1qBs4+6mjaq611pWPiyl15CGpkaIL9m0G3uei2ts1wdb0UacWfbSsQnOWodHi8hF\n9mZf8wwFIf2pIh5hoSKo9qgbu5LbF92WZpqnea55shfFCuHBSnLWWBnWTlvpNQF6\nRHVd54spIGm5yBUFq4wMl+x16SnIxxAnG+7ilnOa2vhf+rvYlzGRPwVqT3MbGeG2\nFYmmsITGvuwTwi7bwCnluSMSvGapzf+kEtIU7S+JLhcdcFuQYztFBcKgEz8Rf1QH\n8IaNR0wQZxarRkkwsk0LoaWtjC8vqG6rGVnkvqo5b1BQEht9ZbMyo2wNMs56FXin\n6xK1N/BrerBRYjvSjxwHBLDWCBueqw6Toc6NBLc3c5O4+7r71MsZdJgVMI3FyhK4\n9FxqkfjKRLlVaUEDdJNH\n=qJVL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T14:15:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDhiYThmOTgxNzMxOTA5N2M1NTIzM2Q4ZDAzMmMzMzE1MTM0ZjczYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745","sha":"7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745"}],"sha":"8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/8ba8f9817319097c55233d8d032c3315134f73a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:55:16Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:55:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mfe): declare local-dev hostnames per deployment, point build baseUrl at the LMS host (#209)\n\n* fix(mfe): declare local-dev hostnames per deployment, point build baseUrl at the LMS host\n\nTwo pieces of MFE-topology drift, both surfaced while fixing the hot-reload\nport collision (#189).\n\nLocal-dev hostnames were literals in each site.config.dev.tsx, and the\nTiltfile and `lehrer dev check` recovered them by regex-parsing that TSX.\nChanging a deployment''s local-dev domain therefore meant editing every Site\nProject, and the tooling could only ever check what it managed to parse.\nThey now come from mfe_slot_config/frontend/shared/src/dev-hosts.json, which\nthe site configs import as @shared/dev-hosts.json and both consumers read\ndirectly, so the tooling checks exactly what the bundle was built with. A\nsite named in the frontend directory but missing from dev-hosts.json is now\na TypeScript error rather than a runtime surprise. shared/ is the location\nbecause it is the only per-deployment directory Dagger mounts into a Site\nProject build; generic gains one for the same reason.\n\nThe mit-ol build configs described a topology we do not deploy: baseUrl on a\ndedicated apps.<deployment>.mit.edu host. None of those three names resolve.\nProduction serves Site Projects as a sub-path of the LMS host, with Fastly\nrewriting /apps/<app>/... to the Site Project and /apps/<deployment>-site/...\nto its assets (ol-infrastructure applications/edxapp/__main__.py, \"Handle\nSite Project routing\"), which is why wrapWithAppsPath nests the routes and\nbasename stays \"/\". FRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG does not set baseUrl, so the\ncompiled value is what the auth redirects fall back to. baseUrl is now the\nLMS origin for all three, and a test holds it there.\n\ngeneric keeps the own-host topology vanilla Open edX uses, but its baseUrl\nnamed localhost:8090 while lehrer-core.star routes compiled MFEs by host as\n<site>.localhost, so nothing served it; it now names default.localhost:8090.\n\nVerified: `lehrer dev check` resolves all four sites from the new file; the\nTiltfile loads and its baseUrl/dev-port cross-check agrees for both\ndeployments; tsc resolves the JSON import (and rejects an unknown site key);\nand the webpack dev server serves a bundle carrying the value from\ndev-hosts.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011hhgaMWi8M5yDQ7gf5QHY9\n\n* fix(mfe): document baseUrl as a per-environment runtime value, not a compiled one\n\nCopilot''s review on #209: one build artifact is promoted CI -> QA ->\nProduction, and the mitx artifact additionally serves mitx-staging, whose LMS\norigins differ again. Pointing the compiled baseUrl at the Production LMS\norigin makes every other environment''s auth fallback redirect users into\nProduction, which is worse than the NXDOMAIN apps.*.mit.edu it replaced: a\ndead host fails visibly, a cross-environment redirect does not.\n\nThe fix belongs in ol-infrastructure, which owns the deployment topology and\nalready supplies every other origin per environment. FRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG now\ncarries baseUrl alongside lmsBaseUrl/loginUrl/logoutUrl, and frontend-base\nawaits the runtime config before configureAuth, so the auth service is built\nwith the environment''s own origin. See mitodl/ol-infrastructure#5695.\n\nThe compiled value stays the Production LMS origin, matching the other\norigins in these files, and matters only before the runtime config lands or\nif the config API fails. Comments, the deployment guide and the test docstring\nnow say that rather than claiming baseUrl is never overridden.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011hhgaMWi8M5yDQ7gf5QHY9\n\n* docs(mfe): name where the apps.*.mit.edu baseUrl placeholder came from\n\nSalvaged from the duplicate PR #213, which carried this provenance and is\notherwise a strict subset of this branch: git log -S dates the host to\n5d68e40, the original OEP-65 frontend-base scaffold (#51). Worth keeping so\nthe next reader knows it was never a real deployment target.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011hhgaMWi8M5yDQ7gf5QHY9\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f1cb0f952df26a2b877924fc28fe89734901e83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/0f1cb0f952df26a2b877924fc28fe89734901e83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f1cb0f952df26a2b877924fc28fe89734901e83\nparent db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788443716 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788443716 -0400\n\nfix(mfe): declare local-dev hostnames per deployment, point build baseUrl at the LMS host (#209)\n\n* fix(mfe): declare local-dev hostnames per deployment, point build baseUrl at the LMS host\n\nTwo pieces of MFE-topology drift, both surfaced while fixing the hot-reload\nport collision (#189).\n\nLocal-dev hostnames were literals in each site.config.dev.tsx, and the\nTiltfile and `lehrer dev check` recovered them by regex-parsing that TSX.\nChanging a deployment''s local-dev domain therefore meant editing every Site\nProject, and the tooling could only ever check what it managed to parse.\nThey now come from mfe_slot_config/frontend/shared/src/dev-hosts.json, which\nthe site configs import as @shared/dev-hosts.json and both consumers read\ndirectly, so the tooling checks exactly what the bundle was built with. A\nsite named in the frontend directory but missing from dev-hosts.json is now\na TypeScript error rather than a runtime surprise. shared/ is the location\nbecause it is the only per-deployment directory Dagger mounts into a Site\nProject build; generic gains one for the same reason.\n\nThe mit-ol build configs described a topology we do not deploy: baseUrl on a\ndedicated apps.<deployment>.mit.edu host. None of those three names resolve.\nProduction serves Site Projects as a sub-path of the LMS host, with Fastly\nrewriting /apps/<app>/... to the Site Project and /apps/<deployment>-site/...\nto its assets (ol-infrastructure applications/edxapp/__main__.py, \"Handle\nSite Project routing\"), which is why wrapWithAppsPath nests the routes and\nbasename stays \"/\". FRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG does not set baseUrl, so the\ncompiled value is what the auth redirects fall back to. baseUrl is now the\nLMS origin for all three, and a test holds it there.\n\ngeneric keeps the own-host topology vanilla Open edX uses, but its baseUrl\nnamed localhost:8090 while lehrer-core.star routes compiled MFEs by host as\n<site>.localhost, so nothing served it; it now names default.localhost:8090.\n\nVerified: `lehrer dev check` resolves all four sites from the new file; the\nTiltfile loads and its baseUrl/dev-port cross-check agrees for both\ndeployments; tsc resolves the JSON import (and rejects an unknown site key);\nand the webpack dev server serves a bundle carrying the value from\ndev-hosts.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011hhgaMWi8M5yDQ7gf5QHY9\n\n* fix(mfe): document baseUrl as a per-environment runtime value, not a compiled one\n\nCopilot''s review on #209: one build artifact is promoted CI -> QA ->\nProduction, and the mitx artifact additionally serves mitx-staging, whose LMS\norigins differ again. Pointing the compiled baseUrl at the Production LMS\norigin makes every other environment''s auth fallback redirect users into\nProduction, which is worse than the NXDOMAIN apps.*.mit.edu it replaced: a\ndead host fails visibly, a cross-environment redirect does not.\n\nThe fix belongs in ol-infrastructure, which owns the deployment topology and\nalready supplies every other origin per environment. FRONTEND_SITE_CONFIG now\ncarries baseUrl alongside lmsBaseUrl/loginUrl/logoutUrl, and frontend-base\nawaits the runtime config before configureAuth, so the auth service is built\nwith the environment''s own origin. See mitodl/ol-infrastructure#5695.\n\nThe compiled value stays the Production LMS origin, matching the other\norigins in these files, and matters only before the runtime config lands or\nif the config API fails. Comments, the deployment guide and the test docstring\nnow say that rather than claiming baseUrl is never overridden.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011hhgaMWi8M5yDQ7gf5QHY9\n\n* docs(mfe): name where the apps.*.mit.edu baseUrl placeholder came from\n\nSalvaged from the duplicate PR #213, which carried this provenance and is\notherwise a strict subset of this branch: git log -S dates the host to\n5d68e40, the original OEP-65 frontend-base scaffold (#51). Worth keeping so\nthe next reader knows it was never a real deployment target.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011hhgaMWi8M5yDQ7gf5QHY9\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmXxECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVHIQAGtIq1J94L7mKUejWT20mNMz\nZFvzo+5RFwihX/eCoWycexVWfvfQkiQR1/uCMvuPob6TBbcAlyAXv4ZrI/+6+jLk\nuIlQj2gqGL9yaMnilt4jXUNtkMMgnRVg5qzOBSZT2R6yj+SCAvYagQJ5+Qc+VfbK\nVQFy0hL28Helzc5NoWtZCA8KUH86jGOvAexSGT65YHkrTGTMtcZx8A08ojb30m2l\nOJhGSAeJdlIGkhwJpPzrqChrbEIAVr+/3A5deXUTrjcox0psi1bg0SLAqoLw6Xy1\n6EFHzGb0VeMrpT7BCGtOpt8GaDP7cq+loL/L1QPdIuKX74srlWTYz3C/fUoPDOkZ\nUKHGJgzD4/UNgRR/2BqbpGs8WwHqK59SfnkNgQET227wBCX7IILMXaJxmMhXUdwS\nzaBxqIf35nes33uQTTOHz8DIoa/bOPFCDJyamcf61mw/OHen2uUHWdG7MWylfgkL\nXUXIFxNnHZq/kNrph5C6Z4kvOe0ks60Spc5Lkad/+/B6VS2pjlZMbIJsjqt8brkM\nJIQAcv2w0KW+rGiRtDzMaP7EVVrDIjztXA0Wk1oBRGcDeW+sntsUtlGvnq3u+sfV\nNOTfUeHtBlPe3gWKC9Q+MRPoQslBcc3rrbxDVTpHdSSqIVjNVeZrjQXHjri/sDJU\nDU4CabEXBgEXW3Ynq+Ke\n=PBMp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T13:55:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDdhOTA2YmQ1MDIwZGU2YjMyNDgwYTc5NmExMTg4MjU0MDM1NmM3NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189","sha":"db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189"}],"sha":"7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/7a906bd5020de6b32480a796a11882540356c745"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:54:36Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T13:54:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: --no-deps on the edx-platform editable install so manifest overrides survive (#214)\n\n* fix: --no-deps on the edx-platform editable install so overrides survive\n\nA deployment override in build_manifest.yaml could be silently discarded,\nproducing an image that did not contain the code the manifest asked for.\n\nThe build installs edx-platform''s dependency set, applies the cell''s\noverrides, and then runs `uv pip install -e .` on edx-platform. That last\nstep re-resolves edx-platform''s own declared dependencies from the index, so\nany override naming a package edx-platform declares is replaced by the\nindexed pin and its dist-info loses direct_url.json.\n\nThis split by release line, which is what made it hard to see. master''s\npyproject.toml declares \"openedx-forum\", so the\n`git+https://github.com/mitodl/forum.git@...#egg=openedx-forum` override was\nreverted to the indexed openedx-forum==0.4.3 on all three master cells.\nrelease/verawood does not declare it, so the same manifest line survived\nthere as 0.4.5 with direct_url.json intact. Identical manifest syntax, images\nrebuilt after the override merged, opposite results.\n\nObserved in the deployed CI images: mitxonline, mitx and mitx-staging all\ncarried 0.4.3 with no direct_url.json, while xpro carried 0.4.5 installed\nfrom git. ol-infrastructure had already moved forum search onto Typesense in\nthose environments on the assumption the fix was present, so three of them\nwere running the unfixed backend.\n\n--no-deps is safe here: _edx_base_deps_script() has already installed the\nfull dependency set (requirements/edx/base.txt + assets.txt, or the uv sync\ngroups on master) and the overrides step ran after it, so this install has\nnothing to resolve and only needs to register the package.\n\nApplied at all three editable-install sites. The test-harness one matters\ntoo: without it the suite runs against packages the shipped image does not\nhave, which is the class of gap that let the Typesense search bugs ship.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012c3Ua8fPhRYnEdQE8snFNW\n\n* fix: re-apply overrides after the testing sync; centralize the editable install\n\nAddresses review feedback on #214.\n\nThe test path was still losing the override. --no-deps stops the editable\ninstall from re-resolving, but _edx_testing_deps_script() runs straight after\nand reconciles any package the checkout itself pins back to the checkout''s\nversion. --inexact does not prevent that; it only stops extraneous packages\nbeing pruned. Confirmed against uv directly:\n\n    uv sync --locked --active --no-install-project --inexact \\\n            --no-default-groups --group testing\n    - packaging==23.2\n    + packaging==24.0\n\nBoth arms are affected, so this is not master-only: master''s uv.lock pins\nopenedx-forum==0.4.3, and release/verawood''s requirements/edx/testing.txt\npins openedx-forum==0.4.2. Re-applying the cell''s overrides after the testing\nstep keeps them the final dependency layer and the test environment faithful\nto the shipped image. Passing only the -r file is deliberate -- the\nsource-built lxml/xmlsec already satisfy the versions pinned there, so uv\nleaves them alone rather than swapping in wheels.\n\n--only-group testing would fix the sync arm alone (verified: it installs the\ngroup and leaves an off-lock package untouched) but does nothing for the\nlegacy arm, so the re-apply covers both instead.\n\nCentralizes the editable install in _edx_platform_editable_install() so one\ncall site cannot regress independently, with regression tests asserting the\nflag -- no Dagger mock needed, following the existing _edx_*_script() helper\ntests. Its docstring also records why the install is editable at all: the\ndist-info carries 133 entry points including every core XBlock, and the build\nwrites the Django settings modules into the tree after this runs.\n\nAlso corrects a cross-reference to a function name that does not exist\n(collect_artifacts -> the flag now lives in the shared helper).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012c3Ua8fPhRYnEdQE8snFNW\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a66e3e1a971b237db31af7a98c96496f6893741d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/a66e3e1a971b237db31af7a98c96496f6893741d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189","verification":{"payload":"tree a66e3e1a971b237db31af7a98c96496f6893741d\nparent 63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788443676 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788443676 -0400\n\nfix: --no-deps on the edx-platform editable install so manifest overrides survive (#214)\n\n* fix: --no-deps on the edx-platform editable install so overrides survive\n\nA deployment override in build_manifest.yaml could be silently discarded,\nproducing an image that did not contain the code the manifest asked for.\n\nThe build installs edx-platform''s dependency set, applies the cell''s\noverrides, and then runs `uv pip install -e .` on edx-platform. That last\nstep re-resolves edx-platform''s own declared dependencies from the index, so\nany override naming a package edx-platform declares is replaced by the\nindexed pin and its dist-info loses direct_url.json.\n\nThis split by release line, which is what made it hard to see. master''s\npyproject.toml declares \"openedx-forum\", so the\n`git+https://github.com/mitodl/forum.git@...#egg=openedx-forum` override was\nreverted to the indexed openedx-forum==0.4.3 on all three master cells.\nrelease/verawood does not declare it, so the same manifest line survived\nthere as 0.4.5 with direct_url.json intact. Identical manifest syntax, images\nrebuilt after the override merged, opposite results.\n\nObserved in the deployed CI images: mitxonline, mitx and mitx-staging all\ncarried 0.4.3 with no direct_url.json, while xpro carried 0.4.5 installed\nfrom git. ol-infrastructure had already moved forum search onto Typesense in\nthose environments on the assumption the fix was present, so three of them\nwere running the unfixed backend.\n\n--no-deps is safe here: _edx_base_deps_script() has already installed the\nfull dependency set (requirements/edx/base.txt + assets.txt, or the uv sync\ngroups on master) and the overrides step ran after it, so this install has\nnothing to resolve and only needs to register the package.\n\nApplied at all three editable-install sites. The test-harness one matters\ntoo: without it the suite runs against packages the shipped image does not\nhave, which is the class of gap that let the Typesense search bugs ship.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012c3Ua8fPhRYnEdQE8snFNW\n\n* fix: re-apply overrides after the testing sync; centralize the editable install\n\nAddresses review feedback on #214.\n\nThe test path was still losing the override. --no-deps stops the editable\ninstall from re-resolving, but _edx_testing_deps_script() runs straight after\nand reconciles any package the checkout itself pins back to the checkout''s\nversion. --inexact does not prevent that; it only stops extraneous packages\nbeing pruned. Confirmed against uv directly:\n\n    uv sync --locked --active --no-install-project --inexact \\\n            --no-default-groups --group testing\n    - packaging==23.2\n    + packaging==24.0\n\nBoth arms are affected, so this is not master-only: master''s uv.lock pins\nopenedx-forum==0.4.3, and release/verawood''s requirements/edx/testing.txt\npins openedx-forum==0.4.2. Re-applying the cell''s overrides after the testing\nstep keeps them the final dependency layer and the test environment faithful\nto the shipped image. Passing only the -r file is deliberate -- the\nsource-built lxml/xmlsec already satisfy the versions pinned there, so uv\nleaves them alone rather than swapping in wheels.\n\n--only-group testing would fix the sync arm alone (verified: it installs the\ngroup and leaves an off-lock package untouched) but does nothing for the\nlegacy arm, so the re-apply covers both instead.\n\nCentralizes the editable install in _edx_platform_editable_install() so one\ncall site cannot regress independently, with regression tests asserting the\nflag -- no Dagger mock needed, following the existing _edx_*_script() helper\ntests. Its docstring also records why the install is editable at all: the\ndist-info carries 133 entry points including every core XBlock, and the build\nwrites the Django settings modules into the tree after this runs.\n\nAlso corrects a cross-reference to a function name that does not exist\n(collect_artifacts -> the flag now lives in the shared helper).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012c3Ua8fPhRYnEdQE8snFNW\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmXwcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY3YQAI2AR7Do3hSEIiFCNb4mgBD8\nZl1y68nW1V/7bKaCRBaufuJ0gjhKZjIK8OnFoqJdlLoByLdUgIB4tifqSKtNxwBE\ngyxvG32fajpWxrz+YcmItI/GyPrLTgSMzf/kQe8NVevKCt7sHKbquu6guC4YvzaU\nLFlpNQMmG7IJ/bHU81VcgoKN9YGUZX2tmYs2b7RUQb8YXEcuH35WthxxhiX+plGS\nAdEIHCH1hdQuw5RCwMzZd2skD1v849p6DoEzh4aFzALaD+9TAApHJjfqWdK4Dwn4\nFp7dQ36LIuvOvFeOeY3UlwIMq+D3IDC8eCm2Uzq6psUAIofSZcDAzzXIcRXBiMH7\nyaSlLDcG/rvk6HMPResz7U6tWSIbDkQq/c2NeFZcd9cRm1I5CeQLQxs53OpMG7/p\n840/IeWZtEltUCoHyOsQvK6AuVw64j5LQIERIyfoveWQn/m4iAHt4WGZ+SVsKxrW\nyuXZytjN8H9Ta7bl7aBeZT7CgKLDbD6yJKhqVDA19qpkVGEM5R7b4sC9c1VZhsYV\nheBs+oHM6yIkuK52R2D6VWHcOJsJ6E1PB5dp1JPB4N7bBlSkukvZ1Mqaam/K7US6\n/o+FnpFQk47EctWNhdfmT/EsM02W+xGAIlQlBn+7AKQ9v/z4EdYrFSP+JgpTr520\nwEblJhN4zt5Ryy52x61b\n=Y9Ca\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T13:54:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKGRiMjNkNDlmY2U0MGRlNjQ0OWNkMDRjNjkyODZlNTZlNzFkZGIxODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e","sha":"63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e"}],"sha":"db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/db23d49fce40de6449cd04c69286e56e71ddb189"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:38:14Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:38:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(local-dev): create edxapp on utf8mb4, not the operator''s utf8 default (#190)\n\n* fix(local-dev): create edxapp on utf8mb4, not the operator''s utf8 default\n\nThe edxapp schema was being created as `CHARACTER SET = ''utf8'' COLLATE =\n''utf8_general_ci''`, three-byte utf8, while notes and edxapp_csmh sat on\nutf8mb4_unicode_ci.\n\n`spec.database` on the MariaDB CR does not create the schema. The reconciler\nturns it into a Database CR named `<mariadb>-database` built with no\ncharacterSet/collate, so the CRD defaults get stamped on and the operator\nissues them as an explicit clause — which outranks the collation-server\nsetting in myCnf. Declaring `mysql-database` ourselves is what stops that: the\nreconciler only builds its own when that key is absent. `spec.database` still\nhas to stay, since IsInitialUserEnabled() needs it to create the edxapp user.\n\nThis matters beyond the wasted bytes. A schema''s default collation is fixed at\nCREATE DATABASE time and never follows a later server-config change, so every\nCREATE TABLE without an explicit COLLATE inherits it, and a foreign key across\ntwo collations is rejected with errno 150 — the longstanding migration failure\ndiagnosed in residential-production and residential-qa.\n\n`lehrer dev db-collation` ports the diagnostic half of ol-infrastructure''s\nbin/mariadb-collation-guard for datadirs created before this, keeping its\nsafe-fix boundary: schema-level ALTER DATABASE only, never an automatic table\nconversion or index repair. `setup` and `start` warn on the two states a\ndeveloper with an existing cluster can land in — a drifted schema, and a\ngenerated Database whose immutable collation now rejects the manifest.\n\ncleanupPolicy: Skip because the Database finalizer runs DROP DATABASE, which\nmakes deleting the resource to re-declare it a data-loss step on the CRD''s\nDelete default.\n\nbackoffLimit drops to 0 on both migrate Jobs. MariaDB DDL is not\ntransactional, so a migration that dies partway leaves what it created behind\nand a retry fails on \"table already exists\", burying the real error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LnWTKtfdrWW73WEzVsGK7L\n\n* fix(local-dev): stop the collation audit reporting failures as clean results\n\nThree review findings from PR #190.\n\n`_mysql` collapsed a failed statement into empty output, so every caller read\n\"the query did not run\" as \"the query found nothing\". `--fix` printed each\nALTER as applied whether or not it landed, and `--check-tables` reported\n\"none reporting an error\" after a query that never executed — the two places\nan audit tool most needs to not lie. It now returns None only for a statement\nthat did not run, surfacing the server''s own error, and \"\" stays a real empty\nresult. `capture_result` in _proc keeps returncode and stderr separate from\nstdout for that.\n\nThe uncollated-Database guard claimed both characterSet and collate are\nimmutable but compared only characterSet. The operator-generated resource\ndiffers in both, so it was caught in practice, but a mismatch in either alone\nis equally fatal and was equally silent. Both are now read and both appear in\nthe warning.\n\nmysql-database was added to the manifest but not to the k8s_resource objects\ngroup, which is what carries resource_deps=[\"mariadb-operator\"]. Tilt would\nhave made it its own resource with no dependency and applied it before the\nchart installed the CRDs. A test now pins the manifest''s CR set to the\nStarlark group, since nothing in either file points at the other.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LnWTKtfdrWW73WEzVsGK7L\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff97fced084648d7d215429a0d8f6f183bf98dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/ff97fced084648d7d215429a0d8f6f183bf98dac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e","verification":{"payload":"tree ff97fced084648d7d215429a0d8f6f183bf98dac\nparent 4c552aa11aa98f360b8e44c7f75572ee786d9341\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788345494 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788345494 -0400\n\nfix(local-dev): create edxapp on utf8mb4, not the operator''s utf8 default (#190)\n\n* fix(local-dev): create edxapp on utf8mb4, not the operator''s utf8 default\n\nThe edxapp schema was being created as `CHARACTER SET = ''utf8'' COLLATE =\n''utf8_general_ci''`, three-byte utf8, while notes and edxapp_csmh sat on\nutf8mb4_unicode_ci.\n\n`spec.database` on the MariaDB CR does not create the schema. The reconciler\nturns it into a Database CR named `<mariadb>-database` built with no\ncharacterSet/collate, so the CRD defaults get stamped on and the operator\nissues them as an explicit clause — which outranks the collation-server\nsetting in myCnf. Declaring `mysql-database` ourselves is what stops that: the\nreconciler only builds its own when that key is absent. `spec.database` still\nhas to stay, since IsInitialUserEnabled() needs it to create the edxapp user.\n\nThis matters beyond the wasted bytes. A schema''s default collation is fixed at\nCREATE DATABASE time and never follows a later server-config change, so every\nCREATE TABLE without an explicit COLLATE inherits it, and a foreign key across\ntwo collations is rejected with errno 150 — the longstanding migration failure\ndiagnosed in residential-production and residential-qa.\n\n`lehrer dev db-collation` ports the diagnostic half of ol-infrastructure''s\nbin/mariadb-collation-guard for datadirs created before this, keeping its\nsafe-fix boundary: schema-level ALTER DATABASE only, never an automatic table\nconversion or index repair. `setup` and `start` warn on the two states a\ndeveloper with an existing cluster can land in — a drifted schema, and a\ngenerated Database whose immutable collation now rejects the manifest.\n\ncleanupPolicy: Skip because the Database finalizer runs DROP DATABASE, which\nmakes deleting the resource to re-declare it a data-loss step on the CRD''s\nDelete default.\n\nbackoffLimit drops to 0 on both migrate Jobs. MariaDB DDL is not\ntransactional, so a migration that dies partway leaves what it created behind\nand a retry fails on \"table already exists\", burying the real error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LnWTKtfdrWW73WEzVsGK7L\n\n* fix(local-dev): stop the collation audit reporting failures as clean results\n\nThree review findings from PR #190.\n\n`_mysql` collapsed a failed statement into empty output, so every caller read\n\"the query did not run\" as \"the query found nothing\". `--fix` printed each\nALTER as applied whether or not it landed, and `--check-tables` reported\n\"none reporting an error\" after a query that never executed — the two places\nan audit tool most needs to not lie. It now returns None only for a statement\nthat did not run, surfacing the server''s own error, and \"\" stays a real empty\nresult. `capture_result` in _proc keeps returncode and stderr separate from\nstdout for that.\n\nThe uncollated-Database guard claimed both characterSet and collate are\nimmutable but compared only characterSet. The operator-generated resource\ndiffers in both, so it was caught in practice, but a mismatch in either alone\nis equally fatal and was equally silent. Both are now read and both appear in\nthe warning.\n\nmysql-database was added to the manifest but not to the k8s_resource objects\ngroup, which is what carries resource_deps=[\"mariadb-operator\"]. Tilt would\nhave made it its own resource with no dependency and applied it before the\nchart installed the CRDs. A test now pins the manifest''s CR set to the\nStarlark group, since nothing in either file points at the other.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LnWTKtfdrWW73WEzVsGK7L\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql/yWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASLoQABXjgMeT+HdPnwdy0TVBl3Qr\nx4/iZ3NFOz59YtXY/G7YsOyf+3jMsXwHMQanCq9Z3NZN7wjVBhSwao0t7WsjpgCo\n0gTYZaBjs+acH1fu2PNYyxormPKbqwCGhvaNxCYnKAImLNytFGhQKq5+rXfaAhQA\nbj89+tOaravkYEEwHTLW6z9HojdX/z8CBFZL/pWRXf9aNSxBWHsvpQCrTz/XyK2V\nD+urLecD3uCiyGtAtbLqq9qexsTV/6LewLc+eY5ciOXqVZ7+dcI2M/AHBxryPIg0\nszUE5938i0D68U2cUHHgDVfVxfOPqwuOHchZKJr1WLWAET3E2/8dXuCjR8Ia9waw\nd4RpHKJ2e0jGPZWfAdA7pFriIoZY9ZA+TRBDAJtBOlwGVGiu4rdFc9uwxamlObBi\nbdvCRCulPCHvACO5+Gr2RiyS0L9oPwDKiqoATmLrPy9oX0rAI+yajZhMuP48kntw\nNSBZQKlj1hELFiVGewLlTHuBdCR8m80bSMRyra4cwmycHtFdom4hGy9B+dwLajgS\niQ3QcFTlnS+PoK86siytyxaD8BS1K/onYN79yTA2ADyxIHWku46OZpKrw0UA/GDv\ni692yudZUGfHgYH8BFuUBFu1blv5w8Qw5Q2AduKl2u45Gjzo3b5TfnvFxCa/p1Ix\nwceW2/QNsE2XlrWgOyJ1\n=i+uI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T10:38:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDYzOTY3YzA1YzlkMjVjYmRlMmNlZmU1MWZlNmQzZWUwZTJhZDAwNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/4c552aa11aa98f360b8e44c7f75572ee786d9341","sha":"4c552aa11aa98f360b8e44c7f75572ee786d9341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/4c552aa11aa98f360b8e44c7f75572ee786d9341"}],"sha":"63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/63967c05c9d25cbde2cefe51fe6d3ee0e2ad006e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/4c552aa11aa98f360b8e44c7f75572ee786d9341/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:33:01Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:33:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mit-ol): regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models (#212)\n\n* fix(mit-ol): regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models\n\nedx-platform master added openedx_learning to INSTALLED_APPS, so the committed\nmodels went stale and the Settings Verification drift check failed for\nmit-ol/master/mitx and mit-ol/master/mitxonline:\n\n    DRIFT: the committed lms/models/aqueduct.py is stale against master\n\nSame class of drift as #187, and the same fix. The whole diff is those two\nlines, in both the lms and cms models:\n\n    # Competency criteria and student progress models\n    \"openedx_learning\",\n\nRegenerated via:\n\n    dagger call platform regenerate-aqueduct-settings \\\n      --deployment-name <mitx|mitxonline> --release-name master \\\n      --build-manifest ./deployments/mit-ol/build_manifest.yaml \\\n      export --path ./generated\n\nRan it for both mitx and mitxonline to check whether mitxonline''s\npackages_to_remove override changes the generated shape — byte-identical for\nlms and cms, as in #187 — so this one regeneration covers all three master\ncells including mitx-staging.\n\nAn AST field-name comparison against the committed versions reports zero fields\nadded and zero removed (lms 393, cms 171): the model shape is unchanged, and\nonly the contents of one INSTALLED_APPS default grew.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* fix(generic): regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models\n\nThe generic deployment carries the same drift, and PR-triggered runs never\nshowed it: the workflow picks cells from changed files, so touching only\ndeployments/mit-ol/ selected only mit-ol cells. `settings-matrix --all` — what\nthe scheduled and manual runs use — includes generic/master/generic with\ndrift: true, so it would have stayed red after the mit-ol fix.\n\ngeneric was two upstream changes behind, not one:\n\n- gains \"openedx_learning\" in INSTALLED_APPS, same as mit-ol (lms and cms)\n- drops ENABLE_MFE_CONFIG_API, which upstream removed from lms.envs.common.\n  mit-ol already dropped it in #200; generic was not regenerated at the time.\n\nSo unlike the mit-ol commit, this one removes a field. AST comparison: generic\nlms one field removed (ENABLE_MFE_CONFIG_API), none added; generic cms no field\nchange. Both models now match mit-ol''s field counts exactly — lms 393, cms 171.\n\nReported by Copilot on #212.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcca2eee2a60867a516408b1e742436b8760d17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/bcca2eee2a60867a516408b1e742436b8760d17c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/4c552aa11aa98f360b8e44c7f75572ee786d9341","verification":{"payload":"tree bcca2eee2a60867a516408b1e742436b8760d17c\nparent dfd6cf6a1d9765e549d73a752581b3f2358191e8\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788345181 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788345181 -0400\n\nfix(mit-ol): regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models (#212)\n\n* fix(mit-ol): regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models\n\nedx-platform master added openedx_learning to INSTALLED_APPS, so the committed\nmodels went stale and the Settings Verification drift check failed for\nmit-ol/master/mitx and mit-ol/master/mitxonline:\n\n    DRIFT: the committed lms/models/aqueduct.py is stale against master\n\nSame class of drift as #187, and the same fix. The whole diff is those two\nlines, in both the lms and cms models:\n\n    # Competency criteria and student progress models\n    \"openedx_learning\",\n\nRegenerated via:\n\n    dagger call platform regenerate-aqueduct-settings \\\n      --deployment-name <mitx|mitxonline> --release-name master \\\n      --build-manifest ./deployments/mit-ol/build_manifest.yaml \\\n      export --path ./generated\n\nRan it for both mitx and mitxonline to check whether mitxonline''s\npackages_to_remove override changes the generated shape — byte-identical for\nlms and cms, as in #187 — so this one regeneration covers all three master\ncells including mitx-staging.\n\nAn AST field-name comparison against the committed versions reports zero fields\nadded and zero removed (lms 393, cms 171): the model shape is unchanged, and\nonly the contents of one INSTALLED_APPS default grew.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n* fix(generic): regenerate the master release''s aqueduct settings models\n\nThe generic deployment carries the same drift, and PR-triggered runs never\nshowed it: the workflow picks cells from changed files, so touching only\ndeployments/mit-ol/ selected only mit-ol cells. `settings-matrix --all` — what\nthe scheduled and manual runs use — includes generic/master/generic with\ndrift: true, so it would have stayed red after the mit-ol fix.\n\ngeneric was two upstream changes behind, not one:\n\n- gains \"openedx_learning\" in INSTALLED_APPS, same as mit-ol (lms and cms)\n- drops ENABLE_MFE_CONFIG_API, which upstream removed from lms.envs.common.\n  mit-ol already dropped it in #200; generic was not regenerated at the time.\n\nSo unlike the mit-ol commit, this one removes a field. AST comparison: generic\nlms one field removed (ENABLE_MFE_CONFIG_API), none added; generic cms no field\nchange. Both models now match mit-ol''s field counts exactly — lms 393, cms 171.\n\nReported by Copilot on #212.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SJbu4a1oSMpGNVrnZ9xu4J\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql/tdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvHcQAAdumeFLOK1Y1EdWOlzzPe7u\nzySk0IPcySHkfY3tzgsYn7Hw+f2KqTb2QMi3dHNMSaivsqbq+I4mwYcMQec3vzOM\nMjr2j+YpgcNOqZv673qPi9ZwTm5RHSKUnx751TRmyOGxnsneW4l1TaIu2KHjav8A\n2JRnII4++x9NvNb3TAxIEuJozyB5sjN7PEEu2tevlMSK354EFeKfRB0cLuZdhTKO\nVbYcA1lDPkc1FGW3s2FbscOAWJZAPRzT996g6Opi3DWSRhm1hqoyDjsWt5Z8zKJa\nNbiAVyToSur8bDulitiW/LEgjPwBPBS8SM28GyGrEBGCm+dele9KBXcQ0gCY2zh3\nMdN7VQbtPYoSiDa/R/qjPwNKeBT6Uh2uhPjpJi+AnF+PnqtSip22rWC8nw3zG02S\npd/cFe9pbTbfeRmh8lFqkbtZJB6WFbdlUFGvIOLA3Gn18htSFrs9J9KTFlYtgO6k\n8x8g2J2ebPGIbs8LwqyCXNqzvh9ouhcv5jxT/hG29zMcM/A58UMAMgKLbeaCNcuy\nS/BiyOFt+kd2D7Qwe3g+4rJy320fosnHb1tHrs8TfcSVouIyIuwWG19/5idre03v\n9WrAYZftb7szNoAytj+tFQYo0txwzXZP21GpJ5CAD2CZGqdGHAcsoJgMCsdkxSsC\n2ICMi8UcLCKVPm38bQNQ\n=wvP8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T10:33:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url