followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/dfd6cf6a1d9765e549d73a752581b3f2358191e8","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKGRmZDZjZjZhMWQ5NzY1ZTU0OWQ3M2E3NTI1ODFiM2YyMzU4MTkxZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b","sha":"4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b"}],"sha":"dfd6cf6a1d9765e549d73a752581b3f2358191e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/dfd6cf6a1d9765e549d73a752581b3f2358191e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T15:41:33Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T15:41:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mit-ol): install forum from our branch, drop the edx-django-utils fork (#208)\n\n* fix(mit-ol): install forum from our branch, drop the edx-django-utils fork\n\nTwo override changes, in opposite directions.\n\nForum: the Typesense search backend is non-functional on every search, not\njust some -- per_page is set above Typesense''s hard cap of 250, and the topic\nfilter names a field the collection schema does not declare. Both have been\nthere since the backend shipped. Fix is openedx/forum#289, which is green and\nawaiting review; until it merges and releases, the master cells install forum\nfrom the branch. Scoped to master only: our branch is based on forum master,\nso pointing verawood or ulmo at it would jump them across release boundaries\nfor no benefit -- both still have forum search on Elasticsearch.\n\nThis changes nothing at runtime today, since typesense:forum_search_enabled is\nfalse everywhere. It is what makes flipping that toggle possible.\n\nedx-django-utils: openedx/edx-django-utils#549 merged and shipped in 8.0.2, so\nthe fork branch is no longer needed. edx-platform master already pins 8.0.2 and\nthe three master cells simply drop the override. The verawood and ulmo cells\ncannot: those branches pin 8.0.1, which predates the fix, so they take an\nexplicit 8.0.2 pin instead. Deleting the override outright would have quietly\nregressed OpenTelemetryBackend.create_span() on four of the seven cells.\n\n* fix(mit-ol): extend the forum override to verawood\n\nI had scoped this to the master cells out of caution rather than evidence.\nHaving actually diffed 0.4.2 against forum master, verawood can take it too.\n\nThe delta is ten commits, and only three modules are genuinely removed once\nthe src/ layout move is normalised away: backends/mongodb/*,\nforum_create_mongodb_indexes, and toggles.py.\n\nNone of that reaches us. All twelve environments already run\nforum_v2.enable_mysql_backend for everyone, so nobody is on the Mongo data\nbackend. Nothing in openedx-platform imports forum.backends.mongodb or\nforum.toggles, and nothing in ol-infrastructure or lehrer invokes the removed\nmanagement command. toggles.py only ever defined the enable_mysql_backend\nwaffle flag itself, which is redundant now that MySQL is the sole backend --\nworth noting that our set_waffle_flags entries for it become dead config.\n\nThe rest is packaging (uv, src layout, semantic-release) and typing.cast()\nwrappers around request.data in the views, which are no-ops at runtime.\n\nulmo stays on 0.4.1, now for a concrete reason rather than caution: forum\nmaster declares requires-python >=3.12 and the ulmo cell builds on 3.11, so\nit cannot install. verawood builds on 3.12, and forum master''s only other\nconstraint is Django>=4.2.\n\nVerified by installing the branch into a clean 3.12 venv: builds, reports\n0.4.5, and the installed forum/search/typesense.py carries\nTYPESENSE_MAX_PER_PAGE = 250 and the singular commentable_id filter.","tree":{"sha":"c8e1c90fd976ff9e4987270ef15b00574681add7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/c8e1c90fd976ff9e4987270ef15b00574681add7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b","verification":{"payload":"tree c8e1c90fd976ff9e4987270ef15b00574681add7\nparent d7baa44a9ef535b5cdd405464a7a1a07fa89ae19\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788277293 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788277293 -0400\n\nfix(mit-ol): install forum from our branch, drop the edx-django-utils fork (#208)\n\n* fix(mit-ol): install forum from our branch, drop the edx-django-utils fork\n\nTwo override changes, in opposite directions.\n\nForum: the Typesense search backend is non-functional on every search, not\njust some -- per_page is set above Typesense''s hard cap of 250, and the topic\nfilter names a field the collection schema does not declare. Both have been\nthere since the backend shipped. Fix is openedx/forum#289, which is green and\nawaiting review; until it merges and releases, the master cells install forum\nfrom the branch. Scoped to master only: our branch is based on forum master,\nso pointing verawood or ulmo at it would jump them across release boundaries\nfor no benefit -- both still have forum search on Elasticsearch.\n\nThis changes nothing at runtime today, since typesense:forum_search_enabled is\nfalse everywhere. It is what makes flipping that toggle possible.\n\nedx-django-utils: openedx/edx-django-utils#549 merged and shipped in 8.0.2, so\nthe fork branch is no longer needed. edx-platform master already pins 8.0.2 and\nthe three master cells simply drop the override. The verawood and ulmo cells\ncannot: those branches pin 8.0.1, which predates the fix, so they take an\nexplicit 8.0.2 pin instead. Deleting the override outright would have quietly\nregressed OpenTelemetryBackend.create_span() on four of the seven cells.\n\n* fix(mit-ol): extend the forum override to verawood\n\nI had scoped this to the master cells out of caution rather than evidence.\nHaving actually diffed 0.4.2 against forum master, verawood can take it too.\n\nThe delta is ten commits, and only three modules are genuinely removed once\nthe src/ layout move is normalised away: backends/mongodb/*,\nforum_create_mongodb_indexes, and toggles.py.\n\nNone of that reaches us. All twelve environments already run\nforum_v2.enable_mysql_backend for everyone, so nobody is on the Mongo data\nbackend. Nothing in openedx-platform imports forum.backends.mongodb or\nforum.toggles, and nothing in ol-infrastructure or lehrer invokes the removed\nmanagement command. toggles.py only ever defined the enable_mysql_backend\nwaffle flag itself, which is redundant now that MySQL is the sole backend --\nworth noting that our set_waffle_flags entries for it become dead config.\n\nThe rest is packaging (uv, src layout, semantic-release) and typing.cast()\nwrappers around request.data in the views, which are no-ops at runtime.\n\nulmo stays on 0.4.1, now for a concrete reason rather than caution: forum\nmaster declares requires-python >=3.12 and the ulmo cell builds on 3.11, so\nit cannot install. verawood builds on 3.12, and forum master''s only other\nconstraint is Django>=4.2.\n\nVerified by installing the branch into a clean 3.12 venv: builds, reports\n0.4.5, and the installed forum/search/typesense.py carries\nTYPESENSE_MAX_PER_PAGE = 250 and the singular commentable_id filter.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlvItCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfQAQAI+6HbHXHlIOssAmisU4njt6\n6dg1t7cmqD7RyGU/rskOPEOQuJPK9K8Js+Y6fP3JTjLBXU3DS1SA+v59JhChrIk5\njsYcIt/fSF1Bu8k+TALOR9M819BG88fzhsVP69+uRSbpVqrCZ+0jz259nVJMkm0E\nxZuRqFz+L1N+2rW1FF95xeZ5EzPMlL7DIGpy7ewMbRUW6byDBMA3S0Qpl6omGOiQ\nvIBH73aHdRomoy1qfskEH9nizWbZktZMRdhA2h3wv5apYIC4skYYdkdIgtW9cTMP\nEwZmZ6HYswIVwhdDcFmG20ntP8qr5BF6WkrhDFAQIERXKmXt1ntsocwGf7NDh/rG\nwwhqBzqbb0u+jS9AudBY/Tk3nTm/0wvsxU8TNG1nHz5A4ev/n3kjYkAMN0f7xVU6\nfTO07oYnv8++t8iokjFEcL2ayltpeYn2TvGjN50RmehG1Tk47B8HrCxs3ZXSBxqj\nDiTAzxrVC1ev5S90sU9AlQ7GSSgao8OXOP+xB+iIYtcicv/I6Tv3iO2IeXa74NNM\nROgXTfEjPiPZQiz8o1efZZ5Mt5MEvgDKuk1cCn2kFiaP0V1wCtjXgFYG9+a2hprV\nEu2xW+DOl74+qpIvlWjon2l8coS4Q54NhZIzqoGozJWfhl6cr4ZyT8bJOIzDNKLe\nIXLDr0isWKC9ey+vXvAC\n=zfx+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T15:41:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b","node_id":"C_kwDORFoK8NoAKDQxMjU5MzI5NjUyNTZlZGFiZWM0MzM3ZmQ3ZTRmNmVmYjE0NjRiMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitodl/lehrer/commit/d7baa44a9ef535b5cdd405464a7a1a07fa89ae19","sha":"d7baa44a9ef535b5cdd405464a7a1a07fa89ae19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/d7baa44a9ef535b5cdd405464a7a1a07fa89ae19"}],"sha":"4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/4125932965256edabec4337fd7e4f6efb1464b2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/479088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/d7baa44a9ef535b5cdd405464a7a1a07fa89ae19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:15:08Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:15:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(docs): realign README, copilot-instructions and deployment guide with the code (#207)\n\n* chore(docs): realign README, copilot-instructions and deployment guide with the code\n\nThe docs described the pre-refactor repo: a single-file `src/lehrer/main.py`\nholding every function, MFE and service builders that fell back to MIT OL''s\nconfig directories, and a `build_platform` stage order that has since changed.\nAn agent or a new operator following them writes flags that no longer parse.\n\nVerified each corrected claim against the source rather than the prose it\nreplaced:\n\n- `build_platform` runs `collected` → `fetch_translations` →\n  `build_static_assets` → `inject_aqueduct_settings` → `docker_image`. Both\n  the README''s numbered stage list and its prose had aqueduct injection\n  second.\n- `slot_config`, `codejail_config` and `notes_config` raise a `ValueError`\n  naming the flag when omitted. The deployment guide advertised a fallback to\n  MIT OL''s directories that does not exist.\n- `build_legacy` has no `enable_ai_drawer`; its `node_version` is a Docker tag\n  defaulting to `20` and its `deployment_name` to `default`. Documented the\n  four parameters the table never had (`mfe_source`, `extra_slot_files`,\n  `env_vars`, `pre_build_commands`) and added `build_legacy_configured` and\n  `watch_legacy`.\n- Parameters the manifest cell resolves are marked `None` → cell, matching\n  `_resolve_field`''s explicit > cell > fallback order, instead of listing the\n  fallback as if it were the default.\n- `custom_settings` supplies no top-level `models/base.py`;\n  `inject_aqueduct_settings` injects it from `src/lehrer/settings/base.py`.\n- Documented the `lehrer-core-boundary` pre-commit hook in the agent\n  instructions. It rejects operator-specific strings anywhere under\n  `lehrer.core`/`lehrer.infra`, Markdown included, which is not discoverable\n  until it fails.\n\nCruft removed: the root `main.py` \"Hello from lehrer!\" stub (the Dagger\nentrypoint is `src/lehrer/main.py`; `dagger functions` still resolves all four\nservice objects with it gone), the second plan numbered 04 (renamed to\n`plans/aqueduct-model-completeness.md` — it is a follow-up note, not a\nnumbered plan, and the other 04 is cross-referenced by name from two other\nfiles), the `local_dev` docstring''s reference to `local-dev/scripts/*.sh`,\nwhich no longer exists, and the spliced paragraph in `infra/DESIGN.md` along\nwith its cross-reference to an uncommitted plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011MmM9AtMhdEV1YpArySbX3\n\n* chore(docs): correct six claims flagged in review\n\nAll six hold up against the source, and on a PR whose whole claim is that the\ndocs now match the code they are the feedback that matters:\n\n- `ci.yml` runs four checks plus three *named* pre-commit hooks\n  (`build-config-schema`, `build-manifest-schema`, `lehrer-core-boundary`),\n  not `pre-commit run --all-files`. Split the local command from the PR gate\n  rather than presenting one as the other.\n- The second `apt-base` installs the same compilers and `-dev` headers as the\n  first, and `nodeenv` is copied across explicitly, so \"the build toolchain\n  never reaches the shipped image\" was wrong. What the copy excludes is the\n  intermediate state of dependency resolution.\n- `strict_translations` covers every step `_tolerant` wraps — the plugin and\n  xblock pulls and compiles as well as `atlas pull` — not just a language\n  fetch. `compilemessages`/`compilejsi18n` are unwrapped and hard-fail either\n  way; said so.\n- `watch_legacy` raises on `slot_config=None` (`mfe.py:406`) exactly as\n  `build_legacy` does, so the table''s `None` default was unreachable.\n- The `lehrer-core-boundary` hook excludes both packages'' `__init__.py`, so\n  \"anywhere under\" overstated it in two places. Documented the exception in\n  both rather than removing it: tightening the lint gate is a behavior change\n  that does not belong in a docs PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011MmM9AtMhdEV1YpArySbX3\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40754e7fcb7de4becec0650438045a26419d18c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/40754e7fcb7de4becec0650438045a26419d18c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/d7baa44a9ef535b5cdd405464a7a1a07fa89ae19","verification":{"payload":"tree 40754e7fcb7de4becec0650438045a26419d18c7\nparent 467e538aab5654d02d1890288d9d11268c5fea9e\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1788214508 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788214508 -0400\n\nchore(docs): realign README, copilot-instructions and deployment guide with the code (#207)\n\n* chore(docs): realign README, copilot-instructions and deployment guide with the code\n\nThe docs described the pre-refactor repo: a single-file `src/lehrer/main.py`\nholding every function, MFE and service builders that fell back to MIT OL''s\nconfig directories, and a `build_platform` stage order that has since changed.\nAn agent or a new operator following them writes flags that no longer parse.\n\nVerified each corrected claim against the source rather than the prose it\nreplaced:\n\n- `build_platform` runs `collected` → `fetch_translations` →\n  `build_static_assets` → `inject_aqueduct_settings` → `docker_image`. Both\n  the README''s numbered stage list and its prose had aqueduct injection\n  second.\n- `slot_config`, `codejail_config` and `notes_config` raise a `ValueError`\n  naming the flag when omitted. The deployment guide advertised a fallback to\n  MIT OL''s directories that does not exist.\n- `build_legacy` has no `enable_ai_drawer`; its `node_version` is a Docker tag\n  defaulting to `20` and its `deployment_name` to `default`. Documented the\n  four parameters the table never had (`mfe_source`, `extra_slot_files`,\n  `env_vars`, `pre_build_commands`) and added `build_legacy_configured` and\n  `watch_legacy`.\n- Parameters the manifest cell resolves are marked `None` → cell, matching\n  `_resolve_field`''s explicit > cell > fallback order, instead of listing the\n  fallback as if it were the default.\n- `custom_settings` supplies no top-level `models/base.py`;\n  `inject_aqueduct_settings` injects it from `src/lehrer/settings/base.py`.\n- Documented the `lehrer-core-boundary` pre-commit hook in the agent\n  instructions. It rejects operator-specific strings anywhere under\n  `lehrer.core`/`lehrer.infra`, Markdown included, which is not discoverable\n  until it fails.\n\nCruft removed: the root `main.py` \"Hello from lehrer!\" stub (the Dagger\nentrypoint is `src/lehrer/main.py`; `dagger functions` still resolves all four\nservice objects with it gone), the second plan numbered 04 (renamed to\n`plans/aqueduct-model-completeness.md` — it is a follow-up note, not a\nnumbered plan, and the other 04 is cross-referenced by name from two other\nfiles), the `local_dev` docstring''s reference to `local-dev/scripts/*.sh`,\nwhich no longer exists, and the spliced paragraph in `infra/DESIGN.md` along\nwith its cross-reference to an uncommitted plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011MmM9AtMhdEV1YpArySbX3\n\n* chore(docs): correct six claims flagged in review\n\nAll six hold up against the source, and on a PR whose whole claim is that the\ndocs now match the code they are the feedback that matters:\n\n- `ci.yml` runs four checks plus three *named* pre-commit hooks\n  (`build-config-schema`, `build-manifest-schema`, `lehrer-core-boundary`),\n  not `pre-commit run --all-files`. Split the local command from the PR gate\n  rather than presenting one as the other.\n- The second `apt-base` installs the same compilers and `-dev` headers as the\n  first, and `nodeenv` is copied across explicitly, so \"the build toolchain\n  never reaches the shipped image\" was wrong. What the copy excludes is the\n  intermediate state of dependency resolution.\n- `strict_translations` covers every step `_tolerant` wraps — the plugin and\n  xblock pulls and compiles as well as `atlas pull` — not just a language\n  fetch. `compilemessages`/`compilejsi18n` are unwrapped and hard-fail either\n  way; said so.\n- `watch_legacy` raises on `slot_config=None` (`mfe.py:406`) exactly as\n  `build_legacy` does, so the table''s `None` default was unreachable.\n- The `lehrer-core-boundary` hook excludes both packages'' `__init__.py`, so\n  \"anywhere under\" overstated it in two places. Documented the exception in\n  both rather than removing it: tightening the lint gate is a behavior change\n  that does not belong in a docs PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011MmM9AtMhdEV1YpArySbX3\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlfzsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARMwQAAxqwjIN07MyPG3Y0wyIt/HT\nB2ZIgCLZx