,"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blarghmatey","id":479088,"login":"blarghmatey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3OTA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/commits/8d3781957473923178393817b557eb1a167ba9c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T18:58:33Z","email":"tmacey@mit.edu","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T18:58:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(xpro): build the instructor dashboard from the verawood fork branch (#199)\n\nAdding a course team member on Verawood CI fails silently for an inactive\naccount, and reports nothing at all when the grant fails for any other reason.\nBoth are MFE-side: the LMS returns the reason per identifier and the modal\ndiscards it. The fix is in review upstream (openedx/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard#234),\nwhich xPRO CI testing should not have to wait on.\n\nmitodl/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard@verawood is v1.2.0, the version the\nnpm range already resolved to, plus those two commits and nothing else. The\nlock pins the commit, so the build stays reproducible while the branch moves.\n\nScope: this is the xpro Site Project, which is per-deployment rather than\nper-release, so it covers the ulmo cell too. Only CI builds from it — QA and\nProduction promote the artifact behind the GitHub issue gate.\n\nRevert once #234 merges and ships in a release.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rw1RKoF87LSNrD1fFVgfCn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44f743daea9102717b8b8bba1266ea647a9cbecd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/trees/44f743daea9102717b8b8bba1266ea647a9cbecd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitodl/lehrer/git/commits/8d3781957473923178393817b557eb1a167ba9c6","verification":{"payload":"tree 44f743daea9102717b8b8bba1266ea647a9cbecd\nparent 91e7bccfe36c954895e6af225d75a09fd66f39de\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@mit.edu> 1787943513 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787943513 -0400\n\nfeat(xpro): build the instructor dashboard from the verawood fork branch (#199)\n\nAdding a course team member on Verawood CI fails silently for an inactive\naccount, and reports nothing at all when the grant fails for any other reason.\nBoth are MFE-side: the LMS returns the reason per identifier and the modal\ndiscards it. The fix is in review upstream (openedx/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard#234),\nwhich xPRO CI testing should not have to wait on.\n\nmitodl/frontend-app-instructor-dashboard@verawood is v1.2.0, the version the\nnpm range already resolved to, plus those two commits and nothing else. The\nlock pins the commit, so the build stays reproducible while the branch moves.\n\nScope: this is the xpro Site Project, which is per-deployment rather than\nper-release, so it covers the ulmo cell too. Only CI builds from it — QA and\nProduction promote the artifact behind the GitHub issue gate.\n\nRevert once #234 merges and ships in a release.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rw1RKoF87LSNrD1fFVgfCn\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkdpZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkh0QACcKNLuLceB8Pa16k4+Zsrim\na4ar3B/i51m3HnpEVY1r3dJYBJsDcubFcfwgtjIZ1rUJExYO1k9qlIr0/h7gYpx7\nhiaOZBw5CoGIIYbJd8Zw38f9bqR8wsJVr7bpXwWstKA+QGniWKqOclAoQPqRkKI2\neYdhqoTsb6OjKIBNTJB0ofo/UYfi0fAKoRb