/aargoncar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commits/4c6cd13438f01c3e40666dc95ebe2a03cefefb91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T06:33:33Z","email":"gonzalo.carmenado@iesa.es","name":"Gonzalo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T06:33:33Z","email":"gonzalo.carmenado@iesa.es","name":"Gonzalo"},"message":"fix(recorder): bypass filesystem dialog, honor test strategy flag, and use double-quote cy.get() for apostrophe selectors\n\n- initFilesystemAccess() returns early when __e2eRecorderTestMode__ is in window,\n  preventing the filesystem setup Swal from intercepting Cypress test flows\n- initSelectorStrategy() reads __e2eTestStrategy__ window flag (set before page load)\n  so Cypress tests can pre-set the strategy without touching IndexedDB\n- selectorLiteral() helper in code-format.utils.ts uses double-quote JS wrapping\n  when a selector contains a single quote, keeping cy.get() calls syntactically valid\n  without backslash escapes — e.g. cy.get(\"[data-cy=\\\"o''brien\\\"]\") instead of\n  cy.get(''[data-cy=\"o\\''brien\"]'')\n- Update recording.service.ts to use selectorLiteral() throughout for all cy.get() commands\n- Update recording.service.spec.ts AC-01 expectations to match new double-quote format\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"185e7e00708fefdc9489620ddce1f5e5871daf21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/git/trees/185e7e00708fefdc9489620ddce1f5e5871daf21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/git/commits/4c6cd13438f01c3e40666dc95ebe2a03cefefb91","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163729672?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/events{/privacy}","followers