,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commits/6644ed65abb45fc18f280a05da05679a3cbff74f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T11:54:33Z","email":"gonzalo.carmenado@iesa.es","name":"Gonzalo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T11:54:33Z","email":"gonzalo.carmenado@iesa.es","name":"Gonzalo"},"message":"fix(recording): ignore picker trigger for decorative non-interactive elements\n\nAfter removing infrastructure ids from the shell, clicking any div/p/h1\nwithout a test selector triggered the picker. Added a guard at the end\nof the non-interactive path: if the element has no button/a/role=button\nancestor, the click is silently ignored. If it does have one (e.g. a\nspan inside a button), re-target to that ancestor and continue normally.\n\nUpdated tests: selectorNotFound now only fires for interactive elements\n(button, a, label, etc.) or their children — not for decorative divs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d253ef4bb1d134f15b2be8ddad151f47730c3028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/git/trees/d253ef4bb1d134f15b2be8ddad151f47730c3028"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/git/commits/6644ed65abb45fc18f280a05da05679a3cbff74f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163729672?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aargoncar","id":163729672,"login":"aargoncar","node_id":"U_kgDOCcJRCA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commit/6644ed65abb45fc18f280a05da05679a3cbff74f","node_id":"C_kwDORFuyzdoAKDY2NDRlZDY1YWJiNDVmYzE4ZjI4MGEwNWRhMDU2NzlhM2NiZmY3NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commit/6c1eed08edf301ee82ecd44e8101bff8b5c820e9","sha":"6c1eed08edf301ee82ecd44e8101bff8b5c820e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commits/6c1eed08edf301ee82ecd44e8101bff8b5c820e9"}],"sha":"6644ed65abb45fc18f280a05da05679a3cbff74f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commits/6644ed65abb45fc18f280a05da05679a3cbff74f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163729672?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aargoncar","id":163729672,"login":"aargoncar","node_id":"U_kgDOCcJRCA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aargoncar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/commits/6c1eed08edf301ee82ecd44e8101bff8b5c820e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T07:03:05Z","email":"gonzalo.carmenado@iesa.es","name":"Gonzalo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T07:03:05Z","email":"gonzalo.carmenado@iesa.es","name":"Gonzalo"},"message":"fix(ejemplo): remove infrastructure ids from shell so picker can trigger in §5.1/§5.2\n\nRemoved id=\"app\", id=\"nav\", id=\"remote-slot\", id=\"recorder-badge\" from\nthe shell — all replaced with class selectors. Because closest(''[id]'')\nwas walking up to these shell elements before the recording service could\ndecide there was no valid selector, §5.1 and §5.2 buttons were recording\ncy.get(''#remote-slot'').click() instead of opening the picker.\n\nRedesigned §5.2 to use id=\"cdk-inner-wrap\" (forbidden prefix) as the\nimmediate wrapper: closest() finds it, getReliableSelector returns null,\nthe new fix fires selectorNotFound$, and the picker opens showing all\nfour quality tiers in the ancestor chain (excellent/good/acceptable/poor).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ffd4337148f3be7f0dc6c23d7d1318395d7abe6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/git/trees/8ffd4337148f3be7f0dc6c23d7d1318395d7abe6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GonzaloCarmenado/lib-e2e-cypress-for-dummys-ts/git/commits/6c1eed08edf301ee82ecd44e8101bff8b5c820e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163729672?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use