tps://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/commits/209ffe6a0ce6301694340539e725ffc7e3a225b9"}],"sha":"6b880b4ca93057ffe242b2ec117458873c8c892f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/commits/6b880b4ca93057ffe242b2ec117458873c8c892f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8247489?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ViewFromTheBox","id":8247489,"login":"ViewFromTheBox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNDc0ODk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/commits/209ffe6a0ce6301694340539e725ffc7e3a225b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:05:30Z","email":"me@jacobmartella.com","name":"Jacob Martella"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:05:30Z","email":"me@jacobmartella.com","name":"Jacob Martella"},"message":"fix: reconcile the tree when a self-update aborts after extraction\n\nWhen `performUpdate()` aborted after extracting a release over `base_path()`,\nthe site was left in a broken, unfinalized hybrid: stale compiled caches, a\nhalf-applied tree, and orphaned build assets and upstream-deleted files that\nextract-on-top can never clean up. On a real install this surfaced as a white\nscreen served entirely from a config cache that no longer matched the code on\ndisk.\n\nThis applies the targeted fixes from #308 without rewriting the hardened\nextraction engine:\n\n- Pre-flight the archive''s `composer.json`/`composer.lock` pair from inside the\n  ZIP before extraction touches the live tree, and refuse a provably out-of-sync\n  release when stale-lock recovery is disabled — so a rejected release never\n  touches `base_path()` and there is nothing to roll back. Stays silent when\n  recovery is enabled (the default), preserving the #273 recover path.\n- Drop the compiled caches (`optimize:clear`, best-effort) on every abort branch\n  — rollback, no-backup, and finish-forward — so the resulting tree never boots\n  behind caches compiled against the failed release.\n- On a successful update, purge orphaned hashed `public/build` assets the current\n  manifest no longer references, and delete paths a release declares removed in\n  an upstream `.artisanpack/removed-paths.json` manifest. Both are best-effort\n  and reuse the existing traversal/symlink/exclusion guards.\n\nAdds four config keys (all defaulting on) and 11 tests.\n\nCloses #308\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df7fd3e6dc81beabb8d562004d940d88d47d08f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/git/trees/df7fd3e6dc81beabb8d562004d940d88d47d08f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/git/commits/209ffe6a0ce6301694340539e725ffc7e3a225b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8247489?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https