","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ViewFromTheBox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/commits/a660df5446b989b0cd8b3b5a6cb98f6a0343e5bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:34:45Z","email":"me@jacobmartella.com","name":"Jacob Martella"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:34:45Z","email":"me@jacobmartella.com","name":"Jacob Martella"},"message":"fix: match plugin manifest slug against the plugin being installed/updated\n\n`PluginManager::validateManifest()` only checked the manifest `slug` for\nformat, never that it matched the plugin the manifest belongs to. Because\nthe row `slug` is derived from the ZIP''s top-level directory while `meta`\nis seated verbatim from the manifest, the two could diverge — letting a\nplugin declare (and, on uninstall, remove via `removeSeededPermissions()`)\npermission rows namespaced under a different plugin''s slug.\n\nMirror `ThemeManager`, which already asserts the manifest slug matches\nafter extraction:\n\n- `PluginManager::installFromZip()` asserts `$manifest[''slug'']` equals the\n  extracted directory slug, rolling back the extracted directory and\n  throwing `PluginValidationException` before any row is created.\n- `UpdateManager::updatePlugin()` asserts `$manifest[''slug'']` equals the\n  plugin being updated, unwinding through the existing backup-restore path.\n\nCloses #315\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"627e6bc37c63f72d5334e54fd499f35d59f03a23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/git/trees/627e6bc37c63f72d5334e54fd499f35d59f03a23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ArtisanPack-UI/cms-framework/g